-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OpenNebula/one/commit/8d242e0c989d094ddf22b3b825eba0b01be65bc2","node_id":"C_kwDOABZZE9oAKDhkMjQyZTBjOTg5ZDA5NGRkZjIyYjNiODI1ZWJhMGIwMWJlNjViYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OpenNebula/one/commit/82196ef2bef9f26d6dd645903df267c8e2e96c7d","sha":"82196ef2bef9f26d6dd645903df267c8e2e96c7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/commits/82196ef2bef9f26d6dd645903df267c8e2e96c7d"}],"sha":"8d242e0c989d094ddf22b3b825eba0b01be65bc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/commits/8d242e0c989d094ddf22b3b825eba0b01be65bc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1098246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xorel","id":1098246,"login":"xorel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTgyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xorel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/commits/82196ef2bef9f26d6dd645903df267c8e2e96c7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:23:47Z","email":"jorel@opennebula.io","name":"Jan Orel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:23:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"B #7899: Fix the remote scripts directory handling (#4379)\n\nThe remote scripts directory (former SCRIPTS_REMOTE_DIR) is now fixed\nto /var/lib/one-remotes and the configuration attribute is gone. The\nold default /var/tmp/one was broken in several ways: /var/tmp content\nis aged away by systemd-tmpfiles, the world-writable parent allows\nsquatting on the directory, and the configurable location was silently\nnot honored by many drivers, probes and static files (sudoers,\nAppArmor, tmpfiles, cron).\n\n  - The remotes are synced to /var/lib/one-remotes on the hosts; the\n    directory is created by the node packages, as it cannot be created\n    by the unprivileged oneadmin\n  - The node monitoring DB moves along to /var/lib/one-remotes-db;\n    it cannot live inside the remotes directory as the sync\n    (rsync --delete) would remove it. The monitord client migrates\n    the DB from the legacy location on its first start\n  - Helpers executed through sudo are installed at a fixed path\n    (/usr/lib/one/sbin) by the node packages, so they are no longer\n    executed from an oneadmin-writable location\n  - Remote hooks (REMOTE = yes) run from /var/lib/one-remotes/hooks.\n    Hook commands given as an absolute path are executed as-is and\n    must be updated manually\n  - Fix remotes sync to run the mkdir on the host: the local shell\n    interpreted the unquoted '';'' and ran it on the frontend instead\n  - onecfg migrator drops SCRIPTS_REMOTE_DIR from oned.conf and the\n    stock :remote_hook_base_path from onehem-server.conf","tree":{"sha":"926da04f95e9cc52ea674d285dd67757d8dc5d23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/trees/926da04f95e9cc52ea674d285dd67757d8dc5d23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/commits/82196ef2bef9f26d6dd645903df267c8e2e96c7d","verification":{"payload":"tree 926da04f95e9cc52ea674d285dd67757d8dc5d23\nparent aae2db9f8db0df3d266c35c5d3be4ec8bf777146\nauthor Jan Orel <jorel@opennebula.io> 1790861027 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790861027 +0200\n\nB #7899: Fix the remote scripts directory handling (#4379)\n\nThe remote scripts directory (former SCRIPTS_REMOTE_DIR) is now fixed\nto /var/lib/one-remotes and the configuration attribute is gone. The\nold default /var/tmp/one was broken in several ways: /var/tmp content\nis aged away by systemd-tmpfiles, the world-writable parent allows\nsquatting on the directory, and the configurable location was silently\nnot honored by many drivers, probes and static files (sudoers,\nAppArmor, tmpfiles, cron).\n\n  - The remotes are synced to /var/lib/one-remotes on the hosts; the\n    directory is created by the node packages, as it cannot be created\n    by the unprivileged oneadmin\n  - The node monitoring DB moves along to /var/lib/one-remotes-db;\n    it cannot live inside the remotes directory as the sync\n    (rsync --delete) would remove it. The monitord client migrates\n    the DB from the legacy location on its first start\n  - Helpers executed through sudo are installed at a fixed path\n    (/usr/lib/one/sbin) by the node packages, so they are no longer\n    executed from an oneadmin-writable location\n  - Remote hooks (REMOTE = yes) run from /var/lib/one-remotes/hooks.\n    Hook commands given as an absolute path are executed as-is and\n    must be updated manually\n  - Fix remotes sync to run the mkdir on the host: the local shell\n    interpreted the unquoted '';'' and ran it on the frontend instead\n  - onecfg migrator drops SCRIPTS_REMOTE_DIR from oned.conf and the\n    stock :remote_hook_base_path from onehem-server.conf","reason":"valid","signature":