:"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTA3NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/commits/7018e274f9b6a12fba337899c3908022b7d0346e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:40:48Z","email":"rsmontero@opennebula.org","name":"Ruben S. Montero"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:40:48Z","email":"rsmontero@opennebula.org","name":"Ruben S. Montero"},"message":"B #8092: Reject live datastore migration of VMs with system snapshots\n\nLive datastore migration uses QEMU blockcopy, which copies the current disk contents but\ndoes not preserve qcow2 internal snapshots. Copying the original disk files afterwards\nto restore those snapshots overwrites disks already in use by QEMU, risking disk\ncorruption and data loss.\n\nReject live datastore migration in oned when the VM has system snapshots. Also check the\nactual qcow2 files in the KVM migration script as a safe guard.\n\nHost-only live migration and migration with external disk snapshots remain supported.\nUse cold datastore migration to preserve internal snapshots.","tree":{"sha":"fe04fb7c9381f7d29f300865995c53e33df29b82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/trees/fe04fb7c9381f7d29f300865995c53e33df29b82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/commits/7018e274f9b6a12fba337899c3908022b7d0346e","verification":{"payload":"tree fe04fb7c9381f7d29f300865995c53e33df29b82\nparent dfd3e16021a2850f01bd8942a69ed02fc28ed142\nauthor Ruben S. Montero <rsmontero@opennebula.org> 1790185248 +0200\ncommitter Ruben S. Montero <rsmontero@opennebula.org> 1790185248 +0200\n\nB #8092: Reject live datastore migration of VMs with system snapshots\n\nLive datastore migration uses QEMU blockcopy, which copies the current disk contents but\ndoes not preserve qcow2 internal snapshots. Copying the original disk files afterwards\nto restore those snapshots overwrites disks already in use by QEMU, risking disk\ncorruption and data loss.\n\nReject live datastore migration in oned when the VM has system snapshots. Also check the\nactual qcow2 files in the KVM migration script as a safe guard.\n\nHost-only live migration and migration with external disk snapshots remain supported.\nUse cold datastore migration to preserve internal snapshots.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEzxcHxw36JXdObq7noM6m+ogKHYcFAmq0DzUACgkQoM6m+ogK\nHYfHpg//fB/4GK/k9uHfvRUZEZur8czre5MkVz81IzwTHvTCNE+GEhhUpjJmztTr\n9lwTRNiFUryZIT5w4eHWg+tVBPIVzRNifN8TA7Qqdzp8Ly9E71UKqjWycl5TbFZJ\nSnOdo3tvUr3NcG9gLN8em5qeUZQjQEoDp5ixTIKCIi61TmawtRlmyKCiwfEOPwAR\nilbD9fzfntq3NAeXpUTACWESkiTOnMpNiLfYr7ulYgQ5eHTuMNZExuAbb+uX8hKK\n1YQfXmXrPgyGxatKC2J1JKiAOpKgbGB6fEcsLEtQ7gAph2e1STLK11pUNlBLI7Nf\nydHKPC66hoxKATbMMryc2AHxQg+RGGF0OmvX6w9b8UxyB+rG2mhkAnku5bhtcF8m\n+2muYJ5zY9xBRIoGfo7aVnyfxmqz77GzRvCYJQEVFXgaAPZX1E4oGh21Q1OJrWsn\nQ1rJD/5qWd0JsAkY8HJ8DRmSRuPnFGe1JDSJ4Dp6etquOwLqkw8px2OML70F8zdV\nTTtbtsFy83ynEuaEoA/slVvtOFjgZhoRTIXyfe7IRgxIGZtPLqkkq+LW7OiBWHQa\nBEtkpYZgVLqfk6ZwYiDu7qyDzomto3xm0QwYn0/NEczfzP0D1mUOo+z4dUreMrmL\n6VeKTaROI3P32zssqXjG3krmoEvuGr1ILZCe5DnpUDFQI4H1Wuk=\n=XmR5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T13:50:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/665074?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmo