t handling, and cleanup.\n- Adds SPICE as a graphics type in VM templates and VM configuration forms, including normalization and restart guidance when changing graphics protocols.\n- Reuses shared loading components across Guacamole and SPICE consoles and provides SPICE connection status and reconnection controls.","tree":{"sha":"d5f20c9aad716984fb62267094180b699f7c4ac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/trees/d5f20c9aad716984fb62267094180b699f7c4ac2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/commits/e18cabeccec7d57aec47202fb6eff8376d551e5f","verification":{"payload":"tree d5f20c9aad716984fb62267094180b699f7c4ac2\nparent 20f7249b021dad567fdc5e1e8c160f79bc3ddb2e\nauthor Jorge Miguel Lobo Escalona <jlobo@opennebula.io> 1789716821 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789716821 +0200\n\nF OpenNebula/One#7667: add spice console (#4504)\n\n- Adds end-to-end SPICE console support for running KVM/QEMU virtual machines.\n- Introduces short-lived SPICE sessions and a WebSocket-to-TCP proxy with authentication, validation, timeout handling, and cleanup.\n- Adds SPICE as a graphics type in VM templates and VM configuration forms, including normalization and restart guidance when changing graphics protocols.\n- Reuses shared loading components across Guacamole and SPICE consoles and provides SPICE connection status and reconnection controls.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrOlVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEv8QAG8IqGafhrZiI2lvqg94Thjc\nmX0/VAN1W87fIy/CdjetaCCY7Z/5l8VnhZ7eiKinLtD/yQyyeOjXY11NUggA3BVP\nbtAbKqlsZGg49B7thCIi6sHvQ0dkH0m9hlduyAyS85ykZtEDDQT8mzw51rxLMI9b\nEhsx0Pe7h007Feg4Z3WnMSXqeLRnWJ9LZeQxRfnIDkZwgblZNjRXNt8izHNCTu7r\nHzhRC/AG7mc3aimeMhbDXkMz5o61rA79gGcIIdNLlTI/X4uR7N7Rr77eP+Pc2DJ7\niI9jPJTDrw5s0s6sH1/sTqgVchskVut1YkZdrt5wO/9ZO59V5YTJHBRcBU4ENINH\n06VYB0PmuezPRUp/AYiqfztvC5AJC8uFTm4QYQyd7uUlbExJs5nuKrsWPakEjgGp\nHSeZF61OJu8kiGy3NDie1WSG+x09K1WEw32yGoAv0gN1UcDqEyaj5tURCrJtN+vx\njt+aSpKedsYA