/api.github.com/users/rsmontero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsmontero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/commits/30d82707ee7c6fe54b2d046325fd02668d0dc496/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T16:32:39Z","email":"rsmontero@opennebula.org","name":"Ruben S. Montero"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T16:36:07Z","email":"rsmontero@opennebula.org","name":"Ruben S. Montero"},"message":"F OpenNebula/one#7579: ODS OneForm Migration\n\n    ODS\n    - Adds reusable GenericController and DocumentController DSLs for REST APIs.\n    - Extends ODS::Document and document pools with typed attributes, safe partial updates, raw access, dependency resolution, and per-resource locking.\n    - Adds reusable document capabilities through StateMachine, Errorable, Historyable, and Jobable.\n    - Introduces a declarative workflow/job framework with lifecycle transitions, recovery, cancellation, failure handling, and ensure actions.\n    - Adds JobScheduler for concurrent execution, resource exclusion, persisted job recovery, stale-result protection, and cancellation coordination.\n    - Adds the common ODS::Command executor with structured logging, timeout, environment/workspace handling, and signal-based cancellation.\n    - Moves shared OpenNebula resource helpers and common validation/serialization logic into ODS.\n    - Adds common handling for sensitive document attributes and automatic secret redaction.\n\n    OneForm\n    - Migrates providers and provisions to ODS documents and reuses the new ODS controller infrastructure.\n    - Replaces the previous lifecycle manager with the declarative ProvisionLCM workflow.\n    - Persists active operations in provisions and supports automatic recovery after service restarts.\n    - Adds asynchronous operation cancellation and replaces retry with recover.\n    - Introduces ResourceManager for dependency-aware, idempotent management and reconciliation of OpenNebula resources.\n    - Updates the provision API with direct REST operations for recovery, cancellation, hosts, public IPs, and deletion.\n    - Improves sensitive provider data handling, including redacted credentials and permission-aware access.\n    - Adapts Terraform and Ansible execution to the ODS job system, including persistent Terraform state, isolated workspaces, improved progress/error logs, and cancellation.\n    - Updates host and public IP management, including batch host deletion and stable UUID-based host reconciliation.\n    - Adds common host template support for Terraform-discovered hosts, including IM_MAD and VMM_MAD.\n    - Adds support for common host templates in deployment definitions, including IM_MAD and VMM_MAD, automatically applied to hosts discovered by Terraform.\n    - Improves driver management, validation, deployment inputs, synchronization, and host templates.\n    - Updates the Ruby client and the oneform, oneprovider, and oneprovision CLIs to match the new API and lifecycle semantics.\n    - Adapt current Sunstone API calls. No new features included.\n    - Adds onedb and onecfg migrations for server and sunstone configuration.\n    - Updates bundled drivers and Ansible inventory handling to match the new implementation and remove obsolete warnings.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 1eab0b458a16e0dfaedfd9cef923ee9c05b5d61c)","tree":{"sha":"3f76a8a8afed4f19f89827c8efe4b910ce4f4b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/trees/3f76a8a8afed4f19f89827c8efe4b910ce4f4b8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenNebula/one/git/commits/30d82707ee7c6fe54b2d046325fd02668d0dc496","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f76a8a8afed4f19f89827c8efe4b910ce4f4b8f\nparent 2bedbe14c3a17dce66463c093565f61264fc33de\nauthor Ruben S. Montero <rsmontero@opennebula.org> 1789576359 +0200\ncommitter Ruben S. Montero <rsmontero@opennebula.org> 1789576567 +0200\n\nF OpenNebula/one#7579: ODS OneForm Migration\n\n    ODS\n    - Adds reusable GenericController and DocumentController DSLs for REST APIs.\n    - Extends ODS::Document and document pools with typed attributes, safe partial updates, raw access, dependency resolution, and per-resource locking.\n    - Adds reusable document capabilities through StateMachine, Errorable, Historyable, and Jobable.\n    - Introduces a declarative workflow/job framework with lifecycle transitions, recovery, cancellation, failure handling, and ensure actions.\n    - Adds JobScheduler for concurrent execution, resource exclusion, persisted job recovery, stale-result protection, and cancellation coordination.\n    - Adds the common ODS::Command executor with structured logging, timeout, environment/workspace handling, and signal-based cancellation.\n    - Moves shared OpenNebula resource helpers and common validation/serialization logic into ODS.\n    - Adds common handling for sensitive document attributes and automatic secret redaction.\n\n    OneForm\n    - Migrates providers and provisions to ODS documents and reuses the new ODS controller infrastructure.\n    - Replaces the previous lifecycle manager with the declarative ProvisionLCM workflow.\n    - Persists active operations in provisions and supports automatic recovery after service restarts.\n    - Adds asynchronous operation cancellation and replaces retry with recover.\n    - Introduces ResourceManager for dependency-aware, idempotent management and reconciliation of OpenNebula resources.\n    - Updates the provision API with direct REST operations for recovery, cancellation, hosts, public IPs, and deletion.\n    - Improves sensitive provider data handling, including redacted credentials and permission-aware access.\n    - Adapts Terraform and Ansible execution to the ODS job system, including persistent Terraform state, isolated workspaces, improved progress/error logs, and cancellation.\n    - Updates host and public IP management, including batch host deletion and stable UUID-based host reconciliation.\n    - Adds common host template support for Terraform-discovered hosts, including IM_MAD and VMM_MAD.\n    - Adds support for common host templates in deployment definitions, including IM_MAD and VMM_MAD, automatically applied to hosts discovered by Terraform.\n    - Improves driver management, validation, deployment inputs, synchronization, and host templates.\n    - Updates the Ruby client and the oneform, oneprovider, and oneprovision CLIs to match the new API and lifecycle semantics.\n    - Adapt current Sunstone API calls. No new features included.\n    - Adds onedb and onecfg migrations for server and sunstone configuration.\n    - Updates bundled drivers and Ansible inventory handling to match the new implementation and remove obsolete warnings.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 1eab0b458a16e0dfaedfd9cef923ee9c05b5d61c)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEzxcHxw36JXdObq7noM6m+ogKHYcFAmqqxXkACgkQoM6m+ogK\nHYcGvQ//ft7ovp86UHJVnM0/lPcj6T3Ik5LUeje/iVZB2l0Ss65oE40U03gfK9so\nRB0wCl7FjCPHZ0T3Fvti2OHi/4x0FNBcjj8cV+OaFQWjc78aUtT5iw1lpuqdbkaR\n0G5wgGeeNXVZDR57vhMvph34NntHru93Nt9xuLwgKPWK/Q+7DyxlGvW/urY8Fb8T\n81fECIByaJSwuW33rrnPeG9MK9ksOLjAnEzJMGcpPIXsW9u1zEORBM3rwn10Z+Nd\nTD1teM4A6x9xOuFJRAFXQrTq+dxlk9jG2100Qaanl7vMMrxKDYrkTIyVuE8dgfOV\nZqJIebfhnRP718THvEss7E3FWJLdeQOIo48rpSjtAss/ZWxWa18JmGKBrY1tQYXM\nGNfUGLX+IGQxv50nSREz//jPtQFx3lec5AS8pMwb/oYZf5bHAKx/zkqZiOtd7G2F\nd4MCRs3cQjGlIpusEP57xoBxntc5XeF1JVC3dueC8F54Ygz/hPCTR2reqODOFwjL\n+aTBqYju0N7KmmBx3vOEgEoBJm6qkwfT7Njxk9/IosMko8MLqO0HfEFwWfxEuUEc\nk4+hNbvf3WuBVRBrP9oz4bHQ4/MPMabHE0c3Q0GCC/HuPf4spUEYZfYAXm2mqHl9\nJCK1LraQJlBinhgtQNxbG59UOWVQDVcjLwpF/xGXeq8aeeh4R24=\n=6qJ0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2