","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/commits/11bf65955a2d6e3c3a5baa288dfa9583ce221a15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:32:47Z","email":"peter.mathis@kombinat.at","name":"Peter Mathis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:32:47Z","email":"peter.mathis@kombinat.at","name":"Peter Mathis"},"message":"feat(core registry): replace option to override an already registered pattern\n\nThe first registration of a pattern name wins, so an add-on bundle\ncould not override a core pattern under its own name — it had to\nblacklist the original and register a replacement under a different\nname with the original trigger, and then bridge the original''s\noptions by hand.\n\n``registry.register(pattern, name, { replace: true })`` now replaces an\nexisting registration; ``Base.extend`` accepts ``replace: true`` as\npattern property. Together with the registry waiting for Module\nFederation remotes before the initial scan, the replacement is in\nplace for the initial scan no matter whether the remote or the core\nbundle registered first. Replacing after the registry was initialized\nlogs a warning: already initialized elements keep the previous\npattern, only new elements get the replacement. The blacklist still\nwins over a replacement.\n\nAlso documents the new Module Federation globals in the README.","tree":{"sha":"ee0446672761806278de4f06b4f7816f9afe73a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/git/trees/ee0446672761806278de4f06b4f7816f9afe73a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/git/commits/11bf65955a2d6e3c3a5baa288dfa9583ce221a15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/511761?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/petschki","id":511761,"login":"petschki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTc2MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Patternslib/Patterns/commit/11bf65955a2d6e3c3a5baa288dfa9583ce221a15","node_id":"C_kwDOAB-HdNoAKDExYmY2NTk1NWEyZDZlM2MzYTViYWEyODhkZmE5NTgzY2UyMjFhMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Patternslib/Patterns/commit/f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331","sha":"f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/commits/f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331"}],"sha":"11bf65955a2d6e3c3a5baa288dfa9583ce221a15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/commits/11bf65955a2d6e3c3a5baa288dfa9583ce221a15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/511761?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/petschki","id":511761,"login":"petschki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTc2MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/commits/f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T11:44:44Z","email":"peter.mathis@kombinat.at","name":"Peter Mathis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T11:44:44Z","email":"peter.mathis@kombinat.at","name":"Peter Mathis"},"message":"feat(core registry): wait for Module Federation remotes before the initial scan\n\nModule Federation remote bundles (add-ons) register their patterns and\ncomponents asynchronously after document ready, while the registry\nscanned the DOM right at document ready. Whether an add-on''s pattern\noverride or component registration was in place for the initial scan\nwas a race between the remote''s chunk loading and the host''s own\ninitialization — usually won by the remote, but not guaranteed.\n\n``registry.init()`` now awaits ``window.__patternslib_mf_initialized``,\nthe promise provided by the Module Federation helper of\n@patternslib/dev, before the initial scan. Without a Module Federation\nhost on the page nothing changes. A timeout (default 5000ms,\n``window.__patternslib_mf_init_timeout``) makes sure a broken or slow\nremote cannot block the page; the scan then runs anyway with a\nwarning. Repeated ``init()`` calls while waiting are ignored.","tree":{"sha":"2d1e45ec5039dc6dc6de2c4903ef52c0debc102d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/git/trees/2d1e45ec5039dc6dc6de2c4903ef52c0debc102d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/git/commits/f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/511761?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/petschki","id":511761,"login":"petschki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTc2MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petschki","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Patternslib/Patterns/commit/f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331","node_id":"C_kwDOAB-HdNoAKGYzNTM5NTZjMzQ1ZDJiMGM3OWZjYTJiM2M3MWE0NTE3MTAzZTMzMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Patternslib/Patterns/commit/2ebcf54fedbacac6dcf78a4af9ba6bc26f615bdc","sha":"2ebcf54fedbacac6dcf78a4af9ba6bc26f615bdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/commits/2ebcf54fedbacac6dcf78a4af9ba6bc26f615bdc"}],"sha":"f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Patternslib/Patterns/commits/f353956c345d2b0c79fca2b3c71a4517103e3331"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/170891?v=4","events_url":"http