l":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/221dd8647ffa32414d0be8ed514b3616ddf42053/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:49:03Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:49:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): Add a cloudflare-pi-durable end-to-end application (#25022)\n\nCloudflare now hosts pi-durable in Durable Objects through the Agents\nSDK `PiHarness`\n([changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-10-02-pi-harness/)).\nThis app runs pi-durable that way, with `@sentry/cloudflare/vite` as the\nonly Sentry setup. It checks that a prompt becomes an `invoke_agent`\ntrace with `chat`, `execute_tool` and provider `http.client` spans, that\na throwing tool is reported on its span, and that a run resumes in a new\ntrace after the Durable Object resets during a tool call. The reset uses\n`ctx.abort()`, which drops the object like an eviction; the next request\nstarts it again, and `PiHarness` resumes pi from its SQLite state.\n\nLike `node-pi-durable` and `cloudflare-think`, it calls a real model\nthrough OpenRouter, so it is optional. The changelog example uses\nWorkers AI (`createAI({ binding: env.AI })`), but the AI binding needs a\nCloudflare account even in local dev, so that path has a unit test in\n#24993 instead.\n\nThis app found a bug that #24993 now fixes: `@sentry/cloudflare`\ninitializes the SDK inside each request, so the client is on the scope\nof that request only. The task phases ran on a copy of the default\nscope, had no client, and dropped every pi-durable span and error.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de6d9fcc3304fa8781e012588e476b2a1bff83c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/de6d9fcc3304fa8781e012588e476b2a1bff83c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/221dd8647ffa32414d0be8ed514b3616ddf42053","verification":{"payload":"tree de6d9fcc3304fa8781e012588e476b2a1bff83c0\nparent 966e1ff0aa4d9b59e8dd7a5e6ac112175ddc6525\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791463743 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791463743 +0200\n\ntest(e2e): Add a cloudflare-pi-durable end-to-end application (#25022)\n\nCloudflare now hosts pi-durable in Durable Objects through the Agents\nSDK `PiHarness`\n([changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-10-02-pi-harness/)).\nThis app runs pi-durable that way, with `@sentry/cloudflare/vite` as the\nonly Sentry setup. It checks that a prompt becomes an `invoke_agent`\ntrace with `chat`, `execute_tool` and provider `http.client` spans, that\na throwing tool is reported on its span, and that a run resumes in a new\ntrace after the Durable Object resets during a tool call. The reset uses\n`ctx.abort()`, which drops the object like an eviction; the next request\nstarts it again, and `PiHarness` resumes pi from its SQLite state.\n\nLike `node-pi-durable` and `cloudflare-think`, it calls a real model\nthrough OpenRouter, so it is optional. The changelog example uses\nWorkers AI (`createAI({ binding: env.AI })`), but the AI binding needs a\nCloudflare account even in local dev, so that path has a unit test in\n#24993 instead.\n\nThis app found a bug that #24993 now fixes: `@sentry/cloudflare`\ninitializes the SDK inside each request, so the client is on the scope\nof that request only. The task phases ran on a copy of the default\nscope, had no client, and dropped every pi-durable span and error.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5E/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdoQQAC/qhE1aV4xU/GrPkU2AkjLZ\neXbRSpyQeJ+NUUOnArDS5amPot2vGPpdQ25QTzY4tYtC6M2FY9SLP09qt8yoVD3p\n5WdaOjZebO+e90mSUtKl37SM7n/WwOxpBR2wUhHwqEwMAVqZKbbIlej5rxauYDjq\nWdFpY3oUst6z5HEVuNwcHNZMpRqWcYH8A95bEjYDyG4py8CJ+nLEJQLAq+GkA4bu\nfvExwBbwVlU+64t3lFkcmKD+8SFK6w4aU2kR6u6v6J0ZJ8QA4DlBwsbS6cZLoTb2\nXHIpUDeg205P78WY+ID9QdW5JIkR38PAzHK0MK2ACRfW7WSmB1J84tBjcpYFU4nm\nYCesyymuxfKZxvy5lPeY4RqTNI25cjAVbJd+c+WpJpZtNlvgyLVPE1QN0XaD6HgI\n3z3F9YOZJHd0VH+/eNQPP1o4/uw2HJQ1cyOT30RWb8mfBBdFodfa/qukCBMn4qqj\nf6djML28skR/Xq2fOo9jSuZpxxHRLZoIf5SCC+7wtY0DbB75+iRsla3xRBu1Mcdu\nRLcC7eq+slSo7hSNFSrGotEJzrVQeXhmPV0hVxzjdTl9aHuBarCUWSKhGZGwRMW4\nlU3p/0TnJ1r3lJH6pF9d207hX4fqeibpV1wgGtpaWp9NOO8yzai7Nykn93+sVnkg\nyi1kwGLp2W8QZ7bpa9MI\n=Q8Y1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T12:49:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/221dd8647ffa32414d0be8ed514b3616ddf42053","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDIyMWRkODY0N2ZmYTMyNDE0ZDBiZThlZDUxNGIzNjE2ZGRmNDIwNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/966e1ff0aa4d9b59e8dd7a5e6ac112175ddc6525","sha":"966e1ff0aa4d9b59e8dd7a5e6ac112175ddc6525","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/966e1ff0aa4d9b59e8dd7a5e6ac112175ddc6525"}],"sha":"221dd8647ffa32414d0be8ed514b3616ddf42053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/221dd8647ffa32414d0be8ed514b3616ddf42053"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/966e1ff0aa4d9b59e8dd7a5e6ac112175ddc6525/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:49:03Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:49:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cloudflare): Skip spans for the pi_ tables of PiHarness (#25028)\n\nThe Agents SDK `PiHarness`\n([changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-10-02-pi-harness/))\nkeeps the state of pi-durable in the SQLite database of the Durable\nObject, in tables with the `pi_` prefix of its session store. Each\nstatement became a `db.query` span: one run with one tool call had 189\nof them next to its 7 agent spans, and the request that submitted the\nprompt had 120 more. These statements are framework bookkeeping, like\nthe ones on the `cf_` tables of `agents`, so they are now skipped the\nsame way, and `durableObjectSqlSpanAllowlist: [/^pi_/]` brings them\nback.\n\nThe cost is the same as for `cf_`: a user table whose name starts with\n`pi_` also loses its spans until it is on the allowlist. Names such as\n`api_keys` or `pipelines` are not affected.\n\nBefore: [196\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/7da432828f034a709be522a7de5bd4e2/),\nafter: [7\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/0a8c909bd53a4d61b78f98af21fc1ebb/)\nfor the same prompt.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"719e0fcfc943ca89bfb162affe94583d262fc7b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/719e0fcfc943ca89bfb162affe94583d262fc7b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/966e1ff0aa4d9b59e8dd7a5e6ac112175ddc6525","verification":{"payload":"tree 719e0fcfc943ca89bfb162affe94583d262fc7b4\nparent b70f6bb6d634da88e82f15c0568b02dcaba6bd39\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791463743 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791463743 +0200\n\nfeat(cloudflare): Skip spans for the pi_ tables of PiHarness (#25028)\n\nThe Agents SDK `PiHarness`\n([changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-10-02-pi-harness/))\nkeeps the state of pi-durable in the SQLite database of the Durable\nObject, in tables with the `pi_` prefix of its session store. Each\nstatement became a `db.query` span: one run with one tool call had 189\nof them next to its 7 agent spans, and the request that submitted the\nprompt had 120 more. These statements are framework bookkeeping, like\nthe ones on the `cf_` tables of `agents`, so they are now skipped the\nsame way, and `durableObjectSqlSpanAllowlist: [/^pi_/]` brings them\nback.\n\nThe cost is the same as for `cf_`: a user table whose name starts with\n`pi_` also loses its spans until it is on the allowlist. Names such as\n`api_keys` or `pipelines` are not affected.\n\nBefore: [196\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/7da432828f034a709be522a7de5bd4e2/),\nafter: [7\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/0a8c909bd53a4d61b78f98af21fc1ebb/)\nfor the same prompt.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5E/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqEEQACXc+pNcdnXttmejJyic/VEN\nexcV+kjHHgHajd2VQIG/LVrsPmxJiC+AwAgI7DVJHKQRZW8YvD02t0HsuBb5GeiL\n6HLUuTLRS4/cNYwWmE8tZ0xEfoAe3J0uzNWXTuxKC2QBR+vhkO8A0/24OhIlJp5f\nG7pnHWfCFg3E3dOHvFgg/rnPZ0VBkThrb9fP4TcfOah6pC54Z3al+ZZMfQkLjtQV\nKLzE8psh8rHx/qYjbXksh1GBztfEBXJ6TVVDqMUeNhVEawfD2VR59SW6uctKa22D\nvcKQiG7DsTgGfJRZNcicm683PBclh91SIyW7XvwR8C3SkPVosOxXk84iiukYjpzL\nXa33eBA+jYFTuJxECN0Q4HEnbdFoN3W5NB2KUsZWcee59WxlzRwp/s48/0tO0Bew\nwP1IgEsFPlBhfibYhlsn/eEyqHuO2Hcg6I