263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/b70f6bb6d634da88e82f15c0568b02dcaba6bd39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:49:03Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:49:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): Add a node-pi-durable end-to-end application (#24994)\n\nAdds an E2E app for the pi-durable instrumentation. It covers what the\nnode integration test cannot: the packed SDK loaded with `--import`,\nreal model requests through OpenRouter, SQLite storage, a subagent, and\na run that resumes after the server crashes during a tool call. A small\nsupervisor restarts the server for that case, as a process manager\nwould.\n\npi-ai sends `anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5` through `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, so\nthe first test also checks that each model request is reported once and\nthat the provider''s HTTP call nests inside its `chat` span.\n\nThe app is optional with a `latest` variant, because\n`E2E_OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is only available in the optional E2E job.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"287fce3dd9398c077ebeb315fcf980090691bfb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/287fce3dd9398c077ebeb315fcf980090691bfb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/b70f6bb6d634da88e82f15c0568b02dcaba6bd39","verification":{"payload":"tree 287fce3dd9398c077ebeb315fcf980090691bfb5\nparent 04f7cb984a497a42ec856d1556b725cb9717e3a4\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791463743 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791463743 +0200\n\ntest(e2e): Add a node-pi-durable end-to-end application (#24994)\n\nAdds an E2E app for the pi-durable instrumentation. It covers what the\nnode integration test cannot: the packed SDK loaded with `--import`,\nreal model requests through OpenRouter, SQLite storage, a subagent, and\na run that resumes after the server crashes during a tool call. A small\nsupervisor restarts the server for that case, as a process manager\nwould.\n\npi-ai sends `anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5` through `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, so\nthe first test also checks that each model request is reported once and\nthat the provider''s HTTP call nests inside its `chat` span.\n\nThe app is optional with a `latest` variant, because\n`E2E_OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is only available in the optional E2E job.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5E/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATkoQAJLhe3iBTfS5OruB/elYjJJQ\nMYXJSw9jToriE45k9fss1wWEGQo3WVOqknoxPuHN4dIuY8MWaAE4cH9qjYN9Bq6Q\nDv4cTFfejI/sa/teffJzPb5cZ+s9GSXWIB5xP6OmvM4AoLV45Zhizbfc5jEtvoAH\nfiwyb1QIY7a8uI/hox/Nngk6uUl3JWL69+VktsL+bsPYqmv6dxmHf/bcB20bbkbj\nKxOowQ7BWdrk1+aPu7vWYlDRdqKEGjweUOgS9F/g/FPWyxYbg1HxoYDnl9KOZWo8\nXJUskru4ji7n//FUo5gYD6U