task (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/98931\">#98931</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Credits</h3>\n<p>Huge thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lukesandberg\"><code>@​lukesandberg</code></a>\nfor helping!</p>\n<h2>v16.3.6</h2>\n<p>This release contains a security fix for <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-vcvr-r3jv-pc5j\">GHSA-vcvr-r3jv-pc5j:\nRemote Code Execution in next/og ImageResponse</a></p>\n<h2>v16.3.5</h2>\n<p>The following bug fixes have been backported. It does not include all\npending features/changes on canary.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>next/image: Skip 0-byte entries when initializing disk LRU cache (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/98185\">#98185</a>)</li>\n<li>next/image: Reject empty images when reading/writing to the disk\ncache (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/98186\">#98186</a>)</li>\n<li>Emit whole-app server NFTs when <code>output: ''standalone''</code> is\nused with an adapter (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/98167\">#98167</a>)</li>\n<li>Add CSP nonce to script tags of loading and template files (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/98403\">#98403</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix <code>use cache</code> prerender signal retention (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/98448\">#98448</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v16.3.4</h2>\n<p>Follow-up release to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v16.3.3\">v16.3.3</a>\nre-enabling AVIF Image Optimization (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/97949\">#97949</a>).</p>\n<p>The following bug fixes have been backported. It does\n<strong>not</strong> include all pending features/changes on canary.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>testmode: Fix infinite recursion in testmode passthrough fetch (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/97691\">#97691</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix build error when aliasing typescript to\n<code>@​typescript/typescript6</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/97997\">#97997</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix unset crossOrigin in Turbopack manifests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/97930\">#97930</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Credits</h3>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/b0fad0d45eb4c4430fda5eeeb442e8a5af08a5f6\"><code>b0fad0d</code></a>\nv16.3.8</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/719e4c67d6e92df60246f95e1d96e2dd60789a52\"><code>719e4c6</code></a>\n[lts-active] Scope response cache keys to their source route (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/218\">#218</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/e92db4536a7f34ae2dbda583cfa1b4e0d06d1865\"><code>e92db45</code></a>\n[lts-active] Fix metadata propagation for deduplicated nested caches (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/223\">#223</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/40c2ba904289a65ed2fd4633c5dfb1bdc29b52de\"><code>40c2ba9</code></a>\n[lts-active] Match Next data paths case-sensitively (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/196\">#196</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/2d9f50a409312696145b82b3157aadb6b1fef476\"><code>2d9f50a</code></a>\n[lts-active] Fix MCP middleware DNS rebinding (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/213\">#213</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/bd9214f9a32854a011bf5fe58e481dffe1bbf598\"><code>bd9214f</code></a>\n[lts-active] Fix draft mode leaks through cross-request <code>''use\ncache''</code> dedupli...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/8db4a627c91e718514406ff5644ea4985dcaaae0\"><code>8db4a62</code></a>\n[lts-active][webpack] Ensure <code>dynamicParams</code> is respected in\n`opengraph-image...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/e002ad68bd676bb0ed0c87bb22e3590304763e0b\"><code>e002ad6</code></a>\n[lts-active] fix(next/image): Pin DNS resolution when fetching external\nimage...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/4c20699e29178d444994cf5a31b8a617ca3a2c80\"><code>4c20699</code></a>\nv16.3.7</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/2521aec5815e7de2121db253d12dae9f13e25361\"><code>2521aec</code></a>\n[backport] turbo-tasks-backend: fix strongly consistent read hanging on\na can...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.2.11...v16.3.8\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=next&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=16.2.11&new-version=16.3.8)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx4IqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzR0QAGOij11L4X+qvnFgB8+BVmYy\nSOe7v96HxTNvs87Y91kWv9y18ONUaFStyqetGZXttaLo7jGDF8Z+/lzKlUF3wXAK\nqXVan+CsdbYhe1Kws/kM4fqCI74xboft31R8NXRpIHZL2cM/ywCpyDCHTAmuy+Nu\nNL8PrHG+eZxxdAdxKpMjIrtRaVPiKcFcyYuuhbXeM6Ze+q6/zxWn43BmpfY+mFeZ\n1pAVmXMGfS/nULfQtZsy5sDKJpNPqYBl9tT+Wxo38Nr74l5ObZ1FfNDaE0lSb97J\nyYHzkl7MDIjgERp4r3g7yt16Ce/PUsHjXHvAt0ExuYOhINyiRT+b+rRcCj7wyXAX\noLzFuiv3AkEayYHBMhf9IT31qkfcpfMWClbBEMiSKa110G+lzcNsSTEKSDsFHXGE\naWKOSJmpWCojwrozOBYQnK87B2Ge/GguXk5kzywih9eemZC1qJQOsTtZMPOfM0K1\n86eTihYyroqPhO4zddySgeWrW0YuJ7ujk9sOEfTKNpLZ0FL5zQAVG0h7fXtluh+v\n/Dvam/poIJJxzo9dKSz/p0PTf5qkaKgl0ZEAxf2TMOOLvzHnReNXoL2Hg3OG0dnt\ntpGnRdAjt7s9yJPhAPytEysRw//dqiV299VTd0bkIq9LnBJRJPyV5EhW5JYRGDzg\n5j3+fH3rYWeEp8wLH4IP\n=CZzR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T11:44:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/b1638a0c92c7020e580739c1367e4fd7d581fa1d","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGIxNjM4YTBjOTJjNzAyMGU1ODA3MzljMTM2N2U0ZmQ3ZDU4MWZhMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/4f9a027988acf007a0ad8d360403221a8069a482","sha":"4f9a027988acf007a0ad8d360403221a8069a482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/4f9a027988acf007a0ad8d360403221a8069a482"}],"sha":"b1638a0c92c7020e580739c1367e4fd7d581fa1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/b1638a0c92c7020e580739c1367e4fd7d581fa1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/4f9a027988acf007a0ad8d360403221a8069a482/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:28:41Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:28:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cloudflare): Wrap vinext Worker entries with `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` (#25000)\n\npart of #19514\npart of JS-1803\n\nWhen a Vite build uses vinext and `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` resolves\nfrom the Worker entry, the Vite plugin of `@sentry/cloudflare` now wraps\nthe entry with `withSentry` from `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare`. Other\nbuilds, and versions of `@sentry/nextjs` without that entry, keep\n`@sentry/cloudflare`.\n\n```diff\n-import * as __SENTRY__ from ''@sentry/cloudflare'';\n+import * as __SENTRY__ from ''@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare'';\n const __SENTRY_DEFAULT_EXPORT__ = { fetch() { ... } };\n export default __SENTRY__.withSentry(() => undefined, __SENTRY_DEFAULT_EXPORT__);\n```\n\n## Why\n\nWith `withSentry` of `@sentry/cloudflare`, a vinext app on Workers sends\nCloudflare data but no Next.js spans. Now it gets the Next.js spans\nwithout a config change.\n\n## Traces\n\nThe same app and requests: vinext on Workers before and after this PR,\nand `next start` on Node.js.\n\n| Request | vinext before | vinext after | Next.js on Node.js |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `GET /parameterized/42` | [`GET`, 1\nspan](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/0f98d8ca6ef645e3ae5bb60c039eeb6d/)\n| [`GET /parameterized/[id]`, 7\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/a26de83affd24b0c8fe7990e567ae8b6/)\n| [`GET /parameterized/[id]`, 7\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/c24bdbb12b134e80a5417fe9d2a59c56/)\n|\n| `GET /api/hello` | [`GET`, 1\nspan](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/df5b9f7976c5487daa7004cc9361eeeb/)\n| [`GET /api/hello`, 4\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/75b4a831b48f4bb1adb13648f5c6419a/)\n| [`GET /api/hello`, 4\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/ea8990c798144e2db75ee88e8bd6e634/)\n|\n| `GET /api/throw` (error) | [`GET`, 1\nspan](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/b6389e0368e44b269e5e07ba9823c29a/)\n| [`GET /api/throw`, 3\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/07caa661217e4f14bb38b182167d08c7/)\n| [`GET /api/throw`, 3\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/c9a3a73e3c7a44d4b7ff6519c8760a7b/)\n|\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"106f4e50dcb2d005bf4f8428d67964568f5d17d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/106f4e50dcb2d005bf4f8428d67964568f5d17d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/4f9a027988acf007a0ad8d360403221a8069a482","verification":{"payload":"tree 106f4e50dcb2d005bf4f8428d67964568f5d17d0\nparent ba3da3321ff0fb770001200a2c24e31be4ffef81\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791458921 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791458921 +0200\n\nfeat(cloudflare): Wrap vinext Worker entries with `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` (#25000)\n\npart of #19514\npart of JS-1803\n\nWhen a Vite build uses vinext and `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` resolves\nfrom the Worker entry, the Vite plugin of `@sentry/cloudflare` now wraps\nthe entry with `withSentry` from `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare`. Other\nbuilds, and versions of `@sentry/nextjs` without that entry, keep\n`@sentry/cloudflare`.\n\n```diff\n-import * as __SENTRY__ from ''@sentry/cloudflare'';\n+import * as __SENTRY__ from ''@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare'';\n const __SENTRY_DEFAULT_EXPORT__ = { fetch() { ... } };\n export default __SENTRY__.withSentry(() => undefined, __SENTRY_DEFAULT_EXPORT__);\n```\n\n## Why\n\nWith `withSentry` of `@sentry/cloudflare`, a vinext app on Workers sends\nCloudflare data but no Next.js spans. Now it gets the Next.js spans\nwithout a config change.\n\n## Traces\n\nThe same app and requests: vinext on Workers before and after this PR,\nand `next start` on Node.js.\n\n| Request | vinext before | vinext after | Next.js on Node.js |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `GET /parameterized/42` | [`GET`, 1\nspan](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/0f98d8ca6ef645e3ae5bb60c039eeb6d/)\n| [`GET /parameterized/[id]`, 7\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/a26de83affd24b0c8fe7990e567ae8b6/)\n| [`GET /parameterized/[id]`, 7\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/c24bdbb12b134e80a5417fe9d2a59c56/)\n|\n| `GET /api/hello` | [`GET`, 1\nspan](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/df5b9f7976c5487daa7004cc9361eeeb/)\n| [`GET /api/hello`, 4\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/75b4a831b48f4bb1adb13648f5c6419a/)\n| [`GET /api/hello`, 4\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/ea8990c798144e2db75ee88e8bd6e634/)\n|\n| `GET /api/throw` (error) | [`GET`, 1\nspan](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/b6389e0368e44b269e5e07ba9823c29a/)\n| [`GET /api/throw`, 3\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/07caa661217e4f14bb38b182167d08c7/)\n| [`GET /api/throw`, 3\nspans](https://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/c9a3a73e3c7a44d4b7ff6519c8760a7b/)\n|\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx35pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdlMQAEzLQmvN4MOYGCk5qev2Zfqs\nEloLbb1nsIFhkpWvK9kkkBK4q4NN/5dgIyUv/7YEvPKLPY3Ov17dkYWjHARftLm6\naQvmTWK6d1Y5Wq0MjqU/BJC7nv6nZpD/Jg0rko9hIXSPbO/fk42gTCvho+PPCepi\nM6+mjilU5xA3GdYDk2GK2gKSzQPffMgwCtZeIFdKTWnscZ7G4M5+8njbvuwsvwnG\n3Z1u7zHWWP95kUiWZpafsFWAWTphG3CACPKGIRSpwukUK97wKi8765t0lrxrQhh9\nYcEilAE5VUt6JJazQB5CTM68iqxMGBcxx7hN72GYiYUk2+vSjNta3a5Ze84Fzo2K\nkUk7MT7PgYb8T9LXHi+wmzGUQ3VxQhALsT3buY