":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/ba3da3321ff0fb770001200a2c24e31be4ffef81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:28:40Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:28:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(nextjs): Run nextjs-16 on Bun, Deno and Cloudflare (#24999)\n\npart of #24830\npart of JS-3835\n\nThis folds `nextjs-16-bun` and `nextjs-16-cf-workers` into `nextjs-16`\nand adds a Deno variant, so one suite runs on Node.js, Bun, Deno and\nCloudflare Workers (OpenNext). Bun and Cloudflare stay required. Deno\nand Cloudflare with the latest Next.js are optional.\n\nNew tests on every runtime check logs, outgoing `baggage` and trace\ncontinuation. Most removed lines are the two deleted apps.\n\n## Why\n\nThe two copies of the app drifted apart, and Deno had no coverage. Now\nall runtimes run the same tests, and each runtime difference is a\nvisible `getRuntime()` branch or skip.\n\n## Known issues\n\n- Bun and Deno need the request isolation and `fetch` integrations of\n`@sentry/bun` and `@sentry/deno` in `sentry.server.config.ts`.\n- Deno needs `--allow-sys` (the app runs `deno run -A`).\n- No `pg` spans on Bun and Workers (no runtime module hook).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"20e1aca107a2dc5432b9ad425947cc07cd7e2326","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/20e1aca107a2dc5432b9ad425947cc07cd7e2326"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/ba3da3321ff0fb770001200a2c24e31be4ffef81","verification":{"payload":"tree 20e1aca107a2dc5432b9ad425947cc07cd7e2326\nparent 2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791458920 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791458920 +0200\n\ntest(nextjs): Run nextjs-16 on Bun, Deno and Cloudflare (#24999)\n\npart of #24830\npart of JS-3835\n\nThis folds `nextjs-16-bun` and `nextjs-16-cf-workers` into `nextjs-16`\nand adds a Deno variant, so one suite runs on Node.js, Bun, Deno and\nCloudflare Workers (OpenNext). Bun and Cloudflare stay required. Deno\nand Cloudflare with the latest Next.js are optional.\n\nNew tests on every runtime check logs, outgoing `baggage` and trace\ncontinuation. Most removed lines are the two deleted apps.\n\n## Why\n\nThe two copies of the app drifted apart, and Deno had no coverage. Now\nall runtimes run the same tests, and each runtime difference is a\nvisible `getRuntime()` branch or skip.\n\n## Known issues\n\n- Bun and Deno need the request isolation and `fetch` integrations of\n`@sentry/bun` and `@sentry/deno` in `sentry.server.config.ts`.\n- Deno needs `--allow-sys` (the app runs `deno run -A`).\n- No `pg` spans on Bun and Workers (no runtime module hook).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx35oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxOAQAKLG0rUi4zYjIhjjWm0LyBn8\nO9eImqYjW6XSFz+lxBSsDqJdd73Ax1BzL3dfqIiopRkPgf/Fl3L0QsGGxn/+u2dz\net9qznkw1ImatSIFo6TGnq3KQsWIK2V1fDMAwJ9VCgQ36QCcthaicIjIG+FhIZSc\nkUcL6bLyPOTJpNledf2A5phirRitcQ4o61W98eiOWj+HmpwutOJSrsnWTs1+X2Wz\nPPhC/9e4rrs5rz4ahp492pYlfpTB83GfX+yO1Khznu6HVdJZ9PJnwasC/JsbhamY\nJ79Zh+kh1gfX7fPaJX7daBpM3y0q/KBLvBeiUyaTgH4gDMy2vAu6GO2JH+r9mY3C\nymdpzro/G6MBRxjpT12W9PZvfWnoJqF6bVFo5RZu+1jRy9l/Za3A0973TqCsYtgH\n/0/LFxmr3kKr0Nc1JvC7b46asK7xAtCOLvWL1jHYcy2LJ7dVeYOgTvJ5uIZ82rCq\n/07MR0o2o+hAWkma18WzSCnobKMgAwCNKxhDdceYO76HViyNtP0tRUCGpfH9j3B/\ntQeKLJfeDmUGzAOjd5ZBaNyUYj2iclVaLmULilz94INvh/xrY7AeVMlhYWW9WELO\n/gzcJ16cIjIyZbw20FuI5SmGoYY558YS+h/LJPK584UyMp3i0rT1g1haWL2MhwoS\n/X9r+U6meGJAozINHF+l\n=8r9g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T11:28:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/ba3da3321ff0fb770001200a2c24e31be4ffef81","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGJhM2RhMzMyMWZmMGZiNzcwMDAxMjAwYTJjMjRlMzFiZTRmZmVmODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b","sha":"2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b"}],"sha":"ba3da3321ff0fb770001200a2c24e31be4ffef81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/ba3da3321ff0fb770001200a2c24e31be4ffef81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:28:40Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:28:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(nextjs): Add `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` (#24998)\n\n(disclaimer, most of the additions are from `withSentry.test.ts` and\nother tests)\n\nAdds `withSentry` from `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` for the Worker entry\nof a Next.js app on Cloudflare Workers, for example\n`.open-next/worker.js` of OpenNext or the fetch handler of vinext. It is\n`withSentry` of `@sentry/cloudflare` with the Next.js handling of the\nserver `init` added, so a Next.js app on Workers gets the spans it gets\non Node.js from one wrapper, without new options. This is the only new\npublic API.\n\nDecisions:\n\n- It installs the OpenTelemetry async context strategy at module load.\nThe AsyncLocalStorage strategy of `@sentry/cloudflare` loses the\nOpenTelemetry context of the Next.js spans, so their parents and context\nvalues break.\n- The request spans of Next.js (`BaseServer.handleRequest`) are ignored,\nso the request span of `withSentry` is the only `http.server` span. The\nother Next.js spans become its children; it gets the route from their\n`next.route` and its status from the response. When the middleware\nanswers the request or throws, the span is named `middleware GET`, like\nthe middleware segment on Node.js.\n- From `compatibility_date` 2026-02-19, `process.cwd()` is `/bundle`\nduring a request. Next.js then misses its router server context and\nextracts the incoming trace again. The propagator keeps the request span\nas parent in that case, else each continued request has two segments.\n- `sentry.server.config.ts` and `sentry.edge.config.ts` still run in the\nWorker but create no client there. Their options do not apply, and a\ndebug log says so. On Workers they are optional: they only set the\n`turbopack` tag and hand over the build release of `withSentryConfig`,\nwhich only code that Next.js compiles can read. Without them, the\nrelease comes from the `withSentry` options, `SENTRY_RELEASE` or\n`CF_VERSION_METADATA`. Apps keep them for `next dev`, which runs on\nNode.js and does not use the Worker entry. `instrumentation.ts` stays\nrequired for `onRequestError`.\n- The Next.js handling is added by a `Nextjs` integration. `withSentry`\nof `@sentry/cloudflare` creates the client itself (once per isolate),\nand the options callback only returns options. The `setup` of an\nintegration is the only place that gets this client before the request\nspan starts, without a new option in `@sentry/cloudflare`. It registers\nthe span hooks of the server `init`, the propagator, the tunnel route\nsampling and the event processor that drops the control flow errors of\nReact and Next.js, so a Worker without `instrumentation.ts` drops them\ntoo. The server `init` checks for this integration, so it does not add\nthe processor to the global scope again.\n- `@sentry/cloudflare` becomes a dependency of `@sentry/nextjs`. Its\ndependencies are already in the dependency tree of `@sentry/nextjs`. It\nalso aligns with other SDKs, such as `@sentry/sveltekit`\n\nKnown difference: on Workers, a release from the `withSentry` options,\n`SENTRY_RELEASE` or `CF_VERSION_METADATA` wins over the build release.\nOn Node.js, the build release wins over the environment.\n\nThe `nextjs-16-cf-workers` e2e app now uses it, which un-skips its\nserver tests and adds tests for D1 spans, the OpenTelemetry context and\ntrace continuation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a663b7c1adcc893131c58d094c4de3d0eec0c9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/6a663b7c1adcc893131c58d094c4de3d0eec0c9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a663b7c1adcc893131c58d094c4de3d0eec0c9d\nparent cd0f3dca88eb522cee888a1cf3881b802e1458a1\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791458920 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791458920 +0200\n\nfeat(nextjs): Add `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` (#24998)\n\n(disclaimer, most of the additions are from `withSentry.test.ts` and\nother tests)\n\nAdds `withSentry` from `@sentry/nextjs/cloudflare` for the Worker entry\nof a Next.js app on Cloudflare Workers, for example\n`.open-next/worker.js` of OpenNext or the fetch handler of vinext. It is\n`withSentry` of `@sentry/cloudflare` with the Next.js handling of the\nserver `init` added, so a Next.js app on Workers gets the spans it gets\non Node.js from one wrapper, without new options. This is the only new\npublic API.\n\nDecisions:\n\n- It installs the OpenTelemetry async context strategy at module load.\nThe AsyncLocalStorage strategy of `@sentry/cloudflare` loses the\nOpenTelemetry context of the Next.js spans, so their parents and context\nvalues break.\n- The request spans of Next.js (`BaseServer.handleRequest`) are ignored,\nso the request span of `withSentry` is the only `http.server` span. The\nother Next.js spans become its children; it gets the route from their\n`next.route` and its status from the response. When the middleware\nanswers the request or throws, the span is named `middleware GET`, like\nthe middleware segment on Node.js.\n- From `compatibility_date` 2026-02-19, `process.cwd()` is `/bundle`\nduring a request. Next.js then misses its router server context and\nextracts the incoming trace again. The propagator keeps the request span\nas parent in that case, else each continued request has two segments.\n- `sentry.server.config.ts` and `sentry.edge.config.ts` still run in the\nWorker but create no client there. Their options do not apply, and a\ndebug log says so. On Workers they are optional: they only set the\n`turbopack` tag and hand over the build release of `withSentryConfig`,\nwhich only code that Next.js compiles can read. Without them, the\nrelease comes from the `withSentry` options, `SENTRY_RELEASE` or\n`CF_VERSION_METADATA`. Apps keep them for `next dev`, which runs on\nNode.js and does not use the Worker entry. `instrumentation.ts` stays\nrequired for `onRequestError`.\n- The Next.js handling is added by a `Nextjs` integration. `withSentry`\nof `@sentry/cloudflare` creates the client itself (once per isolate),\nand the options callback only returns options. The `setup` of an\nintegration is the only place that gets this client before the request\nspan starts, without a new option in `@sentry/cloudflare`. It registers\nthe span hooks of the server `init`, the propagator, the tunnel route\nsampling and the event processor that drops the control flow errors of\nReact and Next.js, so a Worker without `instrumentation.ts` drops them\ntoo. The server `init` checks for this integration, so it does not add\nthe processor to the global scope again.\n- `@sentry/cloudflare` becomes a dependency of `@sentry/nextjs`. Its\ndependencies are already in the dependency tree of `@sentry/nextjs`. It\nalso aligns with other SDKs, such as `@sentry/sveltekit`\n\nKnown difference: on Workers, a release from the `withSentry` options,\n`SENTRY_RELEASE` or `CF_VERSION_METADATA` wins over the build release.\nOn Node.js, the build release wins over the environment.\n\nThe `nextjs-16-cf-workers` e2e app now uses it, which un-skips its\nserver tests and adds tests for D1 spans, the OpenTelemetry context and\ntrace continuation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx35oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK4UQAJJCSSGdBwVdz2KOQT+Yybbi\nbDPQyilOESdEz2L/QSIUDIK6bs1UBz3N+noU1kkM9BLzIV6op9rPzabDneoD66fN\nsvioQQ2PqdLr/vF5khAMWkjeaIvNLOWopb/I0ZvipxrxDHp4AR9myej7h/WRHnOK\nOgwK5OCnuttP+FC7FFXdiSCypthhRPf/0/C7JvCS1h8qfu8jRftZmj6WuQ0Bt9fZ\notbE3PWsPNVYIX5qIwzhInacRUQL+QXjKkZV+Iqhui8ydwCFt8qy+KPKJTJXz1+5\nwyiTVKw8wc9XzB7J+KbBiGcMvkk7+a8Hb/Nr+IZMDyIa47DMM7nzaBcSrbLLyuBA\n1bBn6XqeILcxjy3+a4QZu4Jh096gi4iMaIvyuy0/nUhxCy0JB4F/yUd5HxGfKaLL\nGWaLGTjOnsfvdoAPtR6gtm99rDdK8RtYZTy4BUkDTqSBDcGKhghfxQzku6+vjVDb\nYlpMmHSKkDpUMOCkHY5AnabnXaQZs73vx5F7Z3Kyqnzkv8oEXgDHeFkJVFG5/aLG\n9mYolhHDjsOus2ZcX5ICxjnGsTXWAFsNZ8fMqKbYeQjAo/TfCtA9gTRNIjAemz2i\n5ovRf9rUzIAW/DSrk2lGUn9/r+jjwqoc9OKzHP4qoMTXldSI4JwS9JeGohBO2BBa\nNmHyazbcnZpJnCKUSsPR\n=L+pp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T11:28:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDI4ODJhMjliNTVkYWM3ZjlhNjFlYjBkZjZjYmJhNWRmNjA2Y2IyOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/cd0f3dca88eb522cee888a1cf3881b802e1458a1","sha":"cd0f3dca88eb522cee888a1cf3881b802e1458a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/cd0f3dca88eb522cee888a1cf3881b802e1458a1"}],"sha":"2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2882a29b55dac7f9a61eb0df6cbba5df606cb29b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20254395?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chargome","id":20254395,"login":"chargome","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjU0Mzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/cd0f3dca88eb522cee888a1cf3881b802e1458a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:16:43Z","email":"charly.gomez1310@gmail.com","name":"Charly Gomez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:16:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): Bump @graphql-tools/utils to 12.0.3 (#25162)\n\nRe-resolves three `@graphql-tools` lockfile entries to replace the\nvulnerable\n`@graphql-tools/utils` copy:\n\n| Package | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `@graphql-tools/schema` | 10.0.31 | 10.1.3 |\n| `@graphql-tools/merge` | 9.1.7 | 9.2.6 |\n| `@graphql-tools/utils` | 11.0.0 | 12.0.3 |\n\nFixes GHSA-7mx3-vvmw-hjmv (high), prototype pollution in `mergeDeep`:\nhttps://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/security/dependabot/2696\n\nThe first patched release is 12.0.1, so the fix has to cross a major. It\nstill\nneeds no `package.json` change: `@apollo/server` already declares\n`@graphql-tools/schema@^10.0.0`, and schema 10.1.3 pulls `utils` into\n12.x.\nLockfile-only diff, dev-only dependency path.\n\nVerified with the affected suites, 52 passing:\n\nyarn vitest run suites/tracing/apollo-graphql\nsuites/tracing/graphql-tracing-channel\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc8f4a8b37bb7b6a7663d16550bb4cc8dd7b5a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/bc8f4a8b37bb7b6a7663d16550bb4cc8dd7b5a17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/cd0f3dca88eb522cee888a1cf3881b802e1458a1","verification":{"payload":"tree bc8f4a8b37bb7b6a7663d16550bb4cc8dd7b5a17\nparent af84269091981d96d2e6d3b7d8b62312b852de65\nauthor Charly Gomez <charly.gomez1310@gmail.com> 1791458203 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791458203 +0000\n\nfix(deps): Bump @graphql-tools/utils to 12.0.3 (#25162)\n\nRe-resolves three `@graphql-tools` lockfile entries to replace the\nvulnerable\n`@graphql-tools/utils` copy:\n\n| Package | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `@graphql-tools/schema` | 10.0.31 | 10.1.3 |\n| `@graphql-tools/merge` | 9.1.7 | 9.2.6 |\n| `@graphql-tools/utils` | 11.0.0 | 12.0.3 |\n\nFixes GHSA-7mx3-vvmw-hjmv (high), prototype pollution in `mergeDeep`:\nhttps://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/security/dependabot/2696\n\nThe first patched release is 12.0.1, so the fix has to cross a major. It\nstill\nneeds no `package.json` change: `@apollo/server` already declares\n`@graphql-tools/schema@^10.0.0`, and schema 10.1.3 pulls `utils` into\n12.x.\nLockfile-only diff, dev-only dependency path.\n\nVerified with the affected suites, 52 passing:\n\nyarn vitest run suites/tracing/apollo-graphql\nsuites/tracing/graphql-tracing-channel\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx3ubCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADOgQADA5Z2pT/AYWSS0gGDf55fvc\nNcjGZzmsfsWuylMdb6dVWkXlGV4dQktqyhOdtJPiGE/qG8hpJnYvZWI7e/h5I9BO\nZzryJq9rRidj0SpYlsMwKVhMOz6ySPtJpBXbWIXyoHobsz6cDjVdivFq7pBTFqf/\n4tsu31cpKrmHcwf/pgl8wx+KBr7JCY2noncVd31QWGIgSeWRP+PGejVZJszO9vaF\n41cr659nmUzQ1h1eggJTT2mGrnumGe6ILnu4lU5i80YgwYrNWesR5P5o2X6dlW7s\nyNu+KKkSssMgKGJAObD8P+tAKRJvne45jR+XdENddscdIUpREiXH4T8TDUujKwkN\nZXHNpGTdu4a2+erEoVF5jZchHNzpuYeexVpvqTwEoFG49BQaEFAy2N+CTJnLBIU4\nFAiOZzGTtjNIiu3fafs