s://api.github.com/users/msonnb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/msonnb","id":26038247,"login":"msonnb","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDM4MjQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/d283c16285c9c0c93cde40f7dee9f0a3865845a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:07:09Z","email":"martin.sonnberger@sentry.io","name":"Martin Sonnberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:07:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): Exclude attachments from internal exception events (#25160)\n\nInternal exception events skip event processors and `beforeSend` to\nprevent recursion, so they must also omit attachments that those\ncallbacks would normally filter. Exclude attachments when building\ninternal event envelopes, including attachments added by send hooks,\nwhile preserving ordinary event attachments and scope state.\n\nFixes [JS-2136](https://linear.app/getsentry/issue/JS-2136).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-6 <codex@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"6be7a9a3d271dc066912d5eea185d03dae60f407","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/6be7a9a3d271dc066912d5eea185d03dae60f407"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/d283c16285c9c0c93cde40f7dee9f0a3865845a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 6be7a9a3d271dc066912d5eea185d03dae60f407\nparent 3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5\nauthor Martin Sonnberger <martin.sonnberger@sentry.io> 1791450429 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791450429 +0200\n\nfix(core): Exclude attachments from internal exception events (#25160)\n\nInternal exception events skip event processors and `beforeSend` to\nprevent recursion, so they must also omit attachments that those\ncallbacks would normally filter. Exclude attachments when building\ninternal event envelopes, including attachments added by send hooks,\nwhile preserving ordinary event attachments and scope state.\n\nFixes [JS-2136](https://linear.app/getsentry/issue/JS-2136).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-6 <codex@openai.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx109CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT5kQADGcgkcLuK7IuwBPc0gfX7VV\niT5Q56tEcIlur0aI+LWy+R5Iwezr5kwAi39Kq8kAwxAsiOAFXslKw+pkkmboiXsS\nIM1X3Dh9MWC5isOz5fhWQ0s0XWD8hAcbkxOmzlxtBXIRlGIE1AdWoePf1qf0ZBOX\nwR+CltMt3CTI00damHkW9vDMYaBo4n8BbdRZnd88YHUNqtpb28XRn1gGguz/oggX\n+MgfLdflKOy2gElDgJJDgIm9dz66X0crwQSBbWZyvOzJXKvlr6hnRH1nbWPOx4uX\nFbIttnir06vqRx7lkU4sLCQNs1ANEkD7MuilY8ev5ACdXWQ1pRmmA42FJ54p3jPG\naeisRT8XgBSKZqlMu8CUpQHuBVl7csf5HiiVyKHV9yIxmQDMaRudekJWDRSkiWwZ\nUac2AhsjwLB4pD9003Rc3cWn7PUHgusbwYODpMJN4EVE8Ye5hH7KCzS9OAawOy4B\niRl08iy7akXTqXVge2xmwIiDE0E8SXm1n6S0ifto2GJ4s9aeT3OQOzEUQBe/Qxbg\nLg7g1Uhl0Ks76CwV3RNlwG1j8HpOHCuGiRrMQin2mA2VH+50mG5BYvCk1TWhriJy\nhHqobn6pJno1NoCG+H2UAdbjtslsDe+Jdjg3ttAbc18/yznxyilnWhGoZvrnWhIt\n/jU9Jjjk5ItugKoZEN1O\n=CItx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:07:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/d283c16285c9c0c93cde40f7dee9f0a3865845a0","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGQyODNjMTYyODVjOWMwYzkzY2RlNDBmN2RlZTlmMGEzODY1ODQ1YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5","sha":"3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5"}],"sha":"d283c16285c9c0c93cde40f7dee9f0a3865845a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/d283c16285c9c0c93cde40f7dee9f0a3865845a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:42:45Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:42:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(effect): Detect HTTP spans named after the request method (#25159)\n\n## Description\n\nThis brings back the `http.server` / `http.client` op and the\n`auto.http.effect` origin on Effect HTTP spans with `effect@4.0.2` and\nlater. The tracer now also maps a span whose name is an HTTP method and\nwhose kind is `server` or `client`.\n\n## Why\n\nEffect-TS/effect#8873, released in `effect@4.0.2`, names HTTP spans\nafter the request method only (`GET` instead of `http.server GET`). The\ntracer derived the op and origin from that name prefix, so the spans\nlost both, and the `effect-4-node` E2E tests failed on `develop`.\n\n## Span name decisions\n\nThe tracer keeps the name that Effect sets (`GET`). With the\n`http.server` op, Sentry shows the segment as `GET /test-transaction`.\nWe could rename it back to `http.server GET`, but Effect chose the\nOpenTelemetry naming on purpose.\n\n## Known issues\n\n- A user span named only after an HTTP method with a `server` or\n`client` kind also gets the HTTP op.\n\n## Sentry traces\n\nBefore (`develop`, `effect@4.0.2`, op `http`, origin `manual`):\nhttps://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/55137135a9a648f79a53d3a08f4d0546/\nAfter (this PR, `effect@4.0.2`, op `http.server`, origin\n`auto.http.effect`):\nhttps://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/11a9e7bfb1834bfbbdb9c4ddedd3dd76/\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"231df2c067b2215766604c92d50c4ce4d9043c10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/231df2c067b2215766604c92d50c4ce4d9043c10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5","verification":{"payload":"tree 231df2c067b2215766604c92d50c4ce4d9043c10\nparent ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791448965 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791448965 +0200\n\nfix(effect): Detect HTTP spans named after the request method (#25159)\n\n## Description\n\nThis brings back the `http.server` / `http.client` op and the\n`auto.http.effect` origin on Effect HTTP spans with `effect@4.0.2` and\nlater. The tracer now also maps a span whose name is an HTTP method and\nwhose kind is `server` or `client`.\n\n## Why\n\nEffect-TS/effect#8873, released in `effect@4.0.2`, names HTTP spans\nafter the request method only (`GET` instead of `http.server GET`). The\ntracer derived the op and origin from that name prefix, so the spans\nlost both, and the `effect-4-node` E2E tests failed on `develop`.\n\n## Span name decisions\n\nThe tracer keeps the name that Effect sets (`GET`). With the\n`http.server` op, Sentry shows the segment as `GET /test-transaction`.\nWe could rename it back to `http.server GET`, but Effect chose the\nOpenTelemetry naming on purpose.\n\n## Known issues\n\n- A user span named only after an HTTP method with a `server` or\n`client` kind also gets the HTTP op.\n\n## Sentry traces\n\nBefore (`develop`, `effect@4.0.2`, op `http`, origin `manual`):\nhttps://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/55137135a9a648f79a53d3a08f4d0546/\nAfter (this PR, `effect@4.0.2`, op `http.server`, origin\n`auto.http.effect`):\nhttps://sentry-sdks.sentry.io/explore/traces/trace/11a9e7bfb1834bfbbdb9c4ddedd3dd76/\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1eFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbNUQAJsAFfZ0buJQIggWMxdoI/G/\nNAPIK9x5otaFG2K5s0sSOZZVax301W2oPxsySuhU1qw+MtZnuQHTXi6j8jl5zSP4\n4pGwhkWF3Kz4dz9xbi2db3NH8Dh3eew8eyt6n/XvnuuWExG4RcR5Jd0x71ePXE8V\nA75SbQuD2E48iVQ/4TpBIYHklKaLycaGk1QkzllEkcgRKwD+wVUkm/8JzLr0u+4V\n0TDCj/OZhqHS8PoMJ2YqADOAWaDAsAO4fwzA1u7d+HcDhrXPgilUE2d+ZioXDzzl\ngRAlsNZ7I/8UwezR3hR0Sbzt3Tv7zp97orrn1R3k83PMK64LYpuZhvPmOqq3Pb/X\nQg+FsO7CDlPkYdCXIY0mP4iEfFquRdKqZsFf+hjUs3MLA2/fVuCGrrBaPvfClg99\nkw9hsz7D5YjiomERTP7mzVzDHQ/3nxx3Wcq6q2Z73CQottYUY3FeUQXVBQ1VLZdX\n5eWLy4aFF85ZZZHjkd0at1VMlPEt5/Gl0N+IqDmsVQqvCK7nnEYZL10Tjmiqh58U\n+AfVoRbljsb5/pwryjqivJtVpZhaI7SzDNPNWvOgX1JBhTtkFzhRod46GcCnDzzH\nc304SgPtbsulWeFG1jUwPWk+q+Sb6lKWgvgQPYL+FMCWVytGRa3enYNMncmF8JbZ\nnNM2tMkdBuawxG+sYMDh\n=Wb7g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:42:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDNkMDFlNWE5YTM5YTRhODFhYzYyNWY4MTRkOWExN2U5OTRhN2JkZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132","sha":"ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132"}],"sha":"3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/3d01e5a9a39a4a81ac625f814d9a17e994a7bdd5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:25:17Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:25:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(cloudflare): Port the remaining static suites to span streaming (#25112)\n\nPorts the last three `cloudflare-integration-tests` suites that still\npinned `traceLifecycle: ''static''`.\n`tracing/propagation/worker-do-rpc-overlapping` (#24447) and the two\n`vite-autoinstrument/*-reexport-instrumented` suites (#23282) landed\nwhile the earlier port PRs were open, so those PRs missed them.\n\nThe re-export suites check that `_INTERNAL_wrapUnlessInstrumented`\nprevents a double wrap, so I made sure that the ported tests still catch\none. With the guard disabled, the Workflow suite receives two `step-one`\nsegment spans, and the WorkerEntrypoint request fails with `TypeError:\nCannot redefine property: __SENTRY_CONTEXT__`.\n\n## Still pinned\n\n- `suites/basic` stays as the static trace lifecycle guard, as named in\n#24196.\n- `suites/request-handler/subpath` stays pinned because of an SDK bug,\nnot a test problem. `wrapRequestHandler` from\n`@sentry/cloudflare/request` still sends a `transaction` envelope. The\n`/request` entry never sets an async context strategy, so `getClient()`\nin `SentrySpan._onSpanEnded` returns `undefined` when the span ends, and\nthe span falls through to `_convertSpanToTransaction`. The scope\ncaptured on the span does hold the streaming client. This needs a fix in\nthe SDK.\n\ncloses #24132\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f05e2a331ab19b2f8d86ecd9856933cdd389488","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/4f05e2a331ab19b2f8d86ecd9856933cdd389488"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f05e2a331ab19b2f8d86ecd9856933cdd389488\nparent d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791390317 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791390317 +0200\n\ntest(cloudflare): Port the remaining static suites to span streaming (#25112)\n\nPorts the last three `cloudflare-integration-tests` suites that still\npinned `traceLifecycle: ''static''`.\n`tracing/propagation/worker-do-rpc-overlapping` (#24447) and the two\n`vite-autoinstrument/*-reexport-instrumented` suites (#23282) landed\nwhile the earlier port PRs were open, so those PRs missed them.\n\nThe re-export suites check that `_INTERNAL_wrapUnlessInstrumented`\nprevents a double wrap, so I made sure that the ported tests still catch\none. With the guard disabled, the Workflow suite receives two `step-one`\nsegment spans, and the WorkerEntrypoint request fails with `TypeError:\nCannot redefine property: __SENTRY_CONTEXT__`.\n\n## Still pinned\n\n- `suites/basic` stays as the static trace lifecycle guard, as named in\n#24196.\n- `suites/request-handler/subpath` stays pinned because of an SDK bug,\nnot a test problem. `wrapRequestHandler` from\n`@sentry/cloudflare/request` still sends a `transaction` envelope. The\n`/request` entry never sets an async context strategy, so `getClient()`\nin `SentrySpan._onSpanEnded` returns `undefined` when the span ends, and\nthe span falls through to `_convertSpanToTransaction`. The scope\ncaptured on the span does hold the streaming client. This needs a fix in\nthe SDK.\n\ncloses #24132\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxnJtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHxQQAKB4JZhhrutNFd4fBcy77uga\nRNjHYnwgjvXGQlBVsPHSDbhlr0Ww66iDQBuYOY3g4rfrJht5BWSkIRK9LFGoX+Ob\n8S5AjRaLjGg0H2zAeTpQyJ9/8XQFOxGAdKEIRTyLjm0quU9MV+xGoMdjJqJc6fIf\ndSRJjf8st98x0zqNCmzHEYIqy3aIZLFPRlImvZGk8jLBSSyVDbQsh079kfzL4b8h\nqwMxfE0S6o9y+AR1kQqs1lMgknjtH0Nxb1730f4+Z/pPXje2jjQ69Sl8syQxx+/f\nZ+F224iKQpy/i3FlsXPGlVKd2XFZOkh/TyNtWgc4phDzPMghuzaVR02diKNm/OfW\nTB71XV3aubnu5GbLdH2IrGsFupefPvSxHrZMmmqktjyfy/vGyBVp6qtHVTOKU7Tl\nsvRH6ULOt9ALLzuGG5LkFsacZlK+j2al+lEPGRprK+OfXjzfIV75HOjvChvPYjYm\nfJB2pFoWGuuB9ozpdrUdNJQuICVUIWoVtHnjEQPqCLCQ6YsURx0jQU0kNBIvrtf0\n9cUGTxWsQ/GZP4clHyvU6ulsLf/k2tIayRqBHCqoEQ+IqLsJGOdjo3obx3toxkSU\n9ep56sSZCkptE+GHwXS7sg/p9iliOSEe7aBdpu3RXOPy/LqOQaFMnETN5kVarQSV\nLBNnhbJ8l+IqSZnkpvNv\n=nqvG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T16:25:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGNhMDVkMmRlOGQ2OTgzMTA3NTdkNTEwMzA3ODlhNWMwMWZkZjUxMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a","sha":"d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a"}],"sha":"ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/ca05d2de8d698310757d51030789a5c01fdf5132"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8420481?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lms24","id":8420481,"login":"Lms24","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjA0ODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:02:13Z","email":"lukas.stracke@sentry.io","name":"Lukas Stracke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:02:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(effect): Convert Effect span times to the Sentry clock (#24972)\n\nEffect spans used Effect''s own clock (a fixed origin plus a monotonic\nclock) for their start, end and event times. #23054 makes Sentry correct\nits clock for drift (e.g. after the device slept), so Effect spans could\nend up shifted by the drift relative to the Sentry spans around them.\nWith this PR, an Effect span now starts on Sentry''s clock, and its end\nand event times are converted by their offset from the span''s start.\nThis is the same per-span offset that OpenTelemetry''s SDK uses. We also\ndo this for our spans now, see #24903 for details.\n\nThe PR keeps Effect''s durations and any end time passed explicitly via\n`span.end(time, exit)`. With `withTracerTiming(false)`, Effect passes\n`0`, and we now use Sentry''s clock instead of setting 1970 timestamps.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ce711333d8b6fb7b710e7ee6d70be93bdad44ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/8ce711333d8b6fb7b710e7ee6d70be93bdad44ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ce711333d8b6fb7b710e7ee6d70be93bdad44ea\nparent 164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994\nauthor Lukas Stracke <lukas.stracke@sentry.io> 1791385333 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791385333 +0200\n\nfix(effect): Convert Effect span times to the Sentry clock (#24972)\n\nEffect spans used Effect''s own clock (a fixed origin plus a monotonic\nclock) for their start, end and event times. #23054 makes Sentry correct\nits clock for drift (e.g. after the device slept), so Effect spans could\nend up shifted by the drift relative to the Sentry spans around them.\nWith this PR, an Effect span now starts on Sentry''s clock, and its end\nand event times are converted by their offset from the span''s start.\nThis is the same per-span offset that OpenTelemetry''s SDK uses. We also\ndo this for our spans now, see #24903 for details.\n\nThe PR keeps Effect''s durations and any end time passed explicitly via\n`span.end(time, exit)`. With `withTracerTiming(false)`, Effect passes\n`0`, and we now use Sentry''s clock instead of setting 1970 timestamps.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxl71CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr9kQAJSVfkdXgrkHNS/6nma438sj\nGBB/KUqVrfKlsyIOPL8ZX1aNAJ3/46deNkXbVj537Xbybzdzk9yEgFKNwNEQPlj6\nS/Z9vdlT4/6m7CH3STQyFdlotrHa462nJnthT8F6RRCAztA0d5hWqjaqCddtdFFX\nAdjSybYpKRbpQFpbDy9ultrH1u2wM3kMfii9es0pl5q6d0DXqum1zEokcA9qixN/\nm2QAe00iabS1grTURV/eG//Wl0BMkfAHyADfaR9kbi4AcKmIo+U5b+yKui+8q7Uu\ntRWPcaPpFHfy5u7gH24TX7FpMDe2u3+C1obxaoAOs8+7/91C2jhKHbUhTvriN1OY\notP77QWcWe34Sxn/BtcOxzKZdiorT1mrQUk0G8yU6qFCI+nABoduB3MCll9Swdvr\nBwUcqo+vfsXbCcV90Q8TZrj8J79RsI9Y8Jm3u54LN/jFLL1HtuV3FCMpKx/8qm7b\nCgsrIuNaULcqfWNNuFjKMAGGdEoz6lGU8ijxlIt7adn9DLhHBBOwgTZfKnLYzCwg\nD4+3B8ZakzY6yE9/CNdpBmhFo0Jv1KeZGp8zDfFt1UosQLPrZZAtLuYHfLp6+8ie\nKISmJnG1CLReIXiAlmLURKLyAJ1xcQ02Vr6YHt1bWEnj4CoFpsQm/j14tBg7RZTk\nGz+XcHB/Q/+yeL2Y3fgN\n=4vcE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:02:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGQ1YWU2MDEyZDM0MDkyNDQ5MjE5NmI2MmVjOWNjMjk4ZGRjNTI5NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994","sha":"164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994"}],"sha":"d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/d5ae6012d340924492196b62ec9cc298ddc5294a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8420481?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lms24","id":8420481,"login":"Lms24","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjA0ODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:02:13Z","email":"lukas.stracke@sentry.io","name":"Lukas Stracke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:02:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): Compute span end time from `performance.now()` duration (#24903)\n\nAfter Spans #23054, spans that run while the time origin is corrected\n(e.g. after the device slept) get the drift added to their duration.\nHowever, If the wall clock jumps backwards, the duration can even be\nnegative. Also, adding sleep time to spans is arguably unexpected and\nunprecedented in comparison to OpenTelemetry.\n\nThis PR changes s `span.end()` without a explicit timestamp to compute\nthe end as start time + `performance.now()` time since the start, [like\nOpenTelemetry\ndoes](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/blob/672b1d216e8b2299d16d7e2dfd184da4bf448cb4/packages/sdk-trace/src/Span.ts#L319-L356).\nStart times still use `timestampInSeconds()`, so real-time started spans\nand spans from performance entries stay on the same timeline.\n\nTradeoff: when a correction happens while a span runs, its end is now\nbased on the old time origin. So children or errors recorded after the\ncorrection can appear after the span ended. Spans with an explicit start\ntime keep using `timestampInSeconds()` for the end.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d30c8fc6d9df8cd73ff26d2601866e76db41a3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/0d30c8fc6d9df8cd73ff26d2601866e76db41a3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d30c8fc6d9df8cd73ff26d2601866e76db41a3e\nparent 0201779bd1836f2c06dea158dd1b0c8842e033a2\nauthor Lukas Stracke <lukas.stracke@sentry.io> 1791385333 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791385333 +0200\n\nfix(core): Compute span end time from `performance.now()` duration (#24903)\n\nAfter Spans #23054, spans that run while the time origin is corrected\n(e.g. after the device slept) get the drift added to their duration.\nHowever, If the wall clock jumps backwards, the duration can even be\nnegative. Also, adding sleep time to spans is arguably unexpected and\nunprecedented in comparison to OpenTelemetry.\n\nThis PR changes s `span.end()` without a explicit timestamp to compute\nthe end as start time + `performance.now()` time since the start, [like\nOpenTelemetry\ndoes](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/blob/672b1d216e8b2299d16d7e2dfd184da4bf448cb4/packages/sdk-trace/src/Span.ts#L319-L356).\nStart times still use `timestampInSeconds()`, so real-time started spans\nand spans from performance entries stay on the same timeline.\n\nTradeoff: when a correction happens while a span runs, its end is now\nbased on the old time origin. So children or errors recorded after the\ncorrection can appear after the span ended. Spans with an explicit start\ntime keep using `timestampInSeconds()` for the end.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxl71CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb98QAHU2Q/jKd8b1mp1IYkdaukdC\nDLiSFsZ6qdFKMFNzs/2XJC2iDM1uBO3lbSfdpdFyuQt4mQZs3AA17MgUFXITnh0J\n8f7y05mmx6d0a2bxgUv7HjjIMSFagxgEyddB/NSWcalPSx3vvoqdUb3OB8CTbt1G\nVvpCYcKRzfI2dH/HX+whmfKDoaYmTytEv7yhpgAyEYQZAtbfjTgiZuCAn9RT3UeE\nZzOrrTDX665EordsGewqliiMOXpcBoT1qeUfLnnxEQTs6F4CzNWxmLikMNRh/DHB\ndVWBzk7AASkZfQsBV5ptKTDmHiBu7ECRb4HAlR1e99Unf0CjRCwplkMvb9I5qgcY\nKOS/YjwbMGctAqdd+tm3yLjcE7qt7Mq13rZ9biB+VausINGk1JIXWNhEGuGtLV8n\nIlrppI2Eq11HaczQike6eEwXqOUyOrwrHcJxq2wQmJq/9iZpOT64nI8Om2Q+R6X6\nTwI4FNkl2iTSlq6HHwivKHRFcqocG7pg9KboDIAMDxK1KThTKPUqiv8xtQ/Y+PLU\nr27e+d0BH4VyaplXZ90ikTD6tbfRF0s9xNjw254AWDdWs3QLmeN8NrwHfosv7mHp\nBonkLn2uwEP7/GyQ13K3Z2gcnKDPKy0ySLSsb89ws1M4akiWKKZdNlsWgU1RltzJ\nCIfGVf8z/noKwB8ccBAP\n=JlT3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:02:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDE2NDc5NGI2YmQ4ODY4ZmQ2NDMwY2Q1MGYyNWFjZDFiMjg5ZWI5OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/0201779bd1836f2c06dea158dd1b0c8842e033a2","sha":"0201779bd1836f2c06dea158dd1b0c8842e033a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/0201779bd1836f2c06dea158dd1b0c8842e033a2"}],"sha":"164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/164794b6bd8868fd6430cd50f25acd1b289eb994"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8420481?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lms24","id":8420481,"login":"Lms24","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjA0ODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lms24","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/0201779bd1836f2c06dea158dd1b0c8842e033a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:02:12Z","email":"lukas.stracke@sentry.io","name":"Lukas Stracke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:02:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): Correct sleep clock drift on telemetry timestamps (#23054)\n\nThis PR fixes* clock drift that occurs when devices go to sleep. After\ndevices sleep for a few seconds, the browser''s monotonic clock (accessed\nvia `performance.now()`) stops counting. Once the sleep stops, the\nmonotonic clock resumes right where it left off before the sleep,\ncausing significant discrepancies between the actual time (wall clock)\nand the browser''s monotonic clock time. Or in other words, there are two\nways to get an absolute timestamp:\n\n- Using the monotonic clock via `peformance.timeOrigin +\nperformance.now()` - has high, sub-millisecond precision and a guarantee\nthat there are no time jumps or adjustments. But suffers from the sleep\nproblem described above\n- Using the wall clock via `Date.now()` - lower millisecond precision,\nis known to be corrected (NTP or via users) and can even cause back\njumps. But no sleep problem.\n\nWith this fix, we make the following adjustments, to kinda get the best\nof both worlds:\n\n- Every `timestampInSecondsCall` checks the monotonic against the wall\nclock. If a threshold of difference is enocuntered, it corrects the\n`timeOrigin` so that we can keep using the precise monotonic clock, but\nanchor its relative time to a corrected time origin.\n- On every time origin correction, we remember the previous origin (up\nto 30 corrections). Needed for performance entries\n- Makes `browserPerformanceTimeOrigin` a time origin corrected helper\nfunction, where you pass in a relative time that comes from monotonic\nclock relative timestamps and it returns the time origin that was most\naccurate at that relative time point.\n- All spans and other telemetry we create from browsers\n`PerformanceEntry` objects carry relative times which are completely\nsleep-drift uncorrected. We use `browserPerformanceTimeOrigin` to return\na corrected time stamp so that we can create an absolute timestamp and\nbring the performance entries to their respective actual time.\n\n### FAQ\n\nIf you think this sounds complicated, I agree. So let me answer the most\nobvious questions, because I asked myself these a lot, too:\n\n**Why not just always use `Date.now()` and avoid the complicated click\ndrift detection and correction logic?**\n\nThe main issue with this is that we still need to rely on relative\nmonotonic clock timestamps for performance entries. We cannot correct\nthem just with `Date.now()` alone but we still need to anchor them. So\neither we rely on the original `window.timeOrigin` and therefore have\nall performance entry telemetry happen much \"earlier\" than its\nsurrounding telemetry relying on `Date.now()`, or we keep the time\norigin correction logic. But even in the second case (where we already\npay the tax for drift detection and correction), telemetry would still\nhave two different anchors: `Date.now()` for regular telemetry and the\ncorrected time origin + monotonic time for performance entry telemetry.\n\nAnother reason is that the monotonic clock gives us sun-millisecond\nprecision while the wall clock stops at a millisecond resolution.\n\n**Why the reduction from a drift detection threshold of 5 minutes to\njust one second?**\n\nBecause we keep everything centered around detection and origin offset\ncorrection, these timestamps need to be as accurate as possible. On\nphones, short frequent sleeps are very likely to happen. A lot of sleeps\ncan accumulate until that 5 minutes threshold is reached. So it''s really\nimportant we make these timestamps as accurate as possible.\n\nFwiw, I reproduced this locally and the drift is already noticeable\nafter just a few seconds of sleep. The 5 minutes threshold was arguably\nfar too big beforehand.\n\n\n**Is there precedence for all of this stuff?**\n\nSomewhat, but I''d argue we''re doing a bit more: OTel uses a mixture of\n`Date.now()` and `performance.now`:\n- Spans start at `Date.now()` and at start time, they record a\n`performance.now()` timestamp. On span end, they also take\n`performance.now()`, compute the diff and convert that to an end\ntimestamp based on the start timestamp + diff. This is neat because it\nguarantees monotony in span durations. I stole this in #24903\n\nIn other places, OTel relies purely on Date.now(), and for performance\nentries, they simply take uncorrected timestamps. So our fix is more\ncomplete.\n\n\\* **So... we''re good now?**\n\nWell, not perfectly and we never will. With this choice we make another\ncommitment (which we already did previously in less obvious cases) to\n`Date.now()`. This value can drift as well, just not for sleeps:\n\n- NTP adjustments: Can make hard correction of the wall clock, or make\nthe clock tick just a bit faster or slower until the device wall clock\nsynced with the network time.\n- User adjustments: Users can adjust the device time at any time into\nany direction.\n\nI think we''ll have to live with both and I''m not particularly worried\nabout them. My main objective is getting rid of the sleep drift.\n\nFixes #2590\nSupersedes #22488, #22585, #23067, #23068\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b78bc588f34a425ab93001e72caf1a78bfdcc6d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/b78bc588f34a425ab93001e72caf1a78bfdcc6d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/0201779bd1836f2c06dea158dd1b0c8842e033a2","verification":{"payload":"tree b78bc588f34a425ab93001e72caf1a78bfdcc6d1\nparent fcb6cdfd8a69852b3d5f51b01c9936f4b1036daa\nauthor Lukas Stracke <lukas.stracke@sentry.io> 1791385332 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791385332 +0200\n\nfix(core): Correct sleep clock drift on telemetry timestamps (#23054)\n\nThis PR fixes* clock drift that occurs when devices go to sleep. After\ndevices sleep for a few seconds, the browser''s monotonic clock (accessed\nvia `performance.now()`) stops counting. Once the sleep stops, the\nmonotonic clock resumes right where it left off before the sleep,\ncausing significant discrepancies between the actual time (wall clock)\nand the browser''s monotonic clock time. Or in other words, there are two\nways to get an absolute timestamp:\n\n- Using the monotonic clock via `peformance.timeOrigin +\nperformance.now()` - has high, sub-millisecond precision and a guarantee\nthat there are no time jumps or adjustments. But suffers from the sleep\nproblem described above\n- Using the wall clock via `Date.now()` - lower millisecond precision,\nis known to be corrected (NTP or via users) and can even cause back\njumps. But no sleep problem.\n\nWith this fix, we make the following adjustments, to kinda get the best\nof both worlds:\n\n- Every `timestampInSecondsCall` checks the monotonic against the wall\nclock. If a threshold of difference is enocuntered, it corrects the\n`timeOrigin` so that we can keep using the precise monotonic clock, but\nanchor its relative time to a corrected time origin.\n- On every time origin correction, we remember the previous origin (up\nto 30 corrections). Needed for performance entries\n- Makes `browserPerformanceTimeOrigin` a time origin corrected helper\nfunction, where you pass in a relative time that comes from monotonic\nclock relative timestamps and it returns the time origin that was most\naccurate at that relative time point.\n- All spans and other telemetry we create from browsers\n`PerformanceEntry` objects carry relative times which are completely\nsleep-drift uncorrected. We use `browserPerformanceTimeOrigin` to return\na corrected time stamp so that we can create an absolute timestamp and\nbring the performance entries to their respective actual time.\n\n### FAQ\n\nIf you think this sounds complicated, I agree. So let me answer the most\nobvious questions, because I asked myself these a lot, too:\n\n**Why not just always use `Date.now()` and avoid the complicated click\ndrift detection and correction logic?**\n\nThe main issue with this is that we still need to rely on relative\nmonotonic clock timestamps for performance entries. We cannot correct\nthem just with `Date.now()` alone but we still need to anchor them. So\neither we rely on the original `window.timeOrigin` and therefore have\nall performance entry telemetry happen much \"earlier\" than its\nsurrounding telemetry relying on `Date.now()`, or we keep the time\norigin correction logic. But even in the second case (where we already\npay the tax for drift detection and correction), telemetry would still\nhave two different anchors: `Date.now()` for regular telemetry and the\ncorrected time origin + monotonic time for performance entry telemetry.\n\nAnother reason is that the monotonic clock gives us sun-millisecond\nprecision while the wall clock stops at a millisecond resolution.\n\n**Why the reduction from a drift detection threshold of 5 minutes to\njust one second?**\n\nBecause we keep everything centered around detection and origin offset\ncorrection, these timestamps need to be as accurate as possible. On\nphones, short frequent sleeps are very likely to happen. A lot of sleeps\ncan accumulate until that 5 minutes threshold is reached. So it''s really\nimportant we make these timestamps as accurate as possible.\n\nFwiw, I reproduced this locally and the drift is already noticeable\nafter just a few seconds of sleep. The 5 minutes threshold was arguably\nfar too big beforehand.\n\n\n**Is there precedence for all of this stuff?**\n\nSomewhat, but I''d argue we''re doing a bit more: OTel uses a mixture of\n`Date.now()` and `performance.now`:\n- Spans start at `Date.now()` and at start time, they record a\n`performance.now()` timestamp. On span end, they also take\n`performance.now()`, compute the diff and convert that to an end\ntimestamp based on the start timestamp + diff. This is neat because it\nguarantees monotony in span durations. I stole this in #24903\n\nIn other places, OTel relies purely on Date.now(), and for performance\nentries, they simply take uncorrected timestamps. So our fix is more\ncomplete.\n\n\\* **So... we''re good now?**\n\nWell, not perfectly and we never will. With this choice we make another\ncommitment (which we already did previously in less obvious cases) to\n`Date.now()`. This value can drift as well, just not for sleeps:\n\n- NTP adjustments: Can make hard correction of the wall clock, or make\nthe clock tick just a bit faster or slower until the device wall clock\nsynced with the network time.\n- User adjustments: Users can adjust the device time at any time into\nany direction.\n\nI think we''ll have to live with both and I''m not particularly worried\nabout them. My main objective is getting rid of the sleep drift.\n\nFixes #2590\nSupersedes #22488, #22585, #23067, #23068\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxl70CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAwgQACqHiqJYmsmhhVzgEfk8Xq1S\nO8MS7p4P3eHFW/Q0s+Oz+eOZ5Gjzx9Di+M+Nj4xxArAIdKLnDT7r7+0F1NGhpQXe\noLthGff1KCCM5o8/MCeKV0qbVztDVLIz9DVV4sQ0kMNDJSKhap59CJ4qUnXdLZU6\nE/HltUl8aDqOLjcNuGHxA47Hvta+mSLvAlMwaFEjV7CuJu/7GDbhscNdyxj2V/xw\nCCaxmrYZ+p2blgVWSCLf01mBnUI/gOB3U1vnvS2YeO0OplyTE23uWWnviIz91QpT\ndStd1m5t/I1PaMxiTWAgPt7Lr98mvUvRQxELej+fYdggW9W3nrznX5HE2CKDePLl\nocLZE/8Jmhx1YJCQDleah2kajNWxxYaigmbH2zviYO8/eEjDjK/7WjTlRCrCMRwk\n5EtWbFTtnpxZLLB9lp5DfKspF0YZODHk6Ru90EK/zvvsqdxp/hQh4FvO4o7d8+FV\nUVIhw3kZw12rb01I0IAAsOIqp2k2H2vjrjtSEVJrlY72nAciKxIIIX9OIbMhB0jF\nZFnvnLnGGN82Ot7NBPk5GrUjaCf1rcD9Kw4N7lbUnl3zoqF+272w1Wh5Ek/zFEIr\nvmfqclBoURJWD4xSCRIbmdxVeSUm0xdSdVy51KY7pmUWLPoOLkVhoojKm0MVAYRm\nVWMNy28TfKkDylNsUxP9\n=DKsT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:02:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ