","sha":"49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392"}],"sha":"fcb6cdfd8a69852b3d5f51b01c9936f4b1036daa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/fcb6cdfd8a69852b3d5f51b01c9936f4b1036daa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2411343?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mydea","id":2411343,"login":"mydea","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MTEzNDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mydea","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:35:14Z","email":"francesco.novy@sentry.io","name":"Francesco Gringl-Novy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:35:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(cloudflare): Widen the wrangler readiness retry window in integration tests (#24925)\n\n`cache-client > cacheClient: true - dedupe drops the same error across\ninvocations` failed on CI on its very first request: wrangler had\nreported \"Ready\", but the request still got 500s for the whole ~5s retry\nbudget in `fetchWithRetry`. wrangler printed no error for it, so it''s\nthe known \"ready but not serving yet\" startup race (#20994, #22083), not\na failure in the worker.\n\nThis widens the budget to ~15s. Requests that are expected to fail\nalready disable retries, so the only cost is that a genuinely unexpected\n500 takes longer to report, which is fine within the 60s test timeout.\nThe \"expected to succeed\" error now also includes the response body: CI\nnever showed what the 500 actually was, and this makes the next\noccurrence diagnosable instead of us widening the window again blindly.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01155841ae54070fe5226f478ef785fcb0ac8ee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/01155841ae54070fe5226f478ef785fcb0ac8ee3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392","verification":{"payload":"tree 01155841ae54070fe5226f478ef785fcb0ac8ee3\nparent f8abf005a5c1c929f766e732740620293ce78f2b\nauthor Francesco Gringl-Novy <francesco.novy@sentry.io> 1791383714 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791383714 +0200\n\ntest(cloudflare): Widen the wrangler readiness retry window in integration tests (#24925)\n\n`cache-client > cacheClient: true - dedupe drops the same error across\ninvocations` failed on CI on its very first request: wrangler had\nreported \"Ready\", but the request still got 500s for the whole ~5s retry\nbudget in `fetchWithRetry`. wrangler printed no error for it, so it''s\nthe known \"ready but not serving yet\" startup race (#20994, #22083), not\na failure in the worker.\n\nThis widens the budget to ~15s. Requests that are expected to fail\nalready disable retries, so the only cost is that a genuinely unexpected\n500 takes longer to report, which is fine within the 60s test timeout.\nThe \"expected to succeed\" error now also includes the response body: CI\nnever showed what the 500 actually was, and this makes the next\noccurrence diagnosable instead of us widening the window again blindly.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxliiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAApAQAFM3Q44iIXltQudHuHgxcWQ/\nSLalkB4MGdEeAVlAHgNBCfE0Hu5EzmH/Z3hjz/VJsp+Ar2tI0U+q2xF77vGX1pMI\ndib9yhfDOhb0LBN3YUf6bevPp63Lwxy8s0QRgk+aJVVNsNgc6rzIoQCOq1K8a9Al\nbcLYbh0qP5y7nTFLf8dDMthR/tYsCVyfypmHZZHJ2XHw0Cvhs6XRiOvEo6cj8r3Y\n7tR+Sw5Wavg89Uf4xD3HIcYfyqFWXJyOjuD6FyI1TkevuhTcwmV+hv9ZTekj1IeV\naKoyduVz63zKzACEFQQKNnqqOgUXR9FekqVKBM+kZBviNQuLFyh4QfQmrdIKFnXj\nKo5NOwg9ZswRWLl0y0Y0lesQcIGDd/1+6ZqBCIV8uIBqhw7IxpBJyYaw17bhV2Bd\nQ/qGvBgqOzv9Fn5HA1NCQdyAfuDn/7OR8+U4+UfYyfe3pPVFhqZtD/8PPjodacG8\nzOjIFu2OvsqHz32HpY8rmzbJuSsDYUDH52YWpoLQreEDdjVF/LGhMdjN2wgYpQdZ\nwQcw9OGk9uRxp132PtoQhZYGRQ87E3+NoPp6gV/VgvpueyAjS29Cld2Ak4/TzC1N\n9ynyz49zMLvemDMD3WxUA5y2gFfUV9XBXTWH1FKW8HrNemvSiCqFv36P20PXYjvN\nni+0oZ4NO4jT584WUbR9\n=v2Up\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:35:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDQ5ZGVlMjY1MjQyM2E4ZWU3MTk2MWY1MGRiZGU5ZTU0NzBjMWYzOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/f8abf005a5c1c929f766e732740620293ce78f2b","sha":"f8abf005a5c1c929f766e732740620293ce78f2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/f8abf005a5c1c929f766e732740620293ce78f2b"}],"sha":"49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/49dee2652423a8ee71961f50dbde9e5470c1f392"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289388318?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zkasuran","id":289388318,"login":"zkasuran","node_id":"U_kgDOET-3Hg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkasuran","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/f8abf005a5c1c929f766e732740620293ce78f2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:28:48Z","email":"zkasuran@gmail.com","name":"Asuran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:28:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server-utils): Record LangGraph span I/O for non-MessagesAnnotation state (#23315)\n\n`instrumentLangGraph` recorded span input and output only when the graph\nstate uses `MessagesAnnotation`. The input read did `args[0].messages ??\n[]` and the output helper returned early when `result.messages` was not\nan array, so a graph on a custom state annotation produced an empty\n`gen_ai.input.messages` and no `gen_ai.response.text`. No error, just an\nempty `invoke_agent` span in the AI Agents view.\n\nThis keeps the `MessagesAnnotation` path unchanged. When there is no\n`messages` array, it serializes the whole input and output state and\nrecords it, wrapped as a single `{ role, content }` message so the\nattribute stays a valid chat array (the convention\n`extractLLMRequestAttributes` already uses in this package). A null\ninput (the resume case) records nothing rather than a misleading empty\narray. Serialization uses core''s circular-safe `stringify` so an unusual\nstate object cannot throw inside the span callback.\n\nFixes getsentry/sentry-javascript#19628\n\nAI assistance (Claude, Anthropic) was used in developing this change.\nThe design, review and verification were done by the author. Verified\nlocally: the `@sentry/server-utils` vitest suite (335 to 339 passing),\nthe new tests failing before and passing after the fix, `oxlint\n--type-aware`, `oxfmt --check`, `tsc` on the changed files, plus a real\nGoogle Gemini LangGraph run showing the span input and output empty\nbefore and populated after.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Abdelrahman Awad <abdelrahman.awad@sentry.io>\nCo-authored-by: Andrei Borza <andrei.borza@sentry.io>","tree":{"sha":"4fe1d09b384e48deffeddc9f103f72fd6b83581d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/4fe1d09b384e48deffeddc9f103f72fd6b83581d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/f8abf005a5c1c929f766e732740620293ce78f2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fe1d09b384e48deffeddc9f103f72fd6b83581d\nparent d3e5b7ba75df45691679a1f6b67e08c4aeef342c\nauthor Asuran <zkasuran@gmail.com> 1791383328 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791383328 +0200\n\nfix(server-utils): Record LangGraph span I/O for non-MessagesAnnotation state (#23315)\n\n`instrumentLangGraph` recorded span input and output only when the graph\nstate uses `MessagesAnnotation`. The input read did `args[0].messages ??\n[]` and the output helper returned early when `result.messages` was not\nan array, so a graph on a custom state annotation produced an empty\n`gen_ai.input.messages` and no `gen_ai.response.text`. No error, just an\nempty `invoke_agent` span in the AI Agents view.\n\nThis keeps the `MessagesAnnotation` path unchanged. When there is no\n`messages` array, it serializes the whole input and output state and\nrecords it, wrapped as a single `{ role, content }` message so the\nattribute stays a valid chat array (the convention\n`extractLLMRequestAttributes` already uses in this package). A null\ninput (the resume case) records nothing rather than a misleading empty\narray. Serialization uses core''s circular-safe `stringify` so an unusual\nstate object cannot throw inside the span callback.\n\nFixes getsentry/sentry-javascript#19628\n\nAI assistance (Claude, Anthropic) was used in developing this change.\nThe design, review and verification were done by the author. Verified\nlocally: the `@sentry/server-utils` vitest suite (335 to 339 passing),\nthe new tests failing before and passing after the fix, `oxlint\n--type-aware`, `oxfmt --check`, `tsc` on the changed files, plus a real\nGoogle Gemini LangGraph run showing the span input and output empty\nbefore and populated after.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Abdelrahman Awad <abdelrahman.awad@sentry.io>\nCo-authored-by: Andrei Borza <andrei.borza@sentry.io>","reason":"va