,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/b47fd85d853b80fe6184490534d559f633cae8cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:17:23Z","email":"charly.gomez1310@gmail.com","name":"Charly Gomez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:33:35Z","email":"charly.gomez1310@gmail.com","name":"Charly Gomez"},"message":"meta(changelog): Update changelog for 11.5.0\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9a56b173e26b861f564828a1ab242ba99356c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/e9a56b173e26b861f564828a1ab242ba99356c09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/b47fd85d853b80fe6184490534d559f633cae8cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20254395?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chargome","id":20254395,"login":"chargome","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjU0Mzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/b47fd85d853b80fe6184490534d559f633cae8cf","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGI0N2ZkODVkODUzYjgwZmU2MTg0NDkwNTM0ZDU1OWY2MzNjYWU4Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/603eb60a651653fe47f6ffff6e998dce57f1c41a","sha":"603eb60a651653fe47f6ffff6e998dce57f1c41a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/603eb60a651653fe47f6ffff6e998dce57f1c41a"}],"sha":"b47fd85d853b80fe6184490534d559f633cae8cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/b47fd85d853b80fe6184490534d559f633cae8cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26038247?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/msonnb","id":26038247,"login":"msonnb","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDM4MjQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/msonnb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/603eb60a651653fe47f6ffff6e998dce57f1c41a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:31:09Z","email":"martin.sonnberger@sentry.io","name":"Martin Sonnberger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:31:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai): Normalize token usage and preserve cache breakdowns (#25074)\n\nCached-token usage was inconsistent across AI integrations: Anthropic\nreported only uncached input tokens, some integrations dropped cache\nbreakdowns, and LangChain could overwrite complete usage with counters\nfrom the final stream chunk. This produced incomplete totals and could\nleave cache counts greater than the reported input count, breaking\ndownstream pricing.\n\nThis PR treats input and output counts as inclusive totals. Cache reads\nand writes are subsets of input, and reasoning tokens are a subset of\noutput. Provider-specific normalization happens before setting those\nattributes, so the breakdowns are never added to an already-inclusive\ntotal.\n\n- **Anthropic:** Include cache reads and writes in input usage and emit\nboth breakdown attributes for regular and streaming responses.\n- **OpenAI:** Preserve cache details from Chat Completions and Responses\nusage without increasing their existing totals.\n- **Google GenAI:** Preserve cached-input usage and include thinking\ntokens in output, with reasoning reported separately.\n- **LangChain:** Prefer normalized message usage over generic\n`tokenUsage`, which can contain only the final stream chunk’s counters.\nNormalize raw Anthropic usage as a fallback and count shared candidate\nusage once per prompt.\n- **LangGraph:** Aggregate cache breakdowns alongside token totals for\nnewly generated messages, excluding conversation history.\n\nRegression coverage includes competing usage sources, repeated streaming\nevents, missing and zero cache counts, batched prompts, and shared\ncandidate usage.\n\nFixes #25069\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-6 <codex@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Andrei <168741329+andreiborza@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcae46f2ec4910236d87d24471460fac1aa3248d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/bcae46f2ec4910236d87d24471460fac1aa3248d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/603eb60a651653fe47f6ffff6e998dce57f1c41a","verification":{"payload":"tree bcae46f2ec4910236d87d24471460fac1aa3248d\nparent dd398d04c3116c246ab7ab18749c55c54fcb0d6c\nauthor Martin Sonnberger <martin.sonnberger@sentry.io> 1791365469 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791365469 +0000\n\nfix(ai): Normalize token usage and preserve cache breakdowns (#25074)\n\nCached-token usage was inconsistent across AI integrations: Anthropic\nreported only uncached input tokens, some integrations dropped cache\nbreakdowns, and LangChain could overwrite complete usage with counters\nfrom the final stream chunk. This produced incomplete totals and could\nleave cache counts greater than the reported input count, breaking\ndownstream pricing.\n\nThis PR treats input and output counts as inclusive totals. Cache reads\nand writes are subsets of input, and reasoning tokens are a subset of\noutput. Provider-specific normalization happens before setting those\nattributes, so the breakdowns are never added to an already-inclusive\ntotal.\n\n- **Anthropic:** Include cache reads and writes in input usage and emit\nboth breakdown attributes for regular and streaming responses.\n- **OpenAI:** Preserve cache details from Chat Completions and Responses\nusage without increasing their existing totals.\n- **Google GenAI:** Preserve cached-input usage and include thinking\ntokens in output, with reasoning reported separately.\n- **LangChain:** Prefer normalized message usage over generic\n`tokenUsage`, which can contain only the final stream chunk’s counters.\nNormalize raw Anthropic usage as a fallback and count shared candidate\nusage once per prompt.\n- **LangGraph:** Aggregate cache breakdowns alongside token totals for\nnewly generated messages, excluding conversation history.\n\nRegression coverage includes competing usage sources, repeated streaming\nevents, missing and zero cache counts, batched prompts, and shared\ncandidate usage.\n\nFixes #25069\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-6 <codex@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Andrei <168741329+andreiborza@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"--