588b901903c5df653c661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/75ae1647c1bdad2ff9a588b901903c5df653c661"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/c7ed7caea071d97eeeea5a834f3ab7dd6d4e2b92/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:22Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(cloudflare): Add Workers AI tracing tests for Clef (#25027)\n\nCloudflare documents Clef (`@cf/cloudflare/clef`) as a drop-in for Jev\nwith the same `state` + `questions` request shape, so it already goes\nthrough the `evaluate` path from #24833. Only Jev had tests, so this\nadds a Clef integration test and a real-Worker E2E test.\n\nThe integration mock returns the documented Clef response, which has no\n`{ state, result }` wrapper (the Jev binding response has one). That\nmakes it cover the unwrapped branch of the evaluate response handling,\nwhich the Jev test does not reach. The E2E test calls the real model, so\nit is the one that confirms what the binding actually returns. The docs\ndo not give a `model` value for the response, so it only asserts that it\ncontains `clef`.\n\nFixes #25011\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"195f203608bbc1ec451526b542a03b889f86c8b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/195f203608bbc1ec451526b542a03b889f86c8b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/c7ed7caea071d97eeeea5a834f3ab7dd6d4e2b92","verification":{"payload":"tree 195f203608bbc1ec451526b542a03b889f86c8b6\nparent 2a085beeacd094b74e5bc78024e6c6591bfe50d1\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791358222 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791358222 +0000\n\ntest(cloudflare): Add Workers AI tracing tests for Clef (#25027)\n\nCloudflare documents Clef (`@cf/cloudflare/clef`) as a drop-in for Jev\nwith the same `state` + `questions` request shape, so it already goes\nthrough the `evaluate` path from #24833. Only Jev had tests, so this\nadds a Clef integration test and a real-Worker E2E test.\n\nThe integration mock returns the documented Clef response, which has no\n`{ state, result }` wrapper (the Jev binding response has one). That\nmakes it cover the unwrapped branch of the evaluate response handling,\nwhich the Jev test does not reach. The E2E test calls the real model, so\nit is the one that confirms what the binding actually returns. The docs\ndo not give a `model` value for the response, so it only asserts that it\ncontains `clef`.\n\nFixes #25011\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfUOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV6QQACT2WoNsWgr7ETTLC/x