024e6c6591bfe50d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20254395?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chargome","id":20254395,"login":"chargome","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjU0Mzk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chargome","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/5fc18dc416aeed33fc56227fd3714b7c58f21d97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:08:57Z","email":"charly.gomez1310@gmail.com","name":"Charly Gomez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:08:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(remix): Pass the project when creating a release (#25079)\n\nThe release API rejects a release without a project, and the project\ngiven to the `sentry` SDK does not reach `release.create`. Since the\nmove to that SDK (#23398), `sentry-upload-sourcemaps` failed with `400\nBad Request` on every run. The unit test mocked the SDK, so it did not\ncatch it. Reproduced against a real org.\n\nBoth upload scripts take the project from `--project`, then\n`SENTRY_PROJECT`, and fail with a clear message when neither is set.\n`@sentry/bundler-plugins` already did this. The React Router Vite plugin\nhas the same bug, fixed separately.\n\nFixes #24989\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46a6a2c173e0074dacf7dcea747b6d3f1ad519c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/46a6a2c173e0074dacf7dcea747b6d3f1ad519c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/5fc18dc416aeed33fc56227fd3714b7c58f21d97","verification":{"payload":"tree 46a6a2c173e0074dacf7dcea747b6d3f1ad519c0\nparent 40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf\nauthor Charly Gomez <charly.gomez1310@gmail.com> 1791356937 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791356937 +0200\n\nfix(remix): Pass the project when creating a release (#25079)\n\nThe release API rejects a release without a project, and the project\ngiven to the `sentry` SDK does not reach `release.create`. Since the\nmove to that SDK (#23398), `sentry-upload-sourcemaps` failed with `400\nBad Request` on every run. The unit test mocked the SDK, so it did not\ncatch it. Reproduced against a real org.\n\nBoth upload scripts take the project from `--project`, then\n`SENTRY_PROJECT`, and fail with a clear message when neither is set.\n`@sentry/bundler-plugins` already did this. The React Router Vite plugin\nhas the same bug, fixed separately.\n\nFixes #24989\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfAJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk9YQAGQVp6+/nbhkRqp67B1ia13E\nbqmmPkLk76O2gdQltcEiUEqnsBgkeecLi2cMLghTOx+E8zMlRK3dn1KsSCc1/WCl\n2ZGT5gcG5174wR3lhKjrMaFt4dgB3vBAIcJFxcjxaZ8WvUIXaD8mlhDEvssQ5r+w\nGMconzA3+jv4ZnjoaknCDNaWTPzcDcykmtXrtamXrWr/cIF4fsb90gtOI7tJcysv\ndFvZ0wmB0PL0WDqFbCGxNUloxKvGMPFeULPJ8bZjMyORmbiYL3kUQ80NFdDNg/ZZ\njvFPVRHEXjQHgU6eg51w1lO/GzegEWQXoAG1dN51zvQh2Fuwljy26vnXmm5+xNqy\nSrRjVcDB1YfGD1kFqOhPlILl9gMp3nKPqR2/WnlPuZ7Sg0DWfl4fdyLaGwqHYkdZ\nF9ftRMEsxJ7sywNb0DS/zM0E+IRpieRfyKwH5BFZRDUAGivLjFd/5wxsij/lNHs1\nXXK6dZUYE10GFlQ7Xnh1ISFKx00eYSGeUOyjm11EphG11tAXYyG8sUFUHCn+oCbT\n80vxCrbDxqrFADyx1MOjGStm0uU4YwE7Gfsbuqo9kJeONVZtAsAumQN+i82lF6K6\nmKsMRedS3eDpZwzD0ahhTx4xTLhMDYS8jqj31u/a8YXP9Aw0XnxrefdTpU2pKmqp\nx5Kz/tgN+9bNpGrUzFWX\n=STCu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T07:08:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/5fc18dc416aeed33fc56227fd3714b7c58f21d97","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDVmYzE4ZGM0MTZhZWVkMzNmYzU2MjI3ZmQzNzE0YjdjNThmMjFkOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf","sha":"40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf"}],"sha":"5fc18dc416aeed33fc56227fd3714b7c58f21d97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/5fc18dc416aeed33fc56227fd3714b7c58f21d97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91732700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RulaKhaled","id":91732700,"login":"RulaKhaled","node_id":"U_kgDOBXe63A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:40:16Z","email":"rola.abuhasna@sentry.io","name":"Rola Abuhasna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:40:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(langchain): Derive gen_ai.conversation.id from the invoke config (#24831)\n\nThe LangChain integration only set `gen_ai.conversation.id` when the\nuser called `Sentry.setConversationId()` themselves. LangGraph read\n`configurable.thread_id`, but stamped it on its own `invoke_agent` span\nonly, so the chat and tool child spans went out without it.\n\nChild runs inherit their parent''s metadata, so this PR reads the\nconversation id from run metadata and sets the attribute on the chat,\nchain and tool spans. On `@langchain/core` 0.1.20 to 1.1.39,\n`ensureConfig` copies every primitive `config.configurable` entry into\nthat metadata, so an id passed to `invoke()` is already there.\n`@langchain/core` 1.1.40 stopped doing that for any handler except\nLangSmith''s tracer. So where we inject our handler, in the chat-model\nhook and the LangGraph `invoke` proxy, we copy the three keys below from\n`configurable` into `metadata` ourselves. Metadata the user set takes\nprecedence.\n\nKeys read, in order:\n\n- `thread_id`, the LangGraph checkpointer key and one of the two keys\nLangSmith groups threads by\n- `session_id`, the other LangSmith key\n- `sessionId`, what `RunnableWithMessageHistory` requires in JS\n\nAn id set on the scope via `Sentry.setConversationId()` still wins.\n`conversationIdIntegration` applies it on `spanStart`, after the initial\nattributes, so an explicit user id overwrites the derived one. The\nintegration test covers this.\n\nLangGraph''s `invoke_agent` span and the tool spans `createReactAgent`\ncreates now use the same helper. So they read the same keys, accept\nnumeric ids, and let an id from `Sentry.setConversationId()` win over\n`thread_id`. Before, `thread_id` overwrote the scope id on the\n`invoke_agent` span only, and the tool spans never picked up\n`thread_id`.\n\nOne gap remains on `@langchain/core` >= 1.1.40. If you pass\n`createLangChainCallbackHandler()` yourself to a chain outside\nLangGraph, the chain and tool spans get no id from `configurable`,\nbecause the handler never sees it. The chat spans still get it. Closing\nthat would mean hooking more than chat models, so it is left for a\nfollow-up.\n\n\n\n\n\n**Bun.** The new suite failed on the Bun runner because `@sentry/bun`\nbuilds its own default integration list and never registered\n`conversationIdIntegration`, so `Sentry.setConversationId()` was a no-op\nthere. The second commit adds it, in the same position Node uses.\n\nPart of #24832.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a56916cc36509b1fffcb912cb07a643168486c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/2a56916cc36509b1fffcb912cb07a643168486c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a56916cc36509b1fffcb912cb07a643168486c9\nparent 2cc2b29250cb7dc24afd7afdf2a85ee0425ed99d\nauthor Rola Abuhasna <rola.abuhasna@sentry.io> 1791301216 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791301216 +0200\n\nfeat(langchain): Derive gen_ai.conversation.id from the invoke config (#24831)\n\nThe LangChain integration only set `gen_ai.conversation.id` when the\nuser called `Sentry.setConversationId()` themselves. LangGraph read\n`configurable.thread_id`, but stamped it on its own `invoke_agent` span\nonly, so the chat and tool child spans went out without it.\n\nChild runs inherit their parent''s metadata, so this PR reads the\nconversation id from run metadata and sets the attribute on the chat,\nchain and tool spans. On `@langchain/core` 0.1.20 to 1.1.39,\n`ensureConfig` copies every primitive `config.configurable` entry into\nthat metadata, so an id passed to `invoke()` is already there.\n`@langchain/core` 1.1.40 stopped doing that for any handler except\nLangSmith''s tracer. So where we inject our handler, in the chat-model\nhook and the LangGraph `invoke` proxy, we copy the three keys below from\n`configurable` into `metadata` ourselves. Metadata the user set takes\nprecedence.\n\nKeys read, in order:\n\n- `thread_id`, the LangGraph checkpointer key and one of the two keys\nLangSmith groups threads by\n- `session_id`, the other LangSmith key\n- `sessionId`, what `RunnableWithMessageHistory` requires in JS\n\nAn id set on the scope via `Sentry.setConversationId()` still wins.\n`conversationIdIntegration` applies it on `spanStart`, after the initial\nattributes, so an explicit user id overwrites the derived one. The\nintegration test covers this.\n\nLangGraph''s `invoke_agent` span and the tool spans `createReactAgent`\ncreates now use the same helper. So they read the same keys, accept\nnumeric ids, and let an id from `Sentry.setConversationId()` win over\n`thread_id`. Before, `thread_id` overwrote the scope id on the\n`invoke_agent` span only, and the tool spans never picked up\n`thread_id`.\n\nOne gap remains on `@langchain/core` >= 1.1.40. If you pass\n`createLangChainCallbackHandler()` yourself to a chain outside\nLangGraph, the chain and tool spans get no id from `configurable`,\nbecause the handler never sees it. The chat spans still get it. Closing\nthat would mean hooking more than chat models, so it is left for a\nfollow-up.\n\n\n\n\n\n**Bun.** The new suite failed on the Bun runner because `@sentry/bun`\nbuilds its own default integration list and never registered\n`conversationIdIntegration`, so `Sentry.setConversationId()` was a no-op\nthere. The second commit adds it, in the same position Node uses.\n\nPart of #24832.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRZgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKK8QADoNmvshqDr6Nj6aDigP0Un3\ninwk0IdWr1EMmhHzCIKyozh0lh5GwwdnBuuiCY1TGJtHoo9ryS0GATl0oiAYefiH\naiM++dz3978ummWRoP5YND8L3pFs4qjBydrTlLAfkX9HEmDVRojlsziKIFNUqJZr\nlI5vZe1AB+QG5VsPVsARswL0jUL5RUBmkNiVQgfSewPXnr9wMR7O101pSfhNc6sJ\n4I8Pi3RGFh4bkLIdT1cKFW8EFPoyoWQhZ8m6yrbWNKDakmj4r9T7w1zLQMAcd6np\n4tY784NrX7UQOwAqSTaK0VqFexHytJCZ1cz86LaBOFKV+SkSIDJn8AUY8hySxjSa\n7RTyjfXpvHqJst1ZrlRwUiTh3KlsNbnxXRxZAeJboht0hZYfCzzLLsdv8FOQx43K\np/dZDQ4pMDlf21gAbPk6bV6cfqM9cOCr0jvegNUBvPhSNXA16I7sGpWaMywoV+7B\nuvH73Ihmfv7whK1sefk3w0hGxwOkNiJaqOQs+LB9dE/B25xW65AMJu9VfBAq9DtD\nZAcaqjpkm+EXxlCkwGazL7diy6VbLpN7G/wB11VBJMhF1je0GMs4e/IBfMQrly6r\n12Mn8HavejvCTtsMNwS9wdBvXv1crsjLQcF9+tuRnduyod/QMLJOSG8n8hUdU2io\nd8/naHG3nRj8V4kkgQtb\n=6Ess\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:40:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKDQwYWQ0Y2E1OTg4ZjU3NjM0ODUwYTQyOTBmMDg1NTljZTA1MDJlYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/2cc2b29250cb7dc24afd7afdf2a85ee0425ed99d","sha":"2cc2b29250cb7dc24afd7afdf2a85ee0425ed99d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2cc2b29250cb7dc24afd7afdf2a85ee0425ed99d"}],"sha":"40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/40ad4ca5988f57634850a4290f08559ce0502ebf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91732700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RulaKhaled","id":91732700,"login":"RulaKhaled","node_id":"U_kgDOBXe63A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RulaKhaled","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2cc2b29250cb7dc24afd7afdf2a85ee0425ed99d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:37:15Z","email":"rola.abuhasna@sentry.io","name":"Rola Abuhasna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:37:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server-utils): Derive the Vercel AI conversation id from the OpenAI conversation option (#24979)\n\nThe Vercel AI integration filled `gen_ai.conversation.id` with\n`providerMetadata.openai.responseId`. That is the id of the response\nthat just came back, so every call got a different value under a\ngrouping attribute and showed up as its own one-span conversation. The\nsame value is already on `gen_ai.response.id`. The mapping came in with\n#16992 and #19903 later had to guard it from overwriting user-set ids.\n\nThe id now comes from `providerOptions.openai.conversation` (or\n`azure`), the Conversations API `conv_` id, which is the same on every\nturn. Child model-call and tool spans inherit it from the active\noperation span. `Sentry.setConversationId()` still wins, since\n`conversationIdIntegration` writes the scope value on `spanStart` after\nthese start attributes. The v6 adapter forwards `providerOptions` so\n`ai` 4 to 6 behave the same.\n\nNot in this PR: reading the id from `runtimeContext` /\n`experimental_telemetry.metadata` goes with #24706 once #24721 lands.\n\nPart of #24832\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3f7a3b992bd5db2ffe9e2d564754c4bfa733ebc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/3f7a3b992bd5db2ffe9e2d564754c4bfa733ebc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/2cc2b29250cb7dc24afd7afdf2a85ee0425ed99d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f7a3b992bd5db2ffe9e2d564754c4bfa733ebc6\nparent 0369ca9d6abf27fe6d8f74d516c8b379f536d2dd\nauthor Rola Abuhasna <rola.abuhasna@sentry.io> 1791301035 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791301035 +0200\n\nfix(server-utils): Derive the Vercel AI conversation id from the OpenAI conversation option (#24979)\n\nThe Vercel AI integration filled `gen_ai.conversation.id` with\n`providerMetadata.openai.responseId`. That is the id of the response\nthat just came back, so every call got a different value under a\ngrouping attribute and showed up as its own one-span conversation. The\nsame value is already on `gen_ai.response.id`. The mapping came in with\n#16992 and #19903 later had to guard it from overwriting user-set ids.\n\nThe id now comes from `providerOptions.openai.conversation` (or\n`azure`), the Conversations API `conv_` id, which is the same on every\nturn. Child model-call and tool spans inherit it from the active\noperation span. `Sentry.setConversationId()` still wins, since\n`conversationIdIntegration` writes the scope value on `spanStart` after\nthese start attributes. The v6 adapter forwards `providerOptions` so\n`ai` 4 to 6 behave the same.\n\nNot in this PR: reading the id from `runtimeContext` /\n`experimental_telemetry.metadata` goes with #24706 once #24721 lands.\n\nPart of #24832\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRWrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbCIQAJjgRuBQFe0siX/hcsoSkj7J\n1kTRMT2Mcch05lbAe+YwhhqV2VMKAwqrVUFz37Y6kqWTpEKs4lypefaw9syyRH7O\nOgVzkJcRcfZsKAgPLWgsLugyZ1Br12QW6qT3+rcyJ6q9Ctaw6dNEJ5UAUxGrTGNo\nRKx8EMIqkQ4GCzelC