ODkzMGVkYmMwODZiMzY2MjNjOGUyMDhlYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/2ea03002bc3ef53de486259d6eb1dd363cc65f12","sha":"2ea03002bc3ef53de486259d6eb1dd363cc65f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2ea03002bc3ef53de486259d6eb1dd363cc65f12"}],"sha":"18e4b7e626f8248930edbc086b36623c8e208eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/18e4b7e626f8248930edbc086b36623c8e208eb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/2ea03002bc3ef53de486259d6eb1dd363cc65f12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:59:04Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:59:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(react-router): Export createSentryServerInstrumentation from the Cloudflare entry (#25042)\n\nThe docs set up React Router''s instrumentation API with `export const\ninstrumentations = [Sentry.createSentryServerInstrumentation()]`, but\nthe Cloudflare entry (`@sentry/react-router/cloudflare`, and\n`@sentry/react-router` under the `workerd` condition) did not export the\nfunction, so a Worker could not follow that step. Its imports are\nruntime-independent, so the Cloudflare entry now exports it too.\n\nWithout the API, the SDK names a request after its route only when React\nRouter renders a document. Resource routes and errors in loaders and\nactions kept the name of the server below React Router: `GET /{*splat}`\non Node and Deno, `GET` or none on Bun and Cloudflare.\n`react-router-8-framework` now exports `instrumentations` on every\nruntime, like the docs, so these are named after the route everywhere.\nThe error tests lose their runtime branches and their todo, and the\nerror mechanism and the `http.server` origin change to the\ninstrumentation API''s values. `react-router-7-framework` still covers\nthe setup without the API.\n\nPart of #24836\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0ff7409350f413da4a41405cc733f7f37856889","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/f0ff7409350f413da4a41405cc733f7f37856889"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/2ea03002bc3ef53de486259d6eb1dd363cc65f12","verification":{"payload":"tree f0ff7409350f413da4a41405cc733f7f37856889\nparent b49fbcca616b4b9df042ab2f724f36727fed0ada\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791298744 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298744 +0200\n\nfeat(react-router): Export createSentryServerInstrumentation from the Cloudflare entry (#25042)\n\nThe docs set up React Router''s instrumentation API with `export const\ninstrumentations = [Sentry.createSentryServerInstrumentation()]`, but\nthe Cloudflare entry (`@sentry/react-router/cloudflare`, and\n`@sentry/react-router` under the `workerd` condition) did not export the\nfunction, so a Worker could not follow that step. Its imports are\nruntime-independent, so the Cloudflare entry now exports it too.\n\nWithout the API, the SDK names a request after its route only when React\nRouter renders a document. Resource routes and errors in loaders and\nactions kept the name of the server below React Router: `GET /{*splat}`\non Node and Deno, `GET` or none on Bun and Cloudflare.\n`react-router-8-framework` now exports `instrumentations` on every\nruntime, like the docs, so these are named after the route everywhere.\nThe error tests lose their runtime branches and their todo, and the\nerror mechanism and the `http.server` origin change to the\ninstrumentation API''s values. `react-router-7-framework` still covers\nthe setup without the API.\n\nPart of #24836\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQy4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFekQABuMFLrTpeesh8+bJEHYlMY2\nq4ECiYqmUHvin4dzDlYn5hBISAKllzlmQGxtLI+dhzH0//YoBEUw7VCUBhsxkigz\n7TCdYWauKXU9bkN5+53FMfAdx4kJgWxNnwxBvRzrA/0vPp509/jvOEfP4D+Ob/vl\nO2myMXXNOzZ1EItfp9jMJ+QAUPOZq924RIdi+SX2Z3Pt0Wef++HzFJiNdcyVpG5Z\na8rinjvLXw04au4D/hB7vJFjLqzAYNL7WwRavgwgjPbbijpudafP2BdC/NoRdJyg\nEjyArkdukYHVbFanZjgiR17SNf0CzI7iPGGMXUifhJfY3/zwhYaf0qcULgMAPVhu\nN5Rd3v57p7Z/IE+m9qcOdZwYD5+KUh17jd+WKl8V1OZShYCuvhbLXBc1/atdxhoJ\ngpAFQt3XLlecb6t3Zh/MVHNqkGxeU1BL40kQ0JxDFfI4NbwzNzlYQjKBVZdi7bPR\nRHg5hIljpOJULvstrBjkB10IxNrV8Gs8a9561Mf1PAJJw80dBiRWKFA6jRSbBcb9\neRo++ObfGNKliOgLNhz0xCdTNqjXbrKDdUuVcmBp+THOEL1yEtNvpBwsFvgKljCh\nfwLh04Wn2nHBfhwtOK3BUOVv584cdFNE33cb9vseXjEJUgPjD/7XGpTvL56X89ep\n8qQxkq8i7pB/RXuW1U3L\n=ji5E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:59:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"http