ithub.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/b49fbcca616b4b9df042ab2f724f36727fed0ada/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:59:03Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:59:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): Cover isolation, trace propagation and logs on all react-router-8-framework runtimes (#25041)\n\nAdds the assertions that #24836 lists and `react-router-8-framework` did\nnot have: per-request isolation, incoming trace continuation, trace\npropagation to an outgoing `fetch`, and logs. They pass on Node, Bun,\nDeno and Cloudflare without a runtime branch, so the audit''s Bun\nfindings for isolation, incoming trace and outgoing `fetch`, and its\nDeno `fetch` finding, no longer reproduce with `@sentry/bun` and\n`@sentry/deno`. With every runtime green, the Bun, Deno and Cloudflare\nvariants move to the required `variants`.\n\nThe isolation test holds the first of two concurrent requests until the\nsecond one has set its tag, so both scopes are in use at the same time\nwithout a timer. The `fetch` test finds its spans through the\n`sentry-trace` header that the target route received, because the server\nspan of a resource route is not named after the route yet (`GET\n/{*splat}` on Node and Deno, `GET` on Bun and Cloudflare).\n\nPart of #24836\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a64826415a371e052721b7344c8822856e9fb3f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/a64826415a371e052721b7344c8822856e9fb3f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/b49fbcca616b4b9df042ab2f724f36727fed0ada","verification":{"payload":"tree a64826415a371e052721b7344c8822856e9fb3f6\nparent ea31682ee6548a361ffd508b1664322eef629b5d\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791298743 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298743 +0200\n\ntest(e2e): Cover isolation, trace propagation and logs on all react-router-8-framework runtimes (#25041)\n\nAdds the assertions that #24836 lists and `react-router-8-framework` did\nnot have: per-request isolation, incoming trace continuation, trace\npropagation to an outgoing `fetch`, and logs. They pass on Node, Bun,\nDeno and Cloudflare without a runtime branch, so the audit''s Bun\nfindings for isolation, incoming trace and outgoing `fetch`, and its\nDeno `fetch` finding, no longer reproduce with `@sentry/bun` and\n`@sentry/deno`. With every runtime green, the Bun, Deno and Cloudflare\nvariants move to the required `variants`.\n\nThe isolation test holds the first of two concurrent requests until the\nsecond one has set its tag, so both scopes are in use at the same time\nwithout a timer. The `fetch` test finds its spans through the\n`sentry-trace` header that the target route received, because the server\nspan of a resource route is not named after the route yet (`GET\n/{*splat}` on Node and Deno, `GET` on Bun and Cloudflare).\n\nPart of #24836\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQy3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7qEQAAYc3ZHlitAM37NstYf8h+oO\nhHjKWLdD586b5efdi6kb63bLYh+Hn4BM5G5vL26ys7ovXkkpzrmNSIB2aXlQsqRK\nb8UqP65UHxpvCpWiqLJ5uWbEoTM4KViqX8Om20iSJrEjhaCgxLJhbFduh4hth6xG\n3H6VlydbHPUHkW6J/RqfKwmkkHU/O1aNtkZGOjabo6DUiMO+KTLNIyS6A5VrS1Wv\nphq1qBGlncWU29DbE8zyOR2Po2LeCyrH2T