263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/345064dae7016c2c48a15f6f1bcbdb87b00fd5f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:05:07Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:05:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(nextjs): Skip `init` inside a request of `@sentry/cloudflare` (#24996)\n\nNext.js calls `register()` inside the first request. When the Worker is\nwrapped with `withSentry` from `@sentry/cloudflare`, the server and edge\n`init` installed the OpenTelemetry async context strategy on the storage\nof that running request, and every later request failed with\n`context.getValue is not a function` (#24603).\n\nOn Workers, `init` now creates no client while a request of `withSentry`\nruns, because that client already handles the request. The SDK detects\nthis from the installed strategy (AsyncLocalStorage, a store is set,\n`Cloudflare-Workers` user agent) instead of a new option, so existing\nsetups need no change. The server `init` still adds its global event\nprocessors and the `turbopack` tag, which also apply to the events of\nthe Cloudflare client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"94ced7f3ea87a8b05ccaeddfadc24f42e93af1b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/94ced7f3ea87a8b05ccaeddfadc24f42e93af1b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/345064dae7016c2c48a15f6f1bcbdb87b00fd5f1","verification":{"payload":"tree 94ced7f3ea87a8b05ccaeddfadc24f42e93af1b3\nparent 9ae9a3027daf12f31c7f848849dd1adbba732bc8\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791295507 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791295507 +0200\n\nfix(nextjs): Skip `init` inside a request of `@sentry/cloudflare` (#24996)\n\nNext.js calls `register()` inside the first request. When the Worker is\nwrapped with `withSentry` from `@sentry/cloudflare`, the server and edge\n`init` installed the OpenTelemetry async context strategy on the storage\nof that running request, and every later request failed with\n`context.getValue is not a function` (#24603).\n\nOn Workers, `init` now creates no client while a request of `withSentry`\nruns, because that client already handles the request. The SDK detects\nthis from the installed strategy (AsyncLocalStorage, a store is set,\n`Cloudflare-Workers` user agent) instead of a new option, so existing\nsetups need no change. The server `init` still adds its global event\nprocessors and the `turbopack` tag, which also apply to the events of\nthe Cloudflare client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQATCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnjIQACmp1E2YC7fvkzzh4U37Bhvb\nAnbvLUJmj0bopo968bcH8O2uwL9MUW7m7I0HT+ULcSeJSO0DwaziLVtHBU1B/f98\n31IAYDILE6NqvTcgBHeqCNRNWdI1y2a