onse arrives with the route the server reported. The scope''s\ntransaction name follows a late rename only while that span is still the\ncurrent one.\n\nRoutes are recorded under the URL that served the response, so a\nredirected fetch does not misname later visits. Pending spans are keyed\nby pathname and bounded; a failed fetch leaves its entry alone, because\nthe Navigation API aborts the previous intercept only after a repeated\nnavigation has re-queued the same path.\n\nFixes #24872\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"63706eac17b9bb8053b676da46f75e5dff9968ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/63706eac17b9bb8053b676da46f75e5dff9968ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/1e3cccdb87610633f15502d1633c450072c80548","verification":{"payload":"tree 63706eac17b9bb8053b676da46f75e5dff9968ba\nparent 32310b5df65b65a6451f9dbc6fc69569526527e4\nauthor Charly Gomez <charly.gomez1310@gmail.com> 1791275889 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791275889 +0200\n\nfeat(remix): Parameterize Remix 3 navigation spans (#25045)\n\nA navigation span is named through the route provider: right away when\nthe app loaded the route before, otherwise once the runtime''s frame\nfetch response arrives with the route the server reported. The scope''s\ntransaction name follows a late rename only while that span is still the\ncurrent one.\n\nRoutes are recorded under the URL that served the response, so a\nredirected fetch does not misname later visits. Pending spans are keyed\nby pathname and bounded; a failed fetch leaves its entry alone, because\nthe Navigation API aborts the previous intercept only after a repeated\nnavigation has re-queued the same path.\n\nFixes #24872\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLNxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA74kQAJsbTGdF