d the scope''s transaction\nname follows so errors group by route. An app with its own\n`routeProvider` keeps it.\n\nNavigations keep their fallback name here; the next PR names them.\n\nPart of #24872\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6975aefa95f94540006cd442823afe1ce3434b6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/6975aefa95f94540006cd442823afe1ce3434b6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/32310b5df65b65a6451f9dbc6fc69569526527e4","verification":{"payload":"tree 6975aefa95f94540006cd442823afe1ce3434b6b\nparent f2fc75c764a6ff6d9e372dd3a272e6a47000b3c4\nauthor Charly Gomez <charly.gomez1310@gmail.com> 1791275888 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791275888 +0200\n\nfeat(remix): Parameterize Remix 3 page load spans (#25053)\n\nThe client registers a cached route provider at `init` (#23551) and\nrecords the route the server reports for the document, read off the\nnavigation timing entry. The page load span, which starts under the low\ncardinality fallback, is renamed after it, and the scope''s transaction\nname follows so errors group by route. An app with its own\n`routeProvider` keeps it.\n\nNavigations keep their fallback name here; the next PR names them.\n\nPart of #24872\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLNwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIwkQADo7tuB3ORWahV6fADP8Mh9e\nPXnnNOhLDHb/cAeCFfOKENpiuvO8u+sfRfJAdcWh+KCZW6mLsxoLwlbhXu382Y87\nZARRaB1yjdXeloGgVJctrqEjLt/E5eWaIS06XR7dCac8+6iiJR318LFMwGaAPYGm\nBclYBenpqOyO+DQhPuSdbVrlsY4Wp/kczTV/vH1R1F19jZMfeR3o28kRYxdCjZrW\nI1rJCB590sY2vtV/W8HHDPpkcgB6fBWU4Tv/pZPhdRS4QeZAYf6UPaquiUBo9XN4\nP80T6Cz/HWLhc4UOyixrY2lOxWEjyUpxnlW5XdZPpxBh106opU66LlfRvpiLAuZl\nXDkz3t3pllvP0BkUTCG+E0ttMOeXF6Qqfv53WlbS+jY0IE2RFc/ZXaG5OmgUDkSD\n00XXmnoIh6L3nUbpZBt7llXKckkJh69eQ92uvtXhhAENcO+oQnnI05lcPg6NWMxR\