ript/commits/cfa5c7577a9fd2a88991b7815b8526c61eabfe3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:55:43Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:55:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bun): Add conversationIdIntegration to the default integrations (#25003)\n\n`@sentry/bun` builds its own list of default integrations, and that list\nhas no `conversationIdIntegration`. The other runtime SDKs install it\n(#24299 added it to Deno), and `@sentry/elysia` takes Bun''s list. So on\nBun and Elysia, a conversation id set with `Sentry.setConversationId()`,\nor by an AI integration on the scope, never reached the `gen_ai` spans.\n\nThis was the only reason the bundled Bun runs of the OpenAI and Vercel\nAI (v4) suites failed, so they run again.\n\nRef #23887\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b74f6c3b6ca042b39ed23abb9b1220e362d1ab84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/b74f6c3b6ca042b39ed23abb9b1220e362d1ab84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/cfa5c7577a9fd2a88991b7815b8526c61eabfe3f","verification":{"payload":"tree b74f6c3b6ca042b39ed23abb9b1220e362d1ab84\nparent 3dae6a50f7dd45d1dccf79b14f468148095e62d4\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791273343 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791273343 +0200\n\nfix(bun): Add conversationIdIntegration to the default integrations (#25003)\n\n`@sentry/bun` builds its own list of default integrations, and that list\nhas no `conversationIdIntegration`. The other runtime SDKs install it\n(#24299 added it to Deno), and `@sentry/elysia` takes Bun''s list. So on\nBun and Elysia, a conversation id set with `Sentry.setConversationId()`,\nor by an AI integration on the scope, never reached the `gen_ai` spans.\n\nThis was the only reason the bundled Bun runs of the OpenAI and Vercel\nAI (v4) suites failed, so they run again.\n\nRef #23887\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKl/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAggkQAIe96Q5a+m0oW2xL95lX+Kde\nokaUicomn2l8NeW4DRjYNmIruaXaTOuHTl7hYNH6JL2wd0VkqD4Whx+nzN5D6++I\nrTtY7UwY+EYvxLI0+9aXuBWd+ccq2tHtpomWInfKb6lGc2I+nNXU0w1ikaAMPfjI\nL21zn43KFbbbg4rhR2EY/RWvMiXSrn7+Xg5vR8pJ9YwoJsjDqcOhuR5/fYlGGFaO\nyvzOhjkwGUHyxTbnvFkXO72v40KOyvB6pH9BaWfcezLj5EQKIXVoSrU0Ou0lmgd1\nuPq3sbpPzIO3miCDUGdNQjh3AQmatB1fuMwVx2hDBj46AZTSJbQj9cJ2EfPfcTYJ\nHeu2GKc0cIrtGfF8j8Q/5eFS9uCRlB0cOYGcgVe7sdU1ygyOCGSbL/Mz1U74LEUj\naelI+7COHnrQJfVPog78YqR+ZMpvmp5RmrUWG7tFkvYTQlrcYXBfqDesrR59wp8V\nJe/U4hqBNYuDYqozfbI/aXTjp6KwYGjU1056zv8BrJA/ML5Gucg7Fsg8Kw1BKh72\nDkiZ/CdZVFW2QuHtbRDWwZM02C0X8kCMilonCXJUFrcrtN0RCV5kgjawE04ptM//\nWyzigPPW0VTedTIWZtQy9wj4p7zDyaaRIPtfzGqAlivACeLtPsLVA8hVL75lByu/\nrP4yPzKuGg4xKRzpiBPP\n=KIOf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:55:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/cfa5c7577a9fd2a88991b7815b8526c61eabfe3f","node_id":"C_kwDOADLKPNoAKGNmYTVjNzU3N2E5ZmQyYTg4OTkxYjc4MTViODUyNmM2MWVhYmZlM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commit/3dae6a50f7dd45d1dccf79b14f468148095e62d4","sha":"3dae6a50f7dd45d1dccf79b14f468148095e62d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/3dae6a50f7dd45d1dccf79b14f468148095e62d4"}],"sha":"cfa5c7577a9fd2a88991b7815b8526c61eabfe3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/cfa5c7577a9fd2a88991b7815b8526c61eabfe3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10677263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JPeer264","id":10677263,"login":"JPeer264","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc3MjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JPeer264","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/commits/3dae6a50f7dd45d1dccf79b14f468148095e62d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:55:42Z","email":"jan.peer@sentry.io","name":"Jan Peer Stöcklmair"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:55:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server-utils): Map Flue messages and token usage to the gen_ai conventions (#24992)\n\nFlue records the messages of its turns in pi-ai''s own shape, with a\n`toolResult` role and `toolCall` parts. Sentry''s AI views only render\nthe gen_ai conventions shape, so tool calls and tool results were\nmissing from Flue conversations, and the tool result showed up with an\ninvalid role. This maps the input and output messages to the\nconventions, the way #24352 did for Google GenAI.\n\nThe token counts come from pi-ai too. Its `input` leaves the cached\ntokens out, while `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` includes them by\ndefinition, so input tokens and input cost were too low whenever prompt\ncaching was active (the default for Anthropic models). The finish reason\nis mapped as well (`toolUse` becomes `tool_call`), and the tool span now\nrecords the result the model receives (Flue''s `effectiveResult`) instead\nof the internal `{ content, details }` wrapper.\n\nThe mapper lives in `ai/pi-ai/` because pi-durable sends the same\nshapes, and its integration uses it too.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5d7c3d49476184bd50c5b5abf51b3c41fa3d3d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/trees/d5d7c3d49476184bd50c5b5abf51b3c41fa3d3d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getsentry/sentry-javascript/git/commits/3dae6a50f7dd45d1dccf79b14f468148095e62d4","verification":{"payload":"tree d5d7c3d49476184bd50c5b5abf51b3c41fa3d3d3\nparent 212fd130d629ff54875c485600f1122154407065\nauthor Jan Peer Stöcklmair <jan.peer@sentry.io> 1791273342 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791273342 +0200\n\nfix(server-utils): Map Flue messages and token usage to the gen_ai conventions (#24992)\n\nFlue records the messages of its turns in pi-ai''s own shape, with a\n`toolResult` role and `toolCall` parts. Sentry''s AI views only render\nthe gen_ai conventions shape, so tool calls and tool results were\nmissing from Flue conversations, and the tool result showed up with an\ninvalid role. This maps the input and output messages to the\nconventions, the way #24352 did for Google GenAI.\n\nThe token counts come from pi-ai too. Its `input` leaves the cached\ntokens out, while `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` includes them by\ndefinition, so input tokens and input cost were too low whenever prompt\ncaching was active (the default for Anthropic models). The finish reason\nis mapped as well (`toolUse` becomes `tool_call`), and the tool span now\nrecords the result the model receives (Flue''s `effectiveResult`) instead\nof the internal `{ content, details }` wrapper.\n\nThe mapper lives in `ai/pi-ai/` because pi-durable sends the same\nshapes, and its integration uses it too.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKl+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsHgQABQEg1GwIIk6+teobkp91BDl\nHcSp2wO8zWlUgnephmAzNSdh+MTkI/jOd966ejeoXhCVTjJDI4XOiQpPPSDXTNL0\n+F2+BILAsY/9Y/Ee2gsKARXP/DuFk6S+IssLmhio24XLN7NEjuP9pbPCpR1p4cPA\nDwaoHeykn4dy+pe0xUdIzvg+5QS8KLHio27C0m4CHm34+8h9Zb5PzeFFzoFhkRps\naRGRO5WqIIrKK459h5kySnTtiGZkxF3qmb7Q9gDt6+GUDcP5noD74DTQeitYvMiB\n0+66+p6IrB3mHSPJQMX4YxmGIpCIRXcHKlzt7Hd7DYhjhTagZrBddqfHESGbeLuQ\njeR3SN77aJC/KQb4ZoW0M5M+0q7C6PFipmtiKK9aFTIU7hD2L5OfoHqDYVEAEawT\nB2MUnxdyfTqg2IooXYeS0oxa0dVu2RtZXrCtzRjqkfjpJxSdW0CnQWeR5/jrqzSA\nPOTVwSqNtjQBP6hQ70Qu8Jadz87EpRcgJ8TzvuXpYe8dJxzkt+p+Nl9+Mg7h16Yt\nea17zvhzPexhBvkX8E0dVONLGlyGxyAT5X0G3UchbmQ14lp3yfANwgZL1f75a8hH\nji5noeqHy6QY40aoaPLvJKgxAIlwVU8uE1R76Fsx8AIkCG+W+FmQbCxUHtAZMQ9O\nSmUSZZQcLHI3RRoZpIax\n=rJzT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:55:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://