ADgiC9oAKDkwYmQwZWMzZjM3MGQ3OTVmYjEwMGRlMjNjMTM2NzA2M2ZlZTg3N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/fc68c4406e21146139dec5a49f40eb25fba8b66e","sha":"fc68c4406e21146139dec5a49f40eb25fba8b66e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/fc68c4406e21146139dec5a49f40eb25fba8b66e"}],"sha":"90bd0ec3f370d795fb100de23c1367063fee877d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/90bd0ec3f370d795fb100de23c1367063fee877d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/fc68c4406e21146139dec5a49f40eb25fba8b66e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T20:28:01Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T20:28:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(javascript): print a mangled program once, naming it afterwards (#22504)\n\n* perf(javascript): print a mangled program once, naming it afterwards\n\nThe mangle phase printed the tree twice: once to count the characters\nthe names are chosen from, once for the result. It now prints before\nthe names are chosen, recording where each name and each import or\nexport `as` clause lies, counts the characters off that text and writes\nthe names into it once chosen, moving the source map''s columns with\nthem. The `let` declarations the improve phase left for after naming\nare written before that print, and the count puts back what they\nchanged. A print that wrote a comment, shebang or preamble still counts\nwith a print of its own, as those are not counted.\n\n* test(javascript): fit two minifier tests to #22473 and #22499 together\n\n#22473 counts a conversion as code that may run, so the value\n#22499''s improved case moved past `console` now has effects and\nstays put; it now moves a comparison, which converts nothing. And\n#22499 now shortens #22473''s literal case, whose assertion holds the\noutput to terser''s, so that case runs with the improve phase off.\n\nWith both in, `vercel/ms` is bigger than oxc''s output again (787\nagainst 781 gzip), so it goes back on OXC_SMALLER, where #22499 had\nretired it on its own. And #22502 leaves terser''s\n`side_effects_cascade_3` no bigger than oxc''s, so it comes off.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD","tree":{"sha":"85eeb70a5e2a9e45b22af70422808ffed4cb92b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/85eeb70a5e2a9e45b22af70422808ffed4cb92b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/fc68c4406e21146139dec5a49f40eb25fba8b66e","verification":{"payload":"tree 85eeb70a5e2a9e45b22af70422808ffed4cb92b7\nparent 79aa5dffb43ea288e98ed1ed571db9ec7f6855d5\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791404881 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791404881 +0300\n\nperf(javascript): print a mangled program once, naming it afterwards (#22504)\n\n* perf(javascript): print a mangled program once, naming it afterwards\n\nThe mangle phase printed the tree twice: once to count the characters\nthe names are chosen from, once for the result. It now prints before\nthe names are chosen, recording where each name and each import or\nexport `as` clause lies, counts the characters off that text and writes\nthe names into it once chosen, moving the source map''s columns with\nthem. The `let` declarations the improve phase left for after naming\nare written before that print, and the count puts back what they\nchanged. A print that wrote a comment, shebang or preamble still counts\nwith a print of its own, as those are not counted.\n\n* test(javascript): fit two minifier tests to #22473 and #22499 together\n\n#22473 counts a conversion as code that may run, so the value\n#22499''s improved case moved past `console` now has effects and\nstays put; it now moves a comparison, which converts nothing. And\n#22499 now shortens #22473''s literal case, whose assertion holds the\noutput to terser''s, so that case runs with the improve phase off.\n\nWith both in, `vercel/ms` is bigger than oxc''s output again (787\nagainst 781 gzip), so it goes back on OXC_SMALLER, where #22499 had\nretired it on its own. And #22502 leaves terser''s\n`side_effects_cascade_3` no bigger than oxc''s, so it comes off.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxqtRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU1cQAG6sOIx5EKw/HKq9hTOCLaWJ\nKX7wnkqdCWFOvnzMVJjs2BsRfTGzMSbkwNAkoSifBgabZEnao3NYo1MWkgYvb+4h\n1JjuafiUEUeTi2svoAqZWeNPbglGuvtQEiD//YWTKnuuzu1GMU7F0RhjbiWphLS2\n7s/u5pX+pfLQ1VAZ51k+/f2bZbl19BMV/qIPzENeH3XMpZe1ORIaWf/B9rQfRy+Z\nkx/SF4yzocqI1NYg9GboOogpMaBnoYBeZnDGHdMHyxgUKFRbDAaTyZaoYiBo7eU1\n5g69lPJQXPC0ijeX5W1IJz+HIyB0UDsp7O0S025CBFva2eoAZNIQijj9tONjvUoF\ngkELbL/ij12oOzk1qb/oTFtJwzdEeeHKG8vJWO4JxjdZtZb+EduH0VjdplUDtqAG\nrJatjcuu3B/B3eKHz7/qW4Y7DZja3b/SA