false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/497e6d8297f9de66c468528b9608f7e5bff1229a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:55:07Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:55:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(javascript): let a function''s last `return` of `undefined` fall off its end in the minifier (#22505)\n\n* feat(javascript): let a function''s tail fall off its end in the minifier\n\nA function''s last `return void x` becomes `x`, a sequence ending in\n`void x` loses its `return`, and `return c?y:void 0` becomes\n`if(c)return y`: each returns `undefined` the same way.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* test(javascript): keep the jsMinify module fixture''s return as terser prints it\n\nThe module fixture asserts byte equality with terser; its `return c ? x :\nundefined` is what the improve phase now writes as an `if`, so it returns\n`null` instead and keeps covering comments and maps.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* test(javascript): cover a function''s last `return void` of a call\n\nterser''s own `return` already drops a `void` of what has no effects, so\nthe branch dropping such a `return` was never reached; the remaining one\nis covered with terser''s defaults off, where `return void f()` survives.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an async generator''s tail `return` in the minifier\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* test(javascript): retire an oxc exclusion `main` no longer needs\n\nA change merged into `main` makes `sequences/side_effects_cascade_3` no\nbigger than oxc''s output, and the stale entry fails the corpora check.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD","tree":{"sha":"79bc8276e455cee00c5d9d2316d008d3361ee307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/79bc8276e455cee00c5d9d2316d008d3361ee307"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/497e6d8297f9de66c468528b9608f7e5bff1229a","verification":{"payload":"tree 79bc8276e455cee00c5d9d2316d008d3361ee307\nparent 8c4d1a3432e7a5a19444efef4fede1b9999d938a\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791395707 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791395707 +0300\n\nfeat(javascript): let a function''s last `return` of `undefined` fall off its end in the minifier (#22505)\n\n* feat(javascript): let a function''s tail fall off its end in the minifier\n\nA function''s last `return void x` becomes `x`, a sequence ending in\n`void x` loses its `return`, and `return c?y:void 0` becomes\n`if(c)return y`: each returns `undefined` the same way.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* test(javascript): keep the jsMinify module fixture''s return as terser prints it\n\nThe module fixture asserts byte equality with terser; its `return c ? x :\nundefined` is what the improve phase now writes as an `if`, so it returns\n`null` instead and keeps covering comments and maps.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* test(javascript): cover a function''s last `return void` of a call\n\nterser''s own `return` already drops a `void` of what has no effects, so\nthe branch dropping such a `return` was never reached; the remaining one\nis covered with terser''s defaults off, where `return void f()` survives.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxr