 new array for every list it walked, so each\ncompressor pass copied every list in the tree, about 50 MB a minify of\ntypescript.js. A list nothing replaces now comes back as it is; a deep\ncopy alone still takes lists of its own, the empty ones included, and a\ndeclaration moved into its one use gives the expression made of it its\nown parameters and statements, as the declaration stays until dropped.\n\nAlso retires fixture/issues/11684/class-decl from SWC_SMALLER, stale on\nmain since #22498 and #22506 landed together (the fix #22511 carries).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC","tree":{"sha":"f30d332a6ad59021cd194a9701701f8ea0320cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/f30d332a6ad59021cd194a9701701f8ea0320cd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/683b7a1c9411a00f3762d5603ccb56b403f8ff35","verification":{"payload":"tree f30d332a6ad59021cd194a9701701f8ea0320cd7\nparent 675f2255fb919ea2173a53a0112c2ff8f0d41d9b\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791386299 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791386299 +0300\n\nperf(javascript): hand back a list no transform changes as it is (#22515)\n\nterser''s MAP returned a new array for every list it walked, so each\ncompressor pass copied every list in the tree, about 50 MB a minify of\ntypescript.js. A list nothing replaces now comes back as it is; a deep\ncopy alone still takes lists of its own, the empty ones included, and a\ndeclaration moved into its one use gives the expression made of it its\nown parameters and statements, as the declaration stays until dropped.\n\nAlso retires fixture/issues/11684/class-decl from SWC_SMALLER, stale on\nmain since #22498 and #22506 landed together (the fix #22511 carries).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxmK7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa