Z1v\niR1zS8rc9Graw6V1NVD9G4TRumsbJIP/V9knwqfgQodekK5E3JvJYX3NaYtPyORe\nKPMLEqczGjpQILlQDF78\n=QME4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:18:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/ad1d016bb3a0eb58945aaacd66245a3b51ec5b36","node_id":"C_kwDOADgiC9oAKGFkMWQwMTZiYjNhMGViNTg5NDVhYWFjZDY2MjQ1YTNiNTFlYzViMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/f9524b3b4a33113423e594977c7e436bb35833ea","sha":"f9524b3b4a33113423e594977c7e436bb35833ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/f9524b3b4a33113423e594977c7e436bb35833ea"}],"sha":"ad1d016bb3a0eb58945aaacd66245a3b51ec5b36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/ad1d016bb3a0eb58945aaacd66245a3b51ec5b36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/f9524b3b4a33113423e594977c7e436bb35833ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:18:02Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:18:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(javascript): fix minified code that threw, read the wrong binding or no longer parsed (#22473)\n\n* test(test262): build production unminified as well\n\nSince the minified modes replaced it, production only ran through a\nminimizer, so a failure of webpack''s own production optimizations was\nlisted in MINIFIED_FAILURES as the minimizer''s. An unminified production\nmode tells the two apart.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): accept a parse error only where one is reported or thrown\n\nA negative parse test passed on any thrown value, so a bundle that ran\ninto the test''s unreachable call passed too. It now needs webpack''s parse\nerror or a SyntaxError from the engine. The top-level `return` cases are\nbuilt as CommonJS, so they are listed as a deliberate divergence.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a switch whose case test reads a binding declared in its body\n\nA case test is evaluated in the switch''s block, so the rewrites to `if` and\nto a block moved it out of the scope of a `let`, `const` or `class` its body\ndeclares: `case (f = () => x, 1): let x = 2` became `if (1 == (f = () => x,\n1)) { let x = 2 }`, where `x` is no longer declared. The correction leaves\nsuch a switch as written, as oxc does.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): minify a function body that declares `arguments` with `let`\n\nThe minifier declares a function''s own `arguments` as a parameter, so a\n`let` or `const arguments` in the body read as a redeclaration and failed\nthe build, as terser''s check does. Under the parameter scopes the correct\nphase turns on, such a declaration shadows the function''s own instead; a\nparameter written `arguments` beside it the parser still refuses. 12\ntest262 cases leave the printer''s list.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a spread, a throwing accessor and a strict empty body the minifier dropped\n\nAn unused `[...it]` or a pure call''s `...it` dropped to `it`, skipping the\niteration a generator observes. A read of `arguments.callee`, or of a\nfunction''s `caller` or `arguments`, and a write to one, dropped where strict\ncode throws. An empty function''s `\"use strict\"` went, so its `caller` no\nlonger threw.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a BigInt operation that throws the minifier dropped\n\nAn unused `1n + 1`, `1n / 0n`, `2n ** -1n`, `5n >>> 1n` or `Symbol() + 0n`\nwent, and with it the TypeError or RangeError it throws. The check reads only\na BigInt literal, a wrapped one or a `Symbol()` call, so an operation on\nneither costs nothing more.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a `for` head''s `let` in the loop when dropping an unused name beside it\n\nDropping `n` from `for (let i = 0, n = f(); ...)` kept `f()` as a\nstatement, which moved `let i` before the loop: closures reading `i` shared\none binding, and two such loops redeclared `i`, a SyntaxError. The unused\nname now stays in the head, carrying its initializer''s effects, as oxc does.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an async generator''s `return undefined`, which awaits\n\n`return undefined` or `return void 0` in an async generator awaits the\nvalue, a tick a bare `return` does not take; the minifier wrote it as a\nbare `return`, or dropped it, changing when the generator settles.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an unused class whose heritage is no constructor\n\n`class extends (() => {})` or `class extends 1` throws a TypeError as it is\ndefined; the minifier dropped such a class nobody read.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an array element''s position when dropping an unused update in it\n\n`[--b, f(), g()][1]` with `b` read nowhere else lost its first element,\nso the index read `g()` where it read `f()`; terser''s fuzzer found it. The\ndropped update now leaves a `0` in its place outside a sequence.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a static member computed as `prototype` computed\n\n`static [\"prototype\"]() {}` throws a TypeError as the class is defined;\nthe minifier wrote it as `static prototype() {}`, an early error that\nstops the whole script from parsing, and dropped an unused class declaring\none, or extending a local async or generator function.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): list as terser''s alone the cases the printer now runs right\n\nThe spreads, `arguments.callee`, function `caller`, BigInt, class\nheritage and static `prototype` cases, the `for` and `switch` scopes and the\nasync generator''s `return undefined` pass with webpack''s printer, so each\nmoves from the groups both minifiers fail to terser''s own.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): name a catch parameter after the function around it in a switch''s discriminant\n\nA switch''s block scope opens before the function scopes of its\ndiscriminant, so counting the scopes opened placed a catch parameter\nthere before its function in the mangler''s walk: the parameter took the\nname an outer variable it reads got next, or kept the name of the `var`\nit redeclares while that `var`''s reads were renamed. Each catch parameter\nis now named where the walk meets its own scope; terser''s fuzzer found it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* docs(changeset): fold the printer fixes into one entry\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): drop an empty strict function''s directive where it is called in place\n\nNothing reads `caller` of a function called where it is written, so its\nlone `\"use strict\"` goes as terser drops it, and the empty call with it, as\noxc writes. The corpora list oxc dropping a class extending a regular\nexpression, which throws as it is defined, and no longer list terser\nrefusing `let arguments`: the uncorrected printer refuses it too.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test: keep a spread class key out of the case terser writes alike\n\nSpreading a non-iterable throws, which the printer now keeps.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* fix(javascript): keep the conversions, reads and writes oxc keeps that terser assumes away\n\nAs oxc reads them, an operation converting a side that may be an object or\na symbol (`o + 1`, `x - 1`, `-x`, `${o}`), an object spreading what may hold\ngetters, a write to a key that converts or to a primitive''s property, a\n`let` read before its declaration, a getter on an object handed to\n`Object.defineProperty`, a write to a `const` or a class expression''s own\nname, `this` before `super()`, a class extending itself, a name read in a\n`with`, and a block''s async or generator function read outside it all run\nor throw. Each is kept where terser dropped it or moved it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): list as terser''s alone the conversions, spreads and TDZ reads the printer now keeps\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): reduce the conversions and spreads kept to what oxc keeps\n\nWhere oxc proves a conversion or a spread runs no code, drop it: a literal\nconverting with the builtins, a `Math` or `Number` constant, a function''s\nown `arguments` spread, a spread string, function or setter. Where it may\nrun code, keep only that part: a template''s or concatenation''s conversions\n(`a${b}c` as `${b}`, `\"a\" + b` as `\"\" + b`) and an object''s spreads. Also\nkeep a concatenation''s conversion where only its truth is read, and merge\nan async generator''s returns wherever that adds or drops no awaited value.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): read a literal as gaining a getter only where it escapes itself\n\nterser counts a property read off a literal and stored as the literal\nescaping, so `var push = array.push` kept every unused `array.slice`.\nTrack the literal''s own escape apart. List what swc still writes shorter\nby dropping conversions oxc keeps, and what oxc drops in a `with` body.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a class whose static key may name `prototype`, and a block''s async function in its block\n\nA static member whose computed key a variable may hold as `\"prototype\"`\nthrows as the class is defined, so the class is kept unless the key is\nknown to be something else. Folding a `switch` no longer writes a block''s\nasync or generator function as a `var`, which only a plain function is.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(minify): list the classes oxc drops though a static key may name `prototype`\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* refactor(javascript): read a static key of no known value in `definesStaticPrototype`\n\nThe check `main` added for a static `prototype` key now also takes a\ncomputed key of no known value as one, unless a number or a well-known\nsymbol, so the class heritage check no longer repeats it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test: list as terser''s alone the test262 cases webpack''s printer now passes\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a read of a lexical binding that may run before its declaration\n\n`{ x; let x; }`, a `typeof x` before `let x`, a closure read in a `for-of`\nhead of the loop''s own binding, and a closure called before its `let` all\nthrow a ReferenceError, which dropping the unused read lost.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* feat(javascript): add `pure_conversions` and keep private names under `keep_fnames`\n\n`compress.pure_conversions`, on by default as terser assumes, can be\nturned off to keep a comparison or a computed key converting what may be\nan object or a symbol, whose `valueOf`, `toString` or throw then still\nruns. `keep_fnames: true` now also keeps private names, which a private\nmethod''s `name` reads.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* feat(javascript): add `pure_heritage`, and keep the name a literal gives a class\n\n`compress.pure_heritage`, on by default as terser assumes, can be turned\noff to keep a class nobody reads where it extends what may be no\nconstructor. Under `keep_classnames` or `keep_fnames`, `{ default: class\n{} }.default`, which names the class `default`, is no longer flattened\ninto the bare class.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): run the printer with its assumptions off, and keep names in both minified modes\n\ntest262 reads functions'' and classes'' `name`, converts objects whose\nconversions throw, and extends what is no constructor, all on purpose.\nBoth minified modes now keep names, and the printer runs with\n`pure_conversions` and `pure_heritage` off, so 194 of its 195 listed\nfailures pass and leave the list; terser''s name cases leave it too.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* docs(changeset): name the options the printer fixes add\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep `pure_conversions` and `pure_heritage` on under `defaults: false`\n\nBoth name assumptions terser makes whatever its other options are, not passes to turn off with the rest.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): share the options terser supports between both minified modes\n\nBoth modes keep names and turn `pure_getters` off, each commented with\nwhat test262 does on purpose; the printer adds only its own switches.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): drop the 30 cases terser passes with `pure_getters` off\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): never quote a kept private name\n\nterser prints a private member''s name as a property''s, quoting one it does\nnot take for an identifier, so a kept non-ASCII name printed as `#\"ࢶ\"`, a\nSyntaxError. The correct phase prints it as a name, as `this.#x` already is.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(javascript): retire an swc size entry the minifier no longer needs\n\nDropping an empty constructor and the `new` arguments nothing reads now\nwrites `fixture/issues/11684/class-decl` as small as swc does.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b","tree":{"sha":"e76ddf830574c0a99da6d0f1e2a8fed50c554926","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/e76ddf830574c0a99da6d0f1e2a8fed50c554926"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/f9524b3b4a33113423e594977c7e436bb35833ea","verification":{"payload":"tree e76ddf830574c0a99da6d0f1e2a8fed50c554926\nparent 86d31e06c4e3ed3c63596ee313549d16d9e76600\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791382682 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791382682 +0300\n\nfix(javascript): fix minified code that threw, read the wrong binding or no longer parsed (#22473)\n\n* test(test262): build production unminified as well\n\nSince the minified modes replaced it, production only ran through a\nminimizer, so a failure of webpack''s own production optimizations was\nlisted in MINIFIED_FAILURES as the minimizer''s. An unminified production\nmode tells the two apart.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): accept a parse error only where one is reported or thrown\n\nA negative parse test passed on any thrown value, so a bundle that ran\ninto the test''s unreachable call passed too. It now needs webpack''s parse\nerror or a SyntaxError from the engine. The top-level `return` cases are\nbuilt as CommonJS, so they are listed as a deliberate divergence.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a switch whose case test reads a binding declared in its body\n\nA case test is evaluated in the switch''s block, so the rewrites to `if` and\nto a block moved it out of the scope of a `let`, `const` or `class` its body\ndeclares: `case (f = () => x, 1): let x = 2` became `if (1 == (f = () => x,\n1)) { let x = 2 }`, where `x` is no longer declared. The correction leaves\nsuch a switch as written, as oxc does.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): minify a function body that declares `arguments` with `let`\n\nThe minifier declares a function''s own `arguments` as a parameter, so a\n`let` or `const arguments` in the body read as a redeclaration and failed\nthe build, as terser''s check does. Under the parameter scopes the correct\nphase turns on, such a declaration shadows the function''s own instead; a\nparameter written `arguments` beside it the parser still refuses. 12\ntest262 cases leave the printer''s list.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a spread, a throwing accessor and a strict empty body the minifier dropped\n\nAn unused `[...it]` or a pure call''s `...it` dropped to `it`, skipping the\niteration a generator observes. A read of `arguments.callee`, or of a\nfunction''s `caller` or `arguments`, and a write to one, dropped where strict\ncode throws. An empty function''s `\"use strict\"` went, so its `caller` no\nlonger threw.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a BigInt operation that throws the minifier dropped\n\nAn unused `1n + 1`, `1n / 0n`, `2n ** -1n`, `5n >>> 1n` or `Symbol() + 0n`\nwent, and with it the TypeError or RangeError it throws. The check reads only\na BigInt literal, a wrapped one or a `Symbol()` call, so an operation on\nneither costs nothing more.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a `for` head''s `let` in the loop when dropping an unused name beside it\n\nDropping `n` from `for (let i = 0, n = f(); ...)` kept `f()` as a\nstatement, which moved `let i` before the loop: closures reading `i` shared\none binding, and two such loops redeclared `i`, a SyntaxError. The unused\nname now stays in the head, carrying its initializer''s effects, as oxc does.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an async generator''s `return undefined`, which awaits\n\n`return undefined` or `return void 0` in an async generator awaits the\nvalue, a tick a bare `return` does not take; the minifier wrote it as a\nbare `return`, or dropped it, changing when the generator settles.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an unused class whose heritage is no constructor\n\n`class extends (() => {})` or `class extends 1` throws a TypeError as it is\ndefined; the minifier dropped such a class nobody read.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep an array element''s position when dropping an unused update in it\n\n`[--b, f(), g()][1]` with `b` read nowhere else lost its first element,\nso the index read `g()` where it read `f()`; terser''s fuzzer found it. The\ndropped update now leaves a `0` in its place outside a sequence.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a static member computed as `prototype` computed\n\n`static [\"prototype\"]() {}` throws a TypeError as the class is defined;\nthe minifier wrote it as `static prototype() {}`, an early error that\nstops the whole script from parsing, and dropped an unused class declaring\none, or extending a local async or generator function.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): list as terser''s alone the cases the printer now runs right\n\nThe spreads, `arguments.callee`, function `caller`, BigInt, class\nheritage and static `prototype` cases, the `for` and `switch` scopes and the\nasync generator''s `return undefined` pass with webpack''s printer, so each\nmoves from the groups both minifiers fail to terser''s own.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): name a catch parameter after the function around it in a switch''s discriminant\n\nA switch''s block scope opens before the function scopes of its\ndiscriminant, so counting the scopes opened placed a catch parameter\nthere before its function in the mangler''s walk: the parameter took the\nname an outer variable it reads got next, or kept the name of the `var`\nit redeclares while that `var`''s reads were renamed. Each catch parameter\nis now named where the walk meets its own scope; terser''s fuzzer found it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* docs(changeset): fold the printer fixes into one entry\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): drop an empty strict function''s directive where it is called in place\n\nNothing reads `caller` of a function called where it is written, so its\nlone `\"use strict\"` goes as terser drops it, and the empty call with it, as\noxc writes. The corpora list oxc dropping a class extending a regular\nexpression, which throws as it is defined, and no longer list terser\nrefusing `let arguments`: the uncorrected printer refuses it too.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test: keep a spread class key out of the case terser writes alike\n\nSpreading a non-iterable throws, which the printer now keeps.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* fix(javascript): keep the conversions, reads and writes oxc keeps that terser assumes away\n\nAs oxc reads them, an operation converting a side that may be an object or\na symbol (`o + 1`, `x - 1`, `-x`, `${o}`), an object spreading what may hold\ngetters, a write to a key that converts or to a primitive''s property, a\n`let` read before its declaration, a getter on an object handed to\n`Object.defineProperty`, a write to a `const` or a class expression''s own\nname, `this` before `super()`, a class extending itself, a name read in a\n`with`, and a block''s async or generator function read outside it all run\nor throw. Each is kept where terser dropped it or moved it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): list as terser''s alone the conversions, spreads and TDZ reads the printer now keeps\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): reduce the conversions and spreads kept to what oxc keeps\n\nWhere oxc proves a conversion or a spread runs no code, drop it: a literal\nconverting with the builtins, a `Math` or `Number` constant, a function''s\nown `arguments` spread, a spread string, function or setter. Where it may\nrun code, keep only that part: a template''s or concatenation''s conversions\n(`a${b}c` as `${b}`, `\"a\" + b` as `\"\" + b`) and an object''s spreads. Also\nkeep a concatenation''s conversion where only its truth is read, and merge\nan async generator''s returns wherever that adds or drops no awaited value.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): read a literal as gaining a getter only where it escapes itself\n\nterser counts a property read off a literal and stored as the literal\nescaping, so `var push = array.push` kept every unused `array.slice`.\nTrack the literal''s own escape apart. List what swc still writes shorter\nby dropping conversions oxc keeps, and what oxc drops in a `with` body.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a class whose static key may name `prototype`, and a block''s async function in its block\n\nA static member whose computed key a variable may hold as `\"prototype\"`\nthrows as the class is defined, so the class is kept unless the key is\nknown to be something else. Folding a `switch` no longer writes a block''s\nasync or generator function as a `var`, which only a plain function is.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(minify): list the classes oxc drops though a static key may name `prototype`\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* refactor(javascript): read a static key of no known value in `definesStaticPrototype`\n\nThe check `main` added for a static `prototype` key now also takes a\ncomputed key of no known value as one, unless a number or a well-known\nsymbol, so the class heritage check no longer repeats it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test: list as terser''s alone the test262 cases webpack''s printer now passes\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ViD41i2KdwwGxrDk7yrjeD\n\n* fix(javascript): keep a read of a lexical binding that may run before its declaration\n\n`{ x; let x; }`, a `typeof x` before `let x`, a closure read in a `for-of`\nhead of the loop''s own binding, and a closure called before its `let` all\nthrow a ReferenceError, which dropping the unused read lost.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* feat(javascript): add `pure_conversions` and keep private names under `keep_fnames`\n\n`compress.pure_conversions`, on by default as terser assumes, can be\nturned off to keep a comparison or a computed key converting what may be\nan object or a symbol, whose `valueOf`, `toString` or throw then still\nruns. `keep_fnames: true` now also keeps private names, which a private\nmethod''s `name` reads.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* feat(javascript): add `pure_heritage`, and keep the name a literal gives a class\n\n`compress.pure_heritage`, on by default as terser assumes, can be turned\noff to keep a class nobody reads where it extends what may be no\nconstructor. Under `keep_classnames` or `keep_fnames`, `{ default: class\n{} }.default`, which names the class `default`, is no longer flattened\ninto the bare class.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): run the printer with its assumptions off, and keep names in both minified modes\n\ntest262 reads functions'' and classes'' `name`, converts objects whose\nconversions throw, and extends what is no constructor, all on purpose.\nBoth minified modes now keep names, and the printer runs with\n`pure_conversions` and `pure_heritage` off, so 194 of its 195 listed\nfailures pass and leave the list; terser''s name cases leave it too.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* docs(changeset): name the options the printer fixes add\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): keep `pure_conversions` and `pure_heritage` on under `defaults: false`\n\nBoth name assumptions terser makes whatever its other options are, not passes to turn off with the rest.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): share the options terser supports between both minified modes\n\nBoth modes keep names and turn `pure_getters` off, each commented with\nwhat test262 does on purpose; the printer adds only its own switches.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(test262): drop the 30 cases terser passes with `pure_getters` off\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* fix(javascript): never quote a kept private name\n\nterser prints a private member''s name as a property''s, quoting one it does\nnot take for an identifier, so a kept non-ASCII name printed as `#\"ࢶ\"`, a\nSyntaxError. The correct phase prints it as a name, as `this.#x` already is.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b\n\n* test(javascript): retire an swc size entry the minifier no longer needs\n\nDropping an empty constructor and the `new` arguments nothing reads now\nwrites `fixture/issues/11684/class-decl` as small as swc does.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cRZoHW2M4sCbrLFgrAc6b","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxlSaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp+wQAJaFjkLljaSBLwO+GrcdDst9\nWlvstvAHaq2pNY8mrvEYV/R5NpddkRC2hVfpefWE12T+Dxegp06WO6g8fTDkEiKJ\nLxOzrd/puEl+q1aOS5OumqqdNefqxv78P1bpTrSpPO24Iqdt2w0VTwrN6Y4vUDH9\njzOoChiNNKBUDUbFnK+VPVw8Rwfs1ujFR62kCqZt3t7cIf8hp3SJoaid7fqWtGj2\nga5j6SUQnwFla5IbdanxBx78+38J+YN7T23duNsWPVK5aSIhT2YYhqW1uHBBJzA0\nu7wvE2H9mOWhFrU20t2JWMjamuYUj/t58UsRRLj6zoIRbzBXUlwv4+AeDatXjHWw\nE3X5p3r4qESNgBIDFhrDS3ZI9HdmXfodjRJiAjwS8qWmdLm5EhR8r9w4fMAHTmUY\nU9k82LdUKtbsI/i/vq9GHa/7BN4ERM6t3z+iZvn8L4XBBaWMh7zJbvuECHNN4tAZ\naGIKj4BjjsZ6/0UJFmWDlgdqM8Pr55x4OMCdA/QRDGfThRXlBgGHFZdnwI5YlP4e\nsEc4ii2dNjsaNSREuNh2AXtXkJK7eijjfxK0IbVXJl8Ta2xORC3dI3BCow4xWj9J\n5cj84MjHYU6Wl0u9zkWcfok3nOlwjpc/OfOnbXYk4teFD0suRkySm9eiwxpk9K8W\noTYUdDuw/MmRfKdLCtI1\n=c0E7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:18:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/or