e313549d16d9e76600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/86d31e06c4e3ed3c63596ee313549d16d9e76600"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/fdc01cdc064b0357768cc0f610d57ae75bc2d367/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:39:10Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:39:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add working-style section to AGENTS.md (#22501)\n\n* docs: add working-style section to AGENTS.md\n\nFold the four Karpathy-inspired guidelines (think before coding, simplicity first, surgical changes, goal-driven execution) into the agent guide, linking to existing rules instead of restating them, and add the two names to the spellcheck word list.\n\n* docs: drop attribution from working-style section\n\nKeep the guidelines unattributed, restore the two items the first cut left out, and remove the spellcheck words only the names needed.\n\n* docs: say when dead code is removed\n\nUnused code that isn''t public API goes; when its use or purpose is unclear, ask.\n\n* docs: add answer-plainly habit\n\nFewest words that keep the meaning; before/after code blocks and tables over prose.\n\n* docs: let measured CPU or memory wins override simplicity\n\nLonger hot-path code that measurably saves CPU or memory beats shorter code, within reason.\n\n* docs: word the performance-over-size rule as a weighing, not a limit\n\n* docs: spell out abbreviations on first use\n\n* docs: tighten the working-style habits\n\nAsk only when readings diverge, report what was not verified, cite code as path:line, link before/after to the PR body rule, and say that a fresh checkout needs yarn install first.\n\n* chore: add SessionStart hook that installs dependencies in cloud sessions\n\nRuns yarn --frozen-lockfile through tooling/retry.js when CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE is set, so lint and tests work without a manual install.\n\n* docs: restore the working-style intro wording\n\n* docs: word the install note for any agent\n\n* docs: drop the spellcheck words the removed names needed","tree":{"sha":"b71fc07648279ad92df064a2ac8d0af284c65702","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/b71fc07648279ad92df064a2ac8d0af284c65702"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/fdc01cdc064b0357768cc0f610d57ae75bc2d367","verification":{"payload":"tree b71fc07648279ad92df064a2ac8d0af284c65702\nparent 9e17070bb00a21842abfb386cffe80956812054f\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791365950 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791365950 +0300\n\ndocs: add working-style section to AGENTS.md (#22501)\n\n* docs: add working-style section to AGENTS.md\n\nFold the four Karpathy-inspired guidelines (think before coding, simplicity first, surgical changes, goal-driven execution) into the agent guide, linking to existing rules instead of restating them, and add the two names to the spellcheck word list.\n\n* docs: drop attribution from working-style section\n\nKeep the guidelines unattributed, restore the two items the first cut left out, and remove the spellcheck words only the names needed.\n\n* docs: say when dead code is removed\n\nUnused code that isn''t public API goes; when its use or purpose is unclear, ask.\n\n* docs: add answer-plainly habit\n\nFewest words that keep the meaning; before/after code blocks and tables over prose.\n\n* docs: let measured CPU or memory wins override simplicity\n\nLonger hot-path code that measurably saves CPU or memory beats shorter code, within reason.\n\n* docs: word the performance-over-size rule as a weighing, not a limit\n\n* docs: spell out abbreviations on first use\n\n* docs: tighten the working-style habits\n\nAsk only when readings diverge, report what was not verified, cite code as path:line, link before/after to the PR body rule, and say that a fresh checkout needs yarn install first.\n\n* chore: add SessionStart hook that installs dependencies in cloud sessions\n\nRuns yarn --frozen-lockfile through tooling/retry.js when CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE is set, so lint and tests work without a manual install.\n\n* docs: restore the working-style intro wording\n\n* docs: word the install note for any agent\n\n* docs: drop the spellcheck words the removed names needed","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhM+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjHQQABagsNxCgI373yXzC2+0Lfx9\nbC0dL5ucvoF/Snxhru+k4luFNsmIz1AAEleJ7BfMhJQ0E3A1VxzTzDzHKi0ppkcI\nEHwJSKIVJkbayTiDXZ2NieQHZFt7hhI+x/Jj9r6n8xMOdOrKLyfi0GuspjmN/JEC\nupEwl5DXMy2wK3kY8UiMYfPRgTDTGQTDw5jQ8bdJlhMS2mYqeI1PwDcgYhBRFUwa\ncgBXlmy2xLf1gdoSeB31DINGwi4kiTzHwEGOK7aSKK4r5Chz+ywmVRXINkjGY8Zq\nTiQXWKi2hMOmvRBRO9OkoM9xVi3d9XsBVqBGTmWtGmuZIT1rvt6hkoHWep43LWrj\n4MvdbFIs37RxR+jxPQSgfhSqO5dg20Y7nNTupcafEFTdjC6UH8mNeriPjjkKTwIu\n8KfStlk02OF1Pm42bp7zvYOEv7BX5XXDawFBl6ET6Dcj