vents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/7704a13d5a22dc758058b4cd862e28557eb52d60","node_id":"C_kwDOADgiC9oAKDc3MDRhMTNkNWEyMmRjNzU4MDU4YjRjZDg2MmUyODU1N2ViNTJkNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b","sha":"25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b"}],"sha":"7704a13d5a22dc758058b4cd862e28557eb52d60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/7704a13d5a22dc758058b4cd862e28557eb52d60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:54Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: move build-driven unit tests to integration and watch cases (#22460)\n\n* test: parse through the javascript syntax parser directly\n\nSpec and unit tests that only need an AST call `parse` from\n`lib/javascript/syntax` instead of `JavascriptParser._parse`; only the\nauto source type fallback tests, which cover `_parse` itself, keep it.\n\n* test(html): move HtmlParser unit tests to integration, watch and syntax tests\n\nBehaviour a build reaches is now asserted on real output in configCases/html\nand a watch case for the template''s dependencies; the JavaScript MIME list\nand empty url() handling move to HtmlSyntax. Only the Buffer source, which no\nbuild produces, stays a HtmlParser unit test.\n\n* test(html): drop the HtmlParser unit test file\n\nIts last case fed the parser a Buffer, which no build produces.\n\n* test: move rebuild and cache unit tests to watch and config cases\n\nCompiler-caching, ChangesAndRemovals, WatcherEvents and the HMR compilation\ntests become watch cases; the cache item types and embedded-source renderer\nchecks become config and watch cases. Only the devtool switch across two\ncompilers on one disk cache stays a unit test.\n\n* test: run persistent cache codegen checks as restart watch cases\n\nA watch case whose test.config sets restartCompiler closes the compiler after\neach step and starts a fresh one, so every step restores the pack from disk.\nThe PersistentCaching codegen tests become such cases; the cache housekeeping\ntests stay unit tests.\n\n* test: move BannerPlugin and MultiCompiler watch tests to cases\n\nBannerPlugin''s footer and stage checks become a config case and its asset\ncaching a watch case; MultiCompiler''s parallelism and dependency ordering in\nwatch mode becomes a watch case. prepareOptions now keeps an array config''s\nparallelism, which the case needs.\n\n* test: move Errors unit tests to integration cases\n\n* test: narrow cache option types in the new cache cases\n\n* test: move Stats, MultiStats, NodeTemplatePlugin and Compiler build tests to cases\n\n* test: move copy, context, dll cache, source release and progress tests to cases\n\n* test: replace mocked plugin unit tests with integration cases\n\n* test(html): keep the empty style fixtures clear of minifier neighbours\n\nThe html invariants minify every fixture twice; an empty style between two\nothers or between paragraphs changed the second pass.\n\n* test: skip two watch cases cacheUnaffected cannot run\n\nOne needs optimization.usedExports, which cacheUnaffected refuses; the other\nchanges the renderer between steps, which it assumes never happens.","tree":{"sha":"1f9e7aa5b18f0a29c222b4398efc0e22bd17cf02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/1f9e7aa5b18f0a29c222b4398efc0e22bd17cf02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f9e7aa5b18f0a29c222b4398efc0e22bd17cf02\nparent 307c7013e73f9ed23a1c3fe076011f141ddcd873\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791319434 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319434 +0300\n\ntest: move build-driven unit tests to integration and watch cases (#22460)\n\n* test: parse through the javascript syntax parser directly\n\nSpec and unit tests that only need an AST call `parse` from\n`lib/javascript/syntax` instead of `JavascriptParser._parse`; only the\nauto source type fallback tests, which cover `_parse` itself, keep it.\n\n* test(html): move HtmlParser unit tests to integration, watch and syntax tests\n\nBehaviour a build reaches is now asserted on real output in configCases/html\nand a watch case for the template''s dependencies; the JavaScript MIME list\nand empty url() handling move to HtmlSyntax. Only the Buffer source, which no\nbuild produces, stays a HtmlParser unit test.\n\n* test(html): drop the HtmlParser unit test file\n\nIts last case fed the parser a Buffer, which no build produces.\n\n* test: move rebuild and cache unit tests to watch and config cases\n\nCompiler-caching, ChangesAndRemovals, WatcherEvents and the HMR compilation\ntests become watch cases; the cache item types and embedded-source renderer\nchecks become config and watch cases. Only the devtool switch across two\ncompilers on one disk cache stays a unit test.\n\n* test: run persistent cache codegen checks as restart watch cases\n\nA watch case whose test.config sets restartCompiler closes the compiler after\neach step and starts a fresh one, so every step restores the pack from disk.\nThe PersistentCaching codegen tests become such cases; the cache housekeeping\ntests stay unit tests.\n\n* test: move BannerPlugin and MultiCompiler watch tests to cases\n\nBannerPlugin''s footer and stage checks become a config case and its asset\ncaching a watch case; MultiCompiler''s parallelism and dependency ordering in\nwatch mode becomes a watch case. prepareOptions now keeps an array config''s\nparallelism, which the case needs.\n\n* test: move Errors unit tests to integration cases\n\n* test: narrow cache option types in the new cache cases\n\n* test: move Stats, MultiStats, NodeTemplatePlugin and Compiler build tests to cases\n\n* test: move copy, context, dll cache, source release and progress tests to cases\n\n* test: replace mocked plugin unit tests with integration cases\n\n* test(html): keep the empty style fixtures clear of minifier neighbours\n\nThe html invariants minify every fixture twice; an empty style between two\nothers or between paragraphs changed the second pass.\n\n* test: skip two watch cases cacheUnaffected cannot run\n\nOne needs optimization.usedExports, which cacheUnaffected refuses; the other\nchanges the renderer between steps, which it assumes never happens.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxV2KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALg8QAEPgjbLkbc5DPivERs3FYake\nydc5KulEbWxGSQgZdqc+TgB2vMhNm2cHO350ROOSIi/CwtVF/3+KZowZxrS9mzS+\nbdPwvMfO5L8/ou2yJ3loXzDGER3d8D7IwsBoR0im7KD92/w51uV4/CM43hWaso69\nAdJX8M7z2UHyTxWQiAFn87JUuZkfzae4i5C6wJH16vakOUUTL6WNqaWkqFroi9EA\nEjwAQv4EiSaY9BH2vuGKSAKxCz8PQsG5JMqbkFYOCs0Hk7JBxbHYz9zG9eLwKSId\nmGln5dKB3GMD1Qzn550kevDetSK4wcHQTm45WGaDxjC/XUrjetq0Uc3O+z8iJtbD\neKsB0UPB0SU6KTdojvY18dcZN68ycecNFy7p6//c2Adss7JeEP2vwLQSxTgGoqXu\nMeTJ6ei0AcAe6jxl7Aq6XA5/0g9NKmxs15N65d52+WaGzsuRQSrikrJh/ghergN1\nBzs0D24z1wLHUhIO8BbpbIGnP/r1dhLjRfaKaBXpYRR3X+uVoOlXr8jx0C70QOt7\nKKFv1gn0QY4yq2ClmcRjYjMgH1GLS6jotninZBd5HhpX5b8WFuZMcg1eIkzegRXU\n0DPB/6Dh7jLUaQDpf5BBhO90L/zc1EZ4Ojj8/L76V21iql12PW8FiRCLh8bo0tWi\nThkjlCKkzEfisnINmug0\n=jOq/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:43:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b","node_id":"C_kwDOADgiC9oAKDI1Y2ExZjUwNWE1NzZmYmFkMzQwZDg0NjAyNGZhOTQzYTZhY2JhMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/307c7013e73f9ed23a1c3fe076011f141ddcd873","sha":"307c7013e73f9ed23a1c3fe076011f141ddcd873","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/307c7013e73f9ed23a1c3fe076011f141ddcd873"}],"sha":"25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/25ca1f505a576fbad340d846024fa943a6acba2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/307c7013e73f9ed23a1c3fe076011f141ddcd873/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:41:52Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:41:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(css): fix minifier cases a wider stylesheet corpus found (#22467)\n\n* fix(css): fix minifier cases a wider stylesheet corpus found\n\nWiden the comparison corpus with 43 open-source stylesheets fetched by\n`npm pack` and checked by integrity, and fix what they found: joined\nat-rule spans, longhands joined across two rules, animation initials,\nvar() in family merges, percentage channels near a byte''s half, the space\nafter var() in custom properties, and the order of prefixed copies.\n\n* fix(css): keep a near-half percentage''s digits only in an rgb() channel\n\n* fix(css): keep the digits a scaled length lands on whole pixels with\n\nRound a length the engine scales by a font size or viewport to nine\nsignificant digits rather than six. Such a value is often a ratio written\nto land on whole pixels (NHS.UK''s 2/19em at 19px), which Chromium stores\nas a float and floors to 1/64px: `.105263em` there computes 1.98438px and\na 1px outline where `0.1052631579em` computes 2px. Nine digits round-trip\na float.\n\nDrop an `@-moz-document` block a later copy of its rule leaves empty, and\nlet the equivalence harness walk Gecko''s `@-moz-document` rules as it\nwalks `@supports`, rather than compare their text.\n\n* fix(css): read an escaped rgb() name before keeping a channel''s digits\n\nA percentage channel a hair off a byte''s half kept its digits only under\n`rgb`/`rgba` spelled plainly; `r\\67 b(...)` names the same function, so\nread the name unescaped. Run the corpus fetch''s `npm pack` through a shell\non Windows, where `npm` is a `.cmd`, with the tarball landing in `cwd` so\nno path is passed through it unquoted.","tree":{"sha":"ece7e95c47f053436cbe178757ee3905f49da4b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/ece7e95c47f053436cbe178757ee3905f49da4b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/307c7013e73f9ed23a1c3fe076011f141ddcd873","verification":{"payload":"tree ece7e95c47f053436cbe178757ee3905f49da4b2\nparent 6423418db3090d170de7d3907f5a7e257a2cc13a\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791319312 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319312 +0300\n\nfix(css): fix minifier cases a wider stylesheet corpus found (#22467)\n\n* fix(css): fix minifier cases a wider stylesheet corpus found\n\nWiden the comparison corpus with 43 open-source stylesheets fetched by\n`npm pack` and checked by integrity, and fix what they found: joined\nat-rule spans, longhands joined across two rules, animation initials,\nvar() in family merges, percentage channels near a byte''s half, the space\nafter var() in custom properties, and the order of prefixed copies.\n\n* fix(css): keep a near-half percentage''s digits only in an rgb() channel\n\n* fix(css): keep the digits a scaled length lands on whole pixels with\n\nRound a length the engine scales by a font size or viewport to nine\nsignificant digits rather than six. Such a value is often a ratio written\nto land on whole pixels (NHS.UK''s 2/19em at 19px), which Chromium stores\nas a float and floors to 1/64px: `.105263em` there computes 1.98438px and\na 1px outline where `0.1052631579em` computes 2px. Nine digits round-trip\na float.\n\nDrop an `@-moz-document` block a later copy of its rule leaves empty, and\nlet the equivalence harness walk Gecko''s `@-moz-document` rules as it\nwalks `@supports`, rather than compare their text.\n\n* fix(css): read an escaped rgb() name before keeping a channel''s digits\n\nA percentage channel a hair off a byte''s half kept its digits only under\n`rgb`/`rgba` spelled plainly; `r\\67 b(...)` names the same function, so\nread the name unescaped. Run the corpus fetch''s `npm pack` through a shell\non Windows, where `npm` is a `.cmd`, with the tarball landing in `cwd` so\nno path is passed through it unquoted.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxV0QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbIQQAHoRwiEUQyjsX0tvWrKrgDGQ\nRS43Ye+tOZnrDXXT3PZ1qVydZHWTG