.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/9f94bf3624d237577737ccb0123c12a12fd3253b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:22:39Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:22:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(css): fold longhands into their shorthand, and shorten flex and basic shapes (#22442)\n\n* feat(css): fold longhands into their shorthand, and shorten flex and basic shapes\n\nThree rewrites lightningcss makes and webpack did not, each checked against\nthe computed style Chromium reads back:\n\n- A longhand right after its own shorthand folds into it: the order-free\n  families (`border-top`, `outline`, `column-rule`, `text-emphasis`,\n  `flex-flow`, `text-decoration` where the target reads every slot), `flex`,\n  and a one-layer `transition` or `animation`. `text-wrap` stays out, read as\n  one keyword before it had longhands, and so does IE10''s `-ms-flex`.\n- `flex` in fewer than three components reads as its three factors, so\n  `1 auto` is `auto` and `1 1` is `1`.\n- A basic shape drops its defaults: a `closest-side` radius, a zero `round`,\n  `nonzero`, and the sides `inset()` repeats. Not the `at` position, which\n  engines read back as written.\n\nThe `animation` keyword slots come from the generator, out of mdn-data.\n\nWriting four border sides as `border-width`/`-style`/`-color` saved raw bytes\nbut cost gzip on every stylesheet it touched, and the 3/4-value\n`background-position` collapse changes what Chromium reads back, so neither\nis here. Over the 30 comparison stylesheets, extracted license comments, the\ngzip total is 56 B smaller and 1,804 B under lightningcss''s.\n\n* fix(css): keep a folded value''s case, fold past dropped aliases, and keep path()''s fill rule outside clip-path\n\nThree things CI found on the fold and the shape rewrite:\n\n- The fold read the printed values lowercased, which writes\n  `placeholderShimmer` back as `placeholdershimmer`, a name no keyframes\n  carry. It now reads them as written.\n- Under a target the prefix pass drops `-webkit-animation-iteration-count`\n  after the fold ran, so the fold took it for a declaration standing between\n  `animation` and its longhand and a second minify folded what the first did\n  not. An alias that pass drops, and any declaration already dropped, now\n  stands between nothing.\n- Only `clip-path` gives `path()` a fill rule, so `offset-path:path(nonzero,\n  …)` is a value the engine drops, which dropping `nonzero` brought back.\n\nThe changeset takes the numbered name and one short sentence.\n\n* fix(css): drop a basic shape''s zero radius only where it is a length\n\n`inset(0 round 0deg)` is a value the engine drops, since a corner radius is a\n`<length-percentage>`; reading any unit as a zero turned it into `inset(0)`,\nwhich clips. The radius is now read as the zero offsets a translation takes.\n\n* refactor(css): read the declaration a path() fill rule stands in directly\n\nA shape is only rewritten inside a declaration''s value, so the fallback for\nno declaration never ran and left the one changed line no test reaches.","tree":{"sha":"8f95eb015aef33982ebf47a0cefebe7256b8536b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/8f95eb015aef33982ebf47a0cefebe7256b8536b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/9f94bf3624d237577737ccb0123c12a12fd3253b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f95eb015aef33982ebf47a0cefebe7256b8536b\nparent 652835567e1f5db4d99c4c62133c8d37e99d738e\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791224559 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791224559 +0300\n\nfeat(css): fold longhands into their shorthand, and shorten flex and basic shapes (#22442)\n\n* feat(css): fold longhands into their shorthand, and shorten flex and basic shapes\n\nThree rewrites lightningcss makes and webpack did not, each checked against\nthe computed style Chromium reads back:\n\n- A longhand right after its own shorthand folds into it: the order-free\n  families (`border-top`, `outline`, `column-rule`, `text-emphasis`,\n  `flex-flow`, `text-decoration` where the target reads every slot), `flex`,\n  and a one-layer `transition` or `animation`. `text-wrap` stays out, read as\n  one keyword before it had longhands, and so does IE10''s `-ms-flex`.\n- `flex` in fewer than three components reads as its three factors, so\n  `1 auto` is `auto` and `1 1` is `1`.\n- A basic shape drops its defaults: a `closest-side` radius, a zero `round`,\n  `nonzero`, and the sides `inset()` repeats. Not the `at` position, which\n  engines read back as written.\n\nThe `animation` keyword slots come from the generator, out of mdn-data.\n\nWriting four border sides as `border-width`/`-style`/`-color` saved raw bytes\nbut cost gzip on every stylesheet it touched, and the 3/4-value\n`background-position` collapse changes what Chromium reads back, so neither\nis here. Over the 30 comparison stylesheets, extracted license comments, the\ngzip total is 56 B smaller and 1,804 B under lightningcss''s.\n\n* fix(css): keep a folded value''s case, fold past dropped aliases, and keep path()''s fill rule outside clip-path\n\nThree things CI found on the fold and the shape rewrite:\n\n- The fold read the printed values lowercased, which writes\n  `placeholderShimmer` back as `placeholdershimmer`, a name no keyframes\n  carry. It now reads them as written.\n- Under a target the prefix pass drops `-webkit-animation-iteration-count`\n  after the fold ran, so the fold took it for a declaration standing between\n  `animation` and its longhand and a second minify folded what the first did\n  not. An alias that pass drops, and any declaration already dropped, now\n  stands between nothing.\n- Only `clip-path` gives `path()` a fill rule, so `offset-path:path(nonzero,\n  …)` is a value the engine drops, which dropping `nonzero` brought back.\n\nThe changeset takes the numbered name and one short sentence.\n\n* fix(css): drop a basic shape''s zero radius only where it is a length\n\n`inset(0 round 0deg)` is a value the engine drops, since a corner radius is a\n`<length-percentage>`; reading any unit as a zero turned it into `inset(0)`,\nwhich clips. The radius is now read as the zero offsets a translation takes.\n\n* refactor(css): read the declaration a path() fill rule stands in directly\n\nA shape is only rewritten inside a declaration''s value, so the fallback for\nno declaration never ran and left the one changed line no test reaches.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw+rvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnf0QAIUVQN8SYhmGTV4TMjxVGOfM\nIt8VBpbxki+3q6b6+9DWYa2MQJcOYFjvB+5Ki5ZSkyOEJKh8hTEEdGb8liAcVDcs\npyi3nuJ0944qAOWWj10Zz9QZAjykDShJsW1X1oYcgTF6/QYdamSlKfD6glZqVruH\niChpNEwVewTRfkGlkR4gO1VgKXDuEwNPqYNOgLNws0Rn3K4orOC+Hz4xOf02qFvA\nGx1GmuWoxCMPUtwRNCoty2Ysmsjpc1HYbeppIkW4xRx8Pz7jdO/Toiyn5Xy5vUdM\n2SwJB7CvAFCKCwtC3j+uNWHZ0BhyvpHjQFpsdUrLp0dBq5/PfoH2EfTV/pjNDiSM\niIfrUQXtpJhtc1zqUVVQWn0a590qRdi3m3SB86Dc71gT6luAmmmICsh2z4D705bO\nnfbXUH0fR/hpXjivzgyfwHZ+Zd6E+zsfhgYipUt8OqUu4pyY0NHIDPmH2M+mzHfa\nLZWnepdcdbmJjWwaILG7gYsyFInW0Vd6hmS9XB43XWTDCK0yAwxO9HM1kavWzDuc\nCZVAtXmft/Zd1y6gxj4YxO