 the watcher never\nnoticed the update and close-pending timed out.\n\n* test(css): re-resolve a WebKit style difference before re-reading it\n\nWebKit kept Beer CSS''s root <div> resolved with nothing inherited through\nrenders of both frames, failing syntax-equivalence (webkit). Each re-read\nnow dirties the element with an inline custom property first.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dp9zrcrMNKB7SPShAVzh4G\n\n* test(css): restore the style attribute a WebKit re-read dirties\n\nLeaving the dirtying custom property set added a `style` attribute, so a\n`[style]` selector could hide a real difference on the re-read.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dp9zrcrMNKB7SPShAVzh4G\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: alexander-akait <sheo13666q@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"aabaa670b713fb24a3d81524ab21ed52a2ae6143","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/aabaa670b713fb24a3d81524ab21ed52a2ae6143"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/745ba27df4f4c6cf1ded4f293974d61decbdf9f3","verification":{"payload":"tree aabaa670b713fb24a3d81524ab21ed52a2ae6143\nparent 8eb4eb626387bcfecfdd74be38962c392e009e10\nauthor Sebastian Beltran <bjohansebas@gmail.com> 1791211855 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791211855 +0300\n\ntest(watch): cover pending close and entry rebuilds (#22435)\n\n* test(watch): cover pending close and entry rebuilds\n\nExtract close, entry context and MultiCompiler watch cases from feat/incremental-make. Refs #21556.\n\n* test(watch): rewrite fixture files so Windows sees the change\n\ncopyFileSync keeps the source mtime on Windows, so the watcher never\nnoticed the update and close-pending timed out.\n\n* test(css): re-resolve a WebKit style difference before re-reading it\n\nWebKit kept Beer CSS''s root <div> resolved with nothing inherited through\nrenders of both frames, failing syntax-equivalence (webkit). Each re-read\nnow dirties the element with an inline custom property first.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dp9zrcrMNKB7SPShAVzh4G\n\n* test(css): restore the style attribute a WebKit re-read dirties\n\nLeaving the dirtying custom property set added a `style` attribute, so a\n`[style]` selector could hide a real difference on the re-read.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dp9zrcrMNKB7SPShAVzh4G\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: alexander-akait <sheo13666q@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw7lPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaOAQAKxzuT1B0pkJXyFTvgjDMDow\namlsY3QDLGbw01v/hJiSQe8YrCsZTYWexEilhpMHrudkKZATKy74LQein6H8I0Ok\n2Cqb5bspNCtreu0Rsrlt3W7YezyOh6mwgHpgic+tYJwLcNttvf3xRc8DnPbkyTVK\nuY44mw0elZ5BWV+A7sqDNR9mFM3wooZ6xq8/p48pFX056NdewVujkKMXfCujW1Dy\nWIviI4ZlqMotvCFted6KEqz/FBVc5vY0DnY7X69O9uc8c61mp1bEq4b49wdILbLi\nmPJQzPw+o8S5J06rxU/2RDrOrszv7bZ6SjNddB7SHzC8ccKXXdefZgN2mC4NVmMq\nvytvklNwpJhKk799vbn3DExBwTHnLMBtxpZLxq6nhMRmsS3nVnR0e2kGsS5cc9uy\nBy0DSjt5xnF1B46gi4I/Eknxsl2Au1S79madOcIrokAcjesXhv8XQJJPyUdJFVQR\nh6a04XYbndMe4ClBxreiHBvC1EJn1ZxNr5T7E4mff/Ws2nwgRzc5BeGYl5ZnZrsc\nRFHRry+HN+4ExnzELLPZ43EfCmyJSobeLuVMxvH+DK3kItvjEoTiXF9RApLhqAbG\nOmGOxUIJJWJ+/fs4bc4ddXAMoqa3VF3wpMMowZcvSEmFNLcEoDpj+BPPVZBkDSiL\nCJiWIrnMZD/6Wen2GW3B\n=Bum5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T14:50:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/745ba27df4f4c6cf1ded4f293974d61decbdf9f3","node_id":"C_kwDOADgiC9oAKDc0NWJhMjdkZjRmNGM2Y2YxZGVkNGYyOTM5NzRkNjFkZWNiZGY5ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/8eb4eb626387bcfecfdd74be38962c392e009e10","sha":"8eb4eb626387bcfecfdd74be38962c392e009e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/8eb4eb626387bcfecfdd74be38962c392e009e10"}],"sha":"745ba27df4f4c6cf1ded4f293974d61decbdf9f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/745ba27df4f4c6cf1ded4f293974d61decbdf9f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143009186?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aryanraj45","id":143009186,"login":"aryanraj45","node_id":"U_kgDOCIYlog","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/8eb4eb626387bcfecfdd74be38962c392e009e10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:49:45Z","email":"143009186+aryanraj45@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raj Aryan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:49:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(javascript): scope a parameter list apart from its body in the minifier (#22439)\n\n* fix(javascript): scope a parameter list apart from its body in the minifier\n\nA name a parameter default or catch pattern reads resolved to what the body or block declares, as terser scopes it, so the mangler renamed the read onto the inner binding and the compressor dropped the outer one as unused. Such a read now skips the body''s bindings. Moves 42 test262 cases off the printer''s list; minifying a 1 MB bundle is within noise.\n\n* fix(javascript): clear parameter ranges once an analysis resolves\n\nAn analysis of a copied function counts its reads from zero but met the ranges an earlier analysis left on the scopes around it, so a read in the body could skip a binding there: P(a=q+q+q+q+q) copying h printed \"out\" for \"in\". Each analysis now clears its ranges after resolving. Adds the kinds the sweep reached: computed keys, writes, typeof, rest, constructors, setters, generators, const and class.","tree":{"sha":"85220c6200b274259f0cb544078800efe6a2e63e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/85220c6200b274259f0cb544078800efe6a2e63e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/8eb4eb626387bcfecfdd74be38962c392e009e10","verification":{"payload":"tree 85220c6200b274259f0cb544078800efe6a2e63e\nparent 52141800095af4a2775a12050c181181e8ef0d57\nauthor Raj Aryan <143009186+aryanraj45@users.noreply.github.com> 1791211785 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791211785 +0300\n\nfix(javascript): scope a parameter list apart from its body in the minifier (#22439)\n\n* fix(javascript): scope a parameter list apart from its body in the minifier\n\nA name a parameter default or catch pattern reads resolved to what the body or block declares, as terser scopes it, so the mangler renamed the read onto the inner binding and the compressor dropped the outer one as unused. Such a read now skips the body''s bindings. Moves 42 test262 cases off the printer''s list; minifying a 1 MB bundle is within noise.\n\n* fix(javascript): clear parameter ranges once an analysis resolves\n\nAn analysis of a copied function counts its reads from zero but met the ranges an earlier analysis left on the scopes around it, so a read in the body could skip a binding there: P(a=q+q+q+q+q) copying h printed \"out\" for \"in\". Each analysis now clears its ranges after resolving. Adds the kinds the sweep reached: computed keys, writes, typeof, rest, constructors, setters, generators, const and class.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw7kJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwzgQAFjD216Gx3NNNuFlCpE+NBAl\ntgKsMMsHtJkchtKo/kdY918p2TH0rlpS17pnwyXbaAWDOk1QazXakyEA0R4tXELT\n4wvobRVeP2LMQtDwNs+/sGh7G1Ub4cTgDMm1Bmqaa1F8eWVaHXyqfKbCZATtys10\nECSLw9DgNdIRap2RY1TUfIwpehpTyNQMwbUCDNBMDM9jhdd5RC4ndQPiSYhH/DRs\nhCEfY0VNuNtKflBkBZBOoVC5okl2IKS7gDPOV5XY1qJd/qLV9MCCSd6EbqIubiHF\n3ywbuRmEWeYC1X+J3qD3NWjU8z/bOJsHFGLqstXBYcd2g3dLbT3tPF7/hxxtfvSl\nfcb6VD8RHiFnhaH+SOsZZPrSJ9nx06di1RS26ZF43pMXS82z2pFzZhj8fHCMXd0t\naH9vxrNzgQNdftPSceQqNDuklUlPh4OSh0jnjZ5h5KsmMjINLhYo/I7OgvqfJW7d\n+CWVbxObRxEi5iQmeAyejVEiBZ+Wo/LzVCyoSwb+MlAGSljS0Krx3tUwQnEXSLfJ\nSJUcTpmr2dqhynIhduJs3R+Li7KPmi4uBRGO+VT6JCQpKYtk7FfD1URGv0uGMubi\nLUrfTz0JWOwqingh1Ug5si4eDkX/wuzfuPZwiLDDEVdit/kXh4czwnA+VfE7XZcG\nKzVM54l/BjBj889b4lf/\n=QQxM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T14:49:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-fl