ions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryanraj45","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/52141800095af4a2775a12050c181181e8ef0d57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:53:53Z","email":"143009186+aryanraj45@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raj Aryan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:53:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(javascript): keep the private names a direct eval reads (#22412)\n\n* fix(javascript): keep the private names a direct eval reads\n\nThe ESTree mangler renamed every #private name, but a direct eval in a class\nreads its names from a string renaming cannot reach, so eval(\"this.#m\") met\na #e and threw a SyntaxError, as terser''s output does. A class whose scope\nuses eval now keeps the names it declares, and no other name is renamed onto\none it keeps. 24 test262 cases print again in the printer''s mode.\n\n* test(javascript): record oxc renaming a private name a direct eval reads\n\nThe oxc case keeping #used for eval(''this.#used'') is now 3 bytes bigger than\noxc''s output, which renames #used to #e and leaves the string as it was, so\nits eval throws a SyntaxError. It is listed with the outputs oxc gets wrong.","tree":{"sha":"8088d824afb08f60e2fdcdd17fc1b2d0d665b253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/8088d824afb08f60e2fdcdd17fc1b2d0d665b253"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/52141800095af4a2775a12050c181181e8ef0d57","verification":{"payload":"tree 8088d824afb08f60e2fdcdd17fc1b2d0d665b253\nparent 362ca217df1adf3044cbae59cee7ef310b0f3da3\nauthor Raj Aryan <143009186+aryanraj45@users.noreply.github.com> 1791204833 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791204833 +0300\n\nfix(javascript): keep the private names a direct eval reads (#22412)\n\n* fix(javascript): keep the private names a direct eval reads\n\nThe ESTree mangler renamed every #private name, but a direct eval in a class\nreads its names from a string renaming cannot reach, so eval(\"this.#m\") met\na #e and threw a SyntaxError, as terser''s output does. A class whose scope\nuses eval now keeps the names it declares, and no other name is renamed onto\none it keeps. 24 test262 cases print again in the printer''s mode.\n\n* test(javascript): record oxc renaming a private name a direct eval reads\n\nThe oxc case keeping #used for eval(''this.#used'') is now 3 bytes bigger than\noxc''s output, which renames #used to #e and leaves the string as it was, so\nits eval throws a SyntaxError. It is listed with the outputs oxc gets wrong.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw53hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3DYQABqmHLNf8KW1d2MCJErpAw1E\nIpeSNjdRrIfx8x2wY3De+GBJADdp//nSIFFSeKGynZg6LL2YLZajYMsuFFHi1AGl\n+EwEiwRd3CG0LASCCuRGjqmKEwbazGqD1agOPSbCyPqPuSjckrfTnjvYZffib7B0\na3yrqo+CB1Nboh8gWQSVmslcAgiJtHKHNibKHAlED+SmIqp4KaM2Ll9s+kBbTki/\nQxFhI6q/G9UN3dokT/zX1MjNjXbIKVG25Q6DDx7wk1FO2cTWD4w4NX9iWinT1udA\nig0yYEdyP08SUy5ykWT+4Z4c4hs4D30pEKsHDUbBUmxMvFLWOKuiGaBdoLYkTphz\nwy1e2ZdtQjdj/tSdEB3Nlf9lAwYSSteZTRCJZKf3cgCg/RQgJE1A6GYLgA9oqmKD\nt4j5Jyub9WMcV6YLCIuYEldV+zoRhO0knRjzM8X3lbjfTPNAw0g3qft6rDrxEEhT\nPW443cdSwH95j8TuKAu7TSXH4dJ7ee8sDTEGJEYP2uZLQWJOej+bD/uSiTgxUFPB\n9/pWweXm8ZmL40/V5qaFaQKg5d7NyfYlkejdL+fdQ1YiOtE/vz8GX1Kfrmu31O2w\nbDCz6FUoaj3WAN+nT33RkrfXtCDpPebvbSzk2cs+LYmlb7o255u8pdAji0VL9/1o\nSFP8IsjqcAQBQdLHjfK5\n=EbOX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T12:53:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"