der-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/f93514ea63d869111931038db85fc74be801975f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:23:45Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:23:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(javascript): analyze the compressor''s scopes with ScopeAnalyzer (#22429)\n\n* refactor(javascript): hold the compressor''s scopes as ScopeAnalyzer scopes\n\nThe compressor''s terser port kept each scope''s fields on its node and each\ndefinition as a sealed `SymbolDef` object. Scopes are now `CompressorScope`s\nand definitions `CompressorVariable`s, subclasses of the shared model that\nthe mangler''s analysis uses; a node holds the scope it opens as its\n`block_scope`. Scope helpers become `MinifierScope` and `CompressorScope`\nmethods. The port''s walk still fills them. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): analyze the compressor''s scopes with ScopeAnalyzer\n\n`figureOutScope` no longer walks the tree itself: a\n`CompressorScopeAnalyzer` subclass of the mangler''s analyzer records what the\ncompressor reads besides, each symbol''s scope, each definition''s declaring\nsymbols, value and reads, labels, and `arguments` reads, and can analyse a\nfunction again inside the scope around it. The port''s two passes and its kind\ntables are deleted, and a compressor scope no longer lists its children,\nwhich nothing reads. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): move a compressor scope with CompressorScope#adopt\n\nterser''s `add_child_scope` becomes `CompressorScope#adopt`: it re-parents the\nscope and merges `uses*` and what the moved scope reads up its new\nancestors. The compressor passes it whether a moved arrow reads `arguments`,\nwhich only its tree''s kinds answer. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): keep the compressor''s globals on the program''s node\n\nThe program''s globals stay on its node as on main, so a scope holds no\nfield only the program''s uses, and a definition drops `should_replace`,\nwhich nothing reads. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): cover a named IIFE''s unread name in the scope tests\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): read a compressor reference''s scope off its name\n\nThe compressor''s analysis records each name read with its flags only: the\nname already holds the scope it is read in, so the list of scopes the\nmangler keeps is not built. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC","tree":{"sha":"8dde6b33db3f2c7a9ead0cec3bf1ec675d6ee8de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/trees/8dde6b33db3f2c7a9ead0cec3bf1ec675d6ee8de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/git/commits/f93514ea63d869111931038db85fc74be801975f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8dde6b33db3f2c7a9ead0cec3bf1ec675d6ee8de\nparent 63f2330a19e7dfd3ec683265171f48c2e617ea6e\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791192225 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791192225 +0300\n\nrefactor(javascript): analyze the compressor''s scopes with ScopeAnalyzer (#22429)\n\n* refactor(javascript): hold the compressor''s scopes as ScopeAnalyzer scopes\n\nThe compressor''s terser port kept each scope''s fields on its node and each\ndefinition as a sealed `SymbolDef` object. Scopes are now `CompressorScope`s\nand definitions `CompressorVariable`s, subclasses of the shared model that\nthe mangler''s analysis uses; a node holds the scope it opens as its\n`block_scope`. Scope helpers become `MinifierScope` and `CompressorScope`\nmethods. The port''s walk still fills them. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): analyze the compressor''s scopes with ScopeAnalyzer\n\n`figureOutScope` no longer walks the tree itself: a\n`CompressorScopeAnalyzer` subclass of the mangler''s analyzer records what the\ncompressor reads besides, each symbol''s scope, each definition''s declaring\nsymbols, value and reads, labels, and `arguments` reads, and can analyse a\nfunction again inside the scope around it. The port''s two passes and its kind\ntables are deleted, and a compressor scope no longer lists its children,\nwhich nothing reads. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): move a compressor scope with CompressorScope#adopt\n\nterser''s `add_child_scope` becomes `CompressorScope#adopt`: it re-parents the\nscope and merges `uses*` and what the moved scope reads up its new\nancestors. The compressor passes it whether a moved arrow reads `arguments`,\nwhich only its tree''s kinds answer. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): keep the compressor''s globals on the program''s node\n\nThe program''s globals stay on its node as on main, so a scope holds no\nfield only the program''s uses, and a definition drops `should_replace`,\nwhich nothing reads. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): cover a named IIFE''s unread name in the scope tests\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC\n\n* refactor(javascript): read a compressor reference''s scope off its name\n\nThe compressor''s analysis records each name read with its flags only: the\nname already holds the scope it is read in, so the list of scopes the\nmangler keeps is not built. Output is byte-identical.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tgxgyb4N35ndP6cC4KcrXC","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2yhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApwIQAECWmxegTtsSzsls/vm+KXVB\nNPzIQt3XfKuyDzVvzoIGMtOo6cZFGJUteE0AUcPHFrTfmTyyKYtqxytotfOvbmVS\n1QF6/UIqxX5wJLJGo1gDH9y5spmTiyUnFPJLXgD3znH0zkia5F8WoiqHH+Qpw4NU\nvsQDMB9bP64QPdQPRCf0U5tv1c7IPUnw+TUguHwPzqosmb8uHBi6O48EGBi1Qr/i\nx//ejBBxXFhS7U7G5JB1o7sPlJOhlbIXbC+0TIcIvhY3jNi/9RKiauz+Dwu01rIF\n30V52cdAPEN6H5Jvh6rYSuhdw2zK6iWeK6kqBxXcowtHOUtjLC0Gm39FI0c5hyE6\nltW8oFf2YNVZCYcNGyPriNm+cFiMuKer7ugcrd0xxIf2sCGT9434peI/KO9o6fn6\nahHWKWyZTZ+h9wBljIX14pB46+uL0YLCLhK8uT0uZ8TTUhlf4Vh36EeBToBbwtUH\n6FPtw0UhYtI4bB2OuvycFgXpihqBPhPHwnUrKxyTnGfXxI4v8+xQFX+myQdPGg/m\n9CaEmnsjtzbVITlkvZ5ZnVDsONxtxz9cvn+W46UDfjrdc/QD+QSkDLzgySbxxncR\nsNwGtXvA4Ub6ZhvRdK0VdlU7QL7YGg7lcZah7lwMejwDxT7MA8i01BNp2s/15yhV\nKWNDNpBMf3Mhcoo39pTl\n=Qt9o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T09:23:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-f