8 +0300\n\nchore: consolidate the changesets into one entry per topic (#2471)\n\n48 unreleased entries described the hot client one step at a time,\nincluding fixes to options that were never released. They are merged\ninto 15, each a few sentences about what the release ships, linked to\nthe pull request that introduced the topic. The README link fix is\ndropped as documentation only.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQplCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlGQQABkzn1wDq7r63np01KLJsxB1\nJG4ZgiYXhFqc6mOgAzmOmIhO7BWG2G6sOiqtF7FZ4r/VW+Lh5MA5eJ8G1AVSjpiH\n6/csS547JwGUeLJLbhKTbFCZkH6k3DmOeg0sDRhX6zW6JAbcvCsnGQcjXEQpmXAN\nRL761zq4nzD3VxVDAF7pqeXflTRNStqKt7ny+BAwb2murHy2prVn9G/0VRG9F8Uu\ne0zX1Qgh+YbOVbQjhhKOaMLiMCSp3r7Aii3d5OezWxks2Cjw+nimtBInztggd9uG\nsCJPm7R+f743jLZh7yV/JaoyEAyAn6mtPUqGWbTK90Vqv6elcpGbuf+Jwx3S42PW\nHuJqR7eXt4p2KN1VXiGDihIF5FkW1D3bDGBAufvVUZs0IZDgZTc63moXAaSZx8YL\naOP85UBmbpNwXlm8G6smP1m7LWRnwQGG5DIXsir7EaG2ppcxaAh5Vv/cPKqsTBBu\n1mDbc1TfZksJB6l/CqtcBkWJOSL15tLNeBGZhoKxe2WvUpsRgu98rer6hP8KM3KR\nFGsS8EcChjitgiyESVbB6jZK/nxyS+LYYEEayrgXTlX6ULmr6sgulCf/0auoFPSK\nyUcGw4LYErSWkTrWgbxWL7wPLTDea2Bd5VXPOKZ97uyzTEwwjIP6nXr7X6LC6VYL\nLeV/8wL4snKAabFucCDr\n=IKCH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:49:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/d15ffc279fff9b30742073ce7d193d25b0b4a7b3","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGQxNWZmYzI3OWZmZjliMzA3NDIwNzNjZTdkMTkzZDI1YjBiNGE3YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197","sha":"191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197"}],"sha":"d15ffc279fff9b30742073ce7d193d25b0b4a7b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/d15ffc279fff9b30742073ce7d193d25b0b4a7b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:54:48Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:54:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): resolve a client path given as parts (#2459)\n\n* feat(hot): resolve a client path given as parts\n\nAn absolute url says everything, which is more than is known where the options\nare written: the host a page will be opened on and the scheme it was served\nover are the browser''s to report. A server behind a proxy, on another host, or\nwith a socket on a port of its own has to name the part that differs and leave\nthe rest to be resolved where it is known.\n\nSo `hot.client.path` takes an object as well as a string. Unset parts come from\nthe page, as do the values only a server could have meant: `0.0.0.0` and `::`\nare what listening on every interface reports and are not addresses a page can\nconnect to, and a port of `0` is one the server picked.\n\nThis is webpack-dev-server''s `createSocketURL`, ported with its own test cases\nso the behaviour is held to what that project has always done — it is client\nlogic, and belongs where the client is. One thing had to change: it mapped\nevery scheme onto `ws`, having only that transport. The two here do not share a\nscheme, and an `EventSource` pointed at `ws://` never connects, so what carries\nover from the page is whether TLS is in play and the scheme is the transport''s\nto choose. A browser e2e over both transports is what caught that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): carry the resolved path into a client path given as parts\n\nA spec replaces the resolved path in the entry query outright, so a spec that\nnames no `pathname` left the client falling back to its own default — which is\nthe same path only until someone sets `hot.path`, and then quietly is not: the\nruntime would connect to `/__webpack_hmr` while the endpoint served somewhere\nelse. The server knows its path, so it fills that part in before serializing.\n\nA spec that names a `pathname` keeps it, and a path given as a string is not\nreached into. The browser test now runs against a server with a path of its\nown, so the part being carried over is one the client''s default gets wrong.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): encode a username and a password one at a time\n\nThe port kept webpack-dev-server''s trick of encoding `user:password` as one\nstring and restoring the first `%3A` as the separator. That finds the\nusername''s own colon when it has one, so the credentials split in the wrong\nplace: `a:b` and `pw` arrived as the username `a` and the password `b:pw`.\nEncoded one at a time instead, which is also what CodeQL was reporting.\n\nAlso corrected a claim in three places — the schema, the README and the\nchangeset — that a page served over TLS *always* gets a secure connection. It\ndoes when the protocol is unset or `\"auto\"`, and when a host naming every\ninterface resolves to the page''s. A protocol said explicitly is kept, which a\ntest in this branch has asserted all along: `http:` on an `https:` page gives\n`ws:`. The prose promised something the tests denied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): read the path spec by what it parses to\n\nSame correction as the logging object: the parts form was detected by testing\nthe first character for `{`, so json with a space before it fell through and\nthe object text was used as the path. Asking what `JSON.parse` returned covers\nthat, and covers what trimming would not — `JSON.parse` also accepts a bare\nnumber, boolean or quoted string, none of which is a path, so requiring an\nobject is the check that was meant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): read a scheme without its colon, and leave a full url unprefixed\n\nTwo more from review, both reachable through the parts form.\n\nA scheme is written both with and without its colon, and the option takes\neither — `formatUrl` puts a missing one back. Deciding whether TLS is in play\nrequired it, so `protocol: \"https\"` read as insecure and gave `ws:` on a\nsecure page, which a browser then refuses to open. Compared without the colon\nnow, and case-insensitively, since neither is part of a scheme. `auto` the\nsame way.\n\n`dynamicPublicPath` prefixes a path with the bundle''s public path, which only\nmakes sense for a path. An endpoint said in full already says where it is, and\nprefixing it names somewhere that does not exist. That was already true of a\nfull url given as a string; the parts form resolving to one made it easy to\narrive at by accident, so the prefixing now skips anything carrying a scheme.\n\nEight cases for the scheme spellings, and a browser test for the second: a\npage under `/assets/` with a resolved url still connects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix: carry the path through an empty pathname, and type the parts form\n\nTwo out-of-diff findings from review.\n\nAn empty `pathname` escaped the carry-over, which tested only for an absent\none — so the client resolved it from its own default rather than from this\nserver''s `hot.path`, which is the same silent wrong-endpoint mismatch the\nabsent case had. Empty is not a path; it means the same as not saying one.\n\nAnd the exported `HotClientOptions.path` was still `string`, so a TypeScript\nconfiguration using the documented object form got a type error for something\nthe schema accepts. It is `string | PathSpec` now, with `PathSpec` carrying a\ndescription per part so the generated declaration says what each one resolves\nto.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e26725beef2a90480655d99bebbc5cb32a126f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/1e26725beef2a90480655d99bebbc5cb32a126f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e26725beef2a90480655d99bebbc5cb32a126f1\nparent 9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791291288 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791291288 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): resolve a client path given as parts (#2459)\n\n* feat(hot): resolve a client path given as parts\n\nAn absolute url says everything, which is more than is known where the options\nare written: the host a page will be opened on and the scheme it was served\nover are the browser''s to report. A server behind a proxy, on another host, or\nwith a socket on a port of its own has to name the part that differs and leave\nthe rest to be resolved where it is known.\n\nSo `hot.client.path` takes an object as well as a string. Unset parts come from\nthe page, as do the values only a server could have meant: `0.0.0.0` and `::`\nare what listening on every interface reports and are not addresses a page can\nconnect to, and a port of `0` is one the server picked.\n\nThis is webpack-dev-server''s `createSocketURL`, ported with its own test cases\nso the behaviour is held to what that project has always done — it is client\nlogic, and belongs where the client is. One thing had to change: it mapped\nevery scheme onto `ws`, having only that transport. The two here do not share a\nscheme, and an `EventSource` pointed at `ws://` never connects, so what carries\nover from the page is whether TLS is in play and the scheme is the transport''s\nto choose. A browser e2e over both transports is what caught that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): carry the resolved path into a client path given as parts\n\nA spec replaces the resolved path in the entry query outright, so a spec that\nnames no `pathname` left the client falling back to its own default — which is\nthe same path only until someone sets `hot.path`, and then quietly is not: the\nruntime would connect to `/__webpack_hmr` while the endpoint served somewhere\nelse. The server knows its path, so it fills that part in before serializing.\n\nA spec that names a `pathname` keeps it, and a path given as a string is not\nreached into. The browser test now runs against a server with a path of its\nown, so the part being carried over is one the client''s default gets wrong.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): encode a username and a password one at a time\n\nThe port kept webpack-dev-server''s trick of encoding `user:password` as one\nstring and restoring the first `%3A` as the separator. That finds the\nusername''s own colon when it has one, so the credentials split in the wrong\nplace: `a:b` and `pw` arrived as the username `a` and the password `b:pw`.\nEncoded one at a time instead, which is also what CodeQL was reporting.\n\nAlso corrected a claim in three places — the schema, the README and the\nchangeset — that a page served over TLS *always* gets a secure connection. It\ndoes when the protocol is unset or `\"auto\"`, and when a host naming every\ninterface resolves to the page''s. A protocol said explicitly is kept, which a\ntest in this branch has asserted all along: `http:` on an `https:` page gives\n`ws:`. The prose promised something the tests denied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): read the path spec by what it parses to\n\nSame correction as the logging object: the parts form was detected by testing\nthe first character for `{`, so json with a space before it fell through and\nthe object text was used as the path. Asking what `JSON.parse` returned covers\nthat, and covers what trimming would not — `JSON.parse` also accepts a bare\nnumber, boolean or quoted string, none of which is a path, so requiring an\nobject is the check that was meant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): read a scheme without its colon, and leave a full url unprefixed\n\nTwo more from review, both reachable through the parts form.\n\nA scheme is written both with and without its colon, and the option takes\neither — `formatUrl` puts a missing one back. Deciding whether TLS is in play\nrequired it, so `protocol: \"https\"` read as insecure and gave `ws:` on a\nsecure page, which a browser then refuses to open. Compared without the colon\nnow, and case-insensitively, since neither is part of a scheme. `auto` the\nsame way.\n\n`dynamicPublicPath` prefixes a path with the bundle''s public path, which only\nmakes sense for a path. An endpoint said in full already says where it is, and\nprefixing it names somewhere that does not exist. That was already true of a\nfull url given as a string; the parts form resolving to one made it easy to\narrive at by accident, so the prefixing now skips anything carrying a scheme.\n\nEight cases for the scheme spellings, and a browser test for the second: a\npage under `/assets/` with a resolved url still connects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix: carry the path through an empty pathname, and type the parts form\n\nTwo out-of-diff findings from review.\n\nAn empty `pathname` escaped the carry-over, which tested only for an absent\none — so the client resolved it from its own default rather than from this\nserver''s `hot.path`, which is the same silent wrong-endpoint mismatch the\nabsent case had. Empty is not a path; it means the same as not saying one.\n\nAnd the exported `HotClientOptions.path` was still `string`, so a TypeScript\nconfiguration using the documented object form got a type error for something\nthe schema accepts. It is `string | PathSpec` now, with `PathSpec` carrying a\ndescription per part so the generated declaration says what each one resolves\nto.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxO+YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYNUQADNje6eyF+Zuxld/cBX5oxCY\nsmSHiaXXJyigRxDV9HB6c7wqflr3Lu8eOyezPIZj0nDp31yHaRTDfEognphnMKxf\niuyxdDksG+uWYJHkFfuqIcvNZcp/NBfc/4h7lTww53izF9Gz0+h1uM7IFfufaW+p\nc14E2E1hVjSwCTRE1457qjaQ6tQl4aKMtATsOEacVB6RM0HY0ygTrtcnBULk4hPF\n7j3O1PPcrx1nWSyJcMQ5yOHIpIq+MPSckBFfwVzv3kqX+gxdqNUIdBwluV+1lt7q\nYoN22PZ77rOGopjfABlUHNi92LpLMPBWjXgDPXc1akhUMJB5acgF+fQEHcTzeP77\nZhV7GKQ9bfHeIXEhyMrmJgpf8OXFuK8Hyau6LPr2sj2UhYd++HjvBQ0G8bgXdc+2\nQmLJG3FcPIa/Y1VdLZa60Wc9KH4Ehf20RQ84LnMRehRYoNu6OL5QZzoaFeE/lCyV\n/86OmDyzrNf11Q7bPwOjnH+8qGPdcEHSbls4rqLAzAZASeTd17+G3rKk8UfrG5cJ\nqQFlXinKV1luUT6TGh86MMEWL6e8JLqkDlmSK06td02E6xK2XE+62MRZ5Z+fVriU\nn15Qm/rp4o77Ixp6BEIP+Mro8woLLgQ5GogCjxCgn4wylc5qx5sRbrohrEHJGSlJ\nb1BUSdebxVZwJE8GWVcG\n=VHDy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:54:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDE5MWZjOTU3OWM2MTFkZTVjZTlmZTYwYzhhZGZlNTY1NTNiYTMxOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a","sha":"9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a"}],"sha":"191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/191fc9579c611de5ce9fe60c8adfe56553ba3197"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:54:30Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:54:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: follow up the review of the client and hot changes (#2470)\n\nItems from the review of the merged work that were never taken:\n\n- Only connect.retries is sent as the largest safe integer for Infinity. A\n  timeout is also the delay handed to setTimeout, which wraps above 2^31 - 1\n  ms, so an infinite one is left to be dropped.\n- An error action with no message posts the text the client logged to the\n  page, rather than undefined, and the posted reason is asserted.\n- An object-form cache.control is copied when the middleware is created, and\n  a test sends a request to check the grouped cache and mime options are what\n  a response reads.\n- The hot.progress deprecation says to remove it before adding a plugin of your\n  own, and hot.cors says what it controls on each transport.\n- The escaping test requires the payload to be visible in the overlay.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5a3917c1b8828c6cd2ac554edd152e884c766ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/f5a3917c1b8828c6cd2ac554edd152e884c766ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a","verification":{"payload":"tree f5a3917c1b8828c6cd2ac554edd152e884c766ab\nparent ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791291270 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791291270 +0300\n\nfix: follow up the review of the client and hot changes (#2470)\n\nItems from the review of the merged work that were never taken:\n\n- Only connect.retries is sent as the largest safe integer for Infinity. A\n  timeout is also the delay handed to setTimeout, which wraps above 2^31 - 1\n  ms, so an infinite one is left to be dropped.\n- An error action with no message posts the text the client logged to the\n  page, rather than undefined, and the posted reason is asserted.\n- An object-form cache.control is copied when the middleware is created, and\n  a test sends a request to check the grouped cache and mime options are what\n  a response reads.\n- The hot.progress deprecation says to remove it before adding a plugin of your\n  own, and hot.cors says what it controls on each transport.\n- The escaping test requires the payload to be visible in the overlay.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxO+GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtCoQAFRl3jtJDiSxCQ8LcET0m9Tw\nbZGht1FFqfdCxaoMsZKAotw3zGhQTQIpKAcSFN6KtZQkYe1+7TGq3SgOGzQHyNtc\nEr7a6U9DQg2oUC3IleMkIo1c+VWRr9nemdwcbJvMGkgDz3MpIDFxKHxAUAGIpWtv\nS6fzvvqha4XzWj0FYD6ttDgqOnAHhAszbQVXwZqv63jDpf9fCGd4m8RNfh1B7n0b\nvwQaVkmAOnbns+/+fqiNBmHX/gLwEilRVxT82B1JfS8Wtum7PWSYcZPBqBWgNWhk\n1XpjrjZuOJ7TwMhTU8hO0Cj4z5KzK82+pm7GIEl7Cgi9LUlemQPmfl/TEPIWxja9\nUEctfN/xXlGD1A+5QWXeCpZbE912HF+HGsqWv/KAKeBYyp6m+myCIjXU0aAKYcKt\nNPlVIVuLMR0oW12ZBCfhMlQ9cIyYXUVJ416DrgjZN8y97S/qg7DROAtg5P27A9ob\nHibXO0CFRtaV/2WYsZa/s2deckEWFadHM+ZsZg+FxXYqCU7R7DeuDZV1ErTnG+9h\nTaajGzcE4UtMM6K1xNHfbnqqlcmPg157Y2XumgmDXQbktG6Dyt9AbT8pgx6/OU+a\nQ0E2SimuBdPYWK4nb/YjGThZh+wJOOXFgN4dsvys274aq8nhTn+Tt9Z6OBpHpPL0\nR6Ns2W3YbcWWOj+LF2NT\n=kk+f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:54:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDlkODIyY2UyMzM2NGEyNGQzMzQ2ODMwMjBmYWIxNGVlMzc0Y2Y3OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd","sha":"ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd"}],"sha":"9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/9d822ce23364a24d334683020fab14ee374cf78a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:38:49Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:38:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(client): keep webpack''s logger, leave out the tapable hook around it (#2467)\n\nThe client logged through webpack/lib/logging/runtime.js, which is a few lines\nof glue around Logger and createConsoleLogger plus a tapable hook the client\nnever uses. tapable requires util and builds its hooks with new Function.\n\nIn a universal or web and node build that put a createRequire of a node\nbuiltin in the client''s bundle, which a page cannot call, and under Trusted\nTypes the hooks could not be compiled at all, which is why every log call had a\nguard around it.\n\nLogger and createConsoleLogger are used as they are, so the levels and labels\nare webpack''s. A test bundles the client for web, universal and web with node,\nand the logger''s own wiring is covered.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"140fdb3b3d56de079a11ab5894875432ca6fe52d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/140fdb3b3d56de079a11ab5894875432ca6fe52d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 140fdb3b3d56de079a11ab5894875432ca6fe52d\nparent 07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791286729 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791286729 +0300\n\nfix(client): keep webpack''s logger, leave out the tapable hook around it (#2467)\n\nThe client logged through webpack/lib/logging/runtime.js, which is a few lines\nof glue around Logger and createConsoleLogger plus a tapable hook the client\nnever uses. tapable requires util and builds its hooks with new Function.\n\nIn a universal or web and node build that put a createRequire of a node\nbuiltin in the client''s bundle, which a page cannot call, and under Trusted\nTypes the hooks could not be compiled at all, which is why every log call had a\nguard around it.\n\nLogger and createConsoleLogger are used as they are, so the levels and labels\nare webpack''s. A test bundles the client for web, universal and web with node,\nand the logger''s own wiring is covered.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----B