IyZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c","sha":"07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c"}],"sha":"ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/ad0cd03c4c2b07639d6842ee976a23de6484b2dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:37:40Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:37:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(client): load the page when a sibling compilation builds, in reload mode (#2468)\n\n* fix(client): load the page when a sibling compilation builds, in reload mode\n\nThe name filter kept a sibling''s build away from the client, which is right\nfor applying an update in place. A page rendered from another bundle''s output,\na server bundle for instance, was then never told to reload when that bundle\nchanged. webpack-dev-server has always reloaded on any compilation''s change.\n\nA build with errors still leaves the page alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test: wait for the sibling''s failed build rather than a fixed delay\n\napp.edit only writes the file, so a three second pause could end before the\nbuild or its event. The test waits for the build to complete with errors, then\nfor the watcher to go quiet, before it checks that the page was left alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bfb2c55a0b3912f85a1bee25d093a5a28ac77dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/4bfb2c55a0b3912f85a1bee25d093a5a28ac77dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bfb2c55a0b3912f85a1bee25d093a5a28ac77dd\nparent 4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791286660 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791286660 +0300\n\nfix(client): load the page when a sibling compilation builds, in reload mode (#2468)\n\n* fix(client): load the page when a sibling compilation builds, in reload mode\n\nThe name filter kept a sibling''s build away from the client, which is right\nfor applying an update in place. A page rendered from another bundle''s output,\na server bundle for instance, was then never told to reload when that bundle\nchanged. webpack-dev-server has always reloaded on any compilation''s change.\n\nA build with errors still leaves the page alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test: wait for the sibling''s failed build rather than a fixed delay\n\napp.edit only writes the file, so a three second pause could end before the\nbuild or its event. The test waits for the build to complete with errors, then\nfor the watcher to go quiet, before it checks that the page was left alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxN2ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ74QAGvq1Tgf6YF9qkBOntrhDa+o\nxlEAsrIr9ZogZe6HN6oXTbc4B5YxjUTj1SJ2QOZq1tFrWBnE/zvkAOXBMUVEdwYL\nQfZ+7IUg3odnksYt8OUPDiAGgmEKFlhN8TksYTPMV4eAomj2SW3Zrfe+aDVGLDKy\n6ZpdCzF8A5Ruhp8C14n4VVxMOOt62ZoZkPzGW4r5CBGVzE+UBEMN7egT7a0QgGYZ\nFd3HtjjZPf30OVUhDY8mZD+ch5a/XJkFWDNcAoISWBcDW54PP8OAvyiIuPWGdfar\nV9DDKkXd4aslAoognnrtokDSFp/oZE1xS7E5zmiTKjkYyXSm/LsWvPKfazwOzlUO\n8/ecoA9TxaIzPBHVOL4633YL4CfKkBR/HDFZe5V+gQqD1GpGcdmXoPNbmbj3b5p+\nmZrlvFWdqRAeW83zkeBcsleJDWrvb+UX+8Hm3jdQjLGInxIlFUP+Noi+6tvA9PDt\noXb0zfCLZ6sD1kgKZSkr6nDU9x43BcAI/FmJAOWSoDdPdx0L/0DdWgPFm4V8PJoH\nZud00khTnBGYU56Zz6jVV53qcbfYe+prNo3QgIw8qSUTYiqDUDQxUMH8XcaBREPW\npWN7H8++DJws3LIkFKHad0l8lHKUy7AkWXg4khMrnmnFTLKaq0jiU2WKdsjx13gu\n2ScVMQq3I8iXKM2NDXUN\n=vmKA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T11:37:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDA3YjlmYmMwM2IzN2ZlYjNmMzMyODBhY2ZlMTAxYWFiMjM5ZDcwOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8","sha":"4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8"}],"sha":"07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/07b9fbc03b37feb3f33280acfe101aab239d708c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:36:29Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:36:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): say when the connection goes away, and clear the build''s problems (#2463)\n\n* feat(hot): say when the connection goes away, and clear the build''s problems\n\nThe client said `connected` and then nothing when the connection was lost: a\nstopped server left a page that looked live, a console that never said\notherwise, and an overlay frozen on the last build''s errors.\n\nIt logs `Disconnected!` once per outage now, at the moment the connection is\nlost — which is what webpack-dev-server''s client has always printed there, and\nthe point its `close` handler ran at. Once per outage rather than once per\nfailed attempt, since Server-Sent Events retry for as long as the page is open.\n\nBuild errors and warnings are cleared from the overlay at the same moment: what\nthe server last said about the build is stale once the server is gone. The\nreporter forgets them rather than just hiding them, so the catch-up a\nreconnection is sent starts from nothing and re-reports whatever is still\nwrong, in the console as well as the overlay.\n\nOnly the build''s problems. webpack-dev-server dismissed the whole overlay, but\na runtime error is the page''s own and a lost connection says nothing about it —\nthe same reasoning that already keeps a successful build from clearing one.\n\nThree browser tests, one per rule, each checked against the mutation that\nbreaks only it: dropping the log fails all three, and also dismissing runtime\nerrors fails only the third. Two console snapshots gain the line; the watchdog\none reads connected → Disconnected! → connected per silent cycle, which is\nwhat that is.\n\nFound moving webpack-dev-server onto this client: eight of its test files and\neighteen snapshot lines depend on `Disconnected!`, and one test waits for it\nwith no timeout, so the swap turned a missing log line into a hung test file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test: wait for the third connection, not the second drop\n\nDisconnected! contains connected, so waiting for three messages containing it\nstopped after two connections and one drop, and the snapshot recorded that.\nMatching with the bracket in front waits for the second watchdog cycle the\ntest says it covers, and the snapshot now holds all five lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test: check that the restored overlay carries the broken build''s error\n\nAny overlay appearing after the reconnection satisfied the assertion. It now\nwaits for the overlay to contain the build''s own diagnostic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ab01a22a34a23bdd26ca93c6a64856f9abba3cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/6ab01a22a34a23bdd26ca93c6a64856f9abba3cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ab01a22a34a23bdd26ca93c6a64856f9abba3cd\nparent 991c3868c66e78ac66e1ce5e3c1cd8f449978f3d\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791286589 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791286589 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): say when the connection goes away, and clear the build''s problems (#2463)\n\n* feat(hot): say when the connection goes away, and clear the build''s problems\n\nThe client said `connected` and then nothing when the connection was lost: a\nstopped server left a page that looked live, a console that never said\notherwise, and an overlay frozen on the last build''s errors.\n\nIt logs `Disconnected!` once per outage now, at the moment the connection is\nlost — which is what webpack-dev-server''s client has always printed there, and\nthe point its `close` handler ran at. Once per outage rather than once per\nfailed attempt, since Server-Sent Events retry for as long as the page is open.\n\nBuild errors and warnings are cleared from the overlay at the same moment: what\nthe server last said about the build is stale once the server is gone. The\nreporter forgets them rather than just hiding them, so the catch-up a\nreconnection is sent starts from nothing and re-reports whatever is still\nwrong, in the console as well as the overlay.\n\nOnly the build''s problems. webpack-dev-server dismissed the whole overlay, but\na runtime error is the page''s own and a lost connection says nothing about it —\nthe same reasoning that already keeps a successful build from clearing one.\n\nThree browser tests, one per rule, each checked against the mutation that\nbreaks only it: dropping the log fails all three, and also dismissing runtime\nerrors fails only the third. Two console snapshots gain the line; the watchdog\none reads connected → Disconnected! → connected per silent cycle, which is\nwhat that is.\n\nFound moving webpack-dev-server onto this client: eight of its test files and\neighteen snapshot lines depend on `Disconnected!`, and one test waits for it\nwith no timeout, so the swap turned a missing log line into a hung test file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test: wait for the third connection, not the second drop\n\nDisconnected! contains connected, so waiting for three messages containing it\nstopped after two connections and one drop, and the snapshot recorded that.\nMatching with the bracket in front waits for the second watchdog cycle the\ntest says it covers, and the snapshot now holds all five lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test: check that the restored overlay carries the broken build''s error\n\nAny overlay appearing after the reconnection satisfied the assertion. It now\nwaits for the overlay to contain the build''s own diagnostic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxN09CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALBEQAG3y/qzkblHgm4yFA6SLMKMp\n5Ws5Fs47cFRaYTNzwlrn+TjdUqAm/DeBc9Cpjl8RiVgSD5UcMEM/C19HpJkPPFyh\nZhl7SM3l8mycBKYknhI8w8q935rNOYS5IfnRNMi1XxLHMXqT5U1Ugi9Vz+LE2VA9\n4FpVC8DOYmXKG+FjkbxPk5Ug59CnD5lUrNqSoX1rWYr5O19xuCRzxC5giiszT4yI\nJLZb6hf+Do+fMQ3kCna1rrZ0nwCoGBVVYGlBiLgld3STvQP4KcMN6wOlou2ITqPQ\n55KQrMqhJ0liB54rPOBZVzWrcbUlD4yJjpGw+xR7jyhWBA+V0JdZAZcwnI8EqrYj\nO5H8alto/5vbH2gc7ocRKjNlwWXOpvtH5hba0I175zEwed8dSALZnl4duHSZkRfp\ntfDuw4P/1uoZyskr0j8/3/PxcvTeD1ANEwFjN2s960cfRAJ5VeZ8ivE7M3VRCrRC\n1myrloUely2f0sVg78BiRqyiGZh1XNOWuVP4ZfX9Z0P0eWSYJ+ODDAH+HFsvLwrd\nLdT+9g2SudhpStNLTmpLVw6e1D1dUNe1xHgeNtFj4ckeFaA0Ykd877XyA+Z41E/a\nAP537GQRWclImKOIOG79DyH+NVmBQu3NKp8x4rDmPeFXkapMJw8XG5pYlFFtHpWC\n1s46ftEtmoSaAA3Gljx1\n=aJIi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T11:36:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDQ3NjFhMjI0ZjY1NGQwMmE4ZDQ5M2RhYzAwNmM4NTI5OTViNzRhZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/991c3868c66e78ac66e1ce5e3c1cd8f449978f3d","sha":"991c3868c66e78ac66e1ce5e3c1cd8f449978f3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/991c3868c66e78ac66e1ce5e3c1cd8f449978f3d"}],"sha":"4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/4761a224f654d02a8d493dac006c852995b74ae8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/991c3868c66e78ac66e1ce5e3c1cd8f449978f3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:47:28Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:47:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(client): keep the hot and live-reload page-url parameters working (#2465)\n\n* fix(client): keep the hot and live-reload page-url parameters working\n\n`apply` replaced the `hot` and `live-reload` booleans, and with them the\npage-url parameters a single tab used to opt out through. A page asking\n`?<prefix>-hot=false` or `?<prefix>-live-reload=false` was silently ignored.\n\nThey narrow the mode in force again, so `hot=false` on a page set to `hmr`\nkeeps the reload, and `apply` in the url wins over them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* docs: say the two replaced page-url parameters still work\n\nThe client options section said only apply can be set per page, which the\nsection on opting one page out now contradicts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5e694adc434812e700470f82d54291b511692af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/a5e694adc434812e700470f82d54291b511692af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/991c3868c66e78ac66e1ce5e3c1cd8f449978f3d","verification":{"payload":"tree a5e694adc434812e700470f82d54291b511692af\nparent e7f53800cc1ef8702954d29f018352479f9a40d8\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1791280048 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791280048 +0300\n\nfix(client): keep the hot and live-reload page-url parameters working (#2465)\n\n* fix(client): keep the hot and live-reload page-url parameters working\n\n`apply` replaced the `hot` and `live-reload` booleans, and with them the\npage-url parameters a single tab used to opt out through. A page asking\n`?<prefix>-hot=false` or `?<prefix>-live-reload=false` was silently ignored.\n\nThey narrow the mode in force again, so `hot=false` on a page set to `hmr`\nkeeps the reload, and `apply` in the url wins over them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* docs: say the two replaced page-url parameters still work\n\nThe client options section said only apply can be set per page, which the\nsection on opting one page out now contradicts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxMOwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWH8QACwkMStnVW9ToXnOV6rCvPp3\nUCXBvGSxe7g8WsGxD5TbD5b2esWKCIQlKzqZXdW+r946tzr75f8t/qUc2YELwqdc\nwD2mKB+iz7RI+41DblD4vDMqR+B62CTfgcGfZgm73+6EK5BcE4SB8fAaS2v5Sw6u\nBmY