998c6","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDcxN2E0MzZjOTI4ZWVjMjM2MmIxMTQxMjVlZGVjNTVhOWNiOTk4YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46","sha":"cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46"}],"sha":"717a436c928eec2362b114125edec55a9cb998c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/717a436c928eec2362b114125edec55a9cb998c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:38:41Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:38:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(client): format one of webpack''s problems, wherever it is read (#2438)\n\nThe overlay took formatted strings only. The middleware formats its own\npayloads on the server, so its client never needed anything else — but a\nserver that sends webpack''s error objects to the browser and formats them\nthere had to write that formatting itself, which is what webpack-dev-server\ncarried a client file for.\n\n`showProblems` now takes an error object as it comes, and the formatting is\n`webpack-dev-middleware/client/problem`: `problemLocation`, `problemBody`,\n`problemLine` and `formatProblem`, the last splitting a problem into the\nheader and body a console wants.\n\nThe server''s own `formatErrors` builds the same shape, so a build reads the\nsame way whether the middleware formatted it or a server sent the object over.\nTwo things it got wrong fall out of that:\n\n  * An error webpack names no module for sent a first line holding a single\n    space. The overlay reads the first line as the heading, so it drew one\n    with nothing in it. The message goes alone now.\n  * A module built by loaders reports its whole request as `moduleName`\n    (`babel-loader!./app.js`), which reads as noise where the file is what\n    matters. The file comes first, the request follows it, and `file` is used\n    when webpack sets one — once, not appended to itself.\n\nA unit test asserts the two formatters agree on every shape rather than\ntrusting them to.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ae96788beb398fbcf3f9cfbaecd6738034a0c13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/6ae96788beb398fbcf3f9cfbaecd6738034a0c13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ae96788beb398fbcf3f9cfbaecd6738034a0c13\nparent d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790764721 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790764721 +0300\n\nfeat(client): format one of webpack''s problems, wherever it is read (#2438)\n\nThe overlay took formatted strings only. The middleware formats its own\npayloads on the server, so its client never needed anything else — but a\nserver that sends webpack''s error objects to the browser and formats them\nthere had to write that formatting itself, which is what webpack-dev-server\ncarried a client file for.\n\n`showProblems` now takes an error object as it comes, and the formatting is\n`webpack-dev-middleware/client/problem`: `problemLocation`, `problemBody`,\n`problemLine` and `formatProblem`, the last splitting a problem into the\nheader and body a console wants.\n\nThe server''s own `formatErrors` builds the same shape, so a build reads the\nsame way whether the middleware formatted it or a server sent the object over.\nTwo things it got wrong fall out of that:\n\n  * An error webpack names no module for sent a first line holding a single\n    space. The overlay reads the first line as the heading, so it drew one\n    with nothing in it. The message goes alone now.\n  * A module built by loaders reports its whole request as `moduleName`\n    (`babel-loader!./app.js`), which reads as noise where the file is what\n    matters. The file comes first, the request follows it, and `file` is used\n    when webpack sets one — once, not appended to itself.\n\nA unit test asserts the two formatters agree on every shape rather than\ntrusting them to.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvOaxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmckQAITTiJkHhF8DuJC1/RR4s2V/\nRt+xybsszON8+3NW2IYkU+lcKa69teu/POyBOuKpiFzYbrCVjD3XUlkt58hzwgck\nLQXDFn2ZY+Kmfv3OjnxPPC3Bq02RnHboZwttyViGt5Tjb60LPZueRZW/99Dpe1Eq\nbwkOOPtwkifjTLfsH2DUOsb0uoCpuXsOl/SlwVNli3dq1p7R92MM87n2/yGBXLJL\nfwLTsjLXpxudqjC/c/nnOtkvDfvkGYmaCkP+cS8oV4sGawW8vKV/II2432J7X/hm\nZuy7r/0cdhWl4QWOUxEDIk24dMn9Db2kyVIcEE7ceu2yZUB1eQvae4Kdjil3MLmW\nlG0BgVku5eE/Uh6BGRdx6CXjqY1DVPairXtyL+yWy8dkJqaUnfYSpGRefiJZZxWx\nlCB9sXJHC/EtvRn7Y/I7VxTPregwQlGkj7ug50w7sO0Ku1cafxUihrEOSSl0ymQA\nU1qAmrdOfCSI+Bs58xuET6CKnvX3RmY3WjyHWRe7AoxdLWG4tMNdb5MRScMwLJkx\nSdrec+LuLaRjMO54huxzTXZABd5iIR3AmXZOYLt8MbFMlhFlW3/5D7qqyDj08+5R\nzNMWYzvIKr+9Mf13A8PAKsaPV0hjwBvG/a8BA7vatOQBvvb9gKG/aMv2KyaimOxi\nQK7YNuHztznLt0Smjmrm\n=agMa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T10:38:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGNjMGIyNDQ4Yzg0NWFhMjMxZDhmZWY1OTNkZGJkY2FmMDljZjNkNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1","sha":"d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1"}],"sha":"cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/cc0b2448c845aa231d8fef593ddbdcaf09cf3d46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:00:03Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:00:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(client): an empty overlay, and an indicator that never left (#2437)\n\nTwo states the page could get stuck in.\n\nAn overlay with nothing in it, covering the app, dismissable only by hand.\nA source reporting an empty list of problems is how a source says it has\nnothing, but it was kept as a slot, so the union of every source''s problems\nwas non-empty and the card mounted empty. Worse once another source cleared:\nthe card stayed, showing only its dismiss hint, on page `-1`. An empty list\nis now the source having nothing, and the overlay closes when no source has\nanything left. The bundled client guards its own call sites, so this is\nreached through `webpack-dev-middleware/client/overlay`, which is a published\nexport.\n\nA building indicator that stayed up for good after a multi-compiler build.\nA progress payload carries no compilation name, so the client attributed it to\nwhichever compilation most recently started building — and in a multi-compiler\nbuild a payload from a still-running compilation could re-mark a sibling that\nhad already finished, and would never report again, as building. Progress now\nreports on the build that is running (`indicator.update`) rather than starting\none, so the badge goes away once every compilation that started has reported\nback.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24f9376212970314e1b1238208033929e9f57fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/24f9376212970314e1b1238208033929e9f57fbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1","verification":{"payload":"tree 24f9376212970314e1b1238208033929e9f57fbd\nparent f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790758803 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790758803 +0300\n\nfix(client): an empty overlay, and an indicator that never left (#2437)\n\nTwo states the page could get stuck in.\n\nAn overlay with nothing in it, covering the app, dismissable only by hand.\nA source reporting an empty list of problems is how a source says it has\nnothing, but it was kept as a slot, so the union of every source''s problems\nwas non-empty and the card mounted empty. Worse once another source cleared:\nthe card stayed, showing only its dismiss hint, on page `-1`. An empty list\nis now the source having nothing, and the overlay closes when no source has\nanything left. The bundled client guards its own call sites, so this is\nreached through `webpack-dev-middleware/client/overlay`, which is a published\nexport.\n\nA building indicator that stayed up for good after a multi-compiler build.\nA progress payload carries no compilation name, so the client attributed it to\nwhichever compilation most recently started building — and in a multi-compiler\nbuild a payload from a still-running compilation could re-mark a sibling that\nhad already finished, and would never report again, as building. Progress now\nreports on the build that is running (`indicator.update`) rather than starting\none, so the badge goes away once every compilation that started has reported\nback.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvM+TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4W8QAGg0ibGgxtGqxx+0tkKOKk7h\n5gG5gkFrLqDbm7TUWjiu91ksMKDWvX+a33XBYMLJWdxDvOmzlI5qnEgL3HLvJRGh\nlVeoLPHecMdFGDZtoCWWESVoBvnYc50m/967T1rEsGMGQqgvuZYafo7l/APjS4u+\nsoZ0IZIz9AFCzYnpMygtpwWnB77TsfNz1uZ2hFBfT4iLipItvhbaKvJ2IFQQGprC\nOwSUXRheKsekgxrnpSMbJJvnek0aKaKdfmx7K5S9J7YRrIcBGgafrBLSPuYhq20l\nkpch/W1vRcpOykqYGAyfebvGtw3c/K7pkfD/4w6trtlgQHmaBA9pyIJaOhsXkIu2\nruGwjsU5+F0HRevpb1tJ8uayywuN7BuGpLtSDgmvTojE4J4XN5/D8ALVuECRlqV+\n3BRG05MbcA65eawPlbGyNcRFdDyIbKJd4Bf6d5oF48t7gpglGYQRz/1zRfhxyi3H\n0kEJuB+/VCnm9mAvDONebINWg2lIZ8yTaudp2EMvqlagD7jgQFgyz03iNWfqoHgX\nNr3r+kbJhAUZkynu6kOgWiSFJ2MPB7qJK5RI1aIxchVopIEzH3SYdBN8W12JspoR\nVTJY8ihMhvri+d575RmnYrS+sczkAeTh80GRiONWeX16cRXqccyCfnWEhKhuKMEz\nQ/KWxnRlfOZkF78qU7rg\n=zYtV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T09:00:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGQ1NGU4N2QwMGE2ZGMwZjA5ZmZlNTNjNjRjZWE2ZjE3OTczYTg0ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a","sha":"f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a"}],"sha":"d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/d54e87d00a6dc0f09ffe53c64cea6f17973a84d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:54:16Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:54:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): every browser option set in node or on the query, one name each (#2436)\n\n* feat(hot): every browser option set in node or on the query\n\n`hot.client` and the injected entry''s query were two overlapping option sets\nwith a gap on each side. They are one set now.\n\n`hot`, `liveReload` and `urlPrefix` were readable from the query alone and can\nbe set in node:\n\n    middleware(compiler, {\n      hot: { client: { hot: false, liveReload: true, urlPrefix: \"my-server\" } },\n    })\n\n`transport`, `path` and `name` go the other way: the middleware set them and\nthey could not be overridden, which left no way to point a client at an\nendpoint reached through a proxy or on another origin. They are defaults now —\nthe resolved `hot.transport`, the resolved `hot.path` and the compilation''s\nname — and `hot.client` is spread over them, so nothing changes for anyone not\nsetting them.\n\n    middleware(compiler, {\n      hot: { client: { path: \"wss://dev.example.com/__webpack_hmr\" } },\n    })\n\nA `hot.transport` of your own gets a client too when `hot.client.transport`\nsays which of the two built-in protocols yours carries; without it the client\nis still yours to add. Overriding the transport without an endpoint of its own\npoints the client back at this middleware speaking the wrong protocol, so that\ncombination is warned about rather than left as a page that never connects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* refactor(client): one name per browser option, no aliases\n\nThe query had picked up two second spellings from webpack-dev-server —\n`webSocketURL` for `path` and `live-reload` for `liveReload` — and the page-url\nparameter was spelled `-live-reload` while the option it turns off is\n`liveReload`. Dropped all three: each option is one name, in `hot.client`, in\nthe entry query and in the page parameters alike. dev-server maps its own\nspellings when it moves over.\n\n`?webpack-dev-middleware-live-reload=false` is now\n`?webpack-dev-middleware-liveReload=false`, still matched case-insensitively.\nNone of this was released.\n\nAdded a test that reads the names the client acts on out of `setOverrides` and\nthe names `hot.client` accepts out of the schema, and fails unless the two\nlists are equal — an option with only one of the two spellings, or a second\nname for one setting, breaks it rather than going unnoticed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7ed20d39df8b29ad7ec78cdd795b956b344132b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/d7ed20d39df8b29ad7ec78cdd795b956b344132b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a","verification":{"payload":"tree d7ed20d39df8b29ad7ec78cdd795b956b344132b\nparent 56535c82158777b33575a2968d523aab1d2e1a4b\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790711656 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790711656 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): every browser option set in node or on the query, one name each (#2436)\n\n* feat(hot): every browser option set in node or on the query\n\n`hot.client` and the injected entry''s query were two overlapping option sets\nwith a gap on each side. They are one set now.\n\n`hot`, `liveReload` and `urlPrefix` were readable from the query alone and can\nbe set in node:\n\n    middleware(compiler, {\n      hot: { client: { hot: false, liveReload: true, urlPrefix: \"my-server\" } },\n    })\n\n`transport`, `path` and `name` go the other way: the middleware set them and\nthey could not be overridden, which left no way to point a client at an\nendpoint reached through a proxy or on another origin. They are defaults now —\nthe resolved `hot.transport`, the resolved `hot.path` and the compilation''s\nname — and `hot.client` is spread over them, so nothing changes for anyone not\nsetting them.\n\n    middleware(compiler, {\n      hot: { client: { path: \"wss://dev.example.com/__webpack_hmr\" } },\n    })\n\nA `hot.transport` of your own gets a client too when `hot.client.transport`\nsays which of the two built-in protocols yours carries; without it the client\nis still yours to add. Overriding the transport without an endpoint of its own\npoints the client back at this middleware speaking the wrong protocol, so that\ncombination is warned about rather than left as a page that never connects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* refactor(client): one name per browser option, no aliases\n\nThe query had picked up two second spellings from webpack-dev-server —\n`webSocketURL` for `path` and `live-reload` for `liveReload` — and the page-url\nparameter was spelled `-live-reload` while the option it turns off is\n`liveReload`. Dropped all three: each option is one name, in `hot.client`, in\nthe entry query and in the page parameters alike. dev-server maps its own\nspellings when it moves over.\n\n`?webpack-dev-middleware-live-reload=false` is now\n`?webpack-dev-middleware-liveReload=false`, still matched case-insensitively.\nNone of this was released.\n\nAdded a test that reads the names the client acts on out of `setOverrides` and\nthe names `hot.client` accepts out of the schema, and fails unless the two\nlists are equal — an option with only one of the two spellings, or a second\nname for one setting, breaks it rather than going unnoticed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvBdoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVnMQAKY+aJaQ+RGNudlKUQfGdi82\nJK096hZNfvmP9wuQusZ//SnIrj91PsDsFX+g+EozxGTg5qIHGPoEFPMkUcB2ZKtT\nCSmC7dgCqB4titWuffzzeWIjTnsOu7ICpn6gRaZdgOLHt700nQVXyhyXOLkk1yY2\nTepxhSeuQ8AmSPtGQ++F0M1DC2lNrWSuTZ7j2u2Z/5EmPMgoEmACnIytDu4jomwO\ngZ652IR4VTmrwJrokQo6W/4EWFnakr0e9pfShhvrYQKrUmK5/L2UCmqJ4VCbzxZn\npQdXNymptqIQb9kTHF7Qt9zEkexbJdNzlvUNqJY692wuy2jSHy+OxkKq5RC0qq7W\npQ2Pi0vr0/5MDDr0HqjYFO5AkRz8cFgmXQm7UqXH/ud9uEJqiqfSLCcUdxPCk/R7\nbDj1/Bxe1qLhbRbJTWH9GffXF/Nt5PUK+mLTyfZq6i9S7cGp3AwdC8YyjJPSlSC3\nF/pxG7We+LSyG8dhl7c3imbDu1goZ3PZB3j5aqvaWIAZhOF8VJYD3O9uRkrAlbg7\naKuiwjxvqLopMkxqc+ivtPXIRJuHidnqCtTkcNf6cl+bKTy4E/02QGJONQj2cWlj\n0qs8xjbOJtgo23zB8RmtD9SqV7QO3HhbhbepMYIMauzAb1T78cG+JLbCzf6pWp1g\nh3ruSwfCxPFccX7jYqNs\n=AW06\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T19:54:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGYzNWE1OTZjMWNmMzhhNzliY2M2N2Y1NmI4M2U0YmY3YjJiNzJhMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/56535c82158777b33575a2968d523aab1d2e1a4b","sha":"56535c82158777b33575a2968d523aab1d2e1a4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/56535c82158777b33575a2968d523aab1d2e1a4b"}],"sha":"f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/f35a596c1cf38a79bcc67f56b83e4bf7b2b72a2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/56535c82158777b33575a2968d523aab1d2e1a4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:18:58Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:18:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(hot): make two assertions that could not fail able to (#2435)\n\n* test(client): measure the worker''s survival from the worker\n\nThe assertion that an update was applied in place read a flag on the page,\nwhich a worker being torn down and started again would not have disturbed — so\nit could not have failed for the thing it was there to catch. The fixture also\nreported a `self.__startedAt` that nothing ever set, so it went as `undefined`\nevery time.\n\nThe worker now names itself once and keeps that across updates, and the two\nmessages are compared. Making the id fresh on every run, which is what a\nworker that did not survive would look like, fails all three tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(hot): cover what the injector actually does\n\n`codecov/patch` was right twice over: eight lines of `src/injectClient.js` had\nnothing running them. Most of `clientQuery` was among them — the one e2e test\nthat reaches it passes a plain option, so neither overlay branch was ever\ntaken, and the filters that travel as source were covered by nothing at all.\n\nSo `clientQuery` is unit tested now, along with the paths that only e2e went\nnear: injection turned off, a compilation no browser runs, and an `entry` that\nis a function and cannot be read.\n\nThe filter assertion rebuilds the function the way the client does and asks it\na question, rather than comparing source text — how it is spelled is the\nformatter''s business.\n\n`src/injectClient.js` goes from 76.82% to 100% of lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83677392bf3f7cac3ae5a719fc2654773195cc03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/83677392bf3f7cac3ae5a719fc2654773195cc03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/56535c82158777b33575a2968d523aab1d2e1a4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 83677392bf3f7cac3ae5a719fc2654773195cc03\nparent 66fed18c1a6f5f52df938675037a8a8fd26292f4\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790698738 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790698738 +0300\n\ntest(hot): make two assertions that could not fail able to (#2435)\n\n* test(client): measure the worker''s survival from the worker\n\nThe assertion that an update was applied in place read a flag on the page,\nwhich a worker being torn down and started again would not have disturbed — so\nit could not have failed for the thing it was there to catch. The fixture also\nreported a `self.__startedAt` that nothing ever set, so it went as `undefined`\nevery time.\n\nThe worker now names itself once and keeps that across updates, and the two\nmessages are compared. Making the id fresh on every run, which is what a\nworker that did not survive would look like, fails all three tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(hot): cover what the injector actually does\n\n`codecov/patch` was right twice over: eight lines of `src/injectClient.js` had\nnothing running them. Most of `clientQuery` was among them — the one e2e test\nthat reaches it passes a plain option, so neither overlay branch was ever\ntaken, and the filters that travel as source were covered by nothing at all.\n\nSo `clientQuery` is unit tested now, along with the paths that only e2e went\nnear: injection turned off, a compilation no browser runs, and an `entry` that\nis a function and cannot be read.\n\nThe filter assertion rebuilds the function the way the client does and asks it\na question, rather than comparing source text — how it is spelled is the\nformatter''s business.\n\n`src/injectClient.js` goes from 76.82% to 100% of lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+TyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwPwQAF+VV/tF48792MSDbJUMl2HL\npFh5V0XLy4klOhlmt0XocoC9haudPXFjRGEqYnKGBFA6895tBLc771app0oZjnCN\nv6ijt9LC46vZ9wZUqyWfzLWgpStOC3u+JmhPad7mLKLxJYcKZendy3oBX2xRX0KV\nxG0O2rCBueJXIOMRUA2yJfD16f6tfFCl1idsaGGNqFJwffmCOwVJ8Ujc4GeIsDtx\n8Os7GTQ3uYL9aaADJUML/F3GYoV4pmkoYDBxWz38ZqveY5lA7qEsEAxvGfKQ65fv\nZyP3OxDljitQOfiNmaltv7451A1pbVxxg8gGOnhGSYq4IbgjzgOdZRgqOzhV/qx7\nsUE8HwEzn1ydXScottG8Dcd8CFVAXn9yYCdrlXltp7a9W9XMrpms9/+JR5f2HhpT\n9JMs0JumI21RZvjob4J6iMTzHWH+vfyLDaABm1jezF+qdgYPpdVxfQpnFbrWMeq4\nLHPdaXEfG/saPZyZtj4gRD6+M3fgtUR/vg3X/Kylzl7RzQ6R1fwiumbWbyry2vNj\nmheCwSFNtY4laAtVivqyssI3YUhOI+MThn8ur9+2x1uEZ8WzbUQzk+FPvnjyNxFc\nftqjWgePxTd8e5lisJW8CHtpn98xj/SvFwCwaJOrLB0ZbhINTlwwef6TonyZlkYY\ncwfpZJwDm5/LiVav02+e\n=+9rV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:18:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserc