ode_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/66fed18c1a6f5f52df938675037a8a8fd26292f4","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDY2ZmVkMThjMWE2ZjVmNTJkZjkzODY3NTAzN2E4YThmZDI2MjkyZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389","sha":"1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389"}],"sha":"66fed18c1a6f5f52df938675037a8a8fd26292f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/66fed18c1a6f5f52df938675037a8a8fd26292f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:01:09Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:01:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): set the client''s options on the middleware (#2432)\n\n* feat(hot): set the client''s options on the middleware\n\nThe runtime''s options could only be written as a query string on an entry\npath, which the `hot` option now creates itself — so enabling `hot` meant\ngiving up the ability to configure the client at all.\n\n`hot.client` takes them in node, next to the rest of the hot configuration,\nand the injected entry carries them over. `overlay` takes the same object as\nthe query, filter functions included: a function cannot travel as JSON, so it\ngoes as its source, the same encoding webpack-dev-server has always used.\n\n`transport`, `path` and `name` stay out of it. The middleware knows all three\nand sets them itself, so the runtime cannot be pointed somewhere the server is\nnot listening, and in a multi-compiler build each bundle''s client is told the\nname of its own compilation — without it a page shows an overlay for a build\nerror in code it does not contain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(hot): cover the middleware''s own onConnect and handleUpgrade\n\n`codecov/patch` failed on five lines in `src/index.js`, and it was right: the\ntwo methods this adds to the middleware instance had no test. What was covered\nwas `createHot`''s pair, reached directly — so the wrappers that the README\ntells people to call, including what they answer with `hot` off, were never\nrun by anything.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(client): cover the two paths the coverage gate found\n\n`codecov/patch` failed on one line, which is fair: the camel-cased\n`liveReload` query spelling had no test, though it is the one an option set on\nthe middleware in node serializes to. There is one now.\n\nThe guard in `turnedOffByUrl` was the other candidate — unreachable in a\nbrowser, where `self` always exists. It is an expression rather than an early\nreturn now, so the safety stays without a statement that nothing can execute.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): serialize an overlay filter the client can rebuild\n\nThree from review.\n\nA method shorthand — `overlay: { errors(message) {} }` — stringifies to\n`errors(message) {}`, which is not an expression, and the client assigns what\narrives after `var callback = `. It threw there, in a page, for a mistake made\nin a configuration file. It is made into a function expression now, and\nanything that still cannot be serialized is refused when the middleware is\ncreated, naming the option.\n\n`hot.client.timeout: 0` passed the schema and was then ignored by the client,\nwhich takes a timeout only when it is above zero. The schema says so now.\n\nAnd the multi-compiler test waited four seconds for a sibling''s build rather\nthan for a sign it had arrived, so it could have passed before a broken client\nhad the chance to fail. The client logs a build before it looks at the name,\nwhich is exactly the signal, so it waits for that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d7bf2ead9a6956b8e057f9694ccc89f13c14a95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/5d7bf2ead9a6956b8e057f9694ccc89f13c14a95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d7bf2ead9a6956b8e057f9694ccc89f13c14a95\nparent a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790694069 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790694069 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): set the client''s options on the middleware (#2432)\n\n* feat(hot): set the client''s options on the middleware\n\nThe runtime''s options could only be written as a query string on an entry\npath, which the `hot` option now creates itself — so enabling `hot` meant\ngiving up the ability to configure the client at all.\n\n`hot.client` takes them in node, next to the rest of the hot configuration,\nand the injected entry carries them over. `overlay` takes the same object as\nthe query, filter functions included: a function cannot travel as JSON, so it\ngoes as its source, the same encoding webpack-dev-server has always used.\n\n`transport`, `path` and `name` stay out of it. The middleware knows all three\nand sets them itself, so the runtime cannot be pointed somewhere the server is\nnot listening, and in a multi-compiler build each bundle''s client is told the\nname of its own compilation — without it a page shows an overlay for a build\nerror in code it does not contain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(hot): cover the middleware''s own onConnect and handleUpgrade\n\n`codecov/patch` failed on five lines in `src/index.js`, and it was right: the\ntwo methods this adds to the middleware instance had no test. What was covered\nwas `createHot`''s pair, reached directly — so the wrappers that the README\ntells people to call, including what they answer with `hot` off, were never\nrun by anything.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(client): cover the two paths the coverage gate found\n\n`codecov/patch` failed on one line, which is fair: the camel-cased\n`liveReload` query spelling had no test, though it is the one an option set on\nthe middleware in node serializes to. There is one now.\n\nThe guard in `turnedOffByUrl` was the other candidate — unreachable in a\nbrowser, where `self` always exists. It is an expression rather than an early\nreturn now, so the safety stays without a statement that nothing can execute.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): serialize an overlay filter the client can rebuild\n\nThree from review.\n\nA method shorthand — `overlay: { errors(message) {} }` — stringifies to\n`errors(message) {}`, which is not an expression, and the client assigns what\narrives after `var callback = `. It threw there, in a page, for a mistake made\nin a configuration file. It is made into a function expression now, and\nanything that still cannot be serialized is refused when the middleware is\ncreated, naming the option.\n\n`hot.client.timeout: 0` passed the schema and was then ignored by the client,\nwhich takes a timeout only when it is above zero. The schema says so now.\n\nAnd the multi-compiler test waited four seconds for a sibling''s build rather\nthan for a sign it had arrived, so it could have passed before a broken client\nhad the chance to fail. The client logs a build before it looks at the name,\nwhich is exactly the signal, so it waits for that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu9K1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6zYQABAp4tsnybljoo2e5pSk0DBj\nDPk3Ca5VTmhxVdqr7aZeVyITS3O03gzDbI/YzfuVAftabzbSP+VXxQW8vqk/LgGu\nOyYst0vd49zIzVPOYp6S6fUHaaboiGwav0mlLmeV5mgb2vXG1dzzAaLW4uCK0yrz\ngijFVUQTHY8HW+GQj9i4NkzO7rEWCBxPPuelwORkdoyWtcWlCFEN5irc+Soaj2in\nU9InUQlEfEoiWBXxeyK2jSKmFyGIyCgzTmWD6IbAiW1j4IgS0yMqGgXDcyHQs946\nyKzc1GcEumz1KynPumCdnKWG5xFM85X8swnSthjdt5RNoolumbFIyygo3PoEap/R\nPBmT0rM81INCksto7CXL4PzLX3V6FgMM5wg9YdPaYjAIgZsKEfLqApiHmgYZ/wJV\ngY0L3+kcIvb7ceNgGcdtmmulhxwT6Zshneq6sdhp5UGYYb7/PXfySiJD9OCZmwI+\nfoYY8X7JOSiOqtmtgFz8adBja0pKhMUDiSSwkNKK/YhXZRcw/xEvo9f6fyY7ONgO\nK/Vz+yZdiI0P0uUsGtpGa4OCqeANqgaseGCaklZ556ZmdgJ10UEGEpjZLvzOnlqW\nBt6tOSF+P7xPgiYkhTYQv6+97PIqT0cOQURzQWktMNyUbJeSjdP4nYSBnuYMncam\nPOo0g5Bvljb0/A7ujHR2\n=01iR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:01:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDE1NjlkZDA3ZWI5MmI1MTRhMzE0MmM3NTAwZDVjMjgzNDE4NTIzODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130","sha":"a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130"}],"sha":"1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/1569dd07eb92b514a3142c7500d5c28341852389"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:36:48Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:36:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): let a server decide who may listen (#2431)\n\n* feat(hot): let a server decide who may listen\n\nThe middleware knew two things a server needs to apply its own rules about\nconnections and kept both to itself: `onConnect` dropped the request before\ncalling back, in both transports, and the only way to serve WebSocket clients\nwas `attach`, which takes the server''s `upgrade` event and answers every\nhandshake on the path.\n\n`onConnect(fn)` now calls `fn(client, req)`, and subscribers run before the\ncatch-up sync, so a client closed there is sent nothing at all rather than\nbeing hung up on after the fact. `handleUpgrade(req, socket, head)` answers a\nsingle upgrade for a server that keeps its own listener, and returns whether\nthe request was this endpoint''s, so one that is not can be passed on.\n\nNo rule about who may connect comes with them. That belongs to whoever owns\nthe server; this is the middleware handing over what it knows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): survive a connect subscriber that closes the middleware\n\nA subscriber is arbitrary code, and closing the middleware from one is a\nreasonable thing for it to do — but `close()` drops the stream, and the\ncatch-up that follows the subscribers then published through nothing.\n\nAlso says in the README that the example reads `Host`, which is the server\nthat was asked for and not the page doing the asking. A rule usually wants\nboth, so the example now shows both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* docs(hot): say what a connect rule can and cannot be built from\n\n`Origin` is something a browser sends on a page''s behalf, and anything that is\nnot a browser can leave it out or send whatever it likes. Useful for keeping\nother pages out of a development server, not a way to know who is connecting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc32c42199ca06b1cd1b8da3bc935593bb93ea79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/cc32c42199ca06b1cd1b8da3bc935593bb93ea79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130","verification":{"payload":"tree cc32c42199ca06b1cd1b8da3bc935593bb93ea79\nparent 818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790642208 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790642208 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): let a server decide who may listen (#2431)\n\n* feat(hot): let a server decide who may listen\n\nThe middleware knew two things a server needs to apply its own rules about\nconnections and kept both to itself: `onConnect` dropped the request before\ncalling back, in both transports, and the only way to serve WebSocket clients\nwas `attach`, which takes the server''s `upgrade` event and answers every\nhandshake on the path.\n\n`onConnect(fn)` now calls `fn(client, req)`, and subscribers run before the\ncatch-up sync, so a client closed there is sent nothing at all rather than\nbeing hung up on after the fact. `handleUpgrade(req, socket, head)` answers a\nsingle upgrade for a server that keeps its own listener, and returns whether\nthe request was this endpoint''s, so one that is not can be passed on.\n\nNo rule about who may connect comes with them. That belongs to whoever owns\nthe server; this is the middleware handing over what it knows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): survive a connect subscriber that closes the middleware\n\nA subscriber is arbitrary code, and closing the middleware from one is a\nreasonable thing for it to do — but `close()` drops the stream, and the\ncatch-up that follows the subscribers then published through nothing.\n\nAlso says in the README that the example reads `Host`, which is the server\nthat was asked for and not the page doing the asking. A rule usually wants\nboth, so the example now shows both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* docs(hot): say what a connect rule can and cannot be built from\n\n`Origin` is something a browser sends on a page''s behalf, and anything that is\nnot a browser can leave it out or send whatever it likes. Useful for keeping\nother pages out of a development server, not a way to know who is connecting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquwggCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbfQQAFF5UVnhXAQONOLAHhNIZGwX\n0gkf6vkbLD60VfBu3FaHLFBknGMuoxLYPkGWlkHHn69yV40uGGoQuM/0shDm29ih\nnd+rv1rE7rqcDjqG3G666MYqO3zEGz7ZB9TAC1PShLvPFZhDtmxQouXwg7SkQXSj\nlpNO9A0vIw078GVKbL0MmEjuOKNH7RCgnZUe9BioQrtnQpUxe4fLEiTiNWCKH4XS\nvRj7FxZoVq5Q8tu+yql3khpYtnIA5sFRSiUWHXJAZkqqVe6STb6pUWrnXuaRJ5w8\nrdayA7L/GUv75/jsc2vKMrIy4vrs0ob+lOpCJjV/AoAfKhK92WYejky1asIpVOsG\nmVMKf4lR/cyR6W34HNLT4Z//37czTBW4KGe7qtFUJtxyYngIn+UpPZjIJq6eGWmO\nkegobnAwKun/v5PoSiDut4fg34AY7qiSnNzarweknICdnh0sIGZ5j51+w1cpWvP8\nd4ocpVd2WXipSwDrdrZ1QuRvyNyRNyYVzM2SOyvZ/zDNWDA5UZE/Bj8HvhWi3PtM\n6ovJYSrd320n72aEsHWiFkVgLk4DvKnv0fLSbX7x38cVyLQUWrjFfh/bWYAEfY49\n/NWtVP9i0MAUG7E9HUu3w8Y8penGFsk7N42RRkPEg+3a7Pf2IUrBWidjqO/6RTD7\n1NobooAbQLsD3y3f6U1n\n=fZoZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T00:36:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGE1OGRiNjVkYTczOTE4ZjUzODdhMjVjYjgzNmQwZDE5MTUzZmYxMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b","sha":"818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b"}],"sha":"a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/a58db65da73918f5387a25cb836d0d19153ff130"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:35:16Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:35:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(client): keep a page current without Hot Module Replacement (#2433)\n\n* feat(client): keep a page current without Hot Module Replacement\n\nThe client had one way to apply a build, and a project without\n`HotModuleReplacementPlugin` got an error telling it to add one. A page can\nalso be brought up to date by loading it again, which is all some projects\nwant, and the only thing that works for a change no compilation knows about.\n\n`hot` says whether a build is applied as an update. `live-reload` reloads the\npage on a build that changed something when it is not — a `sync` is left alone,\nsince it reports what the page is already running. Both default to `true`, so\nHot Module Replacement stays what happens unless it is turned off.\n\nA `reload` action reloads every page on demand, whatever those two are set to,\nfor a file served from disk or anything else no compilation can report.\n\n`urlPrefix` names the page-url parameters that turn either off for a single\npage, so a server built on this middleware keeps the ones its users know.\n\n`live-reload` was accepted as another spelling of `reload` and now means what\nit says: `reload` is the fallback for an update that was tried and could not be\napplied, which is a different question. It was never released under the old\nmeaning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): read the page-url opt-out as a parameter, not as text\n\nSearching `location.search` for the text of a parameter was wrong three ways:\n`?note=webpack-dev-middleware-hot=false` carries the words without being the\nparameter, `…-hot=falsehood` begins with `false` without being it, and the\nsearch was lowercased while the configured prefix was not, so a `urlPrefix`\nwith any capital in it never matched at all.\n\nThe query is parsed now — by the same parser the resource query goes through,\nso it is no stricter about encoding than the rest of the client. The name is\ncompared whole and case-insensitively on both sides, and only the value\n`false` turns anything off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec4df69c28129739bc764ea52587baa8935f7236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/ec4df69c28129739bc764ea52587baa8935f7236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b","verification":{"payload":"tree ec4df69c28129739bc764ea52587baa8935f7236\nparent 00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790642116 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790642116 +0300\n\nfeat(client): keep a page current without Hot Module Replacement (#2433)\n\n* feat(client): keep a page current without Hot Module Replacement\n\nThe client had one way to apply a build, and a project without\n`HotModuleReplacementPlugin` got an error telling it to add one. A page can\nalso be brought up to date by loading it again, which is all some projects\nwant, and the only thing that works for a change no compilation knows about.\n\n`hot` says whether a build is applied as an update. `live-reload` reloads the\npage on a build that changed something when it is not — a `sync` is left alone,\nsince it reports what the page is already running. Both default to `true`, so\nHot Module Replacement stays what happens unless it is turned off.\n\nA `reload` action reloads every page on demand, whatever those two are set to,\nfor a file served from disk or anything else no compilation can report.\n\n`urlPrefix` names the page-url parameters that turn either off for a single\npage, so a server built on this middleware keeps the ones its users know.\n\n`live-reload` was accepted as another spelling of `reload` and now means what\nit says: `reload` is the fallback for an update that was tried and could not be\napplied, which is a different question. It was never released under the old\nmeaning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): read the page-url opt-out as a parameter, not as text\n\nSearching `location.search` for the text of a parameter was wrong three ways:\n`?note=webpack-dev-middleware-hot=false` carries the words without being the\nparameter, `…-hot=falsehood` begins with `false` without being it, and the\nsearch was lowercased while the configured prefix was not, so a `urlPrefix`\nwith any capital in it never matched at all.\n\nThe query is parsed now — by the same parser the resource query goes through,\nso it is no stricter about encoding than the rest of the client. The name is\ncompared whole and case-insensitively on both sides, and only the value\n`false` turns anything off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquwfECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe5cQAGLHAX/ibccLYgiNezrS3MQF\no1jpEgrJOPJkfHLC3SDcD01jSDe6IUyo1RKCc6672GAySCnFWJ5d4mS7vgQwSqkX\nMzXa61s46QoQKWmivq8rETJUVUt4ojMdkiI/FXGlLpmj41nfgu9KESmRCxBLgDF6\nfQtnYgIAdOW0ZkvV84vsOzRZKy4RQ0C5fHZxjKdPpT0ute2uedOWctRiuPLr0wVd\nrRBRrJ4+aUyk0InjU705nZujir7Smi9+bbQcyqhogzN0/qWeb32h4pj9gJ2RHqKT\n8DdfTPDc9rpWAmT2ljQ77TbCihmfR13rtriXJDa7hIFG4gzf/eJvWyNrwMMsSXJA\nBu8pdhzESXA0nZJfpMNXFmmsfYYOa0A8riE/NTS1L7UTSv80JPZ4k80L1VcJBMWp\n6hvKGFNzCjHIQO4pGUpeCp8eEp1LvkKChcQ8BVdxBjmL1EDb1/DC5axirq7F5JAX\nwVBJ5fZJAndvb3HKjEcHiMQSjKAg577t65uxFgDsZFVkwoE7FpfEmSJhAt4WHD9F\n/p7vzVuFqwxBv0bunrShGhGdyVK6Hez754+zyVxPKHMVDez1sxVansg6JAzBvcS0\n4j9cdvdnVEN6qoytMn2V4wvLjMfnrPQdIKVpHltWe3aHsbc1ZU9BZy0nrLGVPrTA\nOwjdh+CFRpVZ+IE1s1EL\n=sqG8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T00:35:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDgxOGVmZDgxZjE0ODU0OWQyNWI5MTgzOTUwMTAzNTA2NjJhNDkxNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c","sha":"00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c"}],"sha":"818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/818efd81f148549d25b918395010350662a4916b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T23:36:43Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T23:36:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): put the client into the compilation (#2430)\n\n* feat(hot): put the client into the compilation\n\nUntil now `hot` served the endpoint and left the rest to the developer: add\n`webpack-dev-middleware/client` to `entry`, apply\n`HotModuleReplacementPlugin`, and keep the client''s query in step with the\nmiddleware''s options by hand. That is three places to get right for a\nfeature whose whole promise is that it works.\n\n`hot` does all of it now. Installing the middleware and turning the option\non is enough — nothing in the webpack configuration changes. The client is\ngiven the endpoint and the transport the middleware resolved, through its\nresource query, so the two agree by construction rather than by the same\nvalue being written twice.\n\nDeliberately careful in three places:\n\n  * a configuration that already has the client as an entry is left alone,\n    so following the old documentation still works and does not produce two\n    copies. The check reads the `entry` shapes it can; a function, an alias\n    or a loader can hide the request, which costs a duplicate entry rather\n    than a broken build, and `hot.inject: false` is the way out;\n  * nothing is injected into a compilation that does not target a browser,\n    which is what `platform`, or `target` before webpack 5.96, is for;\n  * `HotModuleReplacementPlugin` is added only when absent, and its presence\n    is reported rather than ignored.\n\nOne behaviour follows from this: `hot` now implies a hot runtime, so a\ncompilation that has one is no longer reachable by simply omitting the\nplugin. `test/e2e/process-update.test.js` covers what the client does\nwithout one, and now asks for that state through `hot.inject: false`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): do not add a client that cannot reach the server\n\nTwo ways the injected client could end up unable to connect.\n\nA custom `hot.transport` carries whatever protocol it was written to carry,\nand the built-in client speaks Server-Sent Events and WebSocket. It was being\ngiven `transport=sse` regardless, so it asked for a stream the transport need\nnot serve and got `426 Upgrade Required` back. No client is added in that case\nnow, and the reminder says whose job it is. `HotModuleReplacementPlugin` is\nstill applied: which transport carries the events has nothing to do with the\nruntime that applies them.\n\nThe other way round for `hasClientEntry`: it matched every request starting\nwith `webpack-dev-middleware/client`, so an entry importing `client/overlay`\n— a real export that connects to nothing — looked like the client and the\nreal one was never added. It now matches the client itself, with or without a\nquery.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* refactor(hot): decide the target on `platform` alone, and document it\n\n`isWebTarget` opened with a fallback for webpack without `compiler.platform`,\nwhich no supported version is: it is set in the `Compiler` constructor, and the\npeer range starts at ^5.101.0. Removed.\n\nThe clause after it looked equally redundant and is not. `platform.universal`\narrived in webpack 5.108, so on 5.101 to 5.107 a universal target reports\n`universal: undefined` and is recognized only by `web` and `node` both being\nnull — which `target: false` also is, hence the guard for it. Kept, with a TODO\nto drop it when the peer range starts at ^5.108.0. Worth noting CI runs the\nlatest webpack only, so that path is not covered there.\n\nTests now pin the verdict for every target webpack resolves a platform from,\nand for the project that wired the client and the plugin up itself before\neither was injected for it: neither is added twice, and a project that had the\nclient without the plugin now gets one.\n\nThe README led with a configuration that added the entry and the plugin by\nhand. It now leads with the option on its own, and says which compilations get\nthe runtime, what changes for a project that wired it up itself, and the two\ncases that want `hot.inject: false`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): leave web workers out, and type the transport properly\n\nThe client connects from its bootstrap only inside `typeof window !==\n\"undefined\"`, and a worker has none — so `target: \"webworker\"` was being given\na client it could never join with, in every worker bundle. Left out until the\nclient can connect without a `window`, with a TODO saying so. Only the worker\ntarget itself: a universal target that includes `webworker` reports `null`\nthere and still runs in a browser.\n\n`transport` was typed `string | EXPECTED_ANY`, which is `any` — a typed caller\ncould pass anything. It now takes the same union `hot.transport` does, which\nimmediately caught what the loose type was hiding: the entry query was built\nfrom a transport that may be a function, and `URLSearchParams` does not take\none. Harmless, since a custom transport never reached that entry, but it is\nnow built where the type is known to be a string.\n\nAlso says plainly that `hot.inject: false` drops the plugin along with the\nclient, rather than only silencing the reminder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): leave Deno out for the same reason as workers\n\nwebpack counts `deno` as a `web` platform, so it was getting a client — and\nDeno removed `window` in 2.0, which is the one thing the client''s bootstrap\nneeds to connect. Same shape as the worker case, so the two are now excluded\ntogether and the reason is stated once, with the TODO on the client rather\nthan on the list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): find the client by path, and per entry point\n\nTwo ways a page ended up with no client at all — the opposite of the duplicate\nthe check exists to prevent.\n\nThe client was recognized by how a request ends, so a project''s own\n`./src/client/index.js` — an ordinary application entry, and a common one —\nwas read as this package''s client and injection was skipped. Requests are now\nresolved and compared against the client''s actual paths.\n\nAnd the answer was for the whole compilation: one entry point having the\nclient meant none of the others got one. They are separate pages, so a build\nwith `landing` and `dashboard` where only `landing` had it left `dashboard`\nconnecting to nothing. Entry points are now answered one at a time — a single\nentry for all of them when none has one, named entries for the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* feat(client): run in a web worker\n\nThe client connected only where there was a `window`, so it did nothing at all\nin a worker. A worker has no `window`, but it has `EventSource`, `WebSocket`\nand webpack''s runtime, which is everything an update needs — so the client\nreads `self`, the same object as `window` in a page and the only one in a\nworker.\n\nThe overlay and the building indicator stay behind `document`, which a worker\ndoes not have. The WebSocket client resolved a relative url with an anchor\nelement and now uses `URL` where there is no document. A reload cannot happen\nfrom inside a worker at all — there is no `location.reload` there — so that\nfallback says so once and leaves the page that started the worker to do it.\n\n`test/e2e/worker.test.js` runs the client in a real worker over both\ntransports and applies an update to it in place; both fail against the\nprevious bootstrap.\n\nInjection into `target: \"webworker\"` is left for the next major release, since\nit changes what every worker bundle contains. The TODO says so, and the\nexclusion no longer claims the client cannot run there, because it can.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* feat(hot): give web worker compilations a client too\n\nHeld back for the next major on the grounds that it changes what worker\nbundles contain — which this option already does to every browser bundle, so\nthat was not a reason. Tried it instead: a `webworker` configuration with no\nclient entry and no plugin, hot from the middleware alone, connects and takes\nan update in place. `test/e2e/worker.test.js` covers that case as well now.\n\nDeno keeps its own TODO: no `window` there either, and nothing here can say\nwhether it has the transports.\n\nBoth TODOs are a line each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5515a78466749bab7a9c889b3c02a0579acf9f67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/5515a78466749bab7a9c889b3c02a0579acf9f67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 5515a78466749bab7a9c889b3c02a0579acf9f67\nparent 236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790638603 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790638603 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): put the client into the compilation (#2430)\n\n* feat(hot): put the client into the compilation\n\nUntil now `hot` served the endpoint and left the rest to the developer: add\n`webpack-dev-middleware/client` to `entry`, apply\n`HotModuleReplacementPlugin`, and keep the client''s query in step with the\nmiddleware''s options by hand. That is three places to get right for a\nfeature whose whole promise is that it works.\n\n`hot` does all of it now. Installing the middleware and turning the option\non is enough — nothing in the webpack configuration changes. The client is\ngiven the endpoint and the transport the middleware resolved, through its\nresource query, so the two agree by construction rather than by the same\nvalue being written twice.\n\nDeliberately careful in three places:\n\n  * a configuration that already has the client as an entry is left alone,\n    so following the old documentation still works and does not produce two\n    copies. The check reads the `entry` shapes it can; a function, an alias\n    or a loader can hide the request, which costs a duplicate entry rather\n    than a broken build, and `hot.inject: false` is the way out;\n  * nothing is injected into a compilation that does not target a browser,\n    which is what `platform`, or `target` before webpack 5.96, is for;\n  * `HotModuleReplacementPlugin` is added only when absent, and its presence\n    is reported rather than ignored.\n\nOne behaviour follows from this: `hot` now implies a hot runtime, so a\ncompilation that has one is no longer reachable by simply omitting the\nplugin. `test/e2e/process-update.test.js` covers what the client does\nwithout one, and now asks for that state through `hot.inject: false`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): do not add a client that cannot reach the server\n\nTwo ways the injected client could end up unable to connect.\n\nA custom `hot.transport` carries whatever protocol it was written to carry,\nand the built-in client speaks Server-Sent Events and WebSocket. It was being\ngiven `transport=sse` regardless, so it asked for a stream the transport need\nnot serve and got `426 Upgrade Required` back. No client is added in that case\nnow, and the reminder says whose job it is. `HotModuleReplacementPlugin` is\nstill applied: which transport carries the events has nothing to do with the\nruntime that applies them.\n\nThe other way round for `hasClientEntry`: it matched every request starting\nwith `webpack-dev-middleware/client`, so an entry importing `client/overlay`\n— a real export that connects to nothing — looked like the client and the\nreal one was never added. It now matches the client itself, with or without a\nquery.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* refactor(hot): decide the target on `platform` alone, and document it\n\n`isWebTarget` opened with a fallback for webpack without `compiler.platform`,\nwhich no supported version is: it is set in the `Compiler` constructor, and the\npeer range starts at ^5.101.0. Removed.\n\nThe clause after it looked equally redundant and is not. `platform.universal`\narrived in webpack 5.108, so on 5.101 to 5.107 a universal target reports\n`universal: undefined` and is recognized only by `web` and `node` both being\nnull — which `target: false` also is, hence the guard for it. Kept, with a TODO\nto drop it when the peer range starts at ^5.108.0. Worth noting CI runs the\nlatest webpack only, so that path is not covered there.\n\nTests now pin the verdict for every target webpack resolves a platform from,\nand for the project that wired the client and the plugin up itself before\neither was injected for it: neither is added twice, and a project that had the\nclient without the plugin now gets one.\n\nThe README led with a configuration that added the entry and the plugin by\nhand. It now leads with the option on its own, and says which compilations get\nthe runtime, what changes for a project that wired it up itself, and the two\ncases that want `hot.inject: false`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): leave web workers out, and type the transport properly\n\nThe client connects from its bootstrap only inside `typeof window !==\n\"undefined\"`, and a worker has none — so `target: \"webworker\"` was being given\na client it could never join with, in every worker bundle. Left out until the\nclient can connect without a `window`, with a TODO saying so. Only the worker\ntarget itself: a universal target that includes `webworker` reports `null`\nthere and still runs in a browser.\n\n`transport` was typed `string | EXPECTED_ANY`, which is `any` — a typed caller\ncould pass anything. It now takes the same union `hot.transport` does, which\nimmediately caught what the loose type was hiding: the entry query was built\nfrom a transport that may be a function, and `URLSearchParams` does not take\none. Harmless, since a custom transport never reached that entry, but it is\nnow built where the type is known to be a string.\n\nAlso says plainly that `hot.inject: false` drops the plugin along with the\nclient, rather than only silencing the reminder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): leave Deno out for the same reason as workers\n\nwebpack counts `deno` as a `web` platform, so it was getting a client — and\nDeno removed `window` in 2.0, which is the one thing the client''s bootstrap\nneeds to connect. Same shape as the worker case, so the two are now excluded\ntogether and the reason is stated once, with the TODO on the client rather\nthan on the list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): find the client by path, and per entry point\n\nTwo ways a page ended up with no client at all — the opposite of the duplicate\nthe check exists to prevent.\n\nThe client was recognized by how a request ends, so a project''s own\n`./src/client/index.js` — an ordinary application entry, and a common one —\nwas read as this package''s client and injection was skipped. Requests are now\nresolved and compared against the client''s actual paths.\n\nAnd the answer was for the whole compilation: one entry point having the\nclient meant none of the others got one. They are separate pages, so a build\nwith `landing` and `dashboard` where only `landing` had it left `dashboard`\nconnecting to nothing. Entry points are now answered one at a time — a single\nentry for all of them when none has one, named entries for the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* feat(client): run in a web worker\n\nThe client connected only where there was a `window`, so it did nothing at all\nin a worker. A worker has no `window`, but it has `EventSource`, `WebSocket`\nand webpack''s runtime, which is everything an update needs — so the client\nreads `self`, the same object as `window` in a page and the only one in a\nworker.\n\nThe overlay and the building indicator stay behind `document`, which a worker\ndoes not have. The WebSocket client resolved a relative url with an anchor\nelement and now uses `URL` where there is no document. A reload cannot happen\nfrom inside a worker at all — there is no `location.reload` there — so that\nfallback says so once and leaves the page that started the worker to do it.\n\n`test/e2e/worker.test.js` runs the client in a real worker over both\ntransports and applies an update to it in place; both fail against the\nprevious bootstrap.\n\nInjection into `target: \"webworker\"` is left for the next major release, since\nit changes what every worker bundle contains. The TODO says so, and the\nexclusion no longer claims the client cannot run there, because it can.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* feat(hot): give web worker compilations a client too\n\nHeld back for the next major on the grounds that it changes what worker\nbundles contain — which this option already does to every browser bundle, so\nthat was not a reason. Tried it instead: a `webworker` configuration with no\nclient entry and no plugin, hot from the middleware alone, connects and takes\nan update in place. `test/e2e/worker.test.js` covers that case as well now.\n\nDeno keeps its own TODO: no `window` there either, and nothing here can say\nwhether it has the transports.\n\nBoth TODOs are a line each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquvoLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALDQQAH07ASxzJTcgYJRSneDqrOoM\nwjT3qOqK4lYbrgk2aNJ59MygRUqxATMPJf1Gc+t44dT7ZHZ0Rt6E9qPH1uNauPu/\nJZ9CHpXILOkxIdglYE6jKRXU7CksoFvnBTB3tjrSpeGzXL2lZM4zr9GARKEYK337\nSdg/oOzxMxmD+dtnMu8ndaDDFZ5KHxKrY8loUi+z4jqwNaE6L1IdJmBmOKRi40s+\nJ8bkcY0+keD9cvXUFtjJZacoW9+zhjjplsit2CvRwY5dwjTLFJLfjt02iYajOnkZ\nS+LEvqqE5uVb+A1fLif01X99+ArR6e7WKenDLt2Kvp5O0yWQsfHLR6874hGehUK4\nnEGnj0+JnK3jclX+Yv/6ZT1QWDm/Ro1nDzmAHPS5p2uIAfE6IgAZNGK0Q2dj3Bhe\n+x1TX+nTH8RYkAcwOmf8Rp8cLsZhUwT1rxEDIZ6LcvfTMA2S5CG3WAK5XelPHejC\nPWSs12VRpwE9AduOmRTM4LTGdcV9iXFs/6Y4gOGY0ajaOK2O7MVcDQqwBwGKqyXv\n8WuzrzEplWPM+03FDe5ha2ve3HGY2a6uaszg1bcdo7kbY/Ne7InOSKG3DLqsfZSY\n7gluOYns51GGb8MSASHGtGs0o9auByPW53XpbMw8m/1Jyc93365Us4xl8V/kid93\n7Zq0bR+UGxx5Du1HrEdY\n=MN77\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T23:36:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDAwNDU0ZTFkNTIyNTU4NmVhZGIxMDYxMWMwMGY0ZTI4NDYwY2FlMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0","sha":"236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0"}],"sha":"00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/00454e1d5225586eadb10611c00f4e28460cae2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:46:31Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:46:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(overlay): let the embedder name the overlay element (#2429)\n\n* feat(overlay): let the embedder name the overlay element\n\nThe element''s id is what anything outside this module finds the overlay\nby — a test, a screenshot tool, an integration that hides it. It was a\nconstant, so a package adopting this overlay in place of its own would\nrename that id for every one of its users at once.\n\nwebpack-dev-server is about to be that package, and its overlay has been\n`webpack-dev-server-client-overlay` for years. With `overlay.id` it keeps\nit, and what would have been a breaking change is a swap nobody outside\nhas to notice.\n\nRead when the element is built and not after: the overlay is one element\nshared by every copy of this module on a page, so the first copy to open\nit names it. Two copies asking for different ids is a misconfiguration\nrather than a case worth supporting, and the comment says so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(overlay): ship the types for the new overlay id option\n\nThe declarations were not regenerated after `id` was added, so it was missing\nfrom `configureOverlay`''s options and from `OverlayOptions` — a TypeScript\nembedder could not pass the option the change exists for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdf2f4c79a10a02b81c38f917cb402a14c95d0eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/bdf2f4c79a10a02b81c38f917cb402a14c95d0eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0","verification":{"payload":"tree bdf2f4c79a10a02b81c38f917cb402a14c95d0eb\nparent 96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790624791 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790624791 +0300\n\nfeat(overlay): let the embedder name the overlay element (#2429)\n\n* feat(overlay): let the embedder name the overlay element\n\nThe element''s id is what anything outside this module finds the overlay\nby — a test, a screenshot tool, an integration that hides it. It was a\nconstant, so a package adopting this overlay in place of its own would\nrename that id for every one of its users at once.\n\nwebpack-dev-server is about to be that package, and its overlay has been\n`webpack-dev-server-client-overlay` for years. With `overlay.id` it keeps\nit, and what would have been a breaking change is a swap nobody outside\nhas to notice.\n\nRead when the element is built and not after: the overlay is one element\nshared by every copy of this module on a page, so the first copy to open\nit names it. Two copies asking for different ids is a misconfiguration\nrather than a case worth supporting, and the comment says so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(overlay): ship the types for the new overlay id option\n\nThe declarations were not regenerated after `id` was added, so it was missing\nfrom `configureOverlay`''s options and from `OverlayOptions` — a TypeScript\nembedder could not pass the option the change exists for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqusQXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOu4QAApMUxk8tt8Etp0OjXaCxtf3\nQzujTgLBTJY77hqAMIOyuKesWe42+cWvv3XFNGQeBch67BSf4whXXK85KvdzOpVS\nWqi9BVPT+suQV50X03qIjOvwgSeTc8YjQnmOIkqTArUtW2uKjLmPMuxfXgXWOIbE\njXXcVI+HSnQQDQN/QPTQuN7WyNlSwQid4rYwdZg7dgXzBIL+p9CMrcQnCUeLNtM2\nMEKOG5RO0uqpdAJMcZstTNbjtjFmj68GGIpeqZyk3IELALFCfnUt9oiCoUbFKrlC\no4wZPNn4Ei5l1ozsNM1jGareEnqKbzDUAiV4ENjxRAuSy0U9YVD39/2gLsvbQAqY\nyzAQkg0ruEza29nS7PhxYAa8RDx5iV2peLjU4YxP0YK/WAUaD9iBe9JX5na2v6v6\nKLYJpJNHHCa2nDYTpeYEXDd0/EYjhmhDQ/0eEWkbj/LEVUBPZhiTC55AapqQvZ9X\nwVPMgDvbq087A6EJ43qr/9btiFUQymyW6eK5CCv4AAwBIaAet5AWrTg0u2B0sQFp\nYGfFA6kRu7MTZbcHOT2yAcA70ShpRC1tW6fkBYs9Y3o2ErFcr14zpfgJPDKmUrsP\nZyf5FZ56BLtUxwzJsCxVPPK0Q5SQp246Q5EEsn5a0ztDXa0sA2BWea51DTLoCufP\nmJxHS2crSNLPvF8fPGpf\n=Yi0l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T19:46:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDIzNmNkZTNmNTVlY2UxYWU1Y2MyNWEyNGE1N2UyN2FkYTRjNjU2ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73","sha":"96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73"}],"sha":"236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/236cde3f55ece1ae5cc25a24a57e27ada4c656d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T11:20:39Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T11:20:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(client): ship types for the client exports, and say it is ESM (#2428)\n\n* fix(client): ship types for the client exports, and say it is ESM\n\nFound while starting the webpack-dev-server side of the client move: none of\nthe five `./client/*` exports could be imported by a TypeScript consumer.\n\n`tsconfig.client.json` only ever checked the client, never emitted for it, so\nthe exports carried no `types` condition and no declarations existed to point\none at. Importing `webpack-dev-middleware/client/ws` failed outright under\n`noImplicitAny` (TS7016).\n\nDeclarations alone were not enough. The client keeps ES module syntax —\nbabel runs with `modules: false` so webpack can tree-shake it — but the\npackage is CommonJS and nothing said otherwise, so under `node16`/`nodenext`\nresolution both the code and the new declarations resolved as CommonJS and\nthe default import came back as the module namespace, which is not a\nconstructor. A nested `package.json` in `client` and `types/client` states\nwhat those directories actually contain. No published path changes, which\nmatters because `client.webSocketTransport` points at one of them.\n\nVerified from the consumer that reported it: webpack-dev-server''s\n`lint:types-client` failed on the import before, and passes against a pack of\nthis branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(build): create the client directories before marking them as ESM\n\nReview finding, and reproducible: `build` runs every `build:*` in parallel,\nso `build:types` can reach the marker script before babel has created\n`client`, and the write fails with `ENOENT`. It went unnoticed because\n`tsc` is the slower of the two here, so babel always happened to win — and\nCI happened to agree.\n\n`build:types` on its own after a `clean` fails every time rather than\noccasionally, which is what made it easy to confirm and now easy to check:\nthat sequence errored before this and exits 0 after it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27b66dc126dfcc0c312214bd5adf27499ba22ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/27b66dc126dfcc0c312214bd5adf27499ba22ee7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73","verification":{"payload":"tree 27b66dc126dfcc0c312214bd5adf27499ba22ee7\nparent 85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790508039 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790508039 +0300\n\nfix(client): ship types for the client exports, and say it is ESM (#2428)\n\n* fix(client): ship types for the client exports, and say it is ESM\n\nFound while starting the webpack-dev-server side of the client move: none of\nthe five `./client/*` exports could be imported by a TypeScript consumer.\n\n`tsconfig.client.json` only ever checked the client, never emitted for it, so\nthe exports carried no `types` condition and no declarations existed to point\none at. Importing `webpack-dev-middleware/client/ws` failed outright under\n`noImplicitAny` (TS7016).\n\nDeclarations alone were not enough. The client keeps ES module syntax —\nbabel runs with `modules: false` so webpack can tree-shake it — but the\npackage is CommonJS and nothing said otherwise, so under `node16`/`nodenext`\nresolution both the code and the new declarations resolved as CommonJS and\nthe default import came back as the module namespace, which is not a\nconstructor. A nested `package.json` in `client` and `types/client` states\nwhat those directories actually contain. No published path changes, which\nmatters because `client.webSocketTransport` points at one of them.\n\nVerified from the consumer that reported it: webpack-dev-server''s\n`lint:types-client` failed on the import before, and passes against a pack of\nthis branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(build): create the client directories before marking them as ESM\n\nReview finding, and reproducible: `build` runs every `build:*` in parallel,\nso `build:types` can reach the marker script before babel has created\n`client`, and the write fails with `ENOENT`. It went unnoticed because\n`tsc` is the slower of the two here, so babel always happened to win — and\nCI happened to agree.\n\n`build:types` on its own after a `clean` fails every time rather than\noccasionally, which is what made it easy to confirm and now easy to check:\nthat sequence errored before this and exits 0 after it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquPwHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA098QALFkLIQJ8MnFXFap9ZLLNeox\nE4xjjcsX7cGu536FOs74SGhEEcnR9BWFkHnQD1QPN6hqnY8dQFdznkdIBnaBnD+x\nRr4qk4CsIJYmuxz+V2s5r5m7oHOwMl92NAgyXUiFkyBdH5lGb3KAoKnzGoRKF3b+\nkGQgHo261BfNkIT+0J9l8GsYNzgh1Sy79vmFp6IcXFBx79HmbGip8RrgOcVqUmXh\nUo/+45L0N4/wfyzkOclN3InU+8eaLxOUh81ttQU+jbtDvtldpKoMf1orlkT1BDCz\nlC+PckoeI3olDADjFHIFndnhdQTsJ/IMXmkHJKFsrV2gBlmYb8oB84n9JfzaKjtl\nQ69cXi+fi+GpCUUanMF1xjgnzhE+emHSeDhCjJ7rD5cJSa372VaXkb32fEvRBvFo\nd7aTZWxGeW/Y8UuB+6XxuxUova3LwDZZioOFGY5SC0O6OUzA8iB+80SlaWh+PgSH\nTxA9CVdVe62PjAFC1FVkH6f5/zK4Y7gJ2uTJKFXwjTTbrcaesoNsqQSXof/qCrBY\nme9LG9LjasWbt7o/kfDDzgvPXJGz9Fwz2rHILH+JahFZSRxZ5ulTvYdksTAn4puP\nGu7REAFwtkZ+eSvNjreu+EdykSdccExVWo8RdTnW+VzJvcLQeXogPJQeOmpO8nYU\nsHhAWBHbnmU+5nOHbckd\n=bE32\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T11:20:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDk2Y2MyMTg2ODU0ODE5NzE4ZGMwNjg2M2VhNDA0ZWRkMzg5MTFiNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27","sha":"85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27"}],"sha":"96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/96cc2186854819718dc06863ea404edd38911b73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T18:59:45Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T18:59:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): ask less of a custom transport (#2427)\n\n* feat(hot): ask less of a custom transport\n\nSix required methods, of which three were only required because of how\n`createHot` happened to call them. Two of those are not a transport''s job\nat all:\n\n`handler` is meaningless unless the transport is served over HTTP. The\nbuilt-in WebSocket one carried it only to answer 426 to a plain request,\nwhich is the right answer for any transport that does not serve requests —\nso that is the default now, and the WebSocket stream no longer has a\n`handler` of its own.\n\n`hasClients` exists to skip building a payload nobody will read. That is an\noptimization a transport can make inside `publish`, and both built-ins\nalready do. A transport that does not offer it is asked to publish rather\nthan assumed to have no clients.\n\nBoth stay accepted, so a transport written against 8.3.0 keeps working, and\na TODO marks them for removal in the next major. What is required is now\n`onConnect`, `publish`, `publishTo` and `close` — and the validation names\nthat shorter set when something is missing.\n\nLeft alone deliberately: the client side keeps its class-constructor shape.\nIt is what `client.webSocketTransport` has always been, so every custom\nclient written for webpack-dev-server works here untouched; symmetry with\nthe factory is not worth breaking those.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): validate the optional methods, and keep `handler` a method\n\nTwo review findings, both regressions from making the two methods optional.\n\nDropping them from the required list stopped them being type-checked at all,\nso `handler: true` passed startup and threw from the endpoint instead —\nexactly the late, far-from-the-option failure this validation exists to\nprevent. Present and not callable is now rejected by name, while absent\nstays fine.\n\n`(eventStream.handler || upgradeRequired)(req, res)` also called the\nhandler unbound. A stream written as an object literal reaching for `this`\nworked before this change, so the call goes back to being a method call and\nthe default is a separate branch. Every other call on the stream was\nalready a method call, so only this one had lost its receiver.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(overlay): stop a second reload racing the runtime-slot assertion\n\nCI surfaced this on an unrelated PR: \"Execution context was destroyed, most\nlikely because of a navigation\".\n\nThe fixture accepts no updates, so every rebuild is a full reload, and the\nwatcher can see one write twice — file timestamp granularity is enough. The\nsecond reload lands inside the `evaluate` that triggers the next error and\ntakes its execution context with it. Nothing in the assertion is wrong; it\njust had no guarantee the page had stopped moving.\n\n`settle()` exists for this and is now awaited before the page is touched\nagain. The test predates the transport work on this branch — it came in with\n#2370 — and is not reachable from anything that work changes, but it fails\nthis branch''s CI, so it is fixed here rather than re-run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(overlay): read the recovered overlay without losing it to the reload\n\nThe red `Client` job, properly diagnosed this time. The failing test is\n\"turns an error overlay into a warning overlay on partial recovery\", not the\none the previous commit hardened — I had inferred it from the line number in\nthe stack, and for a puppeteer error jest points at the blank line between\ntests, so the name was the only reliable signal and I had grepped it away.\n\nThe race: recovering from a build that failed cannot be applied hot, so the\npage reloads. `waitForFunction` survives that, because puppeteer re-installs\nit in the new document, but the `page.evaluate` that read the overlay\nafterwards does not — and dies with \"Execution context was destroyed\" when\nthe reload lands between the two. Reproduced locally at roughly one run in\nten.\n\nWaiting and reading are now one step, through a `waitForOverlayText` helper\nthat returns the text the wait matched, with a retry for the narrower race\nwhere the navigation arrives after it resolved. The assertion still reads\nthe text, so a missing \"WARNING\" fails as a comparison rather than a\ntimeout. Twenty consecutive runs of the case, and no occurrence of the\nerror.\n\nThe `settle()` added to \"resets the runtime slot on a clean build\" in the\nprevious commit stays: that test has the same reload hazard, so guarding it\nis right even though it was not what CI was failing on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a80d4d079785459e6d33843390d03acea0a0f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/5a80d4d079785459e6d33843390d03acea0a0f76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a80d4d079785459e6d33843390d03acea0a0f76\nparent 408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790449185 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790449185 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): ask less of a custom transport (#2427)\n\n* feat(hot): ask less of a custom transport\n\nSix required methods, of which three were only required because of how\n`createHot` happened to call them. Two of those are not a transport''s job\nat all:\n\n`handler` is meaningless unless the transport is served over HTTP. The\nbuilt-in WebSocket one carried it only to answer 426 to a plain request,\nwhich is the right answer for any transport that does not serve requests —\nso that is the default now, and the WebSocket stream no longer has a\n`handler` of its own.\n\n`hasClients` exists to skip building a payload nobody will read. That is an\noptimization a transport can make inside `publish`, and both built-ins\nalready do. A transport that does not offer it is asked to publish rather\nthan assumed to have no clients.\n\nBoth stay accepted, so a transport written against 8.3.0 keeps working, and\na TODO marks them for removal in the next major. What is required is now\n`onConnect`, `publish`, `publishTo` and `close` — and the validation names\nthat shorter set when something is missing.\n\nLeft alone deliberately: the client side keeps its class-constructor shape.\nIt is what `client.webSocketTransport` has always been, so every custom\nclient written for webpack-dev-server works here untouched; symmetry with\nthe factory is not worth breaking those.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(hot): validate the optional methods, and keep `handler` a method\n\nTwo review findings, both regressions from making the two methods optional.\n\nDropping them from the required list stopped them being type-checked at all,\nso `handler: true` passed startup and threw from the endpoint instead —\nexactly the late, far-from-the-option failure this validation exists to\nprevent. Present and not callable is now rejected by name, while absent\nstays fine.\n\n`(eventStream.handler || upgradeRequired)(req, res)` also called the\nhandler unbound. A stream written as an object literal reaching for `this`\nworked before this change, so the call goes back to being a method call and\nthe default is a separate branch. Every other call on the stream was\nalready a method call, so only this one had lost its receiver.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(overlay): stop a second reload racing the runtime-slot assertion\n\nCI surfaced this on an unrelated PR: \"Execution context was destroyed, most\nlikely because of a navigation\".\n\nThe fixture accepts no updates, so every rebuild is a full reload, and the\nwatcher can see one write twice — file timestamp granularity is enough. The\nsecond reload lands inside the `evaluate` that triggers the next error and\ntakes its execution context with it. Nothing in the assertion is wrong; it\njust had no guarantee the page had stopped moving.\n\n`settle()` exists for this and is now awaited before the page is touched\nagain. The test predates the transport work on this branch — it came in with\n#2370 — and is not reachable from anything that work changes, but it fails\nthis branch''s CI, so it is fixed here rather than re-run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* test(overlay): read the recovered overlay without losing it to the reload\n\nThe red `Client` job, properly diagnosed this time. The failing test is\n\"turns an error overlay into a warning overlay on partial recovery\", not the\none the previous commit hardened — I had inferred it from the line number in\nthe stack, and for a puppeteer error jest points at the blank line between\ntests, so the name was the only reliable signal and I had grepped it away.\n\nThe race: recovering from a build that failed cannot be applied hot, so the\npage reloads. `waitForFunction` survives that, because puppeteer re-installs\nit in the new document, but the `page.evaluate` that read the overlay\nafterwards does not — and dies with \"Execution context was destroyed\" when\nthe reload lands between the two. Reproduced locally at roughly one run in\nten.\n\nWaiting and reading are now one step, through a `waitForOverlayText` helper\nthat returns the text the wait matched, with a retry for the narrower race\nwhere the navigation arrives after it resolved. The assertion still reads\nthe text, so a missing \"WARNING\" fails as a comparison rather than a\ntimeout. Twenty consecutive runs of the case, and no occurrence of the\nerror.\n\nThe `settle()` added to \"resets the runtime slot on a clean build\" in the\nprevious commit stays: that test has the same reload hazard, so guarding it\nis right even though it was not what CI was failing on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquBYhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA75IQAIrW/trDjn0CLuuNCrjwB3ZP\nztOy4oL5KS9yJ3WbLIYhLzk0KpRqMQLJmsbU0aNmdMNJKPjMa0bpu8d+UpXxc4L7\nenRHNc6y2O3XiBuMVwiaGW2Aadn3ITR1NDg2N5V7LaJBr998P2fFHzbTjKUScruk\nFmEA1hWJgB0L2GwqF9GcjdCJJkxta+Z+mEakMry/RfVYehEgOnsevU9rfT0NTCv5\nQZsfHsdx2m833C//tfVJNyZ0+3OnDycLHCI9m/yDsAbL6VRJAfVGIkMPVrshOUIk\nK0sP60Oj/6A9qVIhx9swF4O03YJ+Ms2m9pxqc4dbjxjkkcP5p8+P0xDX81lvSwDS\nVA0IbYYuedotN8o6YXqGmEkc5wVgnA/uyPtKZm3IpjLYHOkDICyeBKrCGSyjPCtz\nHgR2m+F2T8qqgSJh1LtrcFXmUq0REv4yNdULvQbMzVjblRFpnwl/rnxEFYBTe/df\nq8ctPpjkarG3WWYOZPChGv+UsGE944H3co2i7GgsxDBQ0BixXQRWlG/zDNxFQA9v\nbqmnw6jJtJW61sz8K1denhysKhw2fTZXjQGz4TorPmTrKD/jf+gskfsTr0J9W1FX\nRtM9jiYmxdPvmp1+WSUCEBCb+Y/24raC/Yf5zn06NziubYcYYTwQU1uewCH1lAdW\nvAGdbhrgS7PFRL/0rqtf\n=stQU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T18:59:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDg1ZjA2MzM5NDhlYjA4OTRhZDI4MzZiMDNhYjIzMjIyYTc0MWVhMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60","sha":"408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60"}],"sha":"85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/85f0633948eb0894ad2836b03ab23222a741ea27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:27:50Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:27:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(client): let `progress` choose between the badge and a bar (#2426)\n\n* feat(client): let `progress` choose between the badge and a bar\n\nwebpack-dev-server''s `client.progress` takes `\"linear\"` and `\"circular\"`\nas well as a boolean, and renders a visibly different indicator for each.\nThis package took a boolean only, so those two values would have silently\ncollapsed into one shape — a value that used to mean something quietly\nmeaning nothing is worse than a value that errors.\n\n`\"circular\"` is the badge this package has always shown, and stays what\n`true` selects, so nothing changes for anyone already using it.\n`\"linear\"` renders a thin bar across the top of the viewport, measured by\nthe percentage the progress payloads carry and sweeping when there is no\npercentage to measure — the same choice the badge makes between its ring\nand its pulsing dot. Built through the CSSOM and the Web Animations API,\nwith no `<style>` element, so a strict `style-src` still allows it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): do not animate the indicator when motion is declined\n\nReview finding. The bar''s sweep ran regardless of\n`prefers-reduced-motion`, which webpack-dev-server''s linear indicator\nhonors in its own stylesheet — so the shape this PR adds for parity was\nmissing the part of it that matters most to the people it matters to.\n\nThe badge''s pulsing dot ignored the preference too, which predates this\nbranch. Both go through one guard now rather than leaving the older one\nwrong: nothing starts while motion is declined, anything already running\nstops if the preference changes mid-build, and the listener that watches\nfor it is dropped when the indicator goes away. Without a sweep the bar\nsays a build is running by sitting still at full width, so the state is\nstill visible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): drop the motion listener from the query that holds it\n\nTwo review findings, both in the reduced-motion guard added a commit ago.\n\n`matchMedia` returns a new `MediaQueryList` for every call, so removing the\nlistener from a freshly built one called `removeEventListener` and changed\nnothing: the object that actually held it kept it, one per build, for the\nlife of the page. Verified in the browser the suite runs rather than from\nthe specification alone. The query the listener was registered on is kept\nand removed from.\n\nCancelling a sweep left `barAnimation` pointing at the cancelled animation\nand the bar frozen at the 40% a sweep starts from — so it read as progress\nthat had stalled, and every later call returned early on the stale\nreference and could never put it right. Declining motion now clears the\nreference and puts the bar at the width it uses when it cannot move.\n\nThe first test written for the listener passed against the bug, because it\ncounted calls rather than what stayed attached; it tracks listeners per\nquery object now, and fails when the removal is aimed at the wrong one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e2a66a425249fc0ec463da494512c5372c1eb70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/9e2a66a425249fc0ec463da494512c5372c1eb70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e2a66a425249fc0ec463da494512c5372c1eb70\nparent 750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790436470 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790436470 +0300\n\nfeat(client): let `progress` choose between the badge and a bar (#2426)\n\n* feat(client): let `progress` choose between the badge and a bar\n\nwebpack-dev-server''s `client.progress` takes `\"linear\"` and `\"circular\"`\nas well as a boolean, and renders a visibly different indicator for each.\nThis package took a boolean only, so those two values would have silently\ncollapsed into one shape — a value that used to mean something quietly\nmeaning nothing is worse than a value that errors.\n\n`\"circular\"` is the badge this package has always shown, and stays what\n`true` selects, so nothing changes for anyone already using it.\n`\"linear\"` renders a thin bar across the top of the viewport, measured by\nthe percentage the progress payloads carry and sweeping when there is no\npercentage to measure — the same choice the badge makes between its ring\nand its pulsing dot. Built through the CSSOM and the Web Animations API,\nwith no `<style>` element, so a strict `style-src` still allows it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): do not animate the indicator when motion is declined\n\nReview finding. The bar''s sweep ran regardless of\n`prefers-reduced-motion`, which webpack-dev-server''s linear indicator\nhonors in its own stylesheet — so the shape this PR adds for parity was\nmissing the part of it that matters most to the people it matters to.\n\nThe badge''s pulsing dot ignored the preference too, which predates this\nbranch. Both go through one guard now rather than leaving the older one\nwrong: nothing starts while motion is declined, anything already running\nstops if the preference changes mid-build, and the listener that watches\nfor it is dropped when the indicator goes away. Without a sweep the bar\nsays a build is running by sitting still at full width, so the state is\nstill visible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): drop the motion listener from the query that holds it\n\nTwo review findings, both in the reduced-motion guard added a commit ago.\n\n`matchMedia` returns a new `MediaQueryList` for every call, so removing the\nlistener from a freshly built one called `removeEventListener` and changed\nnothing: the object that actually held it kept it, one per build, for the\nlife of the page. Verified in the browser the suite runs rather than from\nthe specification alone. The query the listener was registered on is kept\nand removed from.\n\nCancelling a sweep left `barAnimation` pointing at the cancelled animation\nand the bar frozen at the 40% a sweep starts from — so it read as progress\nthat had stalled, and every later call returned early on the stale\nreference and could never put it right. Declining motion now clears the\nreference and puts the bar at the width it uses when it cannot move.\n\nThe first test written for the listener passed against the bug, because it\ncounted calls rather than what stayed attached; it tracks listeners per\nquery object now, and fails when the removal is aimed at the wrong one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+R2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA48sQAKfvQMC243V24mwHrlDWXDdz\naBpI8CQQY2BaJFzkIfcvKp5bUOAYLuQevF93dA8K880Bkyw2lLrWapZK7lEXIlTO\n4odXYJ9IYbFIT04EulvckV+dvuMXEwYYRiJWTcIRrpNxneL8g6rglpGO2FSsS+V/\nxSTTkp3r40jSRHsZ/en2nRscIQGXtclHDN/ytTUgw4EQqrxf8Avqv4G6l5z5Oej5\nVy9bmZFcIlXb6Tht3aBMQW3qBoaU9QgB6f9s/7CC23oRsfstl9TzhMtYHf5Q02DU\nE4Wf4m2ZQ3czG01Pq7/f1GT0UTIC3kC12f+2414QaHkl4BPdzGcdGQ/0MwQa8Cfb\n1e0q/lNiWOzXWaP3nj/i2cAMQInOEGPhedE4Hav0k6m7OtQP82Zipdpp1IARErTl\n5YY6ibo4bREZ3I+38ac+AGE257HN5WTJJLCXyyApQWpsLEyzfYkeBzvXUW1eSnod\neWVJinFPvWGTHFfHvQOh4dmBqrW9XVbIdG7Hv6qeH5QMAXW8EJo0+8HDD2dpxNXi\n6P0+n0xdLlF8GB0IHR8yDOiv0KMeFyu7Ph5iTv9IiG3OKq5o+rCtEjMmvQo+1WNv\nNOZrpNOCabFsc2zfQi+eH8zQEpU+BGs5fxKe+RNbdtV7ang87Fa4R7HqMDz0Wt1I\nagIDbDqXonWvAaI1VOKb\n=XWpx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T15:27:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDQwODM5NjAzNWE2NTM3NWY5YTgzNjhiY2Y1ZjUxOGZiNzAyNzBjNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3","sha":"750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3"}],"sha":"408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/408396035a65375f9a8368bcf5f518fb70270c60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:16:45Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:16:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(client): post build events to the page, and guard reloads (#2425)\n\n* feat(client): post build events to the page, and guard reloads\n\nThree gaps against webpack-dev-server''s client, found by comparing what\nsurvives if dev-server deletes its own and re-exports this one.\n\nIts client posts every build event out through `self.postMessage` \"so\nplugins can consume it\", and this one posted nothing at all — so anything\nlistening for `webpackOk` and its siblings would have gone quiet without a\nword. Undocumented, which makes it easy to drop and hard to notice. All\neight are posted now, under the same names and payloads, including the bare\n`webpackHotUpdate<hash>` string. `webpackClose` announces an outage once\nrather than once per retry, matching the `retries === 0` guard the other\nclient reports it behind.\n\nA reload while the page is already navigating away reloads a page the\nbrowser is leaving, so `beforeunload` now holds reloads off — released\nagain after a grace period, since a `beforeunload` can be cancelled, and\nsettled by `pagehide`/`pageshow` for a page that comes back out of the\nback/forward cache. In an `about:blank` iframe a reload reloaded the blank\ndocument and lost the app; the nearest ancestor with a url of its own is\nreloaded instead, and a cross-origin one is left alone rather than thrown\non.\n\nA runtime error filter could not see what a rejection carried: a plain\nobject was wrapped in an `Error` and dropped. It is kept as `cause` now, so\na filter deciding on a status code has somewhere to read it from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): keep `cause` on old browsers, and hold a cancelled reload\n\nTwo review findings.\n\n`new Error(message, { cause })` is ES2022, and this file is compiled to an\nES5 baseline for browsers that predate it — where the option is quietly\nignored and a `runtimeErrors` filter would find nothing to read. Defined\nafterwards instead, and non-enumerable, which is the descriptor the option\nwould have given it.\n\nA reload asked for while the page looked like it was leaving was dropped.\nA `beforeunload` can be cancelled, and then the page is staying and still\nwants the update, with nothing to ask again until the next rebuild — so it\nis held for the grace period and performed when the navigation turns out\nnot to have happened. Dropped for good on `pagehide`, where the page\nreally is going, and on `pageshow`, where it came back from the cache\nshowing its own state and a reload from before the navigation is stale.\n\nCovered by unit tests over a driven fake page, which is what makes the\ntiming and the three events testable at all.\n\nA third finding, that `onDisconnect` reports a first attempt that never\nopened, is accurate but deliberate: webpack-dev-server reports that case\ntoo, from the same reset-on-open counter, and a page loaded while the\nserver is down has no connection either. Its wording said \"a connection\nthat was open\", which was wrong about its own behavior; the comment and\nthe type now say what it does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a35f9c5941387f6dda0959bc76156d320bf84ac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/a35f9c5941387f6dda0959bc76156d320bf84ac3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3","verification":{"payload":"tree a35f9c5941387f6dda0959bc76156d320bf84ac3\nparent cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790435805 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790435805 +0300\n\nfeat(client): post build events to the page, and guard reloads (#2425)\n\n* feat(client): post build events to the page, and guard reloads\n\nThree gaps against webpack-dev-server''s client, found by comparing what\nsurvives if dev-server deletes its own and re-exports this one.\n\nIts client posts every build event out through `self.postMessage` \"so\nplugins can consume it\", and this one posted nothing at all — so anything\nlistening for `webpackOk` and its siblings would have gone quiet without a\nword. Undocumented, which makes it easy to drop and hard to notice. All\neight are posted now, under the same names and payloads, including the bare\n`webpackHotUpdate<hash>` string. `webpackClose` announces an outage once\nrather than once per retry, matching the `retries === 0` guard the other\nclient reports it behind.\n\nA reload while the page is already navigating away reloads a page the\nbrowser is leaving, so `beforeunload` now holds reloads off — released\nagain after a grace period, since a `beforeunload` can be cancelled, and\nsettled by `pagehide`/`pageshow` for a page that comes back out of the\nback/forward cache. In an `about:blank` iframe a reload reloaded the blank\ndocument and lost the app; the nearest ancestor with a url of its own is\nreloaded instead, and a cross-origin one is left alone rather than thrown\non.\n\nA runtime error filter could not see what a rejection carried: a plain\nobject was wrapped in an `Error` and dropped. It is kept as `cause` now, so\na filter deciding on a status code has somewhere to read it from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n* fix(client): keep `cause` on old browsers, and hold a cancelled reload\n\nTwo review findings.\n\n`new Error(message, { cause })` is ES2022, and this file is compiled to an\nES5 baseline for browsers that predate it — where the option is quietly\nignored and a `runtimeErrors` filter would find nothing to read. Defined\nafterwards instead, and non-enumerable, which is the descriptor the option\nwould have given it.\n\nA reload asked for while the page looked like it was leaving was dropped.\nA `beforeunload` can be cancelled, and then the page is staying and still\nwants the update, with nothing to ask again until the next rebuild — so it\nis held for the grace period and performed when the navigation turns out\nnot to have happened. Dropped for good on `pagehide`, where the page\nreally is going, and on `pageshow`, where it came back from the cache\nshowing its own state and a reload from before the navigation is stale.\n\nCovered by unit tests over a driven fake page, which is what makes the\ntiming and the three events testable at all.\n\nA third finding, that `onDisconnect` reports a first attempt that never\nopened, is accurate but deliberate: webpack-dev-server reports that case\ntoo, from the same reset-on-open counter, and a page loaded while the\nserver is down has no connection either. Its wording said \"a connection\nthat was open\", which was wrong about its own behavior; the comment and\nthe type now say what it does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+HdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU/sQABUENKgHcMMBYqTO7igZEKNX\nyDrwq6z9griQ5zY3Ja08T2SQNBSViOufPulSRDXVIXqb7Z1SOleeAK8q7H0H8QTX\nehSaNMUX6uINQ2CxxrGHTnshbMLKXuZVABhjA5aJB38Bv3P21A/Xq9X8mC17Pggu\nUSATHVCJIOTs731Hx7+uQtcIEw+y9AGxr8KlUx2L18jhgygPxRNHGsEGMHUI2c9W\n3gQz7us/idVGrWl6YQF2VDZqJfoyif1PuzxVI9yqlzbKWxm5QE9xHeM0GpEgRiDy\nbCTlXxKEUSnYxCAPTvmapTWq1+AEUAZ8F9vArW5CAZs1y2xvug05dRvVwjUxDNG6\nlwIcCF0sDM7zPsW+z6E3jvZ3XTqV3WsMKTpiJLKNKfW2MUsY2K0EGSWSjlS+KW4a\nK/0nqPgnRMRQzHb5ufJlNR7rkIT3ZaB/PsJ8mhtTEwuUHK4QuIrZ4HUv09lkZ+lL\nungxXt/WsdnRX62EycYkHkVKM6yGjnv8VlPBK6oTFg1oXgqU5VvEvpLTEDvOkmgp\nFDukYqJmqGOAv+zMzoA5X1A8akqGNyRtHgap8a3jZu8V8PbZOgIbV7+kO+u6Xv5R\nEXUFOpdlTKEiKVBWqxx4fmsaxi4TjEY5Q3Ck0zfzjhe5w8eIPNSTmLtrvgQOMlYe\n80lMJk9EIvbe0DkAxjOB\n=rtrQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T15:16:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDc1MGVkZDc3MjU0MzNlMjc1YTQ3Mjc1YTk5Yjk0OTY1ZGVlMWMwYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4","sha":"cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4"}],"sha":"750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/750edd7725433e275a47275a99b94965dee1c0b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T13:21:07Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T13:21:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(overlay): keep a runtime error a successful build cannot vouch for (#2424)\n\nAn entry that throws while it is still evaluating puts the overlay up\nbefore the transport has finished connecting. The catch-up sync arrives\nright behind it reporting no problems, and the reporter cleared the\nruntime slot on every clean build — so the overlay was dismissed\nmilliseconds after appearing, and a page that threw on load looked fine.\nThis is webpack-dev-server#5024, which webpack-dev-server fixes by\nsplitting the two cases; this one had not.\n\nA build that merely succeeded says nothing about an error the page threw\nby itself, so it no longer clears those. A rebuild does, from `building`,\nbecause that replaces the code the error came from — matching\nwebpack-dev-server''s `BUILD_OK` and `DISMISS` split. What a rebuild looks\nlike from the outside is unchanged.\n\nAlso covers the `runtimeErrors` filter arriving through the resource\nquery, which turned out to work already: encoded in both the layers\nwebpack-dev-server uses, a filter round-trips intact. Writing that query\nby hand does not, since `encodeURIComponent` leaves `!` alone and webpack\nreads it as the inline-loader separator.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a3af737307b230c138e2a93760a608b55de309d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/8a3af737307b230c138e2a93760a608b55de309d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a3af737307b230c138e2a93760a608b55de309d\nparent 8bb0fdd99d1e27ef918d3d1701e08560baae9b40\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790428867 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790428867 +0300\n\nfix(overlay): keep a runtime error a successful build cannot vouch for (#2424)\n\nAn entry that throws while it is still evaluating puts the overlay up\nbefore the transport has finished connecting. The catch-up sync arrives\nright behind it reporting no problems, and the reporter cleared the\nruntime slot on every clean build — so the overlay was dismissed\nmilliseconds after appearing, and a page that threw on load looked fine.\nThis is webpack-dev-server#5024, which webpack-dev-server fixes by\nsplitting the two cases; this one had not.\n\nA build that merely succeeded says nothing about an error the page threw\nby itself, so it no longer clears those. A rebuild does, from `building`,\nbecause that replaces the code the error came from — matching\nwebpack-dev-server''s `BUILD_OK` and `DISMISS` split. What a rebuild looks\nlike from the outside is unchanged.\n\nAlso covers the `runtimeErrors` filter arriving through the resource\nquery, which turned out to work already: encoded in both the layers\nwebpack-dev-server uses, a filter round-trips intact. Writing that query\nby hand does not, since `encodeURIComponent` leaves `!` alone and webpack\nreads it as the inline-loader separator.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt8bDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXmgQAKlBBWxEsf9kaQ9bYP9i/ReO\nqbw7QZ91kU4Fbz2ZCoHxQXS0LQ/GIUZ2LgXpCmswrxEs6EM072qIj3YIyqc8jJWp\no9eWQniMSvEh992ljyh5nH6J79DrJVWYfscekqoBSZ0NbkpL9B74g5JmIprHNqjs\nk/Fl3nkXvci1zXTyhLhQcWw8LIgiWLbdd4opVZWq+J7f2UpaGGvNvLOMJSiDLF02\nUa0oZvIWOhCLcx8K00fj/7EqOUyhojjB1EVMGbP66VQHAT+eDjP/dj/cH9M3X4OE\nKUogHT5OnaGBUaj9XL+4gNob56aNsNpzylM7LuD9ce33QOCm9FZujB6V89cxJ9GY\nnPAu2MXRsevD40W13s31HA1TWApD5qq4Rb9aHl1EeWsBq6lV7db/O7t+oz4fdLwt\nGeQ/3YB4U/80U7guBWTBbSR81YnY462JgzsOZP9ds94yj/eO3RbU3xvh6spzutu4\np7qSLgDU6//u6vlMbob29bV2ndQUgyoKNJMDVY96O5zJ3SGNmw7GrAToq07LRJiQ\n7fOp9mGHTjQcBMiRXtNDFahI+HsbQ14IK3orU8NhRyJkLLWpMsthNYGbr9N5b/Sw\nItfuF80VJJIJFJlQnOYM+SmDS+WMIAUhh9vJaS8HBT80JyJ/HtYo2kRq49UC9P3s\n5lDUkScJtQfvoVBOKBKr\n=EwBG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T13:21:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGNjNDk0NmZkZWVlNWM2MTMxZjAyODQzNDVhNDM3NmJiNTE2ODk0YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/8bb0fdd99d1e27ef918d3d1701e08560baae9b40","sha":"8bb0fdd99d1e27ef918d3d1701e08560baae9b40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/8bb0fdd99d1e27ef918d3d1701e08560baae9b40"}],"sha":"cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/cc4946fdeee5c6131f0284345a4376bb516894b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/8bb0fdd99d1e27ef918d3d1701e08560baae9b40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:12:50Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:12:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(overlay): take focus when opening and hand it back when closing (#2423)\n\n* fix(overlay): take focus when opening and hand it back when closing\n\nThe overlay opened without touching focus, so reaching it meant clicking\ninto the frame first: Escape and the arrow keys did nothing until then, and\na screen reader stayed wherever the page was. Its frame had no accessible\nname either, leaving it announced by its `about:blank` url.\n\nOnly the render that opens it takes focus — paginating re-renders the card,\nand moving focus then would take it off the button being clicked.\n\nThese are the parts webpack-dev-server''s own overlay has and this one did\nnot, which it would otherwise lose by switching to this one.\n\n* test(overlay): cover the webpack-dev-server behaviors this overlay had no test for\n\nMapping webpack-dev-server''s 39 end-to-end overlay cases onto this one''s 36\nfound six behaviors it relies on that nothing here pinned: an `errors`\nfilter keeping one problem and rejecting all of them, a failure in the very\nfirst build (which arrives through the catch-up sync rather than a rebuild),\none broken rebuild replacing another''s overlay, Escape working a second\ntime, and markup in a build error reaching the card as text.\n\nAll six already behave the way webpack-dev-server''s do — these are the\ntests, not fixes.\n\n* fix(client): report connecting over either transport, and cover both\n\n`connected` was logged by the Server-Sent Events transport itself, so a page\nusing the WebSocket one got no sign it had connected at all. It is said by\nthe shared socket now, on the same event, so neither transport can be the\none that stays quiet.\n\nFound by running the same four behaviors over both: connecting and applying\na hot update, falling back to a reload when nothing accepts it, showing and\nclearing a build error, and catching up a client on what it missed. The\nharness takes `transport: \"ws\"`, which also exercises `attach` — the\nWebSocket path had no browser coverage before this.\n\n* fix(client): close the gaps between the two transports\n\nThe WebSocket one logged a raw `error`, which the Server-Sent Events one\nnever did. Making both say it would have been the wrong way to agree:\n`EventSource` fires `error` on every routine reconnection, and a WebSocket\n`error` carries no detail by specification, so it prints an opaque object.\nNeither logs it now — the shared socket already reports the reconnection,\nwhich is the part worth reading.\n\nThe WebSocket one also had no equivalent of the other''s `closed` guard, so\na close or message the browser had already queued still reached the caller\nafter it had closed, and the shared socket would reconnect a connection\nnobody wanted.\n\nThe contract they share is now tested once and run against each, which is\nwhat turned both of these up, and all three files are fully covered.\n\n* fix(overlay): keep focus where the user left it\n\nTwo gaps in the focus handling, both found in review.\n\n`document.activeElement` names a shadow host rather than the control\nfocused inside it, and focusing a host that does not delegate focus does\nnothing at all — so the overlay dropped focus instead of handing it back.\nDescend into open roots before remembering what to restore.\n\nPaging through problems rebuilds the card, which destroys the very button\nthat was clicked; focus then fell back to the frame''s body, so a keyboard\nuser lost the navigation after the first press. Each control is named\nacross the re-render and the equivalent one takes focus again.\n\nThe test helper could not have caught either over a WebSocket, because it\ncould not restart a server at all: an upgraded socket is no longer the\nHTTP server''s to close, so `stopHttp()` waited on a connected client\nforever, and the replacement server was never handed back to the\ntransport. Both fixed, and the reconnect story now runs over both\ntransports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa46f40959ea50642a6b5c9e682985791635cb25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/fa46f40959ea50642a6b5c9e682985791635cb25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/8bb0fdd99d1e27ef918d3d1701e08560baae9b40","verification":{"payload":"tree fa46f40959ea50642a6b5c9e682985791635cb25\nparent eed5f19c6ec1718706cb54b5919563f1c4ddbd8f\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790424770 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790424770 +0300\n\nfix(overlay): take focus when opening and hand it back when closing (#2423)\n\n* fix(overlay): take focus when opening and hand it back when closing\n\nThe overlay opened without touching focus, so reaching it meant clicking\ninto the frame first: Escape and the arrow keys did nothing until then, and\na screen reader stayed wherever the page was. Its frame had no accessible\nname either, leaving it announced by its `about:blank` url.\n\nOnly the render that opens it takes focus — paginating re-renders the card,\nand moving focus then would take it off the button being clicked.\n\nThese are the parts webpack-dev-server''s own overlay has and this one did\nnot, which it would otherwise lose by switching to this one.\n\n* test(overlay): cover the webpack-dev-server behaviors this overlay had no test for\n\nMapping webpack-dev-server''s 39 end-to-end overlay cases onto this one''s 36\nfound six behaviors it relies on that nothing here pinned: an `errors`\nfilter keeping one problem and rejecting all of them, a failure in the very\nfirst build (which arrives through the catch-up sync rather than a rebuild),\none broken rebuild replacing another''s overlay, Escape working a second\ntime, and markup in a build error reaching the card as text.\n\nAll six already behave the way webpack-dev-server''s do — these are the\ntests, not fixes.\n\n* fix(client): report connecting over either transport, and cover both\n\n`connected` was logged by the Server-Sent Events transport itself, so a page\nusing the WebSocket one got no sign it had connected at all. It is said by\nthe shared socket now, on the same event, so neither transport can be the\none that stays quiet.\n\nFound by running the same four behaviors over both: connecting and applying\na hot update, falling back to a reload when nothing accepts it, showing and\nclearing a build error, and catching up a client on what it missed. The\nharness takes `transport: \"ws\"`, which also exercises `attach` — the\nWebSocket path had no browser coverage before this.\n\n* fix(client): close the gaps between the two transports\n\nThe WebSocket one logged a raw `error`, which the Server-Sent Events one\nnever did. Making both say it would have been the wrong way to agree:\n`EventSource` fires `error` on every routine reconnection, and a WebSocket\n`error` carries no detail by specification, so it prints an opaque object.\nNeither logs it now — the shared socket already reports the reconnection,\nwhich is the part worth reading.\n\nThe WebSocket one also had no equivalent of the other''s `closed` guard, so\na close or message the browser had already queued still reached the caller\nafter it had closed, and the shared socket would reconnect a connection\nnobody wanted.\n\nThe contract they share is now tested once and run against each, which is\nwhat turned both of these up, and all three files are fully covered.\n\n* fix(overlay): keep focus where the user left it\n\nTwo gaps in the focus handling, both found in review.\n\n`document.activeElement` names a shadow host rather than the control\nfocused inside it, and focusing a host that does not delegate focus does\nnothing at all — so the overlay dropped focus instead of handing it back.\nDescend into open roots before remembering what to restore.\n\nPaging through problems rebuilds the card, which destroys the very button\nthat was clicked; focus then fell back to the frame''s body, so a keyboard\nuser lost the navigation after the first press. Each control is named\nacross the re-render and the equivalent one takes focus again.\n\nThe test helper could not have caught either over a WebSocket, because it\ncould not restart a server at all: an upgraded socket is no longer the\nHTTP server''s to close, so `stopHttp()` waited on a connected client\nforever, and the replacement server was never handed back to the\ntransport. Both fixed, and the reconnect story now runs over both\ntransports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UjuMAuk9o6UazjHzcAQCTA\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt7bCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe6oQAIYuvdfqjwYCfBM/gSF2nFkl\n538SYYZ8o/fvY8OJ4DY0StSj7lVim6bUxuc8NU2paMoIXaHewR7avhn6+0FuF7yM\nt5t8GcwlolnG0y7x3xSSxesUdCNnnurmWThN8+WoF1Xn4JdwJBI/rRa6jLn+NpxH\nyHo36pX8HQzEzSSH0ri6psPwnqVoCR0LVP4SvR0ihqFDJkx4LOMuaBaqeoMBb5SS\npEi3upztco1QXx7DVPiB/I3tAEZ6HbYQ9WpsXv8WVpDh9yneQD3GDcQJDAqADJIt\n/o6rReEDljV9sZ67ghmWldW0uQVCx75RkIqgAad3sSedxp12qXeItzv97WlpVl/W\n3gL+nUrLvel4RDv5d+qznek7XgJ69hWOSRxHY/kszvURCj6AMfj8r10waWKe824r\nf1lLOlr7k+CTYAoqGPPaeqJE/kA4KeIkBKmn6sDinKvug/bku7bXRZIGYrdTPnC8\nDWz4SmDEbTzdhUIBLSRa6qiKQjgt1MWei36DccVkrktu9CTep4rCPCfsQpDVWoy8\nh+qfFkpB4ROLhRUWaCp3nyxMDcrjQy70vPgO3EaO9H7Ei4Ver4RlsSONBlfF+dzv\n/n+8mE7xZCmQYPvOemQarbd4/WJoRockpNHh3ifRJzjV9+wSHn341xBAdYD+xbhd\nm4ZaC6Xv9HJdYyCWCZaP\n=LOB8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T12:12:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"ht