ttps://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/c7a7990e229ebcb8e39e66895852822a811f79a2"}],"sha":"eed5f19c6ec1718706cb54b5919563f1c4ddbd8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/eed5f19c6ec1718706cb54b5919563f1c4ddbd8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/c7a7990e229ebcb8e39e66895852822a811f79a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:57:22Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:57:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(client): speak WebSocket as well as Server-Sent Events (#2421)\n\n* feat(client): speak WebSocket as well as Server-Sent Events\n\nThe runtime built its own EventSource inline, so the server''s new\n`hot.transport: \"ws\"` had nothing to talk to. The transport is a class\nbehind `onOpen`/`onClose`/`onMessage`/`close` now, chosen by a `transport`\nquery parameter, and a client injected as `__webpack_dev_server_client__`\nwins over both — the shape webpack-dev-server''s `client.webSocketTransport`\nalready has, so one written for it works here unchanged.\n\nReconnecting moves out of the transport into one loop the two share, which\nkeeps what each of them did: Server-Sent Events retry at a steady interval\nfor as long as the page is open, a WebSocket backs off and gives up after\n`reconnect` attempts.\n\n* fix(client): resolve the endpoint before handing it to WebSocket\n\n`WebSocket` only learned to take a relative or `http(s):` url in 2024 —\nChrome 125, Firefox 124, Safari 17.3 — and throws on one before that. The\nendpoint defaults to a path, so `transport=ws` threw outright on exactly the\nolder browsers this ES5 runtime exists to support. It is resolved to an\nabsolute `ws:`/`wss:` url first now.\n\nThe startup check also asked the browser for `EventSource` even where an\ninjected client was going to do the connecting, and the documented way to\nreuse a built-in transport used `require()`, which the ESM client build\ncannot answer.\n\n* fix(client): keep Server-Sent Events quiet between reconnections\n\nReconnecting moved into the shared loop, which announces each attempt the\nway webpack-dev-server''s always has. That is affordable for a WebSocket,\nwhich gives up after ten tries; Server-Sent Events retry for as long as the\npage is open, so it meant saying so every few seconds, all day — and they\nhad never said it at all. Two e2e snapshots pin exactly that silence.\n\nWhether to announce an attempt is the caller''s now, defaulting to whether\nthe attempts are bounded.","tree":{"sha":"6e05221fea90657b7b7ef1159e957d29a52aae9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/6e05221fea90657b7b7ef1159e957d29a52aae9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/c7a7990e229ebcb8e39e66895852822a811f79a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e05221fea90657b7b7ef1159e957d29a52aae9a\nparent dfdce46250c74d7a782301dae649f82060573a38\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790276242 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790276242 +0300\n\nfeat(client): speak WebSocket as well as Server-Sent Events (#2421)\n\n* feat(client): speak WebSocket as well as Server-Sent Events\n\nThe runtime built its own EventSource inline, so the server''s new\n`hot.transport: \"ws\"` had nothing to talk to. The transport is a class\nbehind `onOpen`/`onClose`/`onMessage`/`close` now, chosen by a `transport`\nquery parameter, and a client injected as `__webpack_dev_server_client__`\nwins over both — the shape webpack-dev-server''s `client.webSocketTransport`\nalready has, so one written for it works here unchanged.\n\nReconnecting moves out of the transport into one loop the two share, which\nkeeps what each of them did: Server-Sent Events retry at a steady interval\nfor as long as the page is open, a WebSocket backs off and gives up after\n`reconnect` attempts.\n\n* fix(client): resolve the endpoint before handing it to WebSocket\n\n`WebSocket` only learned to take a relative or `http(s):` url in 2024 —\nChrome 125, Firefox 124, Safari 17.3 — and throws on one before that. The\nendpoint defaults to a path, so `transport=ws` threw outright on exactly the\nolder browsers this ES5 runtime exists to support. It is resolved to an\nabsolute `ws:`/`wss:` url first now.\n\nThe startup check also asked the browser for `EventSource` even where an\ninjected client was going to do the connecting, and the documented way to\nreuse a built-in transport used `require()`, which the ESM client build\ncannot answer.\n\n* fix(client): keep Server-Sent Events quiet between reconnections\n\nReconnecting moved into the shared loop, which announces each attempt the\nway webpack-dev-server''s always has. That is affordable for a WebSocket,\nwhich gives up after ten tries; Server-Sent Events retry for as long as the\npage is open, so it meant saying so every few seconds, all day — and they\nhad never said it at all. Two e2e snapshots pin exactly that silence.\n\nWhether to announce an attempt is the caller''s now, defaulting to whether\nthe attempts are bounded.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtXKSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjsQQACH5DY9Msa28Ckao5sNpCxch\nhxs+oIRCHiyALow0juXFPBIYrrauNP5W4j5MMXsgCtpwaRmWFO0pfu6ldbgnQxYV\ndm1KdjvnL2znmYWfpLKr7Hln3NSbrTirV49o7i2mcP3G9UUif4qi6ahWISfohELC\nh1eTAZiHeo3zr4XXk3zvaPG625Pv1puFhtt4aeQnul2hjIqx97nlDj1sP8W9lh/p\n9pG0xDeK0wGbOf1UhtoigX6j/hP8pHgoGYCGl0j2C7GrULgadVIXIoRZHo5/Pqso\npKEAEcqnXGc6cjRH2Wc/J436gVeORBxdIOwpkRn9ruW9HD2rUHsclnUoKMc1fnjp\nGsxy6QeJX2C8g/4ewEEQ814PvXDGGbrzsuGcsYnPMj5RzZVpv8DFEpWoz4BLjmiq\nKd3/Nm4EVB/2l6HBO8m1mxPmA2JTjoEKkxsZV+Zbie8ScPTqRMQbj7tIV6X0LbXs\nRp3nN1lJ+WAMDAVlVRCZSLZ2kjvAyQWYx1GENOxp9nr+c3WHFIdEAKmf2vLDf3WY\nwD051pwu2Jz+7DEr/x6ZlhTRl7FLOL1EqUOTmWtE+t3QpNLEGXPAJHZksONWCfX3\nMRP6J9rUEfw65kkGFrgeKWEciMAIIL2uK3R49ylt9tJdynGaXh082H7WXBcTAIWE\nP83W4Okw5Z+5N2BQQA31\n=uXZi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:57:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/c7a7990e229ebcb8e39e66895852822a811f79a2","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGM3YTc5OTBlMjI5ZWJjYjhlMzllNjY4OTU4NTI4MjJhODExZjc5YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/dfdce46250c74d7a782301dae649f82060573a38","sha":"dfdce46250c74d7a782301dae649f82060573a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/dfdce46250c74d7a782301dae649f82060573a38"}],"sha":"c7a7990e229ebcb8e39e66895852822a811f79a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/c7a7990e229ebcb8e39e66895852822a811f79a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/dfdce46250c74d7a782301dae649f82060573a38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:10:15Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T15:10:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): serve the events over a WebSocket too (#2420)\n\n* feat(hot): serve the events over a WebSocket too\n\n`hot.transport` chooses between Server-Sent Events and a WebSocket. Both\nanswer the same calls, so nothing downstream of `createHot` knows which one\nit publishes to, and the SSE path is unchanged.\n\nA WebSocket handshake is an upgrade the HTTP server answers, which the\nmiddleware never sees, so the server is handed over through `hot.server` or\nthe middleware''s new `attach` method. `ws` is an optional dependency, needed\nonly by this transport.\n\n* feat(hot): let transport be a function building your own\n\n`hot.transport` took one of two names, so the only way to carry the events\nover anything else was to fork the middleware. It now also takes a function,\nwhich is handed the resolved path and heartbeat and returns the same client\nstream the built-in two are.\n\nA returned object missing one of those calls throws, naming what is absent,\nrather than failing later from wherever it is first published to.\n\n* fix(hot): keep ws out of the published types, and let a transport name its client\n\n`StreamClient` referred to `import(\"ws\")`, and `types/index.d.ts` reaches it,\nso every consumer loaded the optional dependency''s declarations — including\none on Server-Sent Events, whose build failed outright with TS2307 under the\ndefault `skipLibCheck: false`. It is a structural type now, and a test fails\nif the import comes back.\n\n`publishTo` also took only that union, so under `strictFunctionTypes` a\ntransport of your own could not be written in TypeScript at all: narrowing\nthe parameter to its own client type was rejected. `ClientStream` and\n`ClientStreamFactory` are parameterized by the client type instead.","tree":{"sha":"c7b117103aebede9c20a73c334ed13baa387a152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/c7b117103aebede9c20a73c334ed13baa387a152"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/dfdce46250c74d7a782301dae649f82060573a38","verification":{"payload":"tree c7b117103aebede9c20a73c334ed13baa387a152\nparent 4b1f3de477207e0cb98bb4c0c55b8656b973bbde\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1790262615 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790262615 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): serve the events over a WebSocket too (#2420)\n\n* feat(hot): serve the events over a WebSocket too\n\n`hot.transport` chooses between Server-Sent Events and a WebSocket. Both\nanswer the same calls, so nothing downstream of `createHot` knows which one\nit publishes to, and the SSE path is unchanged.\n\nA WebSocket handshake is an upgrade the HTTP server answers, which the\nmiddleware never sees, so the server is handed over through `hot.server` or\nthe middleware''s new `attach` method. `ws` is an optional dependency, needed\nonly by this transport.\n\n* feat(hot): let transport be a function building your own\n\n`hot.transport` took one of two names, so the only way to carry the events\nover anything else was to fork the middleware. It now also takes a function,\nwhich is handed the resolved path and heartbeat and returns the same client\nstream the built-in two are.\n\nA returned object missing one of those calls throws, naming what is absent,\nrather than failing later from wherever it is first published to.\n\n* fix(hot): keep ws out of the published types, and let a transport name its client\n\n`StreamClient` referred to `import(\"ws\")`, and `types/index.d.ts` reaches it,\nso every consumer loaded the optional dependency''s declarations — including\none on Server-Sent Events, whose build failed outright with TS2307 under the\ndefault `skipLibCheck: false`. It is a structural type now, and a test fails\nif the import comes back.\n\n`publishTo` also took only that union, so under `strictFunctionTypes` a\ntransport of your own could not be written in TypeScript at all: narrowing\nthe parameter to its own client type was rejected. `ClientStream` and\n`ClientStreamFactory` are parameterized by the client type instead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtT1XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJLsQAJMqjU1a7El8vibYGLaGh7QT\nR5SMSAl7rIHZ5kiQHvpyRe6+UoWo4YmR8vRoaacm0vpmyCxJ24xzFSer9RwIJtIX\n746JQ8pDhMUSawjuJ5rrlTe8mUeIDYEzXaJ7huWQJFI9sjF/VUmauMda9d4umh6L\nV0aTVnAj3ZK7/I5igqBvY0QjlZGbwxpc0Ix9GEPxAmSW7Zu6uwwTf6IK6bHIMHP+\no1cuRXZ9hmuBETFsCJMDmZMymSf0hPPdrkbofCfk/3Nk7n8pSeXJBQDqez9uN9bU\ncxwUmWXhaj+nCh0tnEhhWH4gZ6sYmhQ2FQFZdfi2ao3qg0YIAv4ekVngSLXf5v8t\nGCl+X5kGTuz2tdKgN3c/BsU6ofFL5Qlp2AIDJMh1vwGE/AqGvuqBLIBF3h3SJIyG\nPIPoGMgQVtMnd5yoov2sdaeVIbtwf7Uj+j0VtaIB98GNCa5TomGG/wOn7bVjPGub\nW5QnzQJSS5Y99nZBoVDrsmGo7fucSF/ntiYvzWU2uIs8KJ0OQIg+Pj0ZznFPTWRi\nCEZUT5kWlvulBLsSmhDLTW+/tnRHXHiGOv7nq0BLX/PHfEE2B+Jpjm/zqtpVcWsZ\npEroz+PSKX4dL23IZMnA8S6WE76jNuivJ2xDXkiJTJUarlBfYbEoEAyjN1M0/xzd\nvZiQcQ3mMFt77lRWrBX3\n=ho74\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T15:10:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subsc