pendency-name: puppeteer\n  dependency-version: 25.10.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* test: keep the browser suite green on puppeteer 25\n\npuppeteer is ESM-only since v25 and jest can only `require` such a module\non node.js 24.9+, so the suite would have run on the newest node alone.\nImport it dynamically instead, which every version `engines` allows can\nload, and turn the helper into the ES module its callers already import.\n\npuppeteer 25 renders an Error logged as a console argument as the first\nline of its stack rather than as an opaque handle, so the snapshot pins\nthe message the fixture threw and the placeholder for it is gone.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: alexander-akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7437699b7ac5101da1dc5cf5b6a124a65e1ebf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/f7437699b7ac5101da1dc5cf5b6a124a65e1ebf5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/7185cb2c2a02c834f567777e2d834772185f0722","verification":{"payload":"tree f7437699b7ac5101da1dc5cf5b6a124a65e1ebf5\nparent 61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789932042 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789932042 +0300\n\nchore(deps-dev): bump puppeteer from 22.15.0 to 25.11.0 (#2409)\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump puppeteer from 22.15.0 to 25.11.0\n\nBumps [puppeteer](https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer) from 22.15.0 to 25.11.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/puppeteer/puppeteer/compare/puppeteer-v22.15.0...puppeteer-v25.11.0)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: puppeteer\n  dependency-version: 25.10.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* test: keep the browser suite green on puppeteer 25\n\npuppeteer is ESM-only since v25 and jest can only `require` such a module\non node.js 24.9+, so the suite would have run on the newest node alone.\nImport it dynamically instead, which every version `engines` allows can\nload, and turn the helper into the ES module its callers already import.\n\npuppeteer 25 renders an Error logged as a console argument as the first\nline of its stack rather than as an opaque handle, so the snapshot pins\nthe message the fixture threw and the placeholder for it is gone.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: alexander-akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsDIKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA204QAFbt/8BtZg6nCHJIxUjswE1Y\noYG64guIKmTEHkwMZGjjGBNDWkCPo4Gw2hCb88EsiFH+Xx4m6Tubcwd1JPfr+PXF\nc2+UBg0Ngf+tre5ycb6zfBtTryVzmWcmmiBGnU+6+TGKMXl2BL7IyMfex2bPf69S\njUlKTiTi+wAmRMeL1P5J0Q4NBLlmyQT24ONnPy6Op/55oASvISRoQkhJngp4DGqy\n5W8WkIfhF/cY5SbrtkdXleOxXMAal5Y2XZa3v6sh/mujELG9sNOybAzPdGBEBEqj\nuzxSnja9qRr/lwqq/11mz9AF8EPsFSsv83wYgd0AEDAp96STrl6PQPufVdjkIlj3\npZQBfHDbr1JbW6+mgJbdnHhw5Jemsz2baamiKJsfOqLnDi9x/hlbbHCzG7Fxi/ws\nF72VKwYCbMmpDWEpxn2uOyQCrDhNN90YJ1JENFPU+XpqYLs9jyEs7qGdab+r35zg\n/J1QFRJRcePNYaDhzeW31HnpMClBnbqNxUDPsTBKQTVC9JySqJ5mjvHXxO6XCn9V\nF//SdNcQ0/29l0vG+473ekXZN2IsyQQ64cyQmGCmba9OObZDUwSwCld37ASWv0ya\ntbNBMFXwa5bakcd/tg+G/RRYiBVOKOHFjQmwr8rETKdxgrkxy8azYOwMh78ngE0v\nRl12es9vdiNL8SvwHJSV\n=EGwy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T19:20:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/7185cb2c2a02c834f567777e2d834772185f0722","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDcxODVjYjJjMmEwMmM4MzRmNTY3Nzc3ZTJkODM0NzcyMTg1ZjA3MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433","sha":"61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433"}],"sha":"7185cb2c2a02c834f567777e2d834772185f0722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/7185cb2c2a02c834f567777e2d834772185f0722"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:16:42Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:16:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: validate options with a precompiled schema (#2413)\n\n* perf: validate options with a precompiled schema\n\nValidating the options compiles the schema with ajv on the first call,\nwhich cost 159ms of the first `middleware()` against 0.08ms for each call\nafter it. Every webpack-dev-server start pays it once.\n\n`src/options.check.js` is that schema precompiled by `ajv`''s standalone\ncodegen. `internalValidate` asks it first and only falls through to\n`compiler.validate`/`schema-utils` when it rejects, so the happy path\nnever loads ajv, `options.json` stays unread until something is actually\nwrong, and an invalid config still gets the same message. The generated\nvalidator agrees with `schema-utils` on all 76 cases of the\n`validation-options` corpus.\n\nChecking here rather than passing the validator to `compiler.validate` as\nits fourth argument keeps this working across the whole supported webpack\nrange, not only versions carrying that parameter.\n\nValidation drops to 1.9ms, and a dev server''s time-to-listening for a\nhello-world falls from 523 +/- 25ms to 438 +/- 17ms.\n\n* chore: document the generator''s callbacks\n\n* chore: complete internalValidate''s JSDoc\n\n* refactor: validate options through the compiler where webpack allows it\n\n`compiler.hooks.validate` and `compiler.validate`''s lazy-schema and\nprecompiled-check parameters landed together in webpack 5.106, so the\nhook doubles as the feature probe for them. When it is there, the\nprecompiled check is handed to the compiler the way webpack''s own plugins\nhand it theirs, rather than being run before it.\n\nThe direct path stays as the fallback, keeping the existing TODO to drop\nit once the minimum supported webpack carries the hook.\n\n* test: cover validation without the validate hook\n\ncodecov flagged the fallback as the uncovered part of the diff: CI\ninstalls webpack 5.110, where `compiler.hooks.validate` always exists, so\nnothing reached the path taken on webpack < 5.106.\n\nReplacing the frozen `compiler.hooks` with a copy that lacks `validate`\nexercises it, and the spy asserts the fallback validated rather than the\ncompiler. Without these two tests, lines 232, 233, 236 and 238 are\nuncovered; with them, every statement in `internalValidate` is.","tree":{"sha":"f6b062fa08f93b6f6916663f016e523fbc624c51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/f6b062fa08f93b6f6916663f016e523fbc624c51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433","verification":{"payload":"tree f6b062fa08f93b6f6916663f016e523fbc624c51\nparent 233389a9bc78a0b96775c571ed76591471449778\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789928202 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789928202 +0300\n\nperf: validate options with a precompiled schema (#2413)\n\n* perf: validate options with a precompiled schema\n\nValidating the options compiles the schema with ajv on the first call,\nwhich cost 159ms of the first `middleware()` against 0.08ms for each call\nafter it. Every webpack-dev-server start pays it once.\n\n`src/options.check.js` is that schema precompiled by `ajv`''s standalone\ncodegen. `internalValidate` asks it first and only falls through to\n`compiler.validate`/`schema-utils` when it rejects, so the happy path\nnever loads ajv, `options.json` stays unread until something is actually\nwrong, and an invalid config still gets the same message. The generated\nvalidator agrees with `schema-utils` on all 76 cases of the\n`validation-options` corpus.\n\nChecking here rather than passing the validator to `compiler.validate` as\nits fourth argument keeps this working across the whole supported webpack\nrange, not only versions carrying that parameter.\n\nValidation drops to 1.9ms, and a dev server''s time-to-listening for a\nhello-world falls from 523 +/- 25ms to 438 +/- 17ms.\n\n* chore: document the generator''s callbacks\n\n* chore: complete internalValidate''s JSDoc\n\n* refactor: validate options through the compiler where webpack allows it\n\n`compiler.hooks.validate` and `compiler.validate`''s lazy-schema and\nprecompiled-check parameters landed together in webpack 5.106, so the\nhook doubles as the feature probe for them. When it is there, the\nprecompiled check is handed to the compiler the way webpack''s own plugins\nhand it theirs, rather than being run before it.\n\nThe direct path stays as the fallback, keeping the existing TODO to drop\nit once the minimum supported webpack carries the hook.\n\n* test: cover validation without the validate hook\n\ncodecov flagged the fallback as the uncovered part of the diff: CI\ninstalls webpack 5.110, where `compiler.hooks.validate` always exists, so\nnothing reached the path taken on webpack < 5.106.\n\nReplacing the frozen `compiler.hooks` with a copy that lacks `validate`\nexercises it, and the spy asserts the fallback validated rather than the\ncompiler. Without these two tests, lines 232, 233, 236 and 238 are\nuncovered; with them, every statement in `internalValidate` is.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsCMKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACeYQAIj/jFumLIqdm8Ye49vOjvOC\neGcdUa8Nm4FFDDvHLEsIt41LZFraoVc+6QqY5EnfH/Pj3mawTE1nfvOs6MTvyA+F\n4osi67Eko8YBRdczuQfvAZ/soT+CIkfoD6z7Qlxu3R97PXu1dpA8dAs/dqRbIW5l\nossEb786yBKgSmVkCS6WKgZGuGyxmMCSSwDp/cyv/SpcZWwXyt/RiBb6aKhTHqyc\nUHgTF2yM+Hbx5Zr3x65LcZ1P3+JoUfWBL+QaubgH2xkc7SneTp+o6WbuK2t2Wi/Q\n2pI/dTGioyhd8ofpbTpNBZ6DfM+9C/gY35u++pPOaaLL6Inx/ceKfBl+veULCX94\nwZ+qMtaC32WF6T/8FXEUeidr1/qU6l1sqBtqm5IcqnLxsLENZfnwsBqUQNeDBrHb\n821WXyF9hvOtxI5LVKGObf1r/f41B6seCLHT9azNgMwuvK1QEEMdLSeBOXGmX6w6\n2/mngmjGuF+rzm94GKnBw+Fh4OnVBZK0kPWwnVOek/YEFkDD6SXkyicVZr82KeVn\noWwYGjNDMfwMH7aVdT7V1nos6QU0De1PToQosy3AYl0ETM23h7KYpV/YjmTqkvbe\noBQPv7NpDRCuFl+cjwcNGH8JR1Ic6x7YhU8pWRZvnnvaL4HaZJPXub4DiRLzFmLk\nZMLnhzNdy9Lj83F90dY0\n=m69P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:16:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKDYxMTM5MzY0YjNhYzU5NDM5NGE0OWJlOGE0ZjE2N2RiZTljZTk0MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/233389a9bc78a0b96775c571ed76591471449778","sha":"233389a9bc78a0b96775c571ed76591471449778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/233389a9bc78a0b96775c571ed76591471449778"}],"sha":"61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/61139364b3ac594394a49be8a4f167dbe9ce9433"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/233389a9bc78a0b96775c571ed76591471449778/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:23:55Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:23:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: cancel superseded pull request runs (#2412)\n\n* ci: cancel superseded pull request runs\n\nThe three per-job concurrency groups already cancelled a superseded job when\nits replacement was queued, but they cancelled pushes to `main`, `next` and\n`hot-middleware` the same way. Those runs publish coverage, and cancelling\none also hides a breakage that is already on the branch.\n\nReplace them with a single workflow-level group that only cancels pull\nrequest runs. Besides fixing that, it cancels the whole superseded run at\nonce rather than job by job as each replacement is queued, it covers jobs\nthat have no group of their own, and a matrix dimension added later cannot\nbe forgotten in a group key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016aGHrb1YaEvaGwNELGEHjF\n\n* ci: give non-pull-request runs a concurrency group of their own\n\n`cancel-in-progress` only protects the run that is already executing. A\nconcurrency group holds at most one pending run, and GitHub cancels that\npending run whenever a newer one enters the group, whatever\n`cancel-in-progress` says. Keying every run of the workflow on the ref\ntherefore did not deliver what the comment promised: with one branch run\nexecuting and a second waiting, a third push would have evicted the second.\n\nGroup only pull request runs by ref; give everything else `github.run_id`,\nso each is a group of one that can be neither cancelled nor evicted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016aGHrb1YaEvaGwNELGEHjF\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8b76545918d39a0f39ed1283bd430f052d4643e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/a8b76545918d39a0f39ed1283bd430f052d4643e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/233389a9bc78a0b96775c571ed76591471449778","verification":{"payload":"tree a8b76545918d39a0f39ed1283bd430f052d4643e\nparent 4f1c3a3d55d82340cf7eaaaeac0bb90b4b63847b\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789748635 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789748635 +0300\n\nci: cancel superseded pull request runs (#2412)\n\n* ci: cancel superseded pull request runs\n\nThe three per-job concurrency groups already cancelled a superseded job when\nits replacement was queued, but they cancelled pushes to `main`, `next` and\n`hot-middleware` the same way. Those runs publish coverage, and cancelling\none also hides a breakage that is already on the branch.\n\nReplace them with a single workflow-level group that only cancels pull\nrequest runs. Besides fixing that, it cancels the whole superseded run at\nonce rather than job by job as each replacement is queued, it covers jobs\nthat have no group of their own, and a matrix dimension added later cannot\nbe forgotten in a group key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016aGHrb1YaEvaGwNELGEHjF\n\n* ci: give non-pull-request runs a concurrency group of their own\n\n`cancel-in-progress` only protects the run that is already executing. A\nconcurrency group holds at most one pending run, and GitHub cancels that\npending run whenever a newer one enters the group, whatever\n`cancel-in-progress` says. Keying every run of the workflow on the ref\ntherefore did not deliver what the comment promised: with one branch run\nexecuting and a second waiting, a third push would have evicted the second.\n\nGroup only pull request runs by ref; give everything else `github.run_id`,\nso each is a group of one that can be neither cancelled nor evicted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016aGHrb1YaEvaGwNELGEHjF\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"v