rs","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/a337174ccb37d33c2559d11c13929c445a29da80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:25:26Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T03:25:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build: update dependencies (#2394)\n\n* build: update dependencies\n\nBring every dependency up to its latest compatible version, including the\nmajor bumps of @types/node, execa and @changesets/cli. Regenerate types/\n(@types/node 26 now declares the node: protocol), reformat README.md for\nprettier 3.9, and refresh the logging snapshots for webpack 5.110.\n\n* build: keep execa on 9.x for the Node 20 baseline\n\nexeca 10 declares engines node >= 22 and calls Set.prototype.union at\nmodule load, which does not exist on Node 20. The package supports\nnode >= 20.9.0 and CI tests Node 20, where every logging test failed\nwith ''TEXT_ENCODINGS.union is not a function''.","tree":{"sha":"16ee2af8a7a971be5c7195d526ea05dc83749e5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/16ee2af8a7a971be5c7195d526ea05dc83749e5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/a337174ccb37d33c2559d11c13929c445a29da80","verification":{"payload":"tree 16ee2af8a7a971be5c7195d526ea05dc83749e5f\nparent 0641f95d09b919b21741dae49a9e2c6e25daf6a1\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788319526 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788319526 -0500\n\nbuild: update dependencies (#2394)\n\n* build: update dependencies\n\nBring every dependency up to its latest compatible version, including the\nmajor bumps of @types/node, execa and @changesets/cli. Regenerate types/\n(@types/node 26 now declares the node: protocol), reformat README.md for\nprettier 3.9, and refresh the logging snapshots for webpack 5.110.\n\n* build: keep execa on 9.x for the Node 20 baseline\n\nexeca 10 declares engines node >= 22 and calls Set.prototype.union at\nmodule load, which does not exist on Node 20. The package supports\nnode >= 20.9.0 and CI tests Node 20, where every logging test failed\nwith ''TEXT_ENCODINGS.union is not a function''.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql5cmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFMYQACEG49GU0QT4JANvPLaKiIec\nEINWcJe51yadIVqjyQoYpnbxwNmtagkXnThNG45/Rau0VA6ndGpDMEGly3DEruVm\nPwNRplGcNvJfqajqNfl/KGLRaSAUbkColgRL2mK6/vGig3BGAqes/yLbOM/kzUZN\nQ7WhSAL4xlwrfeuIyqU0KQM+wTGL00LZnpw+/DqXOUaspd4RjTwaAdWljWxJdkd4\nLw5MDR9xtDZM1ZXZ93rm+LhfiAxjwLTZ9oOosuPI+H7TmTk/aRRKkOAb5MMuhk6E\nOg72b0e0ba2l70xwJ33M1s0lr1O/caJX7qeBhFkfOA/uvRxbINNcdHNY+95I0qkZ\nXQ8bK2JK6jubBSEeXIM0rxPIMS6Kkjwf/NXjR0KWQ1Gtf0Mz4jfLllKmNsTIeKur\nQoUFAD8DjpdXaCbbGK9Vlz/4pFhspjsZz5/W7RukDqwTAy05VnDJYEVI90skGCny\nOFwR9d81D4prv6PrGvw9lM0dl9ROXo8p3K7sFFGpiUlzcJPZq8jg45G7VE0lEfqT\nFtolGnXpuUOmqwBFN+fHsX9+FsWHn5CczdmPxrE5lGJm/VWVmh/gr5t82mU0JIPm\nMZvP77y2s/0QBJ7+sSnBx0fhkqF2p9uythuZtAoYnf+IEsGArxe6eujGjPSh94Uv\nUucvmOyslmUTJsGtXqiy\n=GMnf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T03:25:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/a337174ccb37d33c2559d11c13929c445a29da80","node_id":"C_kwDOAFGXAtoAKGEzMzcxNzRjY2IzN2QzM2MyNTU5ZDExYzEzOTI5YzQ0NWEyOWRhODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commit/0641f95d09b919b21741dae49a9e2c6e25daf6a1","sha":"0641f95d09b919b21741dae49a9e2c6e25daf6a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/0641f95d09b919b21741dae49a9e2c6e25daf6a1"}],"sha":"a337174ccb37d33c2559d11c13929c445a29da80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/a337174ccb37d33c2559d11c13929c445a29da80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/0641f95d09b919b21741dae49a9e2c6e25daf6a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:06:19Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:06:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(hot): take the payload''s diagnostics from the stats option, deprecate statsOptions (#2392)\n\n* fix(hot): keep the stats fields the client needs, deprecate statsOptions\n\n8.2.0 shipped `hot.statsOptions`, and two of its values break hot module\nreplacement on a released API:\n\n- `{ hash: false }` removed the field `upToDate()` compares, so the client\n  never matched and stopped applying updates, silently.\n- `{ children: true }` sent `extractBundles` down its other branch and\n  published a child compilation''s hash in place of the bundle''s, so every\n  rebuild ended in \"Cannot find update (Full reload needed)\". Any project\n  whose plugins use child compilers could hit it.\n\n`hash`, `timings` and `children` now keep their values whatever the option\nasks for, which leaves `{ warnings: false }` — the one use that ever worked —\nintact. With `children` off, `extractBundles` was identity in every branch,\nso it is gone.\n\nThe option is deprecated in the same change and removed in the next major.\nNothing else it can express reaches a client: the payload is six fixed\nfields, so `{ all: true }` produces a byte-identical payload for ten times\nthe `toJson` cost.\n\n* docs(hot): mark the statsOptions removal in code\n\nA TODO at each of the two sites that go — the spread in `toBundles` and the\ndeprecation warning in `createHot` — following the `// TODO in the next major\nrelease` convention already in `src/`, and the typedef now carries it so a\nTypeScript user sees it on the property.\n\n* docs(hot): say what statsOptions still does until it is removed\n\nThe deprecation warning read as though the option had stopped working, and\nthe README''s warning-filtering section listed only the replacements. Both\nnow say that everything but `hash`, `timings` and `children` still applies\nuntil the next major.\n\n* feat(hot): take the payload''s diagnostics from the stats option\n\n`hot.statsOptions` duplicated an axis `stats` already covers, and `stats`\nalready accepts a preset, a boolean or an object. The payload''s `errors` and\n`warnings` now come from it — resolved per compilation through webpack''s own\n`createStatsOptions`, so `\"errors-only\"` means there what it means in the\nterminal — and one setting governs what a build reports in both places.\n\n`hot.statsOptions` still wins where it is set, so nothing that worked stops\nworking before it is removed.\n\nNote that `stats: false` now also keeps errors and warnings out of the\nbrowser, which is the point of the coupling but worth knowing when quieting\nthe terminal: the client''s ''?logging='' and ''?overlay='' control the browser\nper page, and webpack''s ''ignoreWarnings'' drops a warning everywhere.\n\n* chore(changeset): release the stats coupling as a minor\n\n`stats` does more than it did: someone quieting their terminal with\n`stats: false` now also stops seeing errors in the browser overlay. That is\nthe point of the coupling, but it is a behavior change a patch should not\ncarry silently, so the bump and the changelog entry say so.\n\n* docs(hot): point away from statsOptions everywhere it is named\n\nIts README section read as documentation for using it — what it merges, what\nit forwards to. It is now a warning plus a table of what to use instead, the\noptions table row says \"do not use\", the schema description says it too (so\na validation error does), and the migration guide maps\nwebpack-hot-middleware''s `statsOptions` onto `stats` rather than onto its\ndeprecated namesake.","tree":{"sha":"c6dcf5b22ef75e343a4e2a03679b54bfcb8dd1e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/c6dcf5b22ef75e343a4e2a03679b54bfcb8dd1e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/0641f95d09b919b21741dae49a9e2c6e25daf6a1","verification":{"payload":"tree c6dcf5b22ef75e343a4e2a03679b54bfcb8dd1e2\nparent 9cedcc1e97caffdd8b84199015833da4bef3ffec\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788296779 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788296779 +0300\n\nfeat(hot): take the payload''s diagnostics from the stats option, deprecate statsOptions (#2392)\n\n* fix(hot): keep the stats fields the client needs, deprecate statsOptions\n\n8.2.0 shipped `hot.statsOptions`, and two of its values break hot module\nreplacement on a released API:\n\n- `{ hash: false }` removed the field `upToDate()` compares, so the client\n  never matched and stopped applying updates, silently.\n- `{ children: true }` sent `extractBundles` down its other branch and\n  published a child compilation''s hash in place of the bundle''s, so every\n  rebuild ended in \"Cannot find update (Full reload needed)\". Any project\n  whose plugins use child compilers could hit it.\n\n`hash`, `timings` and `children` now keep their values whatever the option\nasks for, which leaves `{ warnings: false }` — the one use that ever worked —\nintact. With `children` off, `extractBundles` was identity in every branch,\nso it is gone.\n\nThe option is deprecated in the same change and removed in the next major.\nNothing else it can express reaches a client: the payload is six fixed\nfields, so `{ all: true }` produces a byte-identical payload for ten times\nthe `toJson` cost.\n\n* docs(hot): mark the statsOptions removal in code\n\nA TODO at each of the two sites that go — the spread in `toBundles` and the\ndeprecation warning in `createHot` — following the `// TODO in the next major\nrelease` convention already in `src/`, and the typedef now carries it so a\nTypeScript user sees it on the property.\n\n* docs(hot): say what statsOptions still does until it is removed\n\nThe deprecation warning read as though the option had stopped working, and\nthe README''s warning-filtering section listed only the replacements. Both\nnow say that everything but `hash`, `timings` and `children` still applies\nuntil the next major.\n\n* feat(hot): take the payload''s diagnostics from the stats option\n\n`hot.statsOptions` duplicated an axis `stats` already covers, and `stats`\nalready accepts a preset, a boolean or an object. The payload''s `errors` and\n`warnings` now come from it — resolved per compilation through webpack''s own\n`createStatsOptions`, so `\"errors-only\"` means there what it means in the\nterminal — and one setting governs what a build reports in both places.\n\n`hot.statsOptions` still wins where it is set, so nothing that worked stops\nworking before it is removed.\n\nNote that `stats: false` now also keeps errors and warnings out of the\nbrowser, which is the point of the coupling but worth knowing when quieting\nthe terminal: the client''s ''?logging='' and ''?overlay='' control the browser\nper page, and webpack''s ''ignoreWarnings'' drops a warning everywhere.\n\n* chore(changeset): release the stats coupling as a minor\n\n`stats` does more than it did: someone quieting their terminal with\n`stats: false` now also stops seeing errors in the browser overlay. That is\nthe point of the coupling, but it is a behavior change a patch should not\ncarry silently, so the bump and the changelog entry say so.\n\n* docs(hot): point away from statsOptions everywhere it is named\n\nIts README section read as documentation for using it — what it merges, what\nit forwards to. It is now a warning plus a table of what to use instead, the\noptions table row says \"do not use\", the schema description says it too (so\na validation error does), and the migration guide maps\nwebpack-hot-middleware''s `statsOptions` onto `stats` rather than onto its\ndeprecated namesake.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlz5LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4osQAKxkKw9UaiEWPUNzAFGJhKrX\nD6rag8tYVMEkFw+kw6pFxLImdwK6oxE/+WBwW7G/2laJg6st6JU4ziJK7iNjAs/e\nZbBUgBK2/obwNOf6rEkfolF5WUfDJTUbf0+HIGUGycxNnxvuXJlUmg5SGELhDpcY\n8izu4Z++aTLH4KqeAX/tzFHzY/HyVx1dA0nTkWy4xAPA3+Zxo3gxpU/Q5fJ5wOol\nGDSxpbGb3JHrEw9E8grXhrWClfIjBONOpL8TOF96ERgRdfrf2Uu5QIDWBN7ntKgy\nRT/51n9OPEIqs8AKilVdGBW3mMYFZ34iR5YyQVqrBEXaFPZ+b4lL0YjlXQ+q1KWx\nnOwCN986AYljhdWkjYfkuYffbw3w2EVixm/vntStPruC/bsBqbepKgGqpGsPdugG\n9llV/YNfcsw4I7YkPKvUyfRcPfpQctBdYtV2esR+CAyBFC2g4An/iFFAeNHzeaGN\no/5CqZ2x2K8Y0tIc6c0LrD+egKx/0IyuArly2pUbCaZ46oLir/NCjTIrvl7ydYm1\nt1fFEDu24scdK+dyJHdITpUa2aiYEW+cwmCz5DB2bXBrbh84nmtgbJHcFhxxJghX\ne4jg//Y8lyICDkkS6DnN/hyIryjhA5TNJbs6vBHFlosSd4vv1Hv9HUI5sqQy8eJw\nKjtEcThtrBvFV9lBEDJu\n=zmQL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T21:06:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","nod