r":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/commits/08ce43d0961b2ce9d3128d6eb697371ae4b226e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:47:27Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:47:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add a webpack-hot-middleware migration guide (#2391)\n\n* docs: add a webpack-hot-middleware migration guide\n\nOne file, migration-from-webpack-hot-middleware.md: prerequisites (the\nnode.js and webpack floors this package has and that one does not), the\nserver and webpack-configuration changes, every server and client option\nmapped, the behavior differences that bite (the `reload` default, warnings\nin the overlay, the dropped module map), the framework recipes that used to\nneed third-party bridges, the troubleshooting carried over from that\nproject''s README, and a checklist. README keeps a pointer instead of a\nsecond copy.\n\n* docs: state the upgrade step and narrow the compatibility claim\n\nRemoving webpack-hot-middleware does not upgrade the package that replaces\nit, so the guide now says to install it and shows the validation error an\nolder version answers `hot` with (taken from schema-utils, not written from\nmemory). The opening claimed the wire format was unchanged, which oversold\nit: the endpoint and its transport are, the payloads, option names and a few\ndefaults are not, and the two sections that cover them are linked from\nthere.\n\n* docs: label the error-output code fence\n\nEvery other fence in the guide names its language; this one did not, which\nmarkdownlint reports as MD040.","tree":{"sha":"ac2fa00cab1aaec82ecaa838b5ac4a156fe94f33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/trees/ac2fa00cab1aaec82ecaa838b5ac4a156fe94f33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack-dev-middleware/git/commits/08ce43d0961b2ce9d3128d6eb697371ae4b226e5","verification":{"payload":"tree ac2fa00cab1aaec82ecaa838b5ac4a156fe94f33\nparent d30b48bde64e04b3b91a3155a8bee3d8c45ecbfd\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788292047 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788292047 +0300\n\ndocs: add a webpack-hot-middleware migration guide (#2391)\n\n* docs: add a webpack-hot-middleware migration guide\n\nOne file, migration-from-webpack-hot-middleware.md: prerequisites (the\nnode.js and webpack floors this package has and that one does not), the\nserver and webpack-configuration changes, every server and client option\nmapped, the behavior differences that bite (the `reload` default, warnings\nin the overlay, the dropped module map), the framework recipes that used to\nneed third-party bridges, the troubleshooting carried over from that\nproject''s README, and a checklist. README keeps a pointer instead of a\nsecond copy.\n\n* docs: state the upgrade step and narrow the compatibility claim\n\nRemoving webpack-hot-middleware does not upgrade the package that replaces\nit, so the guide now says to install it and shows the validation error an\nolder version answers `hot` with (taken from schema-utils, not written from\nmemory). The opening claimed the wire format was unchanged, which oversold\nit: the endpoint and its transport are, the payloads, option names and a few\ndefaults are not, and the two sections that cover them are linked from\nthere.\n\n* docs: label the error-output code fence\n\nEvery other fence in the guide names its language; this one did not, which\nmarkdownlint reports as MD040.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlyvPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjhUQAFybm9DPFB/pa1VLYbcTP7Gu\nlUQHN9BNyH8eGlzNqjgCajnwOIsihQislsVMUIXJjyGABt/P5zZXmOYVyXlVAo8q\nEIewB2eXwyRmV6y2l2225j0gEZB2on2qf0t7dcWp6hFperMvrxicCgqTFPWzMnTn\noLeoicCqQxvcO31AUOazEAHJ8QBiWA88zeDsiRo3NTU2hVmLXhYZ6oMiYhOVvrYc\njLQ8YHHUSXYnSm7s9zFHo2OunqQuOmSD8vm8uwOePb/BM9gZK1i4dn8heftJoVZH\naKsY2GXTAw6TaycLrDSQ7OwgYnmB5/LNpgyBZ0n9gvT6Oh4un7fJAqTuwtyZYcYR\n5dLcHtuzDmmlkPFknVFPjJYm1aLNBcx4Wzzn8qYQb7+QkXGTNTTRmFoStHRtCknt\n3JyuA856mcqVdOToY9COBT56rM2edQ0kz/EBN29wnzpCbQErsILq6mJNMBSyD4FN\nmsdouzLVgOkLhXvOEFfNgXbBQ9hVcBCZ5xrAzO3DS2K9bKKaXY8kfiPBh+74ygJh\nzyUWr7UbuwX9pEpCx1YyUExKoauBIIpEhcEkZ36ZpyGVBm/mObLSxmLgGxGXl4OW\nSpofwo2NNc+cYoSw79aiuWhOVt/Oivf0vBP9+prgmOSxWkSibU/0QgBCYWo83rFK\niRPYc45coJP39EQya8em\n=Q9+M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T19:47:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web