ules\n(DisguiseMetaphors, LabelAndExplain, EmphaticItalics, MicDrop,\nFalseExclusivity), each trimmed of the patterns that fire on pre-2023\nposts, plus BenBalter.Redundancy moved from the book. It also fixes the\nBuzzwords message (arguments were swapped) and several false positives.\n\nThe remaining ai-tells candidates were measured against posts before\nand after ChatGPT and none earned a place: they fire on pre-2023 voice,\nduplicate AIPatterns, or never fire. The .vale.ini comment records the\nmeasurement so it doesn''t need redoing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7bec1f3ba5bc0203f193bc20201ff3eba82d95d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/7bec1f3ba5bc0203f193bc20201ff3eba82d95d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/db1709eb37b7d9b55e3861452269d2eb25acf7d1","verification":{"payload":"tree 7bec1f3ba5bc0203f193bc20201ff3eba82d95d3\nparent cb5c691d97b8ba3bb847d4042a48d1ed717cef87\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791324916 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791325102 -0400\n\nBump vale-styles to v0.0.6 and record why ai-tells stays off\n\nv0.0.6 adds curated AIPatterns versions of five ai-tells rules\n(DisguiseMetaphors, LabelAndExplain, EmphaticItalics, MicDrop,\nFalseExclusivity), each trimmed of the patterns that fire on pre-2023\nposts, plus BenBalter.Redundancy moved from the book. It also fixes the\nBuzzwords message (arguments were swapped) and several false positives.\n\nThe remaining ai-tells candidates were measured against posts before\nand after ChatGPT and none earned a place: they fire on pre-2023 voice,\nduplicate AIPatterns, or never fire. The .vale.ini comment records the\nmeasurement so it doesn''t need redoing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0