e the link was the whole point (a \"Continue\nReading →\" to the dead article, a bare URL repeating a citation) drop\nit outright; a bare URL would just be autolinked again.\n\nThe WP Document Revisions \"Development version\" link pointed at a\ndevelop branch the repo no longer has; it now points at main, the\ncurrent default branch, rather than being removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"385c930d3f5ca89e5133ef6ac85064dfcbf75415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/385c930d3f5ca89e5133ef6ac85064dfcbf75415"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/16cc60a29ea2b4051f3cd00688047254dd137d51","verification":{"payload":"tree 385c930d3f5ca89e5133ef6ac85064dfcbf75415\nparent 85dcd93c6b04d90a054e13ea8f2d4ac1341a444d\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791129989 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791129989 -0400\n\nUnlink dead links that have no archived copy\n\nRefs #1915. These links are dead and the Wayback Machine has no 200\nsnapshot of them, so there''s nothing to point readers at. Keep the link\ntext and drop the link. Where the link was the whole point (a \"Continue\nReading →\" to the dead article, a bare URL repeating a citation) drop\nit outright; a bare URL would just be autolinked again.\n\nThe WP Document Revisions \"Development version\" link pointed at a\ndevelop branch the repo no longer has; it now points at main, the\ncurrent default branch, rather than being removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQP2kBSrB2lh/uQBrRmp1V7qmuLgXmbISIC0vwVpo+v4rbMPeZpsABCJ4IGU8uziQ6H\np/Uo3Vz5nR6/Gck9S4XA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T16:06:31Z"}},"committer":{"