_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/518f23c9ea93220089b6a5b061c4e9c7cc5ddd57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:14Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:14Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Make script/remark report-only, as documented, and drop a stale test\n\nscript/remark and script/README.md both said it was report-only, but it\nran `npm run lint-md`, which runs markdownlint-cli2 --fix over every\nMarkdown file. It now runs `remark .` and lint-md-check.\n\narchived-posts.test.ts asserted against its own inline copy of the\nfilter, never the real isListablePost, so it couldn''t catch a\nregression; post-filtering.test.ts already covers the real functions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"edc2fe03bdd90ed82915f96ebf10286b0c471f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/edc2fe03bdd90ed82915f96ebf10286b0c471f6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/518f23c9ea93220089b6a5b061c4e9c7cc5ddd57","verification":{"payload":"tree edc2fe03bdd90ed82915f96ebf10286b0c471f6d\nparent fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126014 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126014 -0400\n\nMake script/remark report-only, as documented, and drop a stale test\n\nscript/remark and script/README.md both said it was report-only, but it\nran `npm run lint-md`, which runs markdownlint-cli2 --fix over every\nMarkdown file. It now runs `remark .` and lint-md-check.\n\narchived-posts.test.ts asserted against its own inline copy of the\nfilter, never the real isListablePost, so it couldn''t catch a\nregression; post-filtering.test.ts already covers the real functions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHF7Kgxj1nz48y3iRbOmoQdzDwVW/MV3SzljOOq7Z4LTSSkXo6pKomtWNETDdq3UZX\ni8cjlhLPvN4VCGAuYcfQI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:00:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/518f23c9ea93220089b6a5b061c4e9c7cc5ddd57","node_id":"C_kwDOAFLaS9oAKDUxOGYyM2M5ZWE5MzIyMDA4OWI2YTViMDYxYzRlOWM3Y2M1ZGRkNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98","sha":"fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98"}],"sha":"518f23c9ea93220089b6a5b061c4e9c7cc5ddd57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/518f23c9ea93220089b6a5b061c4e9c7cc5ddd57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:14Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:14Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Record the inbound referrer origin, not the page URL, on events\n\nThe Worker stored the request''s Referer header as the event referrer.\nFor a same-origin beacon that''s the page the event fired on, full URL\nwith query string, so blob3 duplicated the path plus any utm/email\nparams: useless for attribution and at odds with the \"no identifiers\"\nnotes in both files.\n\nThe client now sends document.referrer and the Worker keeps only its\norigin (http/https only). Nothing queries blob3 yet, so no consumers\nneed updating; rows written before this deploy have page URLs there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d26de7c5e25d575265d3ec4629e8bd76473ee3d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/d26de7c5e25d575265d3ec4629e8bd76473ee3d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98","verification":{"payload":"tree d26de7c5e25d575265d3ec4629e8bd76473ee3d6\nparent 91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126014 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126014 -0400\n\nRecord the inbound referrer origin, not the page URL, on events\n\nThe Worker stored the request''s Referer header as the event referrer.\nFor a same-origin beacon that''s the page the event fired on, full URL\nwith query string, so blob3 duplicated the path plus any utm/email\nparams: useless for attribution and at odds with the \"no identifiers\"\nnotes in both files.\n\nThe client now sends document.referrer and the Worker keeps only its\norigin (http/https only). Nothing queries blob3 yet, so no consumers\nneed updating; rows written before this deploy have page URLs there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOqBkbvBEiul15DlbJsJQ8ol5RridtKtBkhT72MSZcfy9nBKk5ZTT2NrRln2Jfd76F\ntkHtylzqxErJIYAubnEgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:00:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98","node_id":"C_kwDOAFLaS9oAKGZhYzQ1YTk5Yjg5YmIzMTk3ODkxNGI0NmQ2M2E2OTRmZTc5OTlmOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d","sha":"91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d"}],"sha":"fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/fac45a99b89bb31978914b46d63a694fe7999f98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:14Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:14Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Allowlist reviewed gitleaks findings so the weekly scan passes\n\nThe scheduled full-history secret scan has failed every week since at\nleast early September on six findings, none of them real secrets:\nplaceholder curl examples in docs/CLOUDFLARE-CACHE.md, per-build Next.js\npreview-mode keys from the old .next/cache, and a 2012 Disqus public API\nkey (meant to be embedded client-side). History can''t be rewritten, so\nlist their fingerprints. A permanently red job hides real findings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8915a7d0356fe1c4331a237fc500ad7f9b4626db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/8915a7d0356fe1c4331a237fc500ad7f9b4626db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8915a7d0356fe1c4331a237fc500ad7f9b4626db\nparent ce8d442505160f02d028dfd4b6c064a46b9aa9ab\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126014 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126014 -0400\n\nAllowlist reviewed gitleaks findings so the weekly scan passes\n\nThe scheduled full-history secret scan has failed every week since at\nleast early September on six findings, none of them real secrets:\nplaceholder curl examples in docs/CLOUDFLARE-CACHE.md, per-build Next.js\npreview-mode keys from the old .next/cache, and a 2012 Disqus public API\nkey (meant to be embedded client-side). History can''t be rewritten, so\nlist their fingerprints. A permanently red job hides real findings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFBIhccYUHwe4IJP0nrWDfsZI8Be5pxU1/uBT3kqBI7+EFmoMTGly8HkyijPC/JHRz\n+ExdmcW5CySIFWJxZ4JwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:00:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d","node_id":"C_kwDOAFLaS9oAKDkxNTc5MTIwYjg1YzVhY2ZhMzExZTA2YzcxMjQ4NDNiOTA0YjQ4MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/ce8d442505160f02d028dfd4b6c064a46b9aa9ab","sha":"ce8d442505160f02d028dfd4b6c064a46b9aa9ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/ce8d442505160f02d028dfd4b6c064a46b9aa9ab"}],"sha":"91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/91579120b85c5acfa311e06c7124843b904b480d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/ce8d442505160f02d028dfd4b6c064a46b9aa9ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:12Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:00:12Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Always run CI so its required checks always report\n\nContent Linting, Code Tests, Run Astro Check and Run Vitest Tests are\nrequired checks, but ci.yml had a `paths` filter on its triggers. A PR\ntouching only filtered-out files never ran the workflow, so the checks\nnever reported and the PR couldn''t merge without an admin bypass. The\nsame bug #2064 fixed for the E2E workflow.\n\nThe filter only excluded ~70 files (public/ images and a few dotfiles,\nincluding .vale-ai-tells.ini, which #2054 is stuck on), so dropping it\ncosts little, unlike the E2E build where a job-level filter pays off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dace67ecff6c17cf562ac6b39ce2abc804bb737a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/dace67ecff6c17cf562ac6b39ce2abc804bb737a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/ce8d442505160f02d028dfd4b6c064a46b9aa9ab","verification":{"payload":"tree dace67ecff6c17cf562ac6b39ce2abc804bb737a\nparent 61541e132ab6f007407a99a061bbcf9791999a64\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126012 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791126012 -0400\n\nAlways run CI so its required checks always report\n\nContent Linting, Code Tests, Run Astro Check and Run Vitest Tests are\nrequired checks, but ci.yml had a `paths` filter on its triggers. A PR\ntouching only filtered-out files never ran the workflow, so the checks\nnever reported and the PR couldn''t merge without an admin bypass. The\nsame bug #2064 fixed for the E2E workflow.\n\nThe filter only excluded ~70 files (public/ images and a few dotfiles,\nincluding .vale-ai-tells.ini, which #2054 is stuck on), so dropping it\ncosts little, unlike the E2E build where a job-level filter pays off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1