:{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:16:53Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:29:47Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Move CLAUDE.md to AGENTS.md\n\nGitHub Copilot reads AGENTS.md (cloud agent, CLI, code review on\nGitHub.com, VS Code) and Claude Code can import it from CLAUDE.md, so\nAGENTS.md can be the one instruction file both tools share. This commit\nis the bare rename so history follows the file; the next one merges in\nthe Copilot instructions and adds the CLAUDE.md import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5bb48f132dc0ba8df077be94b5a8d0ee9d072f11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/5bb48f132dc0ba8df077be94b5a8d0ee9d072f11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/7de44c0a3ae4f17a3c379c96f8e4c5d2445d2205","verification":{"payload":"tree 5bb48f132dc0ba8df077be94b5a8d0ee9d072f11\nparent 09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791055013 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791120587 -0400\n\nMove CLAUDE.md to AGENTS.md\n\nGitHub Copilot reads AGENTS.md (cloud agent, CLI, code review on\nGitHub.com, VS Code) and Claude Code can import it from CLAUDE.md, so\nAGENTS.md can be the one instruction file both tools share. This commit\nis the bare rename so history follows the file; the next one merges in\nthe Copilot instructions and adds the CLAUDE.md import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEKhCmwaqzoy9IFAa1HjqCq+PUEwmIUAvd9EPaJ6CMVhBm+nvbOSE/pAcj9UMAiNha\na/4lIiYsJE55M9jvYctgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T13:30:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/7de44c0a3ae4f17a3c379c96f8e4c5d2445d2205","node_id":"C_kwDOAFLaS9oAKDdkZTQ0YzBhM2FlNGYxN2EzYzM3OWM5NmY4ZTRjNWQyNDQ1ZDIyMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commit/09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a","sha":"09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a"}],"sha":"7de44c0a3ae4f17a3c379c96f8e4c5d2445d2205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/7de44c0a3ae4f17a3c379c96f8e4c5d2445d2205"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:11:29Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:11:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Remove em dashes from agent-instruction files and gate them in CI (#2062)\n\nCLAUDE.md bans em dashes as the top AI tell, but the agent-instruction\nfiles (CLAUDE.md itself, copilot-instructions.md, and the .github/agents\nprompts) still used them, about 60 in all. Those files model the voice\nagents write in, so every \"craft—clear\" in them quietly taught the\npattern the rule forbids. Each one is now a comma, colon, semicolon,\nparentheses, or a sentence split, chosen per sentence. The rule''s own\n`—` examples stay, since they''re in code spans.\n\nAIPatterns.EmDash is only a warning (kept that way in 334a5da0 so the\npost archive can be cleaned up over time), and script/vale gates on\nerrors and never looked at .github, so nothing stopped these from\ncoming back. script/vale now runs that one rule over the\nagent-instruction files and fails on any hit, and CI''s path filter\npicks up changes under .github/agents, .github/instructions, and\ncopilot-instructions.md so edits there trigger the check.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d325126f20a80605fe6d1836caf8312d003528e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/8d325126f20a80605fe6d1836caf8312d003528e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d325126f20a80605fe6d1836caf8312d003528e\nparent 19b14ecbe24154b41675373b898c83d01eacf1d9\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791119489 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791119489 -0400\n\nRemove em dashes from agent-instruction files and gate them in CI (#2062)\n\nCLAUDE.md bans em dashes as the top AI tell, but the agent-instruction\nfiles (CLAUDE.md itself, copilot-instructions.md, and the .github/agents\nprompts) still used them, about 60 in all. Those files model the voice\nagents write in, so every \"craft—clear\" in them quietly taught the\npattern the rule forbids. Each one is now a comma, colon, semicolon,\nparentheses, or a sentence split, chosen per sentence. The rule''s own\n`—` examples stay, since they''re in code spans.\n\nAIPatterns.EmDash is only a warning (kept that way in 334a5da0 so the\npost archive can be cleaned up over time), and script/vale gates on\nerrors and never looked at .github, so nothing stopped these from\ncoming back. script/vale now runs that one rule over the\nagent-instruction files and fails on any hit, and CI''s path filter\npicks up changes under .github/agents, .github/instructions, and\ncopilot-instructions.md so edits there trigger the check.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwlCBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAOcQAI4trKJsRa4UtCxyO4d55jd4\nfhYF54pvwgo7rEnrofpcV8gOjzKcUKjN31V5aC3NgxFSDKT7PjHY+gG+eRjTCRhF\nUwM2Khs/oIq0l4Du1SIFJd5n0KRzD8e5ow7I1lpDI1Kuri3i3bUkEcL4sx0fq5Js\nxd45i2Jem7cJCeQTjQ1MfT/1Itdyd3vAUyeQwucmVh69konGHy71zuY55L6p31Mw\nOLd+3oQZcW9Ri6FNMTl15K0kBcu+84MEi6cAv6Xc18sNAHeMVQe5+us9Xr37teUt\n9loCTi0sy4UNTPRAiw5pN1dYE/vtAona