ter/benbalter.github.com/commits/09ff349b819ce896197b34b017ced3d93dbffe7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/commits/19b14ecbe24154b41675373b898c83d01eacf1d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T12:50:42Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T12:50:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Drop generic rules from CLAUDE.md and clean up non-inclusive terms (#2061)\n\nBen''s global CLAUDE.md now covers shipping the smallest change, linting only touched files, and running typecheck/tests before committing, so restating them here creates a second source of truth that can drift. This keeps the repo-specific parts: the actual commands, and why repo-wide lint is dangerous here (`npm run lint`/`lint-md` run eslint --fix and markdownlint --fix across every file). It also drops a duplicated \"run npm run check before committing\" line; the copy under Testing remains.\n\nPer the global inclusive-language guidance, swaps \"sanity check\" for \"spot-check\" in a strip-markdown test fixture (free text, not tied to any post), and removes \"whitelisted\"/\"whitelists\" from the spellcheck dictionary. Nothing in the repo uses those words, so retext-spell will now flag them in future drafts instead of silently accepting them.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b8071daa4096a8c886b84f559e0a0c67d2cb521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/2b8071daa4096a8c886b84f559e0a0c67d2cb521"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/19b14ecbe24154b41675373b898c83d01eacf1d9","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b8071daa4096a8c886b84f559e0a0c67d2cb521\nparent 368aecbec8cfe1be3059b3ac9190f091dd919a32\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791118242 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791118242 -0400\n\nDrop generic rules from CLAUDE.md and clean up non-inclusive terms (#2061)\n\nBen''s global CLAUDE.md now covers shipping the smallest change, linting only touched files, and running typecheck/tests before committing, so restating them here creates a second source of truth that can drift. This keeps the repo-specific parts: the actual commands, and why repo-wide lint is dangerous here (`npm run lint`/`lint-md` run eslint --fix and markdownlint --fix across every file). It also drops a duplicated \"run npm run check before committing\" line; the copy under Testing remains.\n\nPer the global inclusive-language guidance, swaps \"sanity check\" for \"spot-check\" in a strip-markdown test fixture (free text, not tied to any post), and removes \"whitelisted\"/\"whitelists\" from the spellcheck dictionary. Nothing in the repo uses those words, so retext-spell will now flag them in future drafts instead of silently accepting them.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwkuiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlA