comment, per the\ninclusive-language guidance.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"900e6ca1f940a7ec06c19b04d48da0ca0fbdb14f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/trees/900e6ca1f940a7ec06c19b04d48da0ca0fbdb14f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/benbalter.github.com/git/commits/4cd15899c1b9abb3db31096581677564f6224263","verification":{"payload":"tree 900e6ca1f940a7ec06c19b04d48da0ca0fbdb14f\nparent 0eb8dc96e2175f15e86fe29f68ea46474aa79dcf\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791054896 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791054896 -0400\n\nAlign agent instructions with global CLAUDE.md conventions (#2057)\n\nThe global CLAUDE.md now asks for unwrapped Markdown (hard wraps make every\nedit reflow neighboring lines) and for CLAUDE.md files to link file and tool\nmentions inline. Most of CLAUDE.md was already one line per item, but the\nBookmarklets and \"most-read posts\" sections were hard-wrapped, and file paths\nwere bare code spans. Unwrapping also clears remark''s list-item-spacing\nwarnings on this file.\n\nAlso swaps \"sanity check\" for \"spot-check\" in a script comment, per the\ninclusive-language guidance.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwVQwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUTkQAJqQZwHPQFvDh5gm/Y6OY5Wd\nNQ3hQgE8VcLO5+zpGrw6TIrau91zWjAksVzsLMIZ7lIYkugmhCRuWVlbh+mXAC+n\noLf5jFGGkdh8wH9TWVHbVpMkd1dp2MgDptjWvRGJ7hsdD/17wqAuRbz8MHgcuwlt\n+G1DZl/bO4e2ZU0iHSNswR7AOAs4s9ca3e2X8u2XbOVsSB4Pg2YSCO8cQmiPBRVT\nXjTaMwwgDeEQWCqNaJutEnE0/NksiLLgJWs1DETOhnvo2s1phXFvlvvpNwG2dhjf\nAcevT2KxK/vjThbJBaYlI+jvHeNW1wDxt4v6gOGoXhZ6Fjz8+ANXVoOolHzsH/bO\nkNEYdSBd7NT6HuLrppef03YtLs7QcZrfdm1WWS4uSvCnQrB32b9koyMw3Uzq9WF6\n5NXMkgTeyEbFqCpWDHTUvzlwSK+nNl58pcRLz1JbWwGvJl9Lq4+ns/f1Bt1XHW3j\naJezrMX6JqlVlUwClWUe9ue8PDDQnWyalQ3TcPjaQVlfepJEusxx8DPB91Y78Xbf\nwDJH9AzwaW4p2zuLFeAESh3dLSNuLu7hiUVCsBEGY7YLuqeVE8tYiPMfT