ns","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/8bbd84119a8ae4addb492081f13c37a21387304e","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDhiYmQ4NDExOWE4YWU0YWRkYjQ5MjA4MWYxM2MzN2EyMTM4NzMwNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/b469775a750e1436e1b176466f4e53ac0c72848b","sha":"b469775a750e1436e1b176466f4e53ac0c72848b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/b469775a750e1436e1b176466f4e53ac0c72848b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361","sha":"5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361"}],"sha":"8bbd84119a8ae4addb492081f13c37a21387304e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/8bbd84119a8ae4addb492081f13c37a21387304e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T11:59:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T11:59:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore: suppress java:S1874 at the single deprecated RBACUtils call\n\nThe PR quality gate failed on one new maintainability issue: RBACUtils is\ndeprecated. The class is deprecated as a whole and not forRemoval, and the\nplatform exports no replacement, so revokePermissionFromRole is the only\nsupported way to drop a weak reference from a role''s j:permissions.\n\nReimplementing it by hand would mean reproducing its path validation, its\nidentifier match and its becomes-empty branch inside a security migration --\nmore risk than the deprecation carries. Suppress the rule at the one call\nsite with the justification the class javadoc already records, rather than\nrewriting working platform code to satisfy a style threshold.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"040c948c3c860643616d7b78b501a974d8bbacdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/040c948c3c860643616d7b78b501a974d8bbacdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361","verification":{"payload":"tree 040c948c3c860643616d7b78b501a974d8bbacdb\nparent ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788782364 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788782364 +0200\n\nchore: suppress java:S1874 at the single deprecated RBACUtils call\n\nThe PR quality gate failed on one new maintainability issue: RBACUtils is\ndeprecated. The class is deprecated as a whole and not forRemoval, and the\nplatform exports no replacement, so revokePermissionFromRole is the only\nsupported way to drop a weak reference from a role''s j:permissions.\n\nReimplementing it by hand would mean reproducing its path validation, its\nidentifier match and its becomes-empty branch inside a security migration --\nmore risk than the deprecation carries. Suppress the rule at the one call\nsite with the justification the class javadoc already records, rather than\nrewriting working platform code to satisfy a style threshold.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqepxwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3m0FAgAuFswS370prbD9gLc4HgFfIhtpi282CarKuYqPjGZh6mPc5Mpb2r34y4j\ncnUVTwm7GsinJIaObZVjrT+LwKFhPqwXQRB6vMnWfC05DQR1oMlv5IzEujXblSL1\nsCJWvzJV6cfiCX0PRNB1h2GBVoqtykKMRiEq/GgluTRCgZu2ogRPigW6teFHMgAV\nARm/1CtLRkZy+3jt3ZPPh7Aw6mbycqwa7vx97RXixDVXdSObP7G/yFDXqgeTQh9c\n41ZuC9TAtuBJTgOqqnty4v0p1N5ba0ozcd2Ib+A2Hzg7HacoNWAxsICQ9MJktOBb\nbD6YgpfL1IMH3Pi/2GibRQkssUSMrQ==\n=2abM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:59:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDUzODhiMmI1MDg4NTc4YTgxMDg3MzQ0YTkzNzgzZmQxMDVlYjIzNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967","sha":"ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967"}],"sha":"5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/5388b2b5088578a81087344a93783fd105eb2361"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:32:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:32:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: correct the SEC-366 specs against the real platform behaviour\n\nBoth specs now pass on the harness. Four things they got wrong, found by running\nthem rather than by reading them:\n\n- grantRoles takes roleNames, not roles, and the principal enum is PrincipalType,\n  not JCRPrincipalType. Read from graphql-dxm-provider 3.7.0 bytecode because\n  Jahia''s security filter blocks GraphQL introspection even for root.\n- The positive-control arm granted site-administrator but probed\n  jahiaForgeModerateModule. That permission belongs to this module''s\n  store-administrator role; Jahia''s site-administrator does not carry it, so the\n  probe read false whether or not the grant landed and the arm proved nothing.\n  All arms now use store-administrator, which is also the role the advisory names\n  as the escalation prize.\n- 24 read the uploaded node back in EDIT. The store front-end renders live, so\n  the action creates its nodes in the live workspace and nothing publishes them.\n- 24 asserted on the ACE node name. Jahia names an ACE after the principal\n  (''GRANT_u_storedev'') and keeps the roles in its j:roles property, so the name\n  alone shows an entry exists for someone, not that it grants owner.\n\nWhat they now establish: a store-developer''s LIVE self-promotion is refused (it\nreturned grantRoles: true before), the EDIT control arm stays refused, the\ncapability probe still moves when the role is granted legitimately, and a\nstore-developer can still complete an upload and end up owning both created\nnodes - the APPS-14 regression the advisory''s own one-line fix would have caused.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbe32bdab26a4d7c74e98512c2e84f8a3fb30e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/bbe32bdab26a4d7c74e98512c2e84f8a3fb30e57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967","verification":{"payload":"tree bbe32bdab26a4d7c74e98512c2e84f8a3fb30e57\nparent 3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788705170 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788705170 +0200\n\ntest: correct the SEC-366 specs against the real platform behaviour\n\nBoth specs now pass on the harness. Four things they got wrong, found by running\nthem rather than by reading them:\n\n- grantRoles takes roleNames, not roles, and the principal enum is PrincipalType,\n  not JCRPrincipalType. Read from graphql-dxm-provider 3.7.0 bytecode because\n  Jahia''s security filter blocks GraphQL introspection even for root.\n- The positive-control arm granted site-administrator but probed\n  jahiaForgeModerateModule. That permission belongs to this module''s\n  store-administrator role; Jahia''s site-administrator does not carry it, so the\n  probe read false whether or not the grant landed and the arm proved nothing.\n  All arms now use store-administrator, which is also the role the advisory names\n  as the escalation prize.\n- 24 read the uploaded node back in EDIT. The store front-end renders live, so\n  the action creates its nodes in the live workspace and nothing publishes them.\n- 24 asserted on the ACE node name. Jahia names an ACE after the principal\n  (''GRANT_u_storedev'') and keeps the roles in its j:roles property, so the name\n  alone shows an entry exists for someone, not that it grants owner.\n\nWhat they now establish: a store-developer''s LIVE self-promotion is refused (it\nreturned grantRoles: true before), the EDIT control arm stays refused, the\ncapability probe still moves when the role is granted legitimately, and a\nstore-developer can still complete an upload and end up owning both created\nnodes - the APPS-14 regression the advisory''s own one-line fix would have caused.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdeZIACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nTiAf+IEfhnRdlKDc9kqoiyMG5TRGzI8gYGb2ek/1MSWqKFgBB+qUBYJaWAgY5\nnISjo7sQwfei+l6yex8dBWUps7Ae7IusqTC5VnZsl6E7iKmM3tp0M2uo4Jl80O4v\nhRP3NQIxQ1kpGB07Hf3vwejjhnSh1/21VQR5Am3N3e2AJv2jbgAS3+fW6r1UcJaZ\n1/hYhggc1MLIsgrcq7NKz7Z4rGgXe+8u4Lcb5x9yzJe+5KuSfE6CMLkY6gj5gjoq\nYPxo2/GucM4eOxf1Ti8cqr1/VLhCXKjSXoQkVxY5fJYb2vXrHYAa9MbBzbdH508T\nXeN5/wwAIlH9NSCM7W4QvbNiKzpaYQ==\n=YfMx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKGZmZDYzOGMyZTZhNjY5ZmQ2Y2YyYWY1NDVlMTk4ZTU2ZTM4ZWI5Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71","sha":"3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71"}],"sha":"ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/ffd638c2e6a669fd6cf2af545e198e56e38eb967"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:32:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:32:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(tests): make the harness actually able to run the suite\n\nThree defects, all of which made the run misreport rather than fail loudly.\n\n1. docker-compose never forwarded PRIVATEAPPSTORE_VERSION or\n   STORE_TEMPLATE_VERSION into the cypress container, so cypress.config.ts fell\n   back to its hardcoded 5.0.1-SNAPSHOT defaults and 01-modulesInstalled\n   asserted a version nobody had built. The pom is at 5.1.0-SNAPSHOT.\n\n2. .env.example pinned PRIVATEAPPSTORE_VERSION to a version older than the pom.\n\n3. .env.example wrote the license as JAHIA_LICENSE=${JAHIA_LICENSE:-\"\"}. That\n   idiom is for bash ''source''; Docker Compose interpolates .env values but does\n   not strip the quotes from the default, so a quoted license arrives as\n   ''\"PGph...'' and the entrypoint base64-decodes it to an empty license.xml.\n   Jahia then boots unlicensed (''Error while loading license file!\n   SAXParseException: Premature end of file'') and every non-root login NPEs in\n   LicenseManager.getJahiaLicensePackage. That single misconfiguration failed 15\n   of 23 specs, none of them for a reason in the code under test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"39666386f9bce13b5c8c99a0632eec9a8acb1bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/39666386f9bce13b5c8c99a0632eec9a8acb1bef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71","verification":{"payload":"tree 39666386f9bce13b5c8c99a0632eec9a8acb1bef\nparent dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788705158 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788705158 +0200\n\nfix(tests): make the harness actually able to run the suite\n\nThree defects, all of which made the run misreport rather than fail loudly.\n\n1. docker-compose never forwarded PRIVATEAPPSTORE_VERSION or\n   STORE_TEMPLATE_VERSION into the cypress container, so cypress.config.ts fell\n   back to its hardcoded 5.0.1-SNAPSHOT defaults and 01-modulesInstalled\n   asserted a version nobody had built. The pom is at 5.1.0-SNAPSHOT.\n\n2. .env.example pinned PRIVATEAPPSTORE_VERSION to a version older than the pom.\n\n3. .env.example wrote the license as JAHIA_LICENSE=${JAHIA_LICENSE:-\"\"}. That\n   idiom is for bash ''source''; Docker Compose interpolates .env values but does\n   not strip the quotes from the default, so a quoted license arrives as\n   ''\"PGph...'' and the entrypoint base64-decodes it to an empty license.xml.\n   Jahia then boots unlicensed (''Error while loading license file!\n   SAXParseException: Premature end of file'') and every non-root login NPEs in\n   LicenseManager.getJahiaLicensePackage. That single misconfiguration failed 15\n   of 23 specs, none of them for a reason in the code under test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdeYYACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kSQQf/ZFmqlL7OUVhM8dHtCoQ6OlRHubZtTkd8wZXy4LYWofEk9JB91dDDvKqL\n263TUgbFM1uJ7ji07G8NWKxBDy6mwwi236E+iLVyylaP+1kMVrA7cN9+4V9SXPIu\nMbmbZ6Oap4Yd3QoLkiMy/+DL3NDxSjLn3bUqOctP1KnqS81EFb/C5DywC+z0TvNK\nBkKfIDQpr/+vFPCghX9UMqCZAkbTGlvEEqowswWDTs6qsXNy4we4gPMtxKcQFUr5\nymlOjHlA59M7KMEP3OkApxAwjaIh7C8JY61oZUIGHPOyHprpRvzRmMVvA0Myx4Hu\nVQIzasoWwcLfpfVhZ71baHbgio13nw==\n=nJYS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDNhYmZkOWZlNTI2ZGQwMDA5YTkyMDU0YTkxYzBlYzgzNWEyZmFhNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d","sha":"dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d"}],"sha":"3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/3abfd9fe526dd0009a92054a91c0ec835a2faa71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T13:07:40Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T13:07:40Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor: address Sonar findings in the SEC-366 code\n\n- Rename OwnerRoleGrants.record to recordOwner: ''record'' is a restricted\n  identifier from Java 16 (java:S6213).\n- Swap doExecuteWithSystemSession(user, workspace, cb) for\n  doExecuteWithSystemSessionAsUser(null, workspace, null, cb): the former is\n  deprecated for removal (java:S5738). A null JahiaUser is the platform''s own\n  path to a plain system session - JCRTemplate''s no-arg\n  doExecuteWithSystemSession forwards to exactly that.\n- Guard the refusal log so sanitizeForLog does not run with error logging off\n  (java:S2629), matching the LOG_UNSAFE_REDIRECT style already in this file.\n- Drop two ''throws RepositoryException'' declarations that nothing in the\n  constructor bodies can throw (java:S1130).\n\nLeaves one MINOR finding: RBACUtils is deprecated with no exported\nreplacement, and reimplementing a weak-reference ACL edit by hand to satisfy a\nstyle rule would put more risk into a security fix than the deprecation\ncarries. Documented in the class javadoc.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3b4f8f4a3fa03887c66e5ff047cc039e88b5945","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/d3b4f8f4a3fa03887c66e5ff047cc039e88b5945"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d","verification":{"payload":"tree d3b4f8f4a3fa03887c66e5ff047cc039e88b5945\nparent acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788700060 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788700060 +0200\n\nrefactor: address Sonar findings in the SEC-366 code\n\n- Rename OwnerRoleGrants.record to recordOwner: ''record'' is a restricted\n  identifier from Java 16 (java:S6213).\n- Swap doExecuteWithSystemSession(user, workspace, cb) for\n  doExecuteWithSystemSessionAsUser(null, workspace, null, cb): the former is\n  deprecated for removal (java:S5738). A null JahiaUser is the platform''s own\n  path to a plain system session - JCRTemplate''s no-arg\n  doExecuteWithSystemSession forwards to exactly that.\n- Guard the refusal log so sanitizeForLog does not run with error logging off\n  (java:S2629), matching the LOG_UNSAFE_REDIRECT style already in this file.\n- Drop two ''throws RepositoryException'' declarations that nothing in the\n  constructor bodies can throw (java:S1130).\n\nLeaves one MINOR finding: RBACUtils is deprecated with no exported\nreplacement, and reimplementing a weak-reference ACL edit by hand to satisfy a\nstyle rule would put more risk into a security fix than the deprecation\ncarries. Documented in the class javadoc.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdZZwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kMYwgAj33hl/SZcUNfX69M3rY2E10xiYmxLiu6m/lNYBAfh/fgQuuaOSm8IaJl\nL9MiDMeBLuwPPb82cb5EkIPGV7h7BpTuq3hOlvYrm54ZeXuQ19AQlTmchy+tiWEX\n48h9GwT6gCyxw6XcGAZL8fSct86aE+nbr0kS++fb7Zql+vhPwVOMbRKpAPGRJrkp\nmcn2w/mrej/rC7NWRxI9sxsfnJu0fmi14bf4hQ/tVlnssyDafsmQtYXz09wVX7R2\nFuiGVfKL0j3elBQCwmQkuNZnocJvpVt8sN635EWaGiskkt18Qdc7j+WZZqTjRgeB\nyAqgpeR50P4ZAQWhQlNLCdcjTgwIUQ==\n=fE0u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKGRjNDA1ZWRlYmRjM2VkMWYxZmU0N2YwMmQwYTg2N2FlYjNlMDVhNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8","sha":"acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8"}],"sha":"dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/dc405edebdc3ed1f1fe47f02d0a867aeb3e05a6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T13:02:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T13:02:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"docs: operator guidance for GHSA-f882-3xwv-3439 (SEC-366)\n\nRecords what upgrading does and does not do, the single log line that confirms\nthe role was repaired, the manual fallback when the repair fails, and the audit\nsignature the advisory asks for: a live ACL entry with no default-workspace\ncounterpart, which is exactly the entry the editing UI cannot show.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"59810b1d64f2e4cc8db1ba48f9ba7a0242413bdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/59810b1d64f2e4cc8db1ba48f9ba7a0242413bdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8","verification":{"payload":"tree 59810b1d64f2e4cc8db1ba48f9ba7a0242413bdc\nparent 17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699741 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699741 +0200\n\ndocs: operator guidance for GHSA-f882-3xwv-3439 (SEC-366)\n\nRecords what upgrading does and does not do, the single log line that confirms\nthe role was repaired, the manual fallback when the repair fails, and the audit\nsignature the advisory asks for: a live ACL entry with no default-workspace\ncounterpart, which is exactly the entry the editing UI cannot show.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdZF0ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mA+wgAyVDUr6zetjXyThToiuUxUSV9Pi7cFmhdxhLG41Ckl3owheIKGDPQb0HG\n6B9PXIBgolP/AEI9G5IG+3IolMXsFFWPiY+Ok7x3C4oeah0m65A45yAq88hfZ5Mq\njgZBJVaAcW2qWrlxyMSwfHyJr6vSqHJUBtxFac3WVXeFlEXNvugdXgzL/XNZbeca\nda8Tw+DnETIwqgoN2g9igK3Qp48xCtp6KWR9k1X+KWBfrxugqZ3Ny7HWCuSTdYYE\nLZsuGdiWxwelRsifB7iuO+RlNA5W2iHrCJY0szdGel96VXujsnfVT7zn5WLIv8K4\nHy3dkfOrcX6vCfl2rPk0KlvsFzy14g==\n=c7az\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKGFjZDI1NGYwZTAyZWRmOWJkMmJhMGZlNGU0NGFlMDFjZDBmM2NkYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f","sha":"17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f"}],"sha":"acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/acd254f0e02edf9bd2ba0fe4e44ae01cd0f3cdc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T13:01:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T13:01:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: e2e coverage for the SEC-366 ACL boundary and the upload it protects\n\n23-storeDeveloperAcl reuses the advisory''s proof-of-concept as the test design\nwith the attack arm''s expectation inverted: the LIVE self-promotion that\nreturned grantRoles: true must now be refused, the EDIT control arm must stay\nrefused, and a positive-control arm grants the role legitimately so the two\nrefusals are provably the permission model discriminating by caller rather than\na broken mutation or a probe stuck on false. Asserts on the capability probe,\nnever on a status code - every arm in the original answered HTTP 200.\n\n24-uploadOwnerAcl guards the regression the advisory''s own suggested fix would\nhave caused. 11-moduleUpload uploads as root, whose jcr:all masks it, so this\nuploads as a real store-developer in the live workspace and asserts the owner\nACE landed on both created nodes. It checks the ACE rather than hasPermission\nbecause site-scoped jcr:write_live would answer yes either way.\n\nNeither spec has been run: the harness needs a Jahia EE license this working\ncopy does not have. Both need a harness pass before merge.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f12bca5c0bcc6b6e6c835f7e3b79a96ef4d341b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/2f12bca5c0bcc6b6e6c835f7e3b79a96ef4d341b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f12bca5c0bcc6b6e6c835f7e3b79a96ef4d341b\nparent 29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699695 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699695 +0200\n\ntest: e2e coverage for the SEC-366 ACL boundary and the upload it protects\n\n23-storeDeveloperAcl reuses the advisory''s proof-of-concept as the test design\nwith the attack arm''s expectation inverted: the LIVE self-promotion that\nreturned grantRoles: true must now be refused, the EDIT control arm must stay\nrefused, and a positive-control arm grants the role legitimately so the two\nrefusals are provably the permission model discriminating by caller rather than\na broken mutation or a probe stuck on false. Asserts on the capability probe,\nnever on a status code - every arm in the original answered HTTP 200.\n\n24-uploadOwnerAcl guards the regression the advisory''s own suggested fix would\nhave caused. 11-moduleUpload uploads as root, whose jcr:all masks it, so this\nuploads as a real store-developer in the live workspace and asserts the owner\nACE landed on both created nodes. It checks the ACE rather than hasPermission\nbecause site-scoped jcr:write_live would answer yes either way.\n\nNeither spec has been run: the harness needs a Jahia EE license this working\ncopy does not have. Both need a harness pass before merge.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdZC8ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kz8AgAmtgkvQ0BySklXpEQkbsQPebSSyU49foqhXfOo5cJoebYpcpjzv1GV/ly\nQJSw+N07JvO6zLkxvqYIsWsw2Nyu5uCUZQXgzdJI0jVBY0uUUgV9sPjN7MvmYewr\nur8KFj/OeT9gV4Dq3RL5dgDGKN/ds15HgU9Th7rA4fiUekqDHlaqytDCYbanOA6k\nrdJBdfpQ6iER0yMFQ3P66aGXCLn48aS6qZOs4RXN277n/vGPGR21YNQI8Sw6eSAd\nZZL5FiYR/040q3gMfkk4+UXiZWWimtPRhALbiP9EoAj0OciovSl3kWKV9CluqT2K\nO4BNFncpBFrhQalryPh4Pl1GAo8/5w==\n=gjnM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDE3MzgyZjNiMmVmMTE0ZjY0ZGZlMzk1ODlmYjUxNjk0NjczMjczOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946","sha":"29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946"}],"sha":"17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/17382f3b2ef114f64dfe39589fb516946732738f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:57:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:57:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: migrate existing installs off the stale live ACL grant (SEC-366)\n\nFixing roles.xml only helps a fresh install. Module role data is imported once\nper module version, so an upgrade does not rewrite a role node already in the\nJCR: every existing installation would keep jcr:modifyAccessControl_live and\nstay exposed. The module now repairs the role on start.\n\nReuses RBACUtils.revokePermissionFromRole rather than hand-editing the\nj:permissions weak references - it is the platform''s own implementation of that\nremoval, matching by permission identifier and handling the becomes-empty case.\nThe permission''s path is read back from the references the role actually holds,\nso the migration does not depend on where Jahia nests JCR privileges under\n/permissions.\n\nChecks both workspaces: the substance of SEC-366 is that this module''s live\nstate diverged unnoticed from its default state, so neither is assumed clean on\nthe strength of the other. Idempotent, silent when already clean, and never\npropagates failure - a migration must not stop the module activating, and the\nerror names the manual remediation when it cannot complete.\n\nUnit tests cover the removal decision (only the _live permission, never its\n_default counterpart, duplicates and malformed pairs) and the subtree check\nthat bounds the elevated owner grant.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"5afd63ac7334cac8d4c2dde3ba3f232438358e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/5afd63ac7334cac8d4c2dde3ba3f232438358e05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946","verification":{"payload":"tree 5afd63ac7334cac8d4c2dde3ba3f232438358e05\nparent c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699454 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699454 +0200\n\nfix: migrate existing installs off the stale live ACL grant (SEC-366)\n\nFixing roles.xml only helps a fresh install. Module role data is imported once\nper module version, so an upgrade does not rewrite a role node already in the\nJCR: every existing installation would keep jcr:modifyAccessControl_live and\nstay exposed. The module now repairs the role on start.\n\nReuses RBACUtils.revokePermissionFromRole rather than hand-editing the\nj:permissions weak references - it is the platform''s own implementation of that\nremoval, matching by permission identifier and handling the becomes-empty case.\nThe permission''s path is read back from the references the role actually holds,\nso the migration does not depend on where Jahia nests JCR privileges under\n/permissions.\n\nChecks both workspaces: the substance of SEC-366 is that this module''s live\nstate diverged unnoticed from its default state, so neither is assumed clean on\nthe strength of the other. Idempotent, silent when already clean, and never\npropagates failure - a migration must not stop the module activating, and the\nerror names the manual remediation when it cannot complete.\n\nUnit tests cover the removal decision (only the _live permission, never its\n_default counterpart, duplicates and malformed pairs) and the subtree check\nthat bounds the elevated owner grant.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdYz4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nOqwf/XMpwlYPJTTRwrsQ3YwkRtbwdGSFCl/X2lsnkRnohMv72iHdJzGR9SnzQ\nIkVUkHqLLY6kiGVT1G56cdccQPYSJLwf0BroegSMhuHb6zy42datfCpFx7rw6klg\n7+bVbg51jisM88hDANatQCXRfO2UfnCL4rUnQHg867KqHnIWsWGXJdHPvW8gTiBo\ntw6hKI/LS7v7ywsQ8US6OJdgAAac+FS7IYTq1wBwqbgeArUjU+7WXRwd37AvkO+j\neP0Bzqand2SoFWAzcAeG6TH5AJ8NrmZBJL9MeHsjb/250/wwJ6z6tYt8zFr2ILEL\nR/W+4i3RDebJ9CBFU6r8l1AiyCXdHw==\n=rUkw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDI5YjkyYzc1Yjg1ZGE2MTkzZTg5MGUwYzg0YjU4ZjU4YWU1NWY5NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b","sha":"c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b"}],"sha":"29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/29b92c75b85da6193e890e0c84b58f58ae55f946"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:55:54Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:55:54Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: register the filters package with the OSGi DS scanner\n\n_dsannotations listed graphql, actions, proxy and settings but not filters, so\nbnd generated no descriptor for PublishedModuleFilter and the component never\nregistered. Verified against the built bundle: OSGI-INF held six descriptors\nand Provide-Capability advertised no RenderFilter service.\n\nThe filter is the render-side half of the store''s moderation gate - it\nredirects away from a jmix:forgeElement whose ''published'' property is false\nwhen the caller lacks jcr:write. With the component inert, an unmoderated\nmodule''s detail page rendered to anyone in live, which also made the\nSECURITY-571 #54 widening to jmix:forgeElement a no-op.\n\nPre-existing and unrelated to SEC-366; committed separately so it can be\nassessed on its own. Also adds the forge.migration package for the SEC-366\nrole migration that follows.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4bbf046d357ef69f850246bc6381c2fb161bac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/b4bbf046d357ef69f850246bc6381c2fb161bac2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b","verification":{"payload":"tree b4bbf046d357ef69f850246bc6381c2fb161bac2\nparent 7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699354 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699354 +0200\n\nfix: register the filters package with the OSGi DS scanner\n\n_dsannotations listed graphql, actions, proxy and settings but not filters, so\nbnd generated no descriptor for PublishedModuleFilter and the component never\nregistered. Verified against the built bundle: OSGI-INF held six descriptors\nand Provide-Capability advertised no RenderFilter service.\n\nThe filter is the render-side half of the store''s moderation gate - it\nredirects away from a jmix:forgeElement whose ''published'' property is false\nwhen the caller lacks jcr:write. With the component inert, an unmoderated\nmodule''s detail page rendered to anyone in live, which also made the\nSECURITY-571 #54 widening to jmix:forgeElement a no-op.\n\nPre-existing and unrelated to SEC-366; committed separately so it can be\nassessed on its own. Also adds the forge.migration package for the SEC-366\nrole migration that follows.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdYtoACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3l43Qf/Q8bNXrmCj0jyAwgchbRdzcT/ct35+J7Lhj8CKSeDw/oJvyljK3NO0Edd\nUHtqU7Q49RcH3BdUBQx3dfg4kr8D3G+7iY4bqt4RsT99jP5n+pY+vxID/Shi2mFe\nrC0jGDJUrEjnwx7LXVXFPJn0Gm20Ag6OuO9tdc1l6j4l1Jtonvsw2TakR4t9A43L\nHflbY3XDkQagL1YcMelP6zojgD/PUwNECOMRX8t+4Z+CJfAtBhjrpPpvdAwmgm9K\nAfgV2ZmZ7iypv8l34/evxSQpEpyfy1g68/KIRptieDBQBry+dHRnBLbneLkm9Xo9\nI0L+iQKePGewZ6MKNHzC5/2GreZQ6w==\n=rcxd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKGMwNGFmYTU1MjRmZTU2MWI3ZTQ0ZDA3Mjc1YzFiMzU5NjJlZTI3NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86","sha":"7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86"}],"sha":"c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/c04afa5524fe561b7e44d07275c1b35962ee274b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:50:20Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:50:20Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: drop jcr:modifyAccessControl_live from store-developer (SEC-366)\n\nCloses GHSA-f882-3xwv-3439. The permission is no longer load-bearing now that\nthe upload''s owner grant runs in a system session, so the role keeps only what\nthe feature actually needs.\n\njcr:write_live is left in place: node creation still runs through the caller''s\nsession, and narrowing it needs a measurement this change cannot make (whether\nJahia''s core owner role covers live write on the node) - tracked separately.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5d7f105995cf7fe4d9ef529b55ea1617ea683d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/a5d7f105995cf7fe4d9ef529b55ea1617ea683d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86","verification":{"payload":"tree a5d7f105995cf7fe4d9ef529b55ea1617ea683d3\nparent 415b8a2e8f195522de61bf49c90daeec345d4905\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699020 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699020 +0200\n\nfix: drop jcr:modifyAccessControl_live from store-developer (SEC-366)\n\nCloses GHSA-f882-3xwv-3439. The permission is no longer load-bearing now that\nthe upload''s owner grant runs in a system session, so the role keeps only what\nthe feature actually needs.\n\njcr:write_live is left in place: node creation still runs through the caller''s\nsession, and narrowing it needs a measurement this change cannot make (whether\nJahia''s core owner role covers live write on the node) - tracked separately.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdYYwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kE2ggAoBFuPiUjURyrTW7E9IT1dU7SA2eMJEYhOfLycZUnabA1mUz9nYzkxDna\njS684XINR1ohtUadPXX5pYp8kLd66wkGSKDwKmaI3D8FbdG/UUNY7v3HYAyXddBl\n2xKFMVQGkuHLad31F+cybpNl9juJR9kvU4qR0/lmstQZKhiAGhVnDgFd6slTy/yA\nZ0hPLFkQDHdKQeFWgBQhM5g1TT91II5zUWVCjqHYquU0HTmhue/5ZiqsPTqfJe5w\n9B41JOpjNGnJiS9QnKq/ECE1f4hrqAmnzVOmNnYDLN05pwClySSk8cUT2pLMwhyp\n3CdufD2aiWzPwvasCIPDstt3ZMi4qw==\n=x5PJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T11:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDdmNDE2MDIwZjk2YTI0MDliYzQwZDNlZTE5ZmU0YzczMTRhNjNmODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/415b8a2e8f195522de61bf49c90daeec345d4905","sha":"415b8a2e8f195522de61bf49c90daeec345d4905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/415b8a2e8f195522de61bf49c90daeec345d4905"}],"sha":"7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/7f416020f96a2409bc40d3ee19fe4c7314a63f86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/415b8a2e8f195522de61bf49c90daeec345d4905/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:50:01Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T12:50:01Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: grant the uploader''s owner role with elevated rights (SEC-366)\n\nThe upload path called node.grantRoles() on the caller''s own live session, which\nis why store-developer shipped jcr:modifyAccessControl_live at site scope\n(commit 25db344, APPS-14). Site-scoped live ACL authority is far more than the\nupload needs and is the substance of GHSA-f882-3xwv-3439: it let a store\ndeveloper rewrite the site''s live ACL, self-promote to store-administrator and\nstrip the site administrators, invisibly, because a live write never enters a\npublication queue.\n\nMove the grant into a system session scoped to the nodes the upload just\ncreated, so the permission is no longer load-bearing and can be removed from\nthe role.\n\nBoth upload paths granted the role on nodes still transient in the caller''s\nsession, which another session cannot see, so OwnerRoleGrants records\nidentifiers as nodes are created and flushes after the caller''s save. Every\nelevated write is constrained: the principal is the caller, the role is the\nconstant ''owner'', the target is re-resolved by identifier rather than by a\npath built from input, and it must live under the repository node the Action\nalready gated with jahiaForgeUploadModule.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcfe7f91bceedbf58341d7d756ed4c19ce24231c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/bcfe7f91bceedbf58341d7d756ed4c19ce24231c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/415b8a2e8f195522de61bf49c90daeec345d4905","verification":{"payload":"tree bcfe7f91bceedbf58341d7d756ed4c19ce24231c\nparent b469775a750e1436e1b176466f4e53ac0c72848b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699001 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1788699001 +0200\n\nfix: grant the uploader''s owner role with elevated rights (SEC-366)\n\nThe upload path called node.grantRoles() on the caller''s own live session, which\nis why store-developer shipped jcr:modifyAccessControl_live at site scope\n(commit 25db344, APPS-14). Site-scoped live ACL authority is far more than the\nupload needs and is the substance of GHSA-f882-3xwv-3439: it let a store\ndeveloper rewrite the site''s live ACL, self-promote to store-administrator and\nstrip the site administrators, invisibly, because a live write never enters a\npublication queue.\n\nMove the grant into a system session scoped to the nodes the upload just\ncreated, so the permission is no longer load-bearing and can be removed from\nthe role.\n\nBoth upload paths granted the role on nodes still transient in the caller''s\nsession, which another session cannot see, so OwnerRoleGrants records\nidentifiers as nodes are created and flushes after the caller''s save. Every\nelevated write is constrained: the principal is the caller, the role is the\nconstant ''owner'', the target is re-resolved by identifier rather than by a\npath built from input, and it must live under the repository node the Action\nalready gated with jahiaForgeUploadModule.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmqdYXkACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL