,"gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/6122c73ab8387d23bfcfb78d23572f66a14c822b","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDYxMjJjNzNhYjgzODdkMjNiZmNmYjc4ZDIzNTcyZjY2YTE0YzgyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/d16b2824e7920f0f3d52844e7383811de551e088","sha":"d16b2824e7920f0f3d52844e7383811de551e088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/d16b2824e7920f0f3d52844e7383811de551e088"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198","sha":"40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198"}],"sha":"6122c73ab8387d23bfcfb78d23572f66a14c822b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/6122c73ab8387d23bfcfb78d23572f66a14c822b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-15T11:49:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-15T11:49:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat(upload): clear message when a module version already exists in the repo\n\nA release repository (e.g. Nexus hosted ''release'') refuses to overwrite a published\nversion: ''mvn deploy:deploy-file'' fails with HTTP 400 ''... cannot be updated''. The\naction mapped every deploy IOException to the generic ''Unable to upload artifact to\nthe repository'', so a re-upload of an existing version (common: forgetting to bump)\nsurfaced an opaque error while the real cause sat in the server log.\n\ndeployArtifact now detects that Nexus phrase (isVersionAlreadyDeployed) and returns an\nactionable message — ''This module version already exists ... Increase the module\nversion and upload again.'' — instead of the generic one. Other deploy failures keep\nthe generic message (detail stays server-side). New i18n key\nforge.uploadJar.error.version.already.deployed; 2 JUnit cases for the detector.\n\n91 -> 93 JUnit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"646b39e2998fb4f3ee46aae3e2cbdfd22ea6a0ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/646b39e2998fb4f3ee46aae3e2cbdfd22ea6a0ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198","verification":{"payload":"tree 646b39e2998fb4f3ee46aae3e2cbdfd22ea6a0ae\nparent f909b50725859e3c0ba0e0a8397b65a2725eb415\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781524150 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781524150 +0200\n\nfeat(upload): clear message when a module version already exists in the repo\n\nA release repository (e.g. Nexus hosted ''release'') refuses to overwrite a published\nversion: ''mvn deploy:deploy-file'' fails with HTTP 400 ''... cannot be updated''. The\naction mapped every deploy IOException to the generic ''Unable to upload artifact to\nthe repository'', so a re-upload of an existing version (common: forgetting to bump)\nsurfaced an opaque error while the real cause sat in the server log.\n\ndeployArtifact now detects that Nexus phrase (isVersionAlreadyDeployed) and returns an\nactionable message — ''This module version already exists ... Increase the module\nversion and upload again.'' — instead of the generic one. Other deploy failures keep\nthe generic message (detail stays server-side). New i18n key\nforge.uploadJar.error.version.already.deployed; 2 JUnit cases for the detector.\n\n91 -> 93 JUnit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmov5rYACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nmQAf/QVutTy81yN0G2MSiIVdmgs4qW/z/CVZ4fn0kN5HJxWu9JP2Wan190WRX\nZ+NZUG8K72B1HGPdNqZ/cT9ELqPzAwKOLLu+XlElXQu5G9/WCQHxOUhS2wzRJLAF\njkARG12THMXnqGMKZd+NtzngRv6pD/x5Ypit+sO6i7ST63UuXpUebKkaXU0iRnZp\n3U23u5sSX0abL9d0z/F6mlA16EJx0VExI9FAWudQNpEtSpdmO83HPAQV1C8kgWbS\n0Hr+7O3Vx3tjEDBaSnMVTmVT1gAAdqu7uKWeoC+Wkc2osQwfbA3DXFhoGHkpT1Em\nnt86NF6tZ8BUwOIvqhrcsSwrNiEaMw==\n=GrA8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-15T11:49:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198","node_id":"C_kwDOAHxHXNoAKDQwZjhmNmVkM2VhODBiMDM3YjcwOTJmYzNhZTRiZWJlNGZlYjExOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-store/commit/f909b50725859e3c0ba0e0a8397b65a2725eb415","sha":"f909b50725859e3c0ba0e0a8397b65a2725eb415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/f909b50725859e3c0ba0e0a8397b65a2725eb415"}],"sha":"40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/40f8f6ed3ea80b037b7092fc3ae4bebe4feb1198"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/commits/f909b50725859e3c0ba0e0a8397b65a2725eb415/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-15T11:48:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-15T11:48:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat(settings): ship a default forge-settings config editable in karaf/etc\n\nAdds META-INF/configurations/org.jahia.modules.forge.forgeSettings-default.cfg so an\nadmin can configure a site''s store (Nexus release repo url/id/user/password, category\nroot, branding) by editing JAHIA_HOME/digital-factory-data/karaf/etc once installed,\ninstead of only via the admin UI. It is a factory-config instance of the existing\nForgeSettingsService PID; the admin sets siteKey to their site. The mandatory\n''# default configuration - won''t be overridden'' first line keeps edits from being\nreverted on the next module (re)deploy (verified: an edit survives redeploy).\n\nAlso makes ForgeSettingsServiceImpl.decodePassword tolerant: the password is stored\nbase64-encoded by save()/the UI, but a value hand-typed into the .cfg may not be valid\nbase64 — fall back to the raw value instead of letting Base64 throw, which would break\nevery get() for the site (proxy, upload deploy, storefront chrome all call it).\n\n88 -> 91 JUnit (3 decodePassword cases).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc041f44ec616001cdcf4bcee15df833101e2cfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/trees/fc041f44ec616001cdcf4bcee15df833101e2cfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-store/git/commits/f909b50725859e3c0ba0e0a8397b65a2725eb415","verification":{"payload":"tree fc041f44ec616001cdcf4bcee15df833101e2cfe\nparent d16b2824e7920f0f3d52844e7383811de551e088\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781524139 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781524139 +0200\n\nfeat(settings): ship a default forge-settings config editable in karaf/etc\n\nAdds META-INF/configurations/org.jahia.modules.forge.forgeSettings-default.cfg so an\nadmin can configure a site''s store (Nexus release repo url/id/user/password, category\nroot, branding) by editing JAHIA_HOME/digital-factory-data/karaf/etc once installed,\ninstead of only via the admin UI. It is a factory-config instance of the existing\nForgeSettingsService PID; the admin sets siteKey to their site. The mandatory\n''# default configuration - won''t be overridden'' first line keeps edits from being\nreverted on the next module (re)deploy (verified: an edit survives redeploy).\n\nAlso makes ForgeSettingsServiceImpl.decodePassword tolerant: the password is stored\nbase64-encoded by save()/the UI, but a value hand-typed into the .cfg may not be valid\nbase64 — fall back to the raw value instead of letting Base64 throw, which would break\nevery get() for the site (proxy, upload deploy, storefront chrome all call it).\n\n88 -> 91 JUnit (3 decodePassword cases).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmov5qsACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3l4dgf9G+EmzXbUIeaNUwiMd9c3OSXtChTXI4ROgnR3/wnGu29v/v3+jRi39F2J\nZgCsiJrVnzzioVy4PqwR8S052Ez+vhxz9NmlKEm7gEqnm/4Ef+6Ony+sXIa4SsP1\ntrUx9WOKQwcrO0xO+6AaF7sgquKEXE22BVb7AvSym138Tte6ZF+j2miJbNAsMezR\ni3PDE0c7exzQHdXaA0GG7qj1o8ar5OpCq5hfDn5xqc+pn5FNCEteddmyLkvTikuz\nHrcvc2DrKLZZzL1EOKmq4RT5wtPdrNMvf9kFYVsi5YHTqumuC5Ji6Ol44fZOAI9v\nZ4WbumOkFpl462blodfhcRvFizuNdg==\n=BCUq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-0