lic"},"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/5d412baf56f1ad65de5cebeab69ca0dcb1ffca63","node_id":"C_kwDOAJB9V9oAKDVkNDEyYmFmNTZmMWFkNjVkZTVjZWJlYWI2OWNhMGRjYjFmZmNhNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b","sha":"cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b"}],"sha":"5d412baf56f1ad65de5cebeab69ca0dcb1ffca63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/5d412baf56f1ad65de5cebeab69ca0dcb1ffca63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/531694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonioo","id":531694,"login":"tonioo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTY5NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:58:43Z","email":"tonio@ngyn.org","name":"Antoine Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:58:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(webmail): compose quality (#4266)\n\n* feat(webmail): better quoting of replies and forwards\n\n- an HTML reply quotes the message in a blockquote, a plain text one\n  prefixes its lines with \"> \" (\">>\" for already quoted ones)\n- the attribution line gives the date of the message and is no longer\n  part of the quote\n- the links of the quoted message are kept: they are only blocked to\n  protect the reader\n- embedded images are kept (data: URIs in the editor, turned back into\n  parts of the message when it is sent or saved), in drafts too\n\n* feat(frontend): images, tables, text styles and links in the HTML editor\n\nThe editor dropped what it didn''t know from quoted messages: images,\ntables, colors and fonts. A toolbar button inserts or edits links.\n\n* fix(webmail): recognize localized reply and forward subject prefixes\n\nOnly \"Re:\" was recognized: replying to \"AW:\" or \"RE :\" subjects added\nanother prefix, and forwarding always added \"Fwd:\", even to an already\nforwarded message.\n\n* feat(webmail): signature position and RFC 3676 separator\n\nThe signature of replies and forwards goes above the quoted message by\ndefault, leaving room to write before it. A new preference puts it below\nthe quoted message instead.\n\nThe signature now starts with the \"-- \" line clients recognize (it was\n\"---\"); converting HTML to plain text keeps its trailing space.\n\n* feat(webmail): send plain text as format=flowed\n\nPlain text messages and the text part of HTML ones were sent with lines\nof any length. They are now cut at 72 characters as format=flowed\n(RFC 3676): clients supporting it join the lines back, others get a\nreadable message.\n\nReceived format=flowed messages are joined back too, when displayed,\nquoted or edited as drafts.\n\n* fix(webmail): keep Bcc in the copies of the messages sent\n\nDjango never writes Bcc into the MIME message: the copy stored into the\nSent folder, or into the Scheduled one, didn''t tell who received the\nmessage as blind carbon copy. Drafts already kept it.\n\n* feat(webmail): keep the names of the recipients\n\nThe API only accepted bare addresses: the names of the recipients of\nreplies, of the contacts picked in the address book and of the\nrecipients of drafts were dropped. Recipients can now be given as\n\"Name <address>\"; scheduled messages store them so that a comma in a\nname is not taken for a separator.\n\nReplying to one''s own message now addresses its recipients instead of\noneself, and Cc and Bcc show contacts like To.","tree":{"sha":"e4084337082492c7347aba933d00c17ce539f325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/trees/e4084337082492c7347aba933d00c17ce539f325"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/commits/cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b","verification":{"payload":"tree e4084337082492c7347aba933d00c17ce539f325\nparent d4dd322e7ee1cefe9cb01b91c0652df93d4e0e68\nauthor Antoine Nguyen <tonio@ngyn.org> 1791277123 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791277123 +0200\n\nfix(webmail): compose quality (#4266)\n\n* feat(webmail): better quoting of replies and forwards\n\n- an HTML reply quotes the message in a blockquote, a plain text one\n  prefixes its lines with \"> \" (\">>\" for already quoted ones)\n- the attribution line gives the date of the message and is no longer\n  part of the quote\n- the links of the quoted message are kept: they are only blocked to\n  protect the reader\n- embedded images are kept (data: URIs in the editor, turned back into\n  parts of the message when it is sent or saved), in drafts too\n\n* feat(frontend): images, tables, text styles and links in the HTML editor\n\nThe editor dropped what it didn''t know from quoted messages: images,\ntables, colors and fonts. A toolbar button inserts or edits links.\n\n* fix(webmail): recognize localized reply and forward subject prefixes\n\nOnly \"Re:\" was recognized: replying to \"AW:\" or \"RE :\" subjects added\nanother prefix, and forwarding always added \"Fwd:\", even to an already\nforwarded message.\n\n* feat(webmail): signature position and RFC 3676 separator\n\nThe signature of replies and forwards goes above the quoted message by\ndefault, leaving room to write before it. A new preference puts it below\nthe quoted message instead.\n\nThe signature now starts with the \"-- \" line clients recognize (it was\n\"---\"); converting HTML to plain text keeps its trailing space.\n\n* feat(webmail): send plain text as format=flowed\n\nPlain text messages and the text part of HTML ones were sent with lines\nof any length. They are now cut at 72 characters as format=flowed\n(RFC 3676): clients supporting it join the lines back, others get a\nreadable message.\n\nReceived format=flowed messages are joined back too, when displayed,\nquoted or edited as drafts.\n\n* fix(webmail): keep Bcc in the copies of the messages sent\n\nDjango never writes Bcc into the MIME message: the copy stored into the\nSent folder, or into the Scheduled one, didn''t tell who received the\nmessage as blind carbon copy. Drafts already kept it.\n\n* feat(webmail): keep the names of the recipients\n\nThe API only accepted bare addresses: the names of the recipients of\nreplies, of the contacts picked in the address book and of the\nrecipients of drafts were dropped. Recipients can now be given as\n\"Name <address>\"; scheduled messages store them so that a comma in a\nname is not taken for a separator.\n\nReplying to one''s own message now addresses its recipients instead of\noneself, and Cc and Bcc show contacts like To.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLhDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkMQQAEfiHtsFUSZ4KjLaUwrR7+vg\nXL890b8nl3bVnbD1gChzvzt7Ukcfge/ydkSGpU8CLbKW/dLNocpn2Cl6Hj/u7UnR\nAm/+uHUCmAU0CBO0lhjhTxSECnVGDHLiXtyapHFpb2GPL1QbL83mqom16OYxe7Hy\n7bO6kIwbzjErFTuLLLNpR2Ei+Rz5ysGLqmX0PTRiPBy6tufMqlmGYuQ/ltDTxh7P\nC8ctzZ47WlLrRK1u/TvQUNDsTipVv91Tp3iRqf2z7RptsuUFa0H8x3otgyKfZxJ7\nuE2n8KRfKPk9Uce16044gQpw6uXVvHCbl8++EEcJu2JFEo2z4u8oS5buyV+bzilL\n9BHjMMCSBGNkz9xDL7jHu6Cu1/U4WomkXGJdDmlyytg8klBhpxzyuC4Tiy+ILOuU\n9J0heBfCbfwMOu9ORBWZWthFXYrpr7FLhS9B5AkUNTxfVUUmvv/KlULMAAUa8OqI\nq5i0vOg8/LpykiHaXQQ8h2/4tJ5ggv+rjBU3IvkYPX53GKgOeObFgT12a9paDTUO\nFUiteDjd41yotY2eSg1/HD1gWLa0MRiD/lOJye6CceRPm4w97AnvityGOpsfk/RP\nj02biafUfOqAPJ1X11sNiAiQndsmevDxNTfVkLiHa2+LuN580AlPr9bABsHHxP9y\n37hnDNdl7bHbCQsw88j+\n=49oV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T08:58:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b","node_id":"C_kwDOAJB9V9oAKGNkY2NkZGY0MWVjMjk0ZWQ0ZDUwZDhkOTE4ZGQ2ZjMwM2I5ZjU5MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/d4dd322e7ee1cefe9cb01b91c0652df93d4e0e68","sha":"d4dd322e7ee1cefe9cb01b91c0652df93d4e0e68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/d4dd322e7ee1cefe9cb01b91c0652df93d4e0e68"}],"sha":"cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/cdccddf41ec294ed4d50d8d918dd6f303b9f590b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/531694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonioo","id":531694,"login":"tonioo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTY5NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/d4dd322e7ee1cefe9cb01b91c0652df93d4e0e68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:45:02Z","email":"tonio@ngyn.org","name":"Antoine Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:45:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(webmail): better handling of message format (#4265)\n\n* fix(webmail): load replies and forwards in the format of the editor\n\nThe quoted message was loaded in the display format, while the editor\nstarted in its own one: with the HTML editor and the plain text display,\na reply opened plain text quoted lines in the HTML editor and lost their\nline breaks.\n\n* fix(webmail): keep list items and indentation in the plain text part\n\nThe HTML editor puts the content of list items into paragraphs: the\nplain text part of the message showed each item marker alone on its\nline. Non-breaking spaces were also collapsed like regular ones.\n\n* fix(frontend): convert the message when switching the editor format\n\nSwitching between HTML and plain text kept the content as is: plain\ntext lost its line breaks in the HTML editor, and HTML tags showed up\nin the plain text one. In a reply, the original message was loaded\nagain and the form rebuilt: what was written, the recipients and the\nsignature were lost.\n\nThe content is now converted (quoted lines become blockquotes and vice\nversa), with a confirmation before the formatting is dropped.\n\nThe compose form loads the session, the allowed senders and the\noriginal message (or the draft) together before being filled, so the\nformat is decided once and the signature is no longer lost when the\noriginal message arrives last. Sending is disabled until then.\n\n* refactor(webmail): convert the editor content on the server\n\nThe conversion between HTML and plain text, made when the format of the\neditor changes, duplicated html2plaintext in the frontend: two\nimplementations to keep in line, and browsers and lxml don''t read\nmalformed HTML the same way.\n\nA new endpoint (compose-sessions/convert/) makes both conversions: the\ntext obtained in the editor is the one sent as the text part of HTML\nmessages. Confirming the loss of formatting is now asked before\nconverting.","tree":{"sha":"779afb85a9f09bec8c63ca60cf94e9ae92cca3b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/trees/779afb85a9f09bec8c63ca60cf94e9ae92cca3b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/commits/d4dd322e7ee1cefe9cb01b91c0652df93d4e0e68","verification":{"payload":"tree 779afb85a9f09bec8c63ca60cf94e9ae92cca3b4\nparent 984c276c1d872e3157e1bacd1ca2d76b702ccf9a\nauthor Antoine Nguyen <tonio@ngyn.org> 1791276302 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791276302 +0200\n\nfix(webmail): better handling of message format (#4265)\n\n* fix(webmail): load replies and forwards in the format of the editor\n\nThe quoted message was loaded in the display format, while the editor\nstarted in its own one: with the HTML editor and the plain text display,\na reply opened plain text quoted lines in the HTML editor and lost their\nline breaks.\n\n* fix(webmail): keep list items and indentation in the plain text part\n\nThe HTML editor puts the content of list items into paragraphs: the\nplain text part of the message showed each item marker alone on its\nline. Non-breaking spaces were also collapsed like regular ones.\n\n* fix(frontend): convert the message when switching the editor format\n\nSwitching between HTML and plain text kept the content as is: plain\ntext lost its line breaks in the HTML editor, and HTML tags showed up\nin the plain text one. In a reply, the original message was loaded\nagain and the form rebuilt: what was written, the recipients and the\nsignature were lost.\n\nThe content is now converted (quoted lines become blockquotes and vice\nversa), with a confirmation before the formatting is dropped.\n\nThe compose form loads the session, the allowed senders and the\noriginal message (or the draft) together before being filled, so the\nformat is decided once and the signature is no longer lost when the\noriginal message arrives last. Sending is disabled until then.\n\n* refactor(webmail): convert the editor content on the server\n\nThe conversion between HTML and plain text, made when the format of the\neditor changes, duplicated html2plaintext in the frontend: two\nimplementations to keep in line, and browsers and lxml don''t read\nmalformed HTML the same way.\n\nA new endpoint (compose-sessions/convert/) makes both conversions: the\ntext obtained in the editor is the one sent as the text part of HTML\nmessages. Confirming the loss of formatting is now asked before\nconverting.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLUOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArx4QACQx3jAfHQKmJfn5OEHEvsSj\nKn8ZcYL3RkvolxQk1Yy2evZf65BcyrwE6xlxizMCaT3vvR547G/Fh+3EpYWdKMh8\nWLZF2zYRRXE/RQoX5Ej30EGyNRvD78j/rwsNhg7meK7HjMW76syiyrJ3/ZCfJ5Fd\nlFnCKE81Kdw1IiB8mJJCXKSdWLdORGW9iPZyyeJ53s9uITy3XFjsR59UTWMjECls\nFn+vruR+1qc5nv6pD4+GS9WJF+VdDbUJGJBnNsu6m+Sq4sDug/MuuWyKVtHJx6Re\n1usVpLS3cAj3na8/HuNfJebNI+GJcDMEdYEXfbzLEyKMGmiabsQQlvO9L6jnzKiV\nI