/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/73f147fbe9dea6011a0b6748eef6b51298b768cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:30:38Z","email":"tonio@ngyn.org","name":"Antoine Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:30:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(calendars): display calendars shared with the user (#4242)\n\n* feat(calendars): display calendars shared with the user\n\nCalendars shared by access rules were only reachable from CalDAV\nclients. They now appear in the calendar view, in a \"Shared with me\"\nsection:\n\n- GET /api/v2/calendars-shared-with-me/ lists them, with their owner\n  and the write access, but without the owner''s share URL.\n- Events of a shared calendar can be read with read access, and\n  modified, created, moved or imported with write access. Writing to\n  a read-only calendar returns 403, a calendar not shared returns 404.\n- Events no longer return the share URL of their calendar.\n- CalDAV authorization and not found errors return 403 and 404\n  instead of 500: Radicale can refuse an access rule removed in the\n  meantime.\n- Events of read-only calendars can''t be dragged nor resized, and\n  open in a read-only form. A calendar failing to load no longer\n  prevents the others from being displayed.\n\n* feat(calendars): let grantees choose the color and visibility of shared calendars\n\nEach grantee can hide a calendar shared with them, or display it with\ntheir own color. These settings are stored on the access rule\n(migration 0010), so they follow the user across browsers:\n\n- PATCH /api/v2/calendars-shared-with-me/<calendar pk>/ updates color\n  and visible. An empty color restores the owner''s one, and the write\n  access can''t be modified.\n- The access rules API doesn''t expose these settings: the owner can''t\n  overwrite them.\n- The \"Shared with me\" menu gets Hide/Show and Color actions. Events of\n  hidden calendars are not loaded.\n\n* fix(calendars): validate calendar colors and use the theme color field\n\nThe color picker of the calendar form could return a color with an\nalpha channel (#rrggbbaa), refused by the database (7 characters).\n\n- Calendar forms use ColorField, already used for the theme colors,\n  which only returns hexadecimal colors without alpha.\n- The API checks that user, domain and shared with me calendar colors\n  are #rrggbb colors.\n- The calendar form displays API errors, and new calendars get the\n  default color.","tree":{"sha":"9b8b326fa0cd48659267f8b45b898980f095b13d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/trees/9b8b326fa0cd48659267f8b45b898980f095b13d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/commits/73f147fbe9dea6011a0b6748eef6b51298b768cd","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b8b326fa0cd48659267f8b45b898980f095b13d\nparent 4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458\nauthor Antoine Nguyen <tonio@ngyn.org> 1790627438 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790627438 +0200\n\nfeat(calendars): display calendars shared with the user (#4242)\n\n* feat(calendars): display calendars shared with the user\n\nCalendars shared by access rules were only reachable from CalDAV\nclients. They now appear in the calendar view, in a \"Shared with me\"\nsection:\n\n- GET /api/v2/calendars-shared-with-me/ lists them, with their owner\n  and the write access, but without the owner''s share URL.\n- Events of a shared calendar can be read with read access, and\n  modified, created, moved or imported with write access. Writing to\n  a read-only calendar returns 403, a calendar not shared returns 404.\n- Events no longer return the share URL of their calendar.\n- CalDAV authorization and not found errors return 403 and 404\n  instead of 500: Radicale can refuse an access rule removed in the\n  meantime.\n- Events of read-only calendars can''t be dragged nor resized, and\n  open in a read-only form. A calendar failing to load no longer\n  prevents the others from being displayed.\n\n* feat(calendars): let grantees choose the color and visibility of shared calendars\n\nEach grantee can hide a calendar shared with them, or display it with\ntheir own color. These settings are stored on the access rule\n(migration 0010), so they follow the user across browsers:\n\n- PATCH /api/v2/calendars-shared-with-me/<calendar pk>/ updates color\n  and visible. An empty color restores the owner''s one, and the write\n  access can''t be modified.\n- The access rules API doesn''t expose these settings: the owner can''t\n  overwrite them.\n- The \"Shared with me\" menu gets Hide/Show and Color actions. Events of\n  hidden calendars are not loaded.\n\n* fix(calendars): validate calendar colors and use the theme color field\n\nThe color picker of the calendar form could return a color with an\nalpha channel (#rrggbbaa), refused by the database (7 characters).\n\n- Calendar forms use ColorField, already used for the theme colors,\n  which only returns hexadecimal colors without alpha.\n- The API checks that user, domain and shared with me calendar colors\n  are #rrggbb colors.\n- The calendar form displays API errors, and new calendars get the\n  default color.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqus5uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVMgQAFf2cAzWPnmoaWbnYApRlp0W\nflAPBdhw3I6NtSb6VFET+PWKIkrY4HvEKYzVtrOvu6ax81fB6tueCWe/lWQO3s+B\nA8RXusPA4g1GcoTpvJrIprnpBEGVL7DqA9tgY413tK5YH5q7jnE2SMlDH3zTvhkG\ngKgYqIEdL5oaNI50xKH2GdIT24Ob2ScZDj/AlL+zE0Hi/JPaxw6Vgt/Fbb7aTspL\nSa0WhW2CDFDZ20tLDJHUPOIPYxLJQNeI0guwuFi5faFwAYAYBs1M97fMPzQ6Tc9f\nLHYBvK7ucNoS1qXOsW2/m4lzt7D41B39qoqlP+riBgk8YTKz2NYhorKUXw5R3IIH\nHYW7BWra5k6EDcj65eL+Z+LptyZHomLtfZd0B3PEqeOl8ivmllNOu93/ONrNrTcs\ns0vhJGd+6PpnALQMCZqPTmlxm5meUn9L6SxTH6+tjOd4XANxK5tBmhFm9W+KpxqC\n/gpmDXYtPRR4g+xQLR35WkBOTT2lUMmJlCI82w/6uyRUAbDMZrYM0oNZREgK05Mr\ndZ52Zov33TyTHCkaWm87Xo1opVQ6PE+0zUB1vQzA31ZeWyuHBaDzS87HXmte4ulC\nN3Np3himgYUDIbDWMkahq2hkjCnQf9lNXV7Y2+n73lZGPq/2vPMuF36bj5rch+s4\nUQKcBNHSvVYMAxririsC\n=ZKLw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T20:30:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/73f147fbe9dea6011a0b6748eef6b51298b768cd","node_id":"C_kwDOAJB9V9oAKDczZjE0N2ZiZTlkZWE2MDExYTBiNjc0OGVlZjZiNTEyOThiNzY4Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458","sha":"4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458"}],"sha":"73f147fbe9dea6011a0b6748eef6b51298b768cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/73f147fbe9dea6011a0b6748eef6b51298b768cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/531694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonioo","id":531694,"login":"tonioo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTY5NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T18:15:52Z","email":"tonio@ngyn.org","name":"Antoine Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T18:15:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(calendars): access rule validation (#4241)\n\n* fix(calendars): require read access in calendar access rules\n\nA rule without any access grants nothing, and a write-only rule is\nuseless: CalDAV clients can''t display a calendar they can''t read. The\nAPI now refuses both, including for direct API calls.\n\nThe sharing form always grants read access and only lets the owner\nchoose write access. Editing a rule created before this change adds\nread access to it when saved. The form also failed to show API errors:\nit read them from the wrong object and used a prop v-select doesn''t\nhave.\n\n* fix(calendars): accept partial updates of access rules without mailbox\n\nAccessRuleSerializer.update() always popped the mailbox from the\nvalidated data, so a PATCH request without it, such as\n{\"write\": true}, raised a KeyError and returned a 500. The rule now\nkeeps its mailbox when none is given.","tree":{"sha":"d463c6ea485c5431206be7c5bf82cc49c5a894c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/trees/d463c6ea485c5431206be7c5bf82cc49c5a894c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/commits/4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458","verification":{"payload":"tree d463c6ea485c5431206be7c5bf82cc49c5a894c7\nparent aad4ab693658c1295fd8cfa951cc5b1a707d7188\nauthor Antoine Nguyen <tonio@ngyn.org> 1790532952 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790532952 +0200\n\nfix(calendars): access rule validation (#4241)\n\n* fix(calendars): require read access in calendar access rules\n\nA rule without any access grants nothing, and a write-only rule is\nuseless: CalDAV clients can''t display a calendar they can''t read. The\nAPI now refuses both, including for direct API calls.\n\nThe sharing form always grants read access and only lets the owner\nchoose write access. Editing a rule created before this change adds\nread access to it when saved. The form also failed to show API errors:\nit read them from the wrong object and used a prop v-select doesn''t\nhave.\n\n* fix(calendars): accept partial updates of access rules without mailbox\n\nAccessRuleSerializer.update() always popped the mailbox from the\nvalidated data, so a PATCH request without it, such as\n{\"write\": true}, raised a KeyError and returned a 500. The rule now\nkeeps its mailbox when none is given.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquV1YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAteoQABq2/4nDdADsWqy0s79yykV8\nv5aLYSYrAXfaGG1yKUIe5Q55TL23Dv1WH+qxrPqoPm08He91iKeNJM4WwCFnvXJI\niedw3VJC01BEJgGbtSOUdLd38G4iOCAD9C+r1WinS0mzcdofaK0ibhLxsPGaIg1m\nzayryqEf6SfEjWTRCs3jUvdslh8U+FeWA7afNfjmqGfWaEvRxyNsOLqRK9HItATl\nw3uUPtk7GFqaOOz8U8mYujMYrOMlhZFHafZJJGt/GxYISXx8u+rnp1J3DxmQ6NN2\njY5BynfIxr3xrU4i54Vh3hhPyAcxoncxTw88LBtPeb9NZjZNIlFYo2gzRKHqVM34\nFBmyudI3KlKu0jnwATo3h96uSRoOZcWB4wSYZ+YJFKEpr6l+LALKnlw+8vVWce1+\nvs5eBpql9btg/hbOxb7Z7SsP578wZlD8RzCuLjcjrQpYcxtNbl2/Kk62QEPE0jIt\nLjkfr9b04zvg8qAuNohekHuxRceOq1US3bvLPBwKYAZOsGjA/+p28JgVJXnqQtMa\nwewZ5zmC/Uj17YgaZ9Qr3m6t5NEsxYhmdcTAwZp4/9xZYoRGbS1Vg8OnO4gfR/hS\nsv/zpBpqvnr85+MOt348OfwlLAEjNGVbD2acldELbr9qQEOVZ7rfaeK09JJBh05H\nBF9znhQr0H8/0+9aI4Ym\n=Vc2O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T18:15:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458","node_id":"C_kwDOAJB9V9oAKDRmYmI4YWFkNDkwNmFkOTllOWQwZGMzM2RhMDBjNzRhYTIzN2I0NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/aad4ab693658c1295fd8cfa951cc5b1a707d7188","sha":"aad4ab693658c1295fd8cfa951cc5b1a707d7188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/aad4ab693658c1295fd8cfa951cc5b1a707d7188"}],"sha":"4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/4fbb8aad4906ad99e9d0dc33da00c74aa237b458"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/531694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonioo","id":531694,"login":"tonioo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTY5NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonioo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/commits/aad4ab693658c1295fd8cfa951cc5b1a707d7188/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:45:36Z","email":"tonio@ngyn.org","name":"Antoine Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:45:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(calendar): calendars rights endpoint (#4238)\n\n* fix(calendars): make rights file section names unique\n\nAccess rule sections were named after the grantee and the calendar\nname, so two owners sharing a calendar with the same name with the same\nuser produced duplicate sections. Token sections had the same issue\nfor calendars sharing a path. Radicale reads the rights file with a\nstrict ConfigParser and refuses to start on a duplicated section.\n\nSection names now include the pk of the rule or calendar.\n\n* fix(calendars): reject calendar names refused by Radicale\n\nA calendar name ends up in its Radicale collection path. Radicale 3.8\nrefuses paths containing any of :''\"*?, (validate_path_value = minimal\nby default) and control characters, and drops . and .. components, so\nsuch calendars could be created in Modoboa but not in Radicale.\n\nThe name validator now rejects these characters and names, on top of\npath separators, and its message lists the forbidden characters.\n\n* feat(calendars): make calendar names unique per owner\n\nNothing prevented a user from creating two calendars with the same\nname, both pointing to the same Radicale collection.\n\n- add unique constraints on (mailbox, name) and (domain, name); the\n  constraint is not put on the path, a TEXT column that MariaDB cannot\n  index, and a renamed calendar keeps its path anyway\n- validate uniqueness in the API, ignoring case, to return a readable\n  error instead of an integrity error\n- pick a free path when creating a calendar, so a new calendar never\n  takes the path of a renamed one\n- rename existing duplicates (\"Name (2)\", ...) before adding the\n  constraints; paths are left untouched so calendars keep their data\n\n* feat(calendars): add rights endpoint for the Radicale rights plugin\n\nRadicale >= 3.3 only reads its rights file at startup, and the file\ngenerated by Modoboa does not reach Radicale when both run on\ndifferent servers without a shared filesystem. Calendars shared\nthrough access rules were therefore not accessible.\n\nAdd POST /api/v2/calendar-rights/, used by the radicale-modoboa-rights\nplugin. It returns, for a given user, the domains whose user calendars\nhe administers, the domains whose shared calendars he manages and the\ncalendars shared with him through access rules.\n\nThe endpoint is restricted to the \"Radicale\" OAuth2 application, which\nauthenticates with its client id and secret (HTTP Basic). Verified\nsecrets are remembered in process to avoid hashing them (PBKDF2) on\neach request.\n\n* refactor(calendars): authenticate Radicale with an OAuth2 access token\n\nThe rights endpoint authenticated Radicale with its client id and\nsecret on each request, through a custom HTTP Basic authentication\nclass. It re-implemented the client secret check and had to remember\nverified secrets, as hashing them (PBKDF2) costs ~110 ms.\n\nRadicale now gets an access token with the client credentials grant\n(/api/o/token/) and sends it as a Bearer token. The endpoint relies on\ndjango-oauth-toolkit''s OAuth2Authentication and only accepts tokens\nissued to the OAuth2 application named Radicale. The secret is checked\nonce per token instead of once per request.\n\n* fix(calendars): write the same shares in the rights file as the API\n\nThe rights file and the rights endpoint computed shares differently:\nthe file gave RrWw to write rules, letting a grantee delete the owner''s\ncalendar, and kept rules granting nothing or involving an inactive\nuser or a disabled domain.\n\nBoth now use the same functions to select effective access rules and\nto translate them into Radicale permissions (r, wd or rwd, ''d''\npreventing the deletion of the calendar itself). Admin and domain\ncalendar rules of the file are left unchanged.\n\n* build(docker): use the Modoboa rights plugin in Radicale\n\nInstall radicale-modoboa-rights in the Radicale image and fetch rights\nfrom the calendar-rights endpoint instead of the generated rights file,\nwhich Radicale only reads at startup.\n\nRadicale now authenticates with its own OAuth2 application, which the\nrights endpoint requires. The plugin is taken from TestPyPI until it is\npublished on PyPI.\n\nThe getting started commands used a wrong container name and broken\nquoting; they now also create the Radicale application.\n\n* test(calendars): restore UserPreferencesTestCase test data lost in merge\n\nThe merge of master split the setUpTestData method of\nUserPreferencesTestCase: its last two lines ended up at the end of\ntest_duplicates_are_renamed, where cls is undefined, and the rest was\nlost, so the preferences tests had no account.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Christophe CHAUVET <christophe.chauvet@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2dfaa424dcb5b5eb366f7b499e165fca0d451ec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/trees/2dfaa424dcb5b5eb366f7b499e165fca0d451ec8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modoboa/modoboa/git/commits/aad4ab693658c1295fd8cfa951cc5b1a707d7188","verification":{"payload":"tree 2dfaa424dcb5b5eb366f7b499e165fca0d451ec8\nparent 6af2f52c429e1939f15b8073ee7457a70002be1a\nauthor Antoine Nguyen <tonio@ngyn.org> 1790531136 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790531136 +0200\n\nfeat(calendar): calendars rights endpoint (#4238)\n\n* fix(calendars): make rights file section names unique\n\nAccess rule sections were named after the grantee and the calendar\nname, so two owners sharing a calendar with the same name with the same\nuser produced duplicate sections. Token sections had the same issue\nfor calendars sharing a path. Radicale reads the rights file with a\nstrict ConfigParser and refuses to start on a duplicated section.\n\nSection names now include the pk of the rule or calendar.\n\n* fix(calendars): reject calendar names refused by Radicale\n\nA calendar name ends up in its Radicale collection path. Radicale 3.8\nrefuses paths containing any of :''\"*?, (validate_path_value = minimal\nby default) and control characters, and drops . and .. components, so\nsuch calendars could be created in Modoboa but not in Radicale.\n\nThe name validator now rejects these characters and names, on top of\npath separators, and its message lists the forbidden characters.\n\n* feat(calendars): make calendar names unique per owner\n\nNothing prevented a user from creating two calendars with the same\nname, both pointing to the same Radicale collection.\n\n- add unique constraints on (mailbox, name) and (domain, name); the\n  constraint is not put on the path, a TEXT column that MariaDB cannot\n  index, and a renamed calendar keeps its path anyway\n- validate uniqueness in the API, ignoring case, to return a readable\n  error instead of an integrity error\n- pick a free path when creating a calendar, so a new calendar never\n  takes the path of a renamed one\n- rename existing duplicates (\"Name (2)\", ...) before adding the\n  constraints; paths are left untouched so calendars keep their data\n\n* feat(calendars): add rights endpoint for the Radicale rights plugin\n\nRadicale >= 3.3 only reads its rights file at startup, and the file\ngenerated by Modoboa does not reach Radicale when both run on\ndifferent servers without a shared filesystem. Calendars shared\nthrough access rules were therefore not accessible.\n\nAdd POST /api/v2/calendar-rights/, used by the radicale-modoboa-rights\nplugin. It returns, for a given user, the domains whose user calendars\nhe administers, the domains whose shared calendars he manages and the\ncalendars shared with him through access rules.\n\nThe endpoint is restricted to the \"Radicale\" OAuth2 application, which\nauthenticates with its client id and secret (HTTP Basic). Verified\nsecrets are remembered in process to avoid hashing them (PBKDF2) on\neach request.\n\n* refactor(calendars): authenticate Radicale with an OAuth2 access token\n\nThe rights endpoint authenticated Radicale with its client id and\nsecret on each request, through a custom HTTP Basic authentication\nclass. It re-implemented the client secret check and had to remember\nverified secrets, as hashing them (PBKDF2) costs ~110 ms.\n\nRadicale now gets an access token with the client credentials grant\n(/api/o/token/) and sends it as a Bearer token. The endpoint relies on\ndjango-oauth-toolkit''s OAuth2Authentication and only accepts tokens\nissued to the OAuth2 application named Radicale. The secret is checked\nonce per token instead of once per request.\n\n* fix(calendars): write the same shares in the rights file as the API\n\nThe rights file and the rights endpoint computed shares differently:\nthe file gave RrWw to write rules, letting a grantee delete the owner''s\ncalendar, and kept rules granting nothing or involving an inactive\nuser or a disabled domain.\n\nBoth now use the same functions to select effective access rules and\nto translate them into Radicale permissions (r, wd or rwd, ''d''\npreventing the deletion of the calendar itself). Admin and domain\ncalendar rules of the file are left unchanged.\n\n* build(docker): use the Modoboa rights plugin in Radicale\n\nInstall radicale-modoboa-rights in the Radicale image and fetch rights\nfrom the calendar-rights endpoint instead of the generated rights file,\nwhich Radicale only reads at startup.\n\nRadicale now authenticates with its own OAuth2 application, which the\nrights endpoint requires. The plugin is taken from TestPyPI until it is\npublished on PyPI.\n\nThe getting started commands used a wrong container name and broken\nquoting; they now also create the Radicale application.\n\n* test(calendars): restore UserPreferencesTestCase test data lost in merge\n\nThe merge of master split the setUpTestData method of\nUserPreferencesTestCase: its last two lines ended up at the end of\ntest_duplicates_are_renamed, where cls is undefined, and the rest was\nlost, so the preferences tests had no account.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Christophe CHAUVET <christophe.chauvet@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquVZACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArG8QAK875NmB+xflMB2LUhE1UUnZ\neX7exHQmY9qhfRvrAgSWAD4KZExYroJDgkImKBb4RiStctT7Bd1V8iohWydnPWu7\newP9NOdBBplyZdQ/5FF68qJTBKe+QSSqmxrEIzDtKoEsPDopfwFVg/gIVBcH8PXQ\nZUZlalbXh4CYkxVkPqezJolSC1oHmufIlIrm0faHNurTdpZ2EXnaumPanHp4LvlS\nXglsafkuzHAyOAlBAqkkVnsB69uky3kIuV9TQZCYePkXDL4y+egaDrG8Qa+5sZyT\nQOxgjUuXUrIJEHRn6mWM21cbhvJlxlfOOzjOa0/HENgf5X84X6FVDKy1qDKsZajh\noXNkA4G4m/Y+O/UtuwQP7urXIkm9z6MBvRLDwXSQnIpBb3VOWypjSmUHxz3OrGoP\naI2S6C/16da2syLO+pUYf6MEO9HYdZMX4oVO/e0BWn3Xzo0eE3HA4u0Q2Uhc0RGr\nv03+SAPq/A6AmL/mhUFw0IdOZrQrnbE7hVXc+QwOp7wOkqleia0IcdY4/Nn8gvii\ne1m+mlQOIHKmjJx0RMHvN/Vv/XLG3tDPqI2AVnqkGbv88yd+3Qdpg8/qmiXMb1K6\nFyZewf4TL7EUjJEdKxhErj49VxvfIfhTl+gVYBh6o5xp8PjGOTTNMNsZVbCs0Zab\npNN1JspBTc+Bs8vXy22x\n=XLPJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T17:45:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","fo