-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commit/46a173a999673eaefb8ed85729a16813e1575028","node_id":"C_kwDOAJ38fNoAKDQ2YTE3M2E5OTk2NzNlYWVmYjhlZDg1NzI5YTE2ODEzZTE1NzUwMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commit/2680961383164bac85f8a32b27d6b041299cdb93","sha":"2680961383164bac85f8a32b27d6b041299cdb93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commits/2680961383164bac85f8a32b27d6b041299cdb93"}],"sha":"46a173a999673eaefb8ed85729a16813e1575028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commits/46a173a999673eaefb8ed85729a16813e1575028"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239930247?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lingeswaranTW","id":239930247,"login":"lingeswaranTW","node_id":"U_kgDODk0Lhw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lingeswaranTW","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commits/2680961383164bac85f8a32b27d6b041299cdb93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:04:30Z","email":"lingeswaran.s@thoughtworks.com","name":"Lingeswaran Subramaniyam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:04:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"BAH-4874 Draft Forms (#1077)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Draft saving experience and Draft visibility indicators - UI (#108)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Draft saving experience and Draft visibility indicators - UI\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add feature toggle\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Fix failing test\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Modify to make CSS classes more specific for Notification banner\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Move all related scope variables to one map\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add signoff feedback items\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add new capability: Disable Save as Draft button until the form is dirty (#113)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add new capability: Disable Save as Draft button until the form is dirty\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add tests to improve coverage\n\n* [110921] Global header draft indicator and overlay (#115)\n\n* Global header draft indicator and overlay\n\n* Add indicator to vist details page as well (#123)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Manual ''Save as Draft'' Trigger (#120)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Manual ''Save as Draft'' Trigger\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 |  Update tests to increase test coverage\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Add tests and update logic\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Add test coverage\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Remove unnecessary comments\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Adding Claude PR Review file\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Update code as per PR comments and PR Review by Claude\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Update as per PR comments, remove dead code\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Fix for spinner not appearing on first click of Save As Draft (#124)\n\n* Feature 111796 resume draft (#126)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Resume Draft from Banner UI\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Fix Resume draft to work for both form1 and form2 forms\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Add resume functionality for auto populate on clicking Consultation\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Code updates based on Cure PR Review plugin implementation\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Modify based on PR review\n\n* Pooja | Bug-108160 | Fix for navigation blocked between consultation tabs (#128)\n\n* Pooja | Fix for Save As Draft button disabling on navigating between Consultation tabs (#137)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113286 | Update unsaved data warning pop-up on navigation from Consultation page (#141)\n\n* Pooja | Feature 113099 discard draft: Discard Draft using banner UI (#139)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Discard Draft using banner UI\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Add discard success banner, handle close button functionality\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Fixes based on Claude PR Review\n\n* Implement the auto interval feature when FormDraftIsEnabled (#142)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Add sign-off feedback changes (#145)\n\n* Feature 112427 auto deletion  (#146)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-112427 | Auto deletion scenario for manual closure of visit\n\n* Pooja | Hive0112427 | Ensure drafts are not allowed to be created when patient has no active visit, fix for pop up not showing up when user fills a form data after discarding a previous draft\n\n* Pooja | Hive-112427 | Add null check before calling discard Drafts\n\n* Auto refresh the draft overlay contents (#147)\n\n* Pooja | Feature 117165 trigger save navigating out (#153)\n\n* Pooja | Add code to Save draft when Proceed button is clicked from the Pop up\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117165 | Trigger save as draft navigation out of patient dashboard\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117165 | Add fixes as suggested by Claude PR Review plugin\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | \"Save as Draft\" button remains enabled after successful save when no changes are made (#160)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-116474 | Bugfix for Issue #5\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix for issue#5 \"Save as Draft\" button remains enabled after successful save when no changes are made\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Remove comments\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Update variable names so they are self-explanatory\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Feedback - Show icon to show a form has data/ unsaved data (#167)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Feedback - Show icon to show a form has data/ unsaved data\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Fix based on Claude PR review plugin\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Update variable name to make it more relevant and self explanatory\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-119365 | Fix for Incorrect Unsaved Indicator State on Draft Resume (#173)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Fix for orange inidicator showing up for saved forms\n\n* Pooja | Bug-119365 | Fix failing tests\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix for issue #4 (#175)\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix for issue #4\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix based on PR review plugin by Claude\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Editing of a form should be disabled if draft is present (#181)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Editing of a form should be disabled if draft is present\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Updates based on recommendations by Claude PR review plugin\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Disable hover state when edit icon is disabled\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|Fixed draft forms not appearing the left panel after encounter expiry (#184)\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|Fixed draft forms nto appearing the left panel after encounter expiry\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|pr plugin fixes\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|Added repetative mock to before block\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Fix issue related to Issue #4 (#190)\n\n* BAH-4874 Missed test changes\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Bugfix for Issue #2 (#196)\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Bugfix for Issue #2\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Removing code change unnecessary for this bugfix\n\n* Fix the auto save timer start (#212)\n\n* Hive-123484|Karthik|prevent duplicate Form 1 draft entries in Observations (#207)\n\n* bugfix|Karthik|prevent duplicate Form 1 draft entries in Observations\n\n- Reuse the existing observation UUID when resuming a Form 1 draft.\n- Update the existing draft instead of creating a new observation instance.\n- Prevent duplicate draft entries from appearing in the Observations navigation panel.\n- Ensure subsequent draft saves continue to update the same draft.\n\n* bugfix-123484|Karthik|fix Form 1 draft duplication and Form 2 template insertion issues\n\n- Remove double assignment typo on line 108\n- Extract template equality check into reusable helper function to handle Form 1 (uuid) and Form 2 (formUuid) comparison correctly, preventing undefined label issues\n- Restore specific observation UUID assertion to verify deduplication retention\n- Add regression test for Form 1 draft-resume deduplication scenario\n- Add test for multiple Form 2 templates with undefined labels to verify guard fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-123346|Karthik|preserve unsaved observation forms when user navigates to other modules (#209)\n\n* bugfix-123346|Karthik|preserve unsaved observation forms when user navigates to other modules\n\n- Preserve partially entered observation data across module navigation.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-123854 | Banti | Fix draft indicator overlay issue (#227)\n\n* Banti | Fix draft indicator overlay issue\n\n* Fix form draft overlay accessible even toggle is off issue\n\n* remove unnecessary methods\n\n* Hive-121639|Karthik|prevent false unsaved changes indicator on form reopen (#224)\n\n* fix-121639|Karthik|Nandini|prevent false unsaved changes indicator on form reopen\n\n- handling of missing observations on reopen\n- Reload observations when template is reopened\n- Preserve observations during save operations\n- Sort the changed obs in the state\n- Proper prioritization of observation sources\n- handling of missing observations on reopen\n- Reload observations when template is reopened\n- Preserve observations during save operations\n- Sort the changed obs in the state\n- Proper prioritization of observation sources\n\n* removes unwanted comments\n\n* chages the save as draft button enable condition\n\n* bugfix-121639|Karthik|Optimize observation deduplication & add functional tests\n\n- Optimize trackedObsUuids from Array to Set for O(n²)→O(n) complexity\n  · Replace array.push() with Set.add() for deduplication\n  · Replace _.includes() with Set.has() for O(1) membership testing\n  · Enables efficient filtering of duplicate observations\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Suhas| Hive-124404 | Form Validation Errors Block Navigation to Patient Dashboard(form1 )\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Hive-120097: Show warning while logging out with drafts present\n\nAdds a drafts-in-progress warning dialog on logout when the clinician\nhas unsaved observation form drafts, gated by the existing\nenableFormDraftFeature config toggle (no new global property).\n\n- logoutService.attemptLogout() centralizes the logout flow: checks\n  formDraftService.hasDraftsForProvider() and shows the warning dialog\n  (existing ngDialog pattern) only when drafts exist; falls back to\n  direct logout on error so a drafts-check failure never blocks logout.\n- Wired at all logout entry points (click and quickLogoutComboKey\n  keyboard shortcut) via the log-out directive; guarded against\n  concurrent invocations with an isAttemptingLogout flag.\n- auditLogService.log(...) moved into logoutService.logoutUser() so\n  it fires once per logout instead of being duplicated per controller.\n- Added shared ui/app/i18n/common/locale_*.json for the warning modal\n  strings (all languages already supported elsewhere in the app), so\n  mergeLocaleFilesService merges common/app/custom translations instead\n  of duplicating strings across all 11 apps.\n- Removed dead $scope.logout in registration''s NavigationController\n  (registration/header.html already used the log-out directive, so\n  this bypassed the new drafts-warning flow entirely).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Rama/Suhas | Hive-120097 | Showing warning while logging out with drafts present\n\nHive-120097-2 - fix package issues\n\nHive-120097-2 - fix package issues\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix phantom validation blocking saves on deleted forms (#237)\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix phantom validation blocking saves on deleted forms\n\nImplement proper form deletion handling to distinguish between pinned\nand unpinned forms, preventing phantom validation and unwanted reappearance\nof deleted forms.\n\nRefactored form deletion logic to:\n\n1. Track deleted forms in $rootScope.deletedFormIds to prevent re-addition\n2. Distinguish between pinned (alwaysShow=true) and unpinned forms:\n   - Pinned forms: Keep in list with cleared data\n   - Unpinned forms: Remove from list immediately\n3. Clear all form state: observations, validations, components, form data\n4. Filter observations to prevent deleted form data from being saved\n5. Update validation handler to dynamically check current selectedObsTemplate\n\n**conceptSetGroupPanelViewValidationHandler.js**\n- Pass consultation parameter to constructor for dynamic form selection checks\n\n**conceptSetGroup.js** (directive remove() function)\n- Extract templateId calculation for consistent identification\n- Create clearTemplateState() helper to properly reset form state\n- Handle pinned vs unpinned forms based on alwaysShow property\n- Track deleted forms in hiveDeletedFormIds\n- Clear observations, formData, validation state, and component\n- Update parent controller''s allTemplates via scope chain walking\n\n**conceptSetPageController.js**\n- Add consultation parameter to validation handler initialization\n- Filter deleted forms from selectedObsTemplate on reinitialize\n- Check deletedFormIds before re-adding forms via insertTemplate/insertInDefaultOrder\n- Filter observations from deleted forms before collection\n- Filter extraObservations to exclude deleted form observations\n- Prevent re-adding deleted forms from observations or URL parameters\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix PR review critical issues - null guards and state management\n\n   Addressed critical safety issues from PR #237 review:\n   - BLOCKER: Guard validation handler initialization on consultation presence\n   - CRITICAL: Reset deletedFormIds on new consultation init to prevent cross-\n   - CRITICAL: Include uuid and id fallbacks in form ID matching for observation filtering\n   - MAJOR: Add null guards for observations in filtering functions\n   - MINOR: Add null guard in clearTemplateState helper\n\n* Rama/Suhas | Hive-120097 | Showing warning while logging out with drafts present\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix PR review critical issues - scope isolation and observation filtering\n\n   Fixes three critical issues from PR review:\n\n   1. BLOCKER - Remove redundant parent scope traversal in conceptSetGroup.js\n      - Eliminated fragile DOM hierarchy dependency (anti-pattern)\n      - allTemplates two-way binding makes traversal unnecessary\n      - Simplified code by 18 lines\n\n   2. CRITICAL - Add missing observation filtering in draft restoration\n      - Prevent deleted forms'' observations from being restored from draft data\n      - Add guard check for deleted forms before restoring form2 observations\n\n   3. CRITICAL - Add concept.uuid filtering in observation collection\n      - Match filtering behavior between concatObservationForms and collectObservationsFromConceptSets\n      - Consistent pattern: filter observations by concept UUID or formFieldPath\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix critical issues - deleted form state persistence and validation\n\nFix two critical defects blocking PR #237 acceptance:\n\n1. Persist deletedFormIds to $scope.consultation (not just $rootScope)\n   - Prevents deleted unpinned forms from reappearing on controller re-init\n   - Fixes re-navigation bug (tab switch, page reload, patient change)\n   - State now survives across consultation scope lifetime\n   - Only applied to unpinned forms (pinned forms still use state-clear)\n\n2. Guard undefined comparisons in isFormSelected validation check\n   - Previously: template.uuid === conceptSet.uuid allowed undefined === undefined\n   - Now: Uses composite key pattern (formUuid || uuid || id) with guards\n   - Fixes phantom validation for ObservationForm templates lacking .uuid\n   - Properly skips validation for all deleted/unselected form types\n\nHIVE-121640 | Consolidate repeated deletedFormIds declarations into helper\n\nExtracted getRootDeletedFormIds() helper to eliminate 9 repeated declarations\nof ''var deletedFormIds = $rootScope.deletedFormIds || [];'' across\nconcatObservationForms, insertInDefaultOrder, insertTemplate, and other\nfunctions. Addresses PR #237 reviewer feedback on DRY violations.\n\n HIVE-121640|Karthik|Scope deletedFormIds to consultation, remove $rootScope dependency\n\n   Moved deletedFormIds tracking from $rootScope (global, never cleared on\n   patient/consultation switch) to $scope.consultation (scoped, auto-resets\n   per consultation). This addresses PR #237 Major #3 architectural issue.\n\n   Changes:\n   - conceptSetGroup.js: Write deletions to $scope.consultation.deletedFormIds\n   - conceptSetPageController.js: Read from consultation instead of $rootScope\n   - Removed $rootScope seeding in init()\n   - Simplified getRootDeletedFormIds() to call getDeletedFormIds()\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix phantom validation blocking saves on deleted forms\n\nImplement proper form deletion handling to distinguish between pinned\nand unpinned forms, preventing phantom validation and unwanted reappearance\nof deleted forms.\n\nRefactored form deletion logic to:\n\n1. Track deleted forms in $rootScope.deletedFormIds to prevent re-addition\n2. Distinguish between pinned (alwaysShow=true) and unpinned forms:\n   - Pinned forms: Keep in list with cleared data\n   - Unpinned forms: Remove from list immediately\n3. Clear all form state: observations, validations, components, form data\n4. Filter observations to prevent deleted form data from being saved\n5. Update validation handler to dynamically check current selectedObsTemplate\n\n**conceptSetGroupPanelViewValidationHandler.js**\n- Pass consultation parameter to constructor for dynamic form selection checks\n\n**conceptSetGroup.js** (directive remove() function)\n- Extract templateId calculation for consistent identification\n- Create clearTemplateState() helper to properly reset form state\n- Handle pinned vs unpinned forms based on alwaysShow property\n- Track deleted forms in hiveDeletedFormIds\n- Clear observations, formData, validation state, and component\n- Update parent controller''s allTemplates via scope chain walking\n\n**conceptSetPageController.js**\n- Add consultation parameter to validation handler initialization\n- Filter deleted forms from selectedObsTemplate on reinitialize\n- Check deletedFormIds before re-adding forms via insertTemplate/insertInDefaultOrder\n- Filter observations from deleted forms before collection\n- Filter extraObservations to exclude deleted form observations\n- Prevent re-adding deleted forms from observations or URL parameters\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix PR review critical issues - null guards and state management\n\n   Addressed critical safety issues from PR #237 review:\n   - BLOCKER: Guard validation handler initialization on consultation presence\n   - CRITICAL: Reset deletedFormIds on new consultation init to prevent cross-\n   - CRITICAL: Include uuid and id fallbacks in form ID matching for observation filtering\n   - MAJOR: Add null guards for observations in filtering functions\n   - MINOR: Add null guard in clearTemplateState helper\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix PR review critical issues - scope isolation and observation filtering\n\n   Fixes three critical issues from PR review:\n\n   1. BLOCKER - Remove redundant parent scope traversal in conceptSetGroup.js\n      - Eliminated fragile DOM hierarchy dependency (anti-pattern)\n      - allTemplates two-way binding makes traversal unnecessary\n      - Simplified code by 18 lines\n\n   2. CRITICAL - Add missing observation filtering in draft restoration\n      - Prevent deleted forms'' observations from being restored from draft data\n      - Add guard check for deleted forms before restoring form2 observations\n\n   3. CRITICAL - Add concept.uuid filtering in observation collection\n      - Match filtering behavior between concatObservationForms and collectObservationsFromConceptSets\n      - Consistent pattern: filter observations by concept UUID or formFieldPath\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix critical issues - deleted form state persistence and validation\n\nFix two critical defects blocking PR #237 acceptance:\n\n1. Persist deletedFormIds to $scope.consultation (not just $rootScope)\n   - Prevents deleted unpinned forms from reappearing on controller re-init\n   - Fixes re-navigation bug (tab switch, page reload, patient change)\n   - State now survives across consultation scope lifetime\n   - Only applied to unpinned forms (pinned forms still use state-clear)\n\n2. Guard undefined comparisons in isFormSelected validation check\n   - Previously: template.uuid === conceptSet.uuid allowed undefined === undefined\n   - Now: Uses composite key pattern (formUuid || uuid || id) with guards\n   - Fixes phantom validation for ObservationForm templates lacking .uuid\n   - Properly skips validation for all deleted/unselected form types\n\nHIVE-121640 | Consolidate repeated deletedFormIds declarations into helper\n\nExtracted getRootDeletedFormIds() helper to eliminate 9 repeated declarations\nof ''var deletedFormIds = $rootScope.deletedFormIds || [];'' across\nconcatObservationForms, insertInDefaultOrder, insertTemplate, and other\nfunctions. Addresses PR #237 reviewer feedback on DRY violations.\n\n HIVE-121640|Karthik|Scope deletedFormIds to consultation, remove $rootScope dependency\n\n   Moved deletedFormIds tracking from $rootScope (global, never cleared on\n   patient/consultation switch) to $scope.consultation (scoped, auto-resets\n   per consultation). This addresses PR #237 Major #3 architectural issue.\n\n   Changes:\n   - conceptSetGroup.js: Write deletions to $scope.consultation.deletedFormIds\n   - conceptSetPageController.js: Read from consultation instead of $rootScope\n   - Removed $rootScope seeding in init()\n   - Simplified getRootDeletedFormIds() to call getDeletedFormIds()\n\n* Fix failing tests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-125649|Suhas|''form2'' reappears/reopens after being deleted and saved\n\n* Fixed PR review by claude\n\n* Fixed package issue - replaced Array with angular\n\n* moved the test file to ui/tests folder, and using existing titles for test titles\n\n* Hive-125302|Karthik|preserve dirty state across draft re-entry (#244)\n\n* bugfix-125302|Karthik|preserve dirty state across draft re-entry\n\nPersist form baselines across controller re-entry, prevent stale drafts from\noverwriting local changes, and keep forms dirty when modified during\npost-save stabilization.\n\nAlso update the draft button to use the form''s dirty state and add coverage\nfor changes made immediately after saving.\nrefactor| simplify persistent dirty-state handling\n\nCentralize patient baseline management and remove redundant draft merging\nlogic to keep dirty-state tracking consistent across consultation re-entry.\n\n* resolves lint issues\n\n* HIVE-125302|Karthik|Fix data loss on form re-entry and save button lockup after draft save\n\n* HIVE-125302|Karthik|Fix save-as-draft button remaining enabled after save with no edits\n\nRefactor dirty-state tracking to use persistent baseline across controller\ninstances, preventing stale drafts from overwriting fresh observations on\nre-entry. Implements smart timeout in post-save stabilization window to\ndistinguish user edits from transient state changes.\n\n---------\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-126558|Karthik|prevent unsaved data popup appearing after main consultation save (#254)\n\n* bugfix-125302|Karthik|fix unsaved data popup appearing after main save\n\nIssue: After saving the main consultation, the popup \"There is unsaved\nconsultation data for this patient\" was appearing incorrectly when navigating\naway, because the watcher kept setting dirtyConsultationForm=true even after\nthe main save completed.\n\n* bugfix|Karthik|prevent watcher from interfering with post-save state\n\nWatcher now respects justSaved flag and skips state updates while it''s\ntrue. This prevents the popup from appearing on navigation after a\nsuccessful save.\n\n* Address pr comments by plugin\n\n* changes merge condition\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* HIVE-120097 | Showing warning while logging out with drafts present  (#255)\n\n* registration-drafts-scrollbar-fix\n\n* added unit test cases\n\n* added unit test case\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ramadevi Adepu <ramadeviadepu@Ramadevis-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Form state fixes: orange icon and draft visibility\n\nFixes form dirty-state tracking and draft resume logic.\n- Integrates form2 interaction tracking into formDirtyStateService\n- Moves draft request deduplication to formDraftService\n- Fixes false dirty trigger on duration field render\n- Fixes race condition on draft data visibility\n- Adds comprehensive test coverage for risky code paths\n- Cleans up whitespace and unnecessary comments\n\n* bugfix|form1| Sync state flags with observation save handler (#261)\n\n* bugfix|form1| Sync state flags with observation save handler\n\nAdd missing $state.dirtyConsultationForm = false and $state.justSaved = true\nto editObservation.js save handler to prevent false \"unsaved consultation data\"\npopup on navigation after form1 save. Aligns behavior with dashboard.js\nhandleEditSave().\n\n* bugfix|form1| Draft-aware state flags for observation save\n\nAdd conditional $state.dirtyConsultationForm = false and $state.justSaved = true\nto editObservation.js, only when !$rootScope.draftData. Prevents false\n\"unsaved consultation data\" popup after observation save while preserving\nit for actual draft changes.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Suhas|Hive-|Form2 Observations Loss on Tab Switch\n\n* Suhas|Hive-|Form2 Observations Loss on Tab Switch\n\n* shows warning while closing a visit if provider has draft\n\n* feat: add draft warning for closing visits\n\nShow a configurable draft warning dialog for logout and visit closure, with context-specific messaging and actions.\n\n* fix: warn only for current patient drafts on visit close\n\n* fix: Adds translations and resolve inconsitent styling among the modules\n\n* Hive-127888 | [Product PR feedback] Add toggle to have the option to discard drafts on Save instead of setting markAsSaved as true\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix for failing build\n\n(cherry picked from commit 3343f5d8963702df4da68ffb853dbd2b84e38d58)\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix for failing build\n\n(cherry picked from commit e979de7d9386af2c0e56b59cc123dcc6315543f2)\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix unit test failures\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix remaining unit test failures\n\n* BAH-4874 | Revert visitController behaviour change, align IPD test with existing behaviour\n\n* BAH-4874 | Normalise line endings and remove duplicated test blocks\n\n* BAH-4874 | Updates to behavior when a visit is closed\n\n* BAH-4874 | Changes as per PR review comments\n\n* BAH-4874 | PR review changes | Resolve provider from authenticated session instead of providerUuid for form drafts\n\n* BAH-4874 |  Reduce code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce further code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce further code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce further code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce code duplication\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix to test failure\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix for Code duplication failure\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix to reduce code duplication\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Pooja Sastry <pooja.sastry@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: sasikiran-tw <sasikiran.jakkula@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Soorya Kumaran C <90232857+SooryaKumaranC-tw@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Avni Tanwar Tw <avni.tanwar@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: iamkarthikdasari <karthik.dasari@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: bantirathod87 <banti.rathod@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: suhas <suhas.katkuri@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: RamadeviAdepu <ramadevi.adepu@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ramadevi Adepu <ramadeviadepu@Ramadevis-MacBook-Pro.local>","tree":{"sha":"6ea821dabc5399c9ab8fb613593a43828fd861af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/git/trees/6ea821dabc5399c9ab8fb613593a43828fd861af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/git/commits/2680961383164bac85f8a32b27d6b041299cdb93","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ea821dabc5399c9ab8fb613593a43828fd861af\nparent b4519b24e3ba7e088dfe25268c8ff8c11d006e86\nauthor Lingeswaran Subramaniyam <lingeswaran.s@thoughtworks.com> 1790053470 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790053470 +0530\n\nBAH-4874 Draft Forms (#1077)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Draft saving experience and Draft visibility indicators - UI (#108)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Draft saving experience and Draft visibility indicators - UI\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add feature toggle\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Fix failing test\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Modify to make CSS classes more specific for Notification banner\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Move all related scope variables to one map\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add signoff feedback items\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add new capability: Disable Save as Draft button until the form is dirty (#113)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add new capability: Disable Save as Draft button until the form is dirty\n\n* Pooja | Hive-109060 | Add tests to improve coverage\n\n* [110921] Global header draft indicator and overlay (#115)\n\n* Global header draft indicator and overlay\n\n* Add indicator to vist details page as well (#123)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Manual ''Save as Draft'' Trigger (#120)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Manual ''Save as Draft'' Trigger\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 |  Update tests to increase test coverage\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Add tests and update logic\n\n* Pooja | Hive-110920 | Add test coverage\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Remove unnecessary comments\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Adding Claude PR Review file\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Update code as per PR comments and PR Review by Claude\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Update as per PR comments, remove dead code\n\n* Pooja | Hive-119020 | Fix for spinner not appearing on first click of Save As Draft (#124)\n\n* Feature 111796 resume draft (#126)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Resume Draft from Banner UI\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Fix Resume draft to work for both form1 and form2 forms\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Add resume functionality for auto populate on clicking Consultation\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Code updates based on Cure PR Review plugin implementation\n\n* Pooja | Hive-111796 | Modify based on PR review\n\n* Pooja | Bug-108160 | Fix for navigation blocked between consultation tabs (#128)\n\n* Pooja | Fix for Save As Draft button disabling on navigating between Consultation tabs (#137)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113286 | Update unsaved data warning pop-up on navigation from Consultation page (#141)\n\n* Pooja | Feature 113099 discard draft: Discard Draft using banner UI (#139)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Discard Draft using banner UI\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Add discard success banner, handle close button functionality\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Fixes based on Claude PR Review\n\n* Implement the auto interval feature when FormDraftIsEnabled (#142)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-113099 | Add sign-off feedback changes (#145)\n\n* Feature 112427 auto deletion  (#146)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-112427 | Auto deletion scenario for manual closure of visit\n\n* Pooja | Hive0112427 | Ensure drafts are not allowed to be created when patient has no active visit, fix for pop up not showing up when user fills a form data after discarding a previous draft\n\n* Pooja | Hive-112427 | Add null check before calling discard Drafts\n\n* Auto refresh the draft overlay contents (#147)\n\n* Pooja | Feature 117165 trigger save navigating out (#153)\n\n* Pooja | Add code to Save draft when Proceed button is clicked from the Pop up\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117165 | Trigger save as draft navigation out of patient dashboard\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117165 | Add fixes as suggested by Claude PR Review plugin\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | \"Save as Draft\" button remains enabled after successful save when no changes are made (#160)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-116474 | Bugfix for Issue #5\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix for issue#5 \"Save as Draft\" button remains enabled after successful save when no changes are made\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Remove comments\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Update variable names so they are self-explanatory\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Feedback - Show icon to show a form has data/ unsaved data (#167)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Feedback - Show icon to show a form has data/ unsaved data\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Fix based on Claude PR review plugin\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Update variable name to make it more relevant and self explanatory\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-119365 | Fix for Incorrect Unsaved Indicator State on Draft Resume (#173)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117176 | Fix for orange inidicator showing up for saved forms\n\n* Pooja | Bug-119365 | Fix failing tests\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix for issue #4 (#175)\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix for issue #4\n\n* Pooja | Bug-116474 | Fix based on PR review plugin by Claude\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Editing of a form should be disabled if draft is present (#181)\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Editing of a form should be disabled if draft is present\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Updates based on recommendations by Claude PR review plugin\n\n* Pooja | Hive-117252 | Disable hover state when edit icon is disabled\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|Fixed draft forms not appearing the left panel after encounter expiry (#184)\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|Fixed draft forms nto appearing the left panel after encounter expiry\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|pr plugin fixes\n\n* Avni|Hive-119596|Added repetative mock to before block\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Fix issue related to Issue #4 (#190)\n\n* BAH-4874 Missed test changes\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Bugfix for Issue #2 (#196)\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Bugfix for Issue #2\n\n* Pooja | Bugfix-116474 | Removing code change unnecessary for this bugfix\n\n* Fix the auto save timer start (#212)\n\n* Hive-123484|Karthik|prevent duplicate Form 1 draft entries in Observations (#207)\n\n* bugfix|Karthik|prevent duplicate Form 1 draft entries in Observations\n\n- Reuse the existing observation UUID when resuming a Form 1 draft.\n- Update the existing draft instead of creating a new observation instance.\n- Prevent duplicate draft entries from appearing in the Observations navigation panel.\n- Ensure subsequent draft saves continue to update the same draft.\n\n* bugfix-123484|Karthik|fix Form 1 draft duplication and Form 2 template insertion issues\n\n- Remove double assignment typo on line 108\n- Extract template equality check into reusable helper function to handle Form 1 (uuid) and Form 2 (formUuid) comparison correctly, preventing undefined label issues\n- Restore specific observation UUID assertion to verify deduplication retention\n- Add regression test for Form 1 draft-resume deduplication scenario\n- Add test for multiple Form 2 templates with undefined labels to verify guard fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-123346|Karthik|preserve unsaved observation forms when user navigates to other modules (#209)\n\n* bugfix-123346|Karthik|preserve unsaved observation forms when user navigates to other modules\n\n- Preserve partially entered observation data across module navigation.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-123854 | Banti | Fix draft indicator overlay issue (#227)\n\n* Banti | Fix draft indicator overlay issue\n\n* Fix form draft overlay accessible even toggle is off issue\n\n* remove unnecessary methods\n\n* Hive-121639|Karthik|prevent false unsaved changes indicator on form reopen (#224)\n\n* fix-121639|Karthik|Nandini|prevent false unsaved changes indicator on form reopen\n\n- handling of missing observations on reopen\n- Reload observations when template is reopened\n- Preserve observations during save operations\n- Sort the changed obs in the state\n- Proper prioritization of observation sources\n- handling of missing observations on reopen\n- Reload observations when template is reopened\n- Preserve observations during save operations\n- Sort the changed obs in the state\n- Proper prioritization of observation sources\n\n* removes unwanted comments\n\n* chages the save as draft button enable condition\n\n* bugfix-121639|Karthik|Optimize observation deduplication & add functional tests\n\n- Optimize trackedObsUuids from Array to Set for O(n²)→O(n) complexity\n  · Replace array.push() with Set.add() for deduplication\n  · Replace _.includes() with Set.has() for O(1) membership testing\n  · Enables efficient filtering of duplicate observations\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Suhas| Hive-124404 | Form Validation Errors Block Navigation to Patient Dashboard(form1 )\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Hive-120097: Show warning while logging out with drafts present\n\nAdds a drafts-in-progress warning dialog on logout when the clinician\nhas unsaved observation form drafts, gated by the existing\nenableFormDraftFeature config toggle (no new global property).\n\n- logoutService.attemptLogout() centralizes the logout flow: checks\n  formDraftService.hasDraftsForProvider() and shows the warning dialog\n  (existing ngDialog pattern) only when drafts exist; falls back to\n  direct logout on error so a drafts-check failure never blocks logout.\n- Wired at all logout entry points (click and quickLogoutComboKey\n  keyboard shortcut) via the log-out directive; guarded against\n  concurrent invocations with an isAttemptingLogout flag.\n- auditLogService.log(...) moved into logoutService.logoutUser() so\n  it fires once per logout instead of being duplicated per controller.\n- Added shared ui/app/i18n/common/locale_*.json for the warning modal\n  strings (all languages already supported elsewhere in the app), so\n  mergeLocaleFilesService merges common/app/custom translations instead\n  of duplicating strings across all 11 apps.\n- Removed dead $scope.logout in registration''s NavigationController\n  (registration/header.html already used the log-out directive, so\n  this bypassed the new drafts-warning flow entirely).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Rama/Suhas | Hive-120097 | Showing warning while logging out with drafts present\n\nHive-120097-2 - fix package issues\n\nHive-120097-2 - fix package issues\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix phantom validation blocking saves on deleted forms (#237)\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix phantom validation blocking saves on deleted forms\n\nImplement proper form deletion handling to distinguish between pinned\nand unpinned forms, preventing phantom validation and unwanted reappearance\nof deleted forms.\n\nRefactored form deletion logic to:\n\n1. Track deleted forms in $rootScope.deletedFormIds to prevent re-addition\n2. Distinguish between pinned (alwaysShow=true) and unpinned forms:\n   - Pinned forms: Keep in list with cleared data\n   - Unpinned forms: Remove from list immediately\n3. Clear all form state: observations, validations, components, form data\n4. Filter observations to prevent deleted form data from being saved\n5. Update validation handler to dynamically check current selectedObsTemplate\n\n**conceptSetGroupPanelViewValidationHandler.js**\n- Pass consultation parameter to constructor for dynamic form selection checks\n\n**conceptSetGroup.js** (directive remove() function)\n- Extract templateId calculation for consistent identification\n- Create clearTemplateState() helper to properly reset form state\n- Handle pinned vs unpinned forms based on alwaysShow property\n- Track deleted forms in hiveDeletedFormIds\n- Clear observations, formData, validation state, and component\n- Update parent controller''s allTemplates via scope chain walking\n\n**conceptSetPageController.js**\n- Add consultation parameter to validation handler initialization\n- Filter deleted forms from selectedObsTemplate on reinitialize\n- Check deletedFormIds before re-adding forms via insertTemplate/insertInDefaultOrder\n- Filter observations from deleted forms before collection\n- Filter extraObservations to exclude deleted form observations\n- Prevent re-adding deleted forms from observations or URL parameters\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix PR review critical issues - null guards and state management\n\n   Addressed critical safety issues from PR #237 review:\n   - BLOCKER: Guard validation handler initialization on consultation presence\n   - CRITICAL: Reset deletedFormIds on new consultation init to prevent cross-\n   - CRITICAL: Include uuid and id fallbacks in form ID matching for observation filtering\n   - MAJOR: Add null guards for observations in filtering functions\n   - MINOR: Add null guard in clearTemplateState helper\n\n* Rama/Suhas | Hive-120097 | Showing warning while logging out with drafts present\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix PR review critical issues - scope isolation and observation filtering\n\n   Fixes three critical issues from PR review:\n\n   1. BLOCKER - Remove redundant parent scope traversal in conceptSetGroup.js\n      - Eliminated fragile DOM hierarchy dependency (anti-pattern)\n      - allTemplates two-way binding makes traversal unnecessary\n      - Simplified code by 18 lines\n\n   2. CRITICAL - Add missing observation filtering in draft restoration\n      - Prevent deleted forms'' observations from being restored from draft data\n      - Add guard check for deleted forms before restoring form2 observations\n\n   3. CRITICAL - Add concept.uuid filtering in observation collection\n      - Match filtering behavior between concatObservationForms and collectObservationsFromConceptSets\n      - Consistent pattern: filter observations by concept UUID or formFieldPath\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix critical issues - deleted form state persistence and validation\n\nFix two critical defects blocking PR #237 acceptance:\n\n1. Persist deletedFormIds to $scope.consultation (not just $rootScope)\n   - Prevents deleted unpinned forms from reappearing on controller re-init\n   - Fixes re-navigation bug (tab switch, page reload, patient change)\n   - State now survives across consultation scope lifetime\n   - Only applied to unpinned forms (pinned forms still use state-clear)\n\n2. Guard undefined comparisons in isFormSelected validation check\n   - Previously: template.uuid === conceptSet.uuid allowed undefined === undefined\n   - Now: Uses composite key pattern (formUuid || uuid || id) with guards\n   - Fixes phantom validation for ObservationForm templates lacking .uuid\n   - Properly skips validation for all deleted/unselected form types\n\nHIVE-121640 | Consolidate repeated deletedFormIds declarations into helper\n\nExtracted getRootDeletedFormIds() helper to eliminate 9 repeated declarations\nof ''var deletedFormIds = $rootScope.deletedFormIds || [];'' across\nconcatObservationForms, insertInDefaultOrder, insertTemplate, and other\nfunctions. Addresses PR #237 reviewer feedback on DRY violations.\n\n HIVE-121640|Karthik|Scope deletedFormIds to consultation, remove $rootScope dependency\n\n   Moved deletedFormIds tracking from $rootScope (global, never cleared on\n   patient/consultation switch) to $scope.consultation (scoped, auto-resets\n   per consultation). This addresses PR #237 Major #3 architectural issue.\n\n   Changes:\n   - conceptSetGroup.js: Write deletions to $scope.consultation.deletedFormIds\n   - conceptSetPageController.js: Read from consultation instead of $rootScope\n   - Removed $rootScope seeding in init()\n   - Simplified getRootDeletedFormIds() to call getDeletedFormIds()\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix phantom validation blocking saves on deleted forms\n\nImplement proper form deletion handling to distinguish between pinned\nand unpinned forms, preventing phantom validation and unwanted reappearance\nof deleted forms.\n\nRefactored form deletion logic to:\n\n1. Track deleted forms in $rootScope.deletedFormIds to prevent re-addition\n2. Distinguish between pinned (alwaysShow=true) and unpinned forms:\n   - Pinned forms: Keep in list with cleared data\n   - Unpinned forms: Remove from list immediately\n3. Clear all form state: observations, validations, components, form data\n4. Filter observations to prevent deleted form data from being saved\n5. Update validation handler to dynamically check current selectedObsTemplate\n\n**conceptSetGroupPanelViewValidationHandler.js**\n- Pass consultation parameter to constructor for dynamic form selection checks\n\n**conceptSetGroup.js** (directive remove() function)\n- Extract templateId calculation for consistent identification\n- Create clearTemplateState() helper to properly reset form state\n- Handle pinned vs unpinned forms based on alwaysShow property\n- Track deleted forms in hiveDeletedFormIds\n- Clear observations, formData, validation state, and component\n- Update parent controller''s allTemplates via scope chain walking\n\n**conceptSetPageController.js**\n- Add consultation parameter to validation handler initialization\n- Filter deleted forms from selectedObsTemplate on reinitialize\n- Check deletedFormIds before re-adding forms via insertTemplate/insertInDefaultOrder\n- Filter observations from deleted forms before collection\n- Filter extraObservations to exclude deleted form observations\n- Prevent re-adding deleted forms from observations or URL parameters\n\n* HIVE-121640|Karthik|Fix PR review critical issues - null guards and state management\n\n   Addressed critical safety issues from PR #237 review:\n   - BLOCKER: Guard validation handler initialization on consultation presence\n   - CRITICAL: Reset deletedFormIds on new consultation init to prevent cross-\n   - CRITICAL: Include uuid and id fallbacks in form ID matching for observation filtering\n   - MAJOR: Add null guards for observations in filtering functions\n   - MINOR: Add null guard in clearTemplateState helper\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix PR review critical issues - scope isolation and observation filtering\n\n   Fixes three critical issues from PR review:\n\n   1. BLOCKER - Remove redundant parent scope traversal in conceptSetGroup.js\n      - Eliminated fragile DOM hierarchy dependency (anti-pattern)\n      - allTemplates two-way binding makes traversal unnecessary\n      - Simplified code by 18 lines\n\n   2. CRITICAL - Add missing observation filtering in draft restoration\n      - Prevent deleted forms'' observations from being restored from draft data\n      - Add guard check for deleted forms before restoring form2 observations\n\n   3. CRITICAL - Add concept.uuid filtering in observation collection\n      - Match filtering behavior between concatObservationForms and collectObservationsFromConceptSets\n      - Consistent pattern: filter observations by concept UUID or formFieldPath\n\n* HIVE-121640 | Fix critical issues - deleted form state persistence and validation\n\nFix two critical defects blocking PR #237 acceptance:\n\n1. Persist deletedFormIds to $scope.consultation (not just $rootScope)\n   - Prevents deleted unpinned forms from reappearing on controller re-init\n   - Fixes re-navigation bug (tab switch, page reload, patient change)\n   - State now survives across consultation scope lifetime\n   - Only applied to unpinned forms (pinned forms still use state-clear)\n\n2. Guard undefined comparisons in isFormSelected validation check\n   - Previously: template.uuid === conceptSet.uuid allowed undefined === undefined\n   - Now: Uses composite key pattern (formUuid || uuid || id) with guards\n   - Fixes phantom validation for ObservationForm templates lacking .uuid\n   - Properly skips validation for all deleted/unselected form types\n\nHIVE-121640 | Consolidate repeated deletedFormIds declarations into helper\n\nExtracted getRootDeletedFormIds() helper to eliminate 9 repeated declarations\nof ''var deletedFormIds = $rootScope.deletedFormIds || [];'' across\nconcatObservationForms, insertInDefaultOrder, insertTemplate, and other\nfunctions. Addresses PR #237 reviewer feedback on DRY violations.\n\n HIVE-121640|Karthik|Scope deletedFormIds to consultation, remove $rootScope dependency\n\n   Moved deletedFormIds tracking from $rootScope (global, never cleared on\n   patient/consultation switch) to $scope.consultation (scoped, auto-resets\n   per consultation). This addresses PR #237 Major #3 architectural issue.\n\n   Changes:\n   - conceptSetGroup.js: Write deletions to $scope.consultation.deletedFormIds\n   - conceptSetPageController.js: Read from consultation instead of $rootScope\n   - Removed $rootScope seeding in init()\n   - Simplified getRootDeletedFormIds() to call getDeletedFormIds()\n\n* Fix failing tests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-125649|Suhas|''form2'' reappears/reopens after being deleted and saved\n\n* Fixed PR review by claude\n\n* Fixed package issue - replaced Array with angular\n\n* moved the test file to ui/tests folder, and using existing titles for test titles\n\n* Hive-125302|Karthik|preserve dirty state across draft re-entry (#244)\n\n* bugfix-125302|Karthik|preserve dirty state across draft re-entry\n\nPersist form baselines across controller re-entry, prevent stale drafts from\noverwriting local changes, and keep forms dirty when modified during\npost-save stabilization.\n\nAlso update the draft button to use the form''s dirty state and add coverage\nfor changes made immediately after saving.\nrefactor| simplify persistent dirty-state handling\n\nCentralize patient baseline management and remove redundant draft merging\nlogic to keep dirty-state tracking consistent across consultation re-entry.\n\n* resolves lint issues\n\n* HIVE-125302|Karthik|Fix data loss on form re-entry and save button lockup after draft save\n\n* HIVE-125302|Karthik|Fix save-as-draft button remaining enabled after save with no edits\n\nRefactor dirty-state tracking to use persistent baseline across controller\ninstances, preventing stale drafts from overwriting fresh observations on\nre-entry. Implements smart timeout in post-save stabilization window to\ndistinguish user edits from transient state changes.\n\n---------\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Hive-126558|Karthik|prevent unsaved data popup appearing after main consultation save (#254)\n\n* bugfix-125302|Karthik|fix unsaved data popup appearing after main save\n\nIssue: After saving the main consultation, the popup \"There is unsaved\nconsultation data for this patient\" was appearing incorrectly when navigating\naway, because the watcher kept setting dirtyConsultationForm=true even after\nthe main save completed.\n\n* bugfix|Karthik|prevent watcher from interfering with post-save state\n\nWatcher now respects justSaved flag and skips state updates while it''s\ntrue. This prevents the popup from appearing on navigation after a\nsuccessful save.\n\n* Address pr comments by plugin\n\n* changes merge condition\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* HIVE-120097 | Showing warning while logging out with drafts present  (#255)\n\n* registration-drafts-scrollbar-fix\n\n* added unit test cases\n\n* added unit test case\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ramadevi Adepu <ramadeviadepu@Ramadevis-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Form state fixes: orange icon and draft visibility\n\nFixes form dirty-state tracking and draft resume logic.\n- Integrates form2 interaction tracking into formDirtyStateService\n- Moves draft request deduplication to formDraftService\n- Fixes false dirty trigger on duration field render\n- Fixes race condition on draft data visibility\n- Adds comprehensive test coverage for risky code paths\n- Cleans up whitespace and unnecessary comments\n\n* bugfix|form1| Sync state flags with observation save handler (#261)\n\n* bugfix|form1| Sync state flags with observation save handler\n\nAdd missing $state.dirtyConsultationForm = false and $state.justSaved = true\nto editObservation.js save handler to prevent false \"unsaved consultation data\"\npopup on navigation after form1 save. Aligns behavior with dashboard.js\nhandleEditSave().\n\n* bugfix|form1| Draft-aware state flags for observation save\n\nAdd conditional $state.dirtyConsultationForm = false and $state.justSaved = true\nto editObservation.js, only when !$rootScope.draftData. Prevents false\n\"unsaved consultation data\" popup after observation save while preserving\nit for actual draft changes.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\n\n* Suhas|Hive-|Form2 Observations Loss on Tab Switch\n\n* Suhas|Hive-|Form2 Observations Loss on Tab Switch\n\n* shows warning while closing a visit if provider has draft\n\n* feat: add draft warning for closing visits\n\nShow a configurable draft warning dialog for logout and visit closure, with context-specific messaging and actions.\n\n* fix: warn only for current patient drafts on visit close\n\n* fix: Adds translations and resolve inconsitent styling among the modules\n\n* Hive-127888 | [Product PR feedback] Add toggle to have the option to discard drafts on Save instead of setting markAsSaved as true\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix for failing build\n\n(cherry picked from commit 3343f5d8963702df4da68ffb853dbd2b84e38d58)\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix for failing build\n\n(cherry picked from commit e979de7d9386af2c0e56b59cc123dcc6315543f2)\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix unit test failures\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix remaining unit test failures\n\n* BAH-4874 | Revert visitController behaviour change, align IPD test with existing behaviour\n\n* BAH-4874 | Normalise line endings and remove duplicated test blocks\n\n* BAH-4874 | Updates to behavior when a visit is closed\n\n* BAH-4874 | Changes as per PR review comments\n\n* BAH-4874 | PR review changes | Resolve provider from authenticated session instead of providerUuid for form drafts\n\n* BAH-4874 |  Reduce code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce further code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce further code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce further code duplication to pass SonarQube quality gate\n\n* BAH-4874 | Reduce code duplication\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix to test failure\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix for Code duplication failure\n\n* BAH-4874 | Fix to reduce code duplication\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Pooja Sastry <pooja.sastry@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: sasikiran-tw <sasikiran.jakkula@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Soorya Kumaran C <90232857+SooryaKumaranC-tw@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Avni Tanwar Tw <avni.tanwar@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: iamkarthikdasari <karthik.dasari@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Karthik Dasari <karthikdasari@Karthiks-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: bantirathod87 <banti.rathod@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: suhas <suhas.katkuri@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: RamadeviAdepu <ramadevi.adepu@thoughtworks.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ramadevi Adepu <ramadeviadepu@Ramadevis-MacBook-Pro.local>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsgxeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfhMQAAL/FdqaTtYwZMP5A+qvXmb3\n/zj+9ZEyp9JyBOFGVGHesujVUoYiRDkf07LSQlChGv9cFVDXtohVTuDgBzKgj/Iv\nX1AlQZqYc56C6JEA2QShiTp14MxqHRfgIBeIkrC38vv6DWFgBd+/qhCQuIqrCAIt\nCjN4eyHCw4iR6hoX9eE4CB+71qkIR2JGyMsNIT2HmeaNUQ1a8M/uTFqFh9cu8x9i\n+BJZMe6ebzt9g8G2CkebNl9C59HCq4Q94/xYgDh9VYeuO32jBGvP/k2lmGOn1kka\nMzVeUSLhgqLExYfDZdrD1EZFAipSlVI8MACFYizjdRrqMSwhPVkpur9TpYoaW9+3\nGrABtiTjgC4zpb5sMRmmOOz9w26rH+kgjtpKLBuMXlfS73s1BHPmFQkoeelu4aXY\nmWqYBHdpkMlt+V31sLvvaP1p8lKGkmBCTj1rFpjMoR/e20BST4K2x1QPiuxF19Eq\nP1QPfmyOUzNjq08ZCeFNWqQZoUlD026SmtQTXNZMipnuGEkJE5Z1i7LfmD9p3Zd3\nzcvT9j/B3tsDfmmTxHXdrGZq4uEQEP67Zzeh37tkZjNZaNdFyWmfBs1yS0QB7IBM\nVN502Ni4bn9ABOIqt0HuFdAnEP4Lv2bUz82EOb2xoFlMTbMKOv/hhdyPsZ0bYQ5R\n8zoYVuyQGpTkZxYI/Acw\n=C5Cb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T05:04:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MD