rl":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commit/0b190909984b73e4e83121afbd8f45534e538ed6","node_id":"C_kwDOAJ38fNoAKDBiMTkwOTA5OTg0YjczZTRlODMxMjFhZmJkOGY0NTUzNGU1MzhlZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commit/3ae550bf3661931e58cfba00ccf7e11d13f37c49","sha":"3ae550bf3661931e58cfba00ccf7e11d13f37c49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commits/3ae550bf3661931e58cfba00ccf7e11d13f37c49"}],"sha":"0b190909984b73e4e83121afbd8f45534e538ed6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commits/0b190909984b73e4e83121afbd8f45534e538ed6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32308441?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vvkpd","id":32308441,"login":"vvkpd","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzA4NDQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vvkpd","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/commits/3ae550bf3661931e58cfba00ccf7e11d13f37c49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T13:58:35Z","email":"32308441+vvkpd@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vivek Pandey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T13:58:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"BAH-4430: Add feature toggle for no known allergy capturing (#1076)\n\n* HIVE-BAH-4430: Vivek: Add feature toggle for no known allergy capturing\n\nAdd enableNoKnownAllergy config flag (default false) read from clinical\napp.json via appService. When disabled, skips the noKnownAllergyUuid fetch\nand hides the \"Does the patient have any known allergies?\" selector in\nAddAllergy, restoring pre-feature behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* HIVE-BAH-4430: Always filter no known allergy from search regardless of toggle\n\nAlways fetch noKnownAllergyUuid so it can be used to filter \"No Known\nAllergy\" out of allergen search results even when enableNoKnownAllergy\nis off. Move the toggle guard to showKnownAllergySelector in AddAllergy\nso the UI selector still only appears when the toggle is on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* HIVE-BAH-4430: Update tests for enableNoKnownAllergy toggle and search filter fix\n\n- Add enableNoKnownAllergy prop to tests that assert on the known allergy\n  selector UI (requires toggle to be explicitly true now)\n- Add test: selector hidden when enableNoKnownAllergy=false even with UUID set\n- Add test: getNoKnownAllergyUuid called even when toggle is off\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fd183d8eb50ae6a49d9d22fd4a32462e6a7b8b8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/git/trees/fd183d8eb50ae6a49d9d22fd4a32462e6a7b8b8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Bahmni/openmrs-module-bahmniapps/git/commits/3ae550bf3661931e58cfba00ccf7e11d13f37c49","verification":{"payload":"tree fd183d8eb50ae6a49d9d22fd4a32462e6a7b8b8c\nparent 8be372b39b144caa3b8e376bd154332d7b20b854\nauthor Vivek Pandey <32308441+vvkpd@users.noreply.github.com> 1785333515 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785333515 +0530\n\nBAH-4430: Add feature toggle for no known allergy capturing (#1076)\n\n* HIVE-BAH-4430: Vivek: Add feature toggle for no known allergy capturing\n\nAdd enableNoKnownAllergy config flag (default false) read from clinical\napp.json via appService. When disabled, skips the noKnownAllergyUuid fetch\nand hides the \"Does the patient have any known allergies?\" selector in\nAddAllergy, restoring pre-feature behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* HIVE-BAH-4430: Always filter no known allergy from search regardless of toggle\n\nAlways fetch noKnownAllergyUuid so it can be used to filter \"No Known\nAllergy\" out of allergen search results even when enableNoKnownAllergy\nis off. Move the toggle guard to showKnownAllergySelector in AddAllergy\nso the UI selector still only appears when the toggle is on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* HIVE-BAH-4430: Update tests for enableNoKnownAllergy toggle and search filter fix\n\n- Add enableNoKnownAllergy prop to tests that assert on the known allergy\n  selector UI (requires toggle to be explicitly true now)\n- Add test: selector hidden when enableNoKnownAllergy=false even with UUID set\n- Add test: getNoKnownAllergyUuid called even when toggle is off\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"vali