 and password without client credentials so the 401\ninvalid_client path stays covered.\n\nhttps://github.com/oauthlib/oauthlib/compare/v3.3.1...v4.0.0\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"84f8046af7d00709f381fbc8fe832331ec494c56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/trees/84f8046af7d00709f381fbc8fe832331ec494c56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/commits/f82b4f8656e5646b99db16a3ef0b9ba9b109e820","verification":{"payload":"tree 84f8046af7d00709f381fbc8fe832331ec494c56\nparent e56f31f2b8bfa9e2f8629ae757218ef56c11e00a\nauthor Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1790709421 -0400\ncommitter Feanil Patel <feanil@axim.org> 1790709421 -0400\n\ntest: update oauth token bad-request test for oauthlib 4.0.0\n\noauthlib 4.0.0 moved client authentication for the password grant out of\ncreate_token_response() and into validate_token_request(), after the\nrequired-parameter checks. A request with only grant_type now fails with\n400 invalid_request (missing username) instead of 401 invalid_client.\n\nUpdate the existing test to expect the 400, and add a test that supplies\nusername and password without client credentials so the 401\ninvalid_client path stays covered.\n\nhttps://github.com/oauthlib/oauthlib/compare/v3.3.1...v4.0.0\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglcBDQ9rliT2kx8WFoOW4vSlEaG\noJlB7ebCkwaIN8IboAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEW13V/e68XE4qP0LdcymjdmuA9IynLs+c4Ng7uYamFIwtFvlfMOXglRyMNbSr6lmY\n4W31Gcs2RTxxJpjGYXmgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T19:17:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781561?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil/followers","following_url"