3b79a56a7db8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pwnage101","id":85151,"login":"pwnage101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/a3a40072782480d17c5fe3535fa1b4252ed38395/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:28:23Z","email":"tsankey@2u.com","name":"Troy Sankey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:43:33Z","email":"tsankey@2u.com","name":"Troy Sankey"},"message":"feat: remove dead linked_enterprise_customer handling from the v2 enrollment service\n\nThe v2 enrollment service carried an old copy-paste of the v1 API, which\nin turn contained enterprise-specific code which handled an\n\"linked_enterprise_customer\" request argument. The code path that\npopulated that request arg is Enterprise Coupon fulfillment which was\n*sunset in September 2025*, so the branch is completely dead.\n\nDelete the branch rather than maintaining it; no filter call or other\nhook should replace it.\n\nENT-12366","tree":{"sha":"1a6ac79aa7c50286b43940a371442f4f1e7cc512","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/trees/1a6ac79aa7c50286b43940a371442f4f1e7cc512"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/commits/a3a40072782480d17c5fe3535fa1b4252ed38395","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pwnage101","id":85151,"login":"pwnage101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pwnage101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/a3a40072782480d17c5fe3535fa1b4252ed38395","node_id":"C_kwDOAJ6OIdoAKGEzYTQwMDcyNzgyNDgwZDE3YzVmZTM1MzVmYTFiNDI1MmVkMzgzOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/ecb9f5ef4b599051cd6c817f8042c4769cd89b8c","sha":"ecb9f5ef4b599051cd6c817f8042c4769cd89b8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/ecb9f5ef4b599051cd6c817f8042c4769cd89b8c"}],"sha":"a3a40072782480d17c5fe3535fa1b4252ed38395","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/a3a40072782480d17c5fe3535fa1b4252ed38395"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/318677094?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alezconsultant","id":318677094,"login":"alezconsultant","node_id":"U_kgDOEv6gZg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alezconsultant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/ecb9f5ef4b599051cd6c817f8042c4769cd89b8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:06:37Z","email":"alezhneu_consultant@unicon.net","name":"alezconsultant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T04:08:52Z","email":"dave@axim.org","name":"David Ormsbee"},"message":"feat: make can_tag_object''s course check authorization-service aware\n\ncan_change_object_tag_objectid in content_tagging/rules.py -- the predicate every direct\nhas_perm(''oel_tagging.can_tag_object'', ...) caller resolves through -- already checked the\nnew openedx-authz service for Content Library objects, but for course objects it only ever\nchecked the legacy has_studio_write_access role, regardless of whether that course had been\nswitched to the new authorization service. ObjectTagOrgView (Studio''s own tag-editing\nendpoint) already had the correct, toggle-aware behavior, but only inside that one view\nclass, so every other caller (including the CBE create-criterion endpoint, openedx-core#665)\nsilently got the wrong, legacy-only answer for switched-over courses.\n\nAdd a branch to can_change_object_tag_objectid, checked after the Content Library case and\nbefore the legacy fallback: when should_use_course_authz_for_object says the course has been\nswitched, return authz_api.is_user_allowed directly, with no\nfallback to legacy roles or org-admin access -- an exclusive switch, matching\nObjectTagOrgView''s existing behavior exactly.\n\nDelete ObjectTagOrgView.ensure_user_has_can_tag_object_permissions: the parent\nObjectTagView''s own version (openedx-core) already resolves through\nhas_perm(oel_tagging.can_tag_object, ...), so this override had become pure duplication of\nlogic that now lives in rules.py. get_permissions and _authz_check stay, since\nensure_has_view_object_tag_permission (the separate, untouched view permission) and\nObjectTagTaxonomyOrgFilterBackend.filter_queryset both still read them directly.\n\nRelated to openedx/openedx-core#795\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"377101ffe2c6fb4eef57194f5253b84b88490de7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/trees/377101ffe2c6fb4eef57194f5253b84b88490de7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/commits/ecb9f5ef4b599051cd6c817f8042c4769cd89b8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41625?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ormsbee","id":41625,"login":"ormsbee","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNjI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ormsbee/repos","si