dbd74c5be0854a6fdaebb3bf00d7"}],"sha":"aac2655cbd5aa73fe640eab0e9a73785276f636c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/aac2655cbd5aa73fe640eab0e9a73785276f636c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139064778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft","id":139064778,"login":"Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft","node_id":"U_kgDOCEn1yg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/1ea88e5a3144081c9b12db3f24011a318a9927c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:37:12Z","email":"139064778+Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:37:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: adopt edx-drf-extensions 10.8.0 building blocks across 6 standardized APIs (#39081)\n\n* feat: adopt the edx-drf-extensions 10.8.0 REST API building blocks\n\nBump edx-drf-extensions to 10.8.0, which now ships the reusable core of\nthe FC-0118 REST API conventions (standardized error envelope, response\nshaping, manual pagination, opaque-key lookup regexes, envelope test\nhelper).\n\nopenedx/core/lib/api/exceptions.py and the StandardizedErrorMixin in\nmixins.py become re-exports of the library implementation, keeping the\n182 existing openedx.core.lib.api import paths working. The library\nhandler delegates to a configurable base handler, so\nEDX_DRF_EXTENSIONS[''STANDARDIZED_ERROR_BASE_HANDLER''] is pointed at\nignored_error_exception_handler to preserve the platform''s ignored-error\nlogging and monitoring unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Enrollments v2 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin and Conflict from the library, apply the\nADR 0036 ?view=minimal preset through MinimalViewMixin (the enrollment\npreset overrides to_minimal_representation, since collapsing the embedded\ncourse_details sub-object to a course_id string is not a plain field\nprojection), and paginate the list action through\nIterablePaginationMixin.paginate_iterable instead of the hand-written\npaginate/serialize/respond sequence. Response shapes are unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Xblock v1 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library, take the router\nlookup_value_regex from the shared USAGE_KEY_LOOKUP_REGEX constant\n(identical pattern), and filter the ?view=minimal payload with the shared\nproject() helper. Response shapes are unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Course Details v3 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library, take the router\nlookup_value_regex from the shared COURSE_KEY_LOOKUP_REGEX constant,\nserve the ADR 0036 ?view=minimal preset through MinimalViewMixin with\nminimal_fields (replacing the local _apply_view_preset helper), and apply\n?fields= selection with the shared project() helper. Response shapes are\nunchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Grading v3 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library and take the router\nlookup_value_regex from the shared COURSE_KEY_LOOKUP_REGEX constant.\nResponse shapes are unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Home v3 and v4 APIs\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library and apply ?fields=\nselection with the shared project() helper. With its last caller\nmigrated, the local apply_field_selection helper is removed from the v3\nutils module. Response shapes are unchanged.\n\n* fix: declare the api shim re-exports via __all__ to satisfy ruff","tree":{"sha":"1e6f573ab93d084fd9ef00a78848de90e1bddcbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/trees/1e6f573ab93d084fd9ef00a78848de90e1bddcbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/commits/1ea88e5a3144081c9b12db3f24011a318a9927c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e6f573ab93d084fd9ef00a78848de90e1bddcbf\nparent 8f802e8ffdfc2e69de12b201d0e65ed2cbaee798\nauthor Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft <139064778+Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft@users.noreply.github.com> 1788961032 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788961032 +0500\n\nfeat: adopt edx-drf-extensions 10.8.0 building blocks across 6 standardized APIs (#39081)\n\n* feat: adopt the edx-drf-extensions 10.8.0 REST API building blocks\n\nBump edx-drf-extensions to 10.8.0, which now ships the reusable core of\nthe FC-0118 REST API conventions (standardized error envelope, response\nshaping, manual pagination, opaque-key lookup regexes, envelope test\nhelper).\n\nopenedx/core/lib/api/exceptions.py and the StandardizedErrorMixin in\nmixins.py become re-exports of the library implementation, keeping the\n182 existing openedx.core.lib.api import paths working. The library\nhandler delegates to a configurable base handler, so\nEDX_DRF_EXTENSIONS[''STANDARDIZED_ERROR_BASE_HANDLER''] is pointed at\nignored_error_exception_handler to preserve the platform''s ignored-error\nlogging and monitoring unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Enrollments v2 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin and Conflict from the library, apply the\nADR 0036 ?view=minimal preset through MinimalViewMixin (the enrollment\npreset overrides to_minimal_representation, since collapsing the embedded\ncourse_details sub-object to a course_id string is not a plain field\nprojection), and paginate the list action through\nIterablePaginationMixin.paginate_iterable instead of the hand-written\npaginate/serialize/respond sequence. Response shapes are unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Xblock v1 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library, take the router\nlookup_value_regex from the shared USAGE_KEY_LOOKUP_REGEX constant\n(identical pattern), and filter the ?view=minimal payload with the shared\nproject() helper. Response shapes are unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Course Details v3 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library, take the router\nlookup_value_regex from the shared COURSE_KEY_LOOKUP_REGEX constant,\nserve the ADR 0036 ?view=minimal preset through MinimalViewMixin with\nminimal_fields (replacing the local _apply_view_preset helper), and apply\n?fields= selection with the shared project() helper. Response shapes are\nunchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Grading v3 API\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library and take the router\nlookup_value_regex from the shared COURSE_KEY_LOOKUP_REGEX constant.\nResponse shapes are unchanged.\n\n* feat: use edx-drf-extensions building blocks in Home v3 and v4 APIs\n\nImport StandardizedErrorMixin from the library and apply ?fields=\nselection with the shared project() helper. With its last caller\nmigrated, the local apply_field_selection helper is removed from the v3\nutils module. Response shapes are unchanged.\n\n* fix: declare the api shim re-exports via __all__ to satisfy ruff","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoWEICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJPIQAHDfRo9Ms+vzgDT1iM6jJjs