\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmBdVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoxQQABTZzIxphKoqvFl50yYoMYu1\n5iOQvMAhvgFUMdV5STqkwf/S9mcgas7EULwMX4BLYwyFYnoyxWDeN32vYS9k7VFH\n9BTF8PQ9R5s1Uzj4G54dsZIbdsMbZNgUDCEvI05ghVTO72mLNVbqNMHyewbbELKK\nczJPBWongJPhzkwJTLfEuCPpf1lj6FIgPMXKYWijljcL3su3iT7AbqWkE3VCjxIp\n7E8rKzRZ8Yo1HwNW570PWNfSDV9hFMDymZU0nLRAt7SY+Ha73XZ6CQY5nM/dV6G1\nsXrJKPf/mhk0rzq2GEYY0cAa4nJL/bq0XJWt+OeibebFHFCamJgPKHNx2TJ6hSu+\n0d7w80sFbjMnGclNa5ljfVyP4n0EYhrfEAerMRTyqhgOMfWOZH/FIfgEy8dE2186\ncTLUrc6PmyZB70nJQAuoIqAmxoY+xLVf4NpyVlDaNK5QgelpsWNLnbJjnGypF9xq\n05E1HRdbxlpYKF02nvBHK57FYK7lMhhPo73sAla/45PbEZRNHbBKG4maZg7c26xj\nWAXHhqpFBW2FyFz10pEAElmOZ5mCWHs6e1tjXNM1AzFfaQxp/jgp4cztOYKcN0rx\nNWjDsm2cqKxzCcTiHZDMnoTiSa0ifv4SdYneeEQUuyuIAoUlrsZ+N9AzAu0k3Ia8\n0RpjQJvKddMN2iXniyYJ\n=5e8a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:32:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/affa96ab415d2c4c419328cd3642c8a20af32de3","node_id":"C_kwDOAJ6OIdoAKGFmZmE5NmFiNDE1ZDJjNGM0MTkzMjhjZDM2NDJjOGEyMGFmMzJkZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02","sha":"ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/486a492fac50e7053902ca8cdd4d61e3d4211015","sha":"486a492fac50e7053902ca8cdd4d61e3d4211015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/486a492fac50e7053902ca8cdd4d61e3d4211015"}],"sha":"affa96ab415d2c4c419328cd3642c8a20af32de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/affa96ab415d2c4c419328cd3642c8a20af32de3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26253150?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhtishamShahid","id":26253150,"login":"AhtishamShahid","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MjUzMTUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhtishamShahid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:24:59Z","email":"ahtisham300@gmail.com","name":"Ahtisham Shahid"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:24:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: recover from orphaned Mongo course index on course creation (#39024)\n\n* fix: recover from orphaned Mongo course index on course creation\n\nThe split modulestore course index is read from MySQL but written to both\nMySQL and Mongo''s active_versions. Mongo writes are not covered by\nATOMIC_REQUESTS, so if a request creates a course and then fails, the MySQL\nrow is rolled back while the Mongo doc survives.\n\nThat course key is then permanently unusable: has_course() reads MySQL and\nreports the course as absent, so creation is retried, and the follower write\nto Mongo raises DuplicateKeyError against UNIQUE(org, course, run). Every\nretry fails identically, and the rollback leaves no MySQL trace of why.\n\nClear any stale Mongo doc before the follower write. This is safe because it\nruns after new_index.save() has succeeded, which means no MySQL row existed\nfor the key, which means any Mongo doc for it is stale.\n\n* fix: only clean up the stale Mongo doc when the insert conflicts\n\nDeleting unconditionally added a Mongo round-trip to every course and library\ncreation, which broke check_mongo_calls in\nTestLibraries::test_create_library (expected 3 calls, 4 were made).\n\nInsert first and clean up only on DuplicateKeyError, so the happy path keeps\nits original call count and the extra work happens only in the rare case\nwhere a stale doc is actually present.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Peter Pinch <pdpinch@mit.edu>","tree":{"sha":"e1e91e96d20356a0d2d7e987240a46508b31cef5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/trees/e1e91e96d20356a0d2d7e987240a46508b31cef5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/commits/ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02","verification":{"payload":"tree e1e91e96d20356a0d2d7e987240a46508b31cef5\nparent 66a40ef1c393d0420345762f24bfb3680cf15c62\nauthor Ahtisham Shahid <ahtisham300@gmail.com> 1788348299 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788348299 +0500\n\nfix: recover from orphaned Mongo course index on course creation (#39024)\n\n* fix: recover from orphaned Mongo course index on course creation\n\nThe split modulestore course index is read from MySQL but written to both\nMySQL and Mongo''s active_versions. Mongo writes are not covered by\nATOMIC_REQUESTS, so if a request creates a course and then fails, the MySQL\nrow is rolled back while the Mongo doc survives.\n\nThat course key is then permanently unusable: has_course() reads MySQL and\nreports the course as absent, so creation is retried, and the follower write\nto Mongo raises DuplicateKeyError against UNIQUE(org, course, run). Every\nretry fails identically, and the rollback leaves no MySQL trace of why.\n\nClear any stale Mongo doc before the follower write. This is safe because it\nruns after new_index.save() has succeeded, which means no MySQL row existed\nfor the key, which means any Mongo doc for it is stale.\n\n* fix: only clean up the stale Mongo doc when the insert conflicts\n\nDeleting unconditionally added a Mongo round-trip to every course and library\ncreation, which broke check_mongo_calls in\nTestLibraries::test_create_library (expected 3 calls, 4 were made).\n\nInsert first and clean up only on DuplicateKeyError, so the happy path keeps\nits original call count and the extra work happens only in the rare case\nwhere a stale doc is actually present.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Peter Pinch <pdpinch@mit.edu>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmAeLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3mYQAGX1E6YcPl3GXw/+hyyht0yi\nvKKIighNqO8uCk2GhDMJA07KR+wbhJ15Hp9el8iP/OEpVwDozKKxqSfqNCr12wR3\n2mF+szKAT8RddVyOAh2J+WmSNQWhS1VPfDhuC92PPmN/x1aNHHECCbFGXF47ALvo\n2woeicg6e0iaCY7BbbhUXkCLNODRAg0KIr9SNmCv9z3R87pcRKnl0Qdj61r1r+CN\nXPWIbtDcOYvRG6noRmQ5ruMXcFZzMprZLCKwn8b753RQJmT0VKcQN2YKrdI1HzIh\n8tyVakFTy6hwRiXnPF8uDkgCwvdxeh3yTs8A0nAdo1FMzjNHWNyEYhFK8gXO38GF\n7VD4kxq0yYhrEYng7iA2PdcnngGtsJ2SOAFJzIqeet3ERYXvch/JfD7E+GevzYHZ\n02WhZ3GJI3MuOL6NIz2XeJ812dZnskAJEQiyp4kKlnlMmE6d49PQaj8cx11/SAct\n61akmiRSsVkPQhZ2+IGRo8mqCP0dot66haRUIHEhX0GS6K9Rm8i+4sD0lQaiDc+q\nb6evrHtv2hVj3wkGPqPvSzuPBrT1J9YQdz9rwFqVMVd719363Hqe5JWqiEPGYhuo\nH0c/iQXjPhwhgnWcoqV6Z1o+AGOYKCxrOfPcWGmsveJnC5zLO2rhmrzk9Kga8PbS\nVpPgKP/OpCEiatlE3qTW\n=ABZy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:25:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02","node_id":"C_kwDOAJ6OIdoAKGFjZTM5ZThiNzBkMWQxZGM4ODE2MzYwYTI1NTZlNzlmZDg3M2ZlMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/openedx-platform/commit/66a40ef1c393d0420345762f24bfb3680cf15c62","sha":"66a40ef1c393d0420345762f24bfb3680cf15c62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/66a40ef1c393d0420345762f24bfb3680cf15c62"}],"sha":"ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/ace39e8b70d1d1dc8816360a2556e79fd873fe02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139064778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft","id":139064778,"login":"Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft","node_id":"U_kgDOCEn1yg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/commits/66a40ef1c393d0420345762f24bfb3680cf15c62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:24:36Z","email":"139064778+Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:24:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add ADR for standardizing REST API URL structure (#39003)\n\n* docs: add ADR for standardizing REST API URL structure\n\nOpen edX REST URLs follow no consistent pattern. The /api/ prefix, the position\nof the version, pluralisation, word separators, and trailing slashes all vary,\nin places between adjacent lines of a single URLconf. The FC-0118 ADRs\n(0025-0037) standardize what happens inside an endpoint but never its address.\n\nAdd docs/decisions/0038-standardize-rest-api-url-structure.rst as an accepted\nADR defining twelve rules: a leading /api/ prefix, singular API names with\nplural collections, domain-based rather than app-based naming, lowercase\nsnake_case segments, mounts that declare their own prefix, exact-match routes\nwith a required trailing slash, version position and form, hierarchy capped at\none level of nesting, opaque-key identifiers resolved by shared path\nconverters, verb-free resource paths, snake_case Django URL names, and a single\nURL namespace shared by the LMS and Studio. Existing endpoints migrate under\nOEP-21 with the conforming path mounted alongside the legacy one.\n\nThis restates the still-applicable rules from the Open edX REST API Conventions\nwiki that OEP-49 defers to, settles what that page left as TBD, and adds a CI\nconformance check so the convention is enforced rather than remembered.\n\nFindings recorded in the ADR:\n\n- /api/courses/ is mounted in both services on unrelated implementations, both\n  at v1, which blocks the endpoint-by-endpoint combined headless LMS+CMS\n  migration.\n- /api/enrollment/v1/enrollment and /api/enrollment/v1/enrollments/ are\n  different views, so pluralisation is load-bearing today.\n- Deprecated Org/Course/Run course keys contain slashes, so nesting one\n  mid-path requires a shared path converter; the platform has three, in two\n  apps, none reusable.\n- Django resolves re_path with re.search, so unanchored patterns in\n  course_experience and learner_home match under arbitrary prefixes.\n\n* docs: address review feedback on the URL structure ADR\n\nFour review comments on PR #39003:\n\n- Fix the RST formatting in rule 11. RST does not nest inline markup, so\n  **``snake_case``**, ... rendered with visible asterisks and backticks. Rule 11\n  now keeps the literal outside the bold lead-in. The same construct in the\n  kebab-case rejected-alternative bullet is fixed the same way.\n\n- Stop requiring slash-tolerant course keys. openedx-platform#31134 removed Old\n  Mongo create and update operations, leaving only read-only access to static\n  assets and the root CourseBlock, so no new deprecated-key course can be\n  authored. New and migrated APIs now accept non-deprecated keys only, which\n  covers course-v1: and ccx-v1: and refuses Org/Course/Run. The converter regex\n  becomes a plain \"no slash\" match with the check made on course_key.deprecated,\n  and mid-path nesting is unambiguous as a result. The now-invalid \"breaks on\n  keys containing /\" clause is dropped from the deep-nesting rejected\n  alternative. Only endpoints still serving pre-existing Old Mongo courses need\n  the slash-tolerant pattern.\n\n- Record that content_staging, olx_rest_api, content_libraries, and\n  lms.djangoapps.instructor are core apps rather than optional extensions. All\n  four are absent from the static INSTALLED_APPS lists and arrive through\n  get_plugin_apps(), so the ADR recommends moving them into INSTALLED_APPS and\n  mounting them explicitly under their own prefix, which is what rule 5 asks of\n  any API. The conformance check still walks the composed resolver, because\n  third-party plugins will always contribute routes the project URLconfs cannot\n  show.\n\n- Answer where the path converters belong: they are generic and need only\n  edx-opaque-keys, so they go in edx-drf-extensions alongside the pagination and\n  JWT classes, with openedx/core/lib shown as the interim home.\n\n* docs: point ADR 0038 at the shipped edx-drf-extensions converters\n\nThe shared opaque-key path converters now live in edx-drf-extensions\n(edx_rest_framework_extensions/url_converters.py, registered via\nregister_url_converters()), so drop the paragraph deferring that\nextraction and update the code example and Implementation Notes to\nreference the library instead of the interim openedx/core/lib/ path.","tree":{"sha":"c5877da58bb54658fa3faf26de49c49cbbd656dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/trees/c5877da58bb54658fa3faf26de49c49cbbd656dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/openedx-platform/git/commits/66a40ef1c393d0420345762f24bfb3680cf15c62","verification":{"payload":"tree c5877da58bb54658fa3faf26de49c49cbbd656dd\nparent cbcf91b0c706f5eaf8a48987af201f094b2e6e6a\nauthor Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft <139064778+Abdul-Muqadim-Arbisoft@users.noreply.github.com> 1788344676 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788344676 +0500\n\ndocs: add ADR for standardizing REST API URL structure (#39003)\n\n* docs: add ADR for standardizing REST API URL structure\n\nOpen edX REST URLs follow no consistent pattern. The /api/ prefix, the position\nof the version, pluralisation, word separators, and trailing slashes all vary,\nin places between adjacent lines of a single URLconf. The FC-0118 ADRs\n(0025-0037) standardize what happens inside an endpoint but never its address.\n\nAdd docs/decisions/0038-standardize-rest-api-url-structure.rst as an accepted\nADR defining twelve rules: a leading /api/ prefix, singular API names with\nplural collections, domain-based rather than app-based naming, lowercase\nsnake_case segments, mounts that declare their own prefix, exact-match routes\nwith a required trailing slash, version position and form, hierarchy capped at\none level of nesting, opaque-key identifiers resolved by shared path\nconverters, verb-free resource paths, snake_case Django URL names, and a single\nURL namespace shared by the LMS and Studio. Existing endpoints migrate under\nOEP-21 with the conforming path mounted alongside the legacy one.\n\nThis restates the still-applicable rules from the Open edX REST API Conventions\nwiki that OEP-49 defers to, settles what that page left as TBD, and adds a CI\nconformance check so the convention is enforced rather than remembered.\n\nFindings recorded in the ADR:\n\n- /api/courses/ is mounted in both services on unrelated implementations, both\n  at v1, which blocks the endpoint-by-endpoint combined headless LMS+CMS\n  migration.\n- /api/enrollment/v1/enrollment and /api/enrollment/v1/enrollments/ are\n  different views, so pluralisation is load-bearing today.\n- Deprecated Org/Course/Run course keys contain slashes, so nesting one\n  mid-path requires a shared path converter; the platform has three, in two\n  apps, none reusable.\n- Django resolves re_path with re.search, so unanchored patterns in\n  course_experience and learner_home match under arbitrary prefixes.\n\n* docs: address review feedback on the URL structure ADR\n\nFour review comments on PR #39003:\n\n- Fix the RST formatting in rule 11. RST does not nest inline markup, so\n  **``snake_case``**, ... rendered with visible asterisks and backticks. Rule 11\n  now keeps the literal outside the bold lead-in. The same construct in the\n  kebab-case rejected-alternative bullet is fixed the same way.\n\n- Stop requiring slash-tolerant course keys. openedx-platform#31134 removed Old\n  Mongo create and update operations, leaving only read-only access to static\n  assets and the root CourseBlock, so no new deprecated-key course can be\n  authored. New and migrated APIs now accept non-deprecated keys only, which\n  covers course-v1: and ccx-v1: and refuses Org/Course/Run. The converter regex\n  becomes a plain \"no slash\" match with the check made on course_key.deprecated,\n  and mid-path nesting is unambiguous as a result. The now-invalid \"breaks on\n  keys containing /\" clause is dropped from the deep-nesting rejected\n  alternative. Only endpoints still serving pre-existing Old Mongo courses need\n  the slash-tolerant pattern.\n\n- Record that content_staging, olx_rest_api, content_libraries, and\n  lms.djangoapps.instructor are core apps rather than optional extensions. All\n  four are absent from the static INSTALLED_APPS lists and arrive through\n  get_plugin_apps(), so the ADR recommends moving them into INSTALLED_APPS and\n  mounting them explicitly under their own prefix, which is what rule 5 asks of\n  any API. The conformance check still walks the composed resolver, because\n  third-party plugins will always contribute routes the project URLconfs cannot\n  show.\n\n- Answer where the path converters belong: they are generic and need only\n  edx-opaque-keys, so they go in edx-drf-extensions alongside the pagination and\n  JWT classes, with openedx/core/lib shown as the interim home.\n\n* docs: point ADR 0038 at the shipped edx-drf-extensions converters\n\nThe shared opaque-key path converters now live in edx-drf-extensions\n(edx_rest_framework_extensions/url_converters.py, registered via\nregister_url_converters()), so drop the paragraph deferring that\nextraction and update the code example and Implementation Notes to\nreference the library instead of the interim openedx/core/lib/ path.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql/lkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2RMQADJoCIfFeCro8HsYotMIskcK\n2P0BCIyjhLjHvC3sMfsjqyR+y124CzH3E9MLp8OOAGedgsevMwGGgLAylXnNiCLy\nIfacjr/IbvQbv5mtNTqT7zxfArsQ5fLkxgxmqt/DF1IadgW6mXwQNpOEAYmcYKI+\nHXC8LgyhZaEjlnx0YBvQYdrTCWGcM8KfxP2EUZeTomSswbgOCpR9lh3wnakOggb2\n+qzPHg1sKg1Lk1mm0XulNwMJtVqgWBg7QqUSZmGu1+U3T+fjjgsqntPqTZJHuE+M\nM4VYwrqmAKmNPa9TRyhAEpVaCieJpHFn+EyBNodPz4lGS05r7kLFKooeQUZSQp7X\n7rbLA1StL4I1bSr7Gl5XIHIIuSvBZmaqYG2aSB6e+wcHL5nf0m/enQCaSlo5dn3K\n5XJZlM3/pBFR8LZGUaa4Da4moVCnrbDRgXPmEaMMP9ql/+KDPdLhorOi1+GCA58n\nVCUBu5WZjcgZ7Gd3mTvUEfXUoazrYyw4jYceyNc+hFCr4UOVUSAgx4W833luNoZp\nfXnmTMTpAIHpSTVTq+0gGE8azVQcaSyZn9DDLB11N6CK9no3vFROec5mWnql1ZGg\nmU/O5oIU1RwP9yJmw7qaxaOHZtVt9AirprS4+Hs0jzDa5fHPRnVwkw+YigtndO6t\nuna8EBFPt7b4ddPJ1HEu\n=1pdd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T10:24:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/