Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/faba2b25da6177fc73700880c4038897369884ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:58:29Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:58:29Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Unwrap global CLAUDE.md and add a no-hard-wrap rule for Markdown\n\nHard-wrapped Markdown makes every edit reflow neighboring lines, burying\nthe real change in the diff, and the breaks come along when the text is\npasted elsewhere. Add the rule, and reflow this file to one line per\nparagraph or list item so it follows its own advice.\n\nReflowed with prettier --prose-wrap never; its _why_ emphasis was put\nback to *why* to match the remark-lint emphasis-marker setting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"181dd551d43487f1b77a8367295c60abaa6d2137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/181dd551d43487f1b77a8367295c60abaa6d2137"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/faba2b25da6177fc73700880c4038897369884ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 181dd551d43487f1b77a8367295c60abaa6d2137\nparent 0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791050309 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791050309 -0400\n\nUnwrap global CLAUDE.md and add a no-hard-wrap rule for Markdown\n\nHard-wrapped Markdown makes every edit reflow neighboring lines, burying\nthe real change in the diff, and the breaks come along when the text is\npasted elsewhere. Add the rule, and reflow this file to one line per\nparagraph or list item so it follows its own advice.\n\nReflowed with prettier --prose-wrap never; its _why_ emphasis was put\nback to *why* to match the remark-lint emphasis-marker setting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQP/dQ+M4r+NryMVhhIoMhigokfi280C4Y14xFXm5O3O8NTi2tKDoH8yjNXNCghvLuj\nMiuQWmIIOB2t/M3/Y74wA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T18:01:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/faba2b25da6177fc73700880c4038897369884ad","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGZhYmEyYjI1ZGE2MTc3ZmM3MzcwMDg4MGM0MDM4ODk3MzY5ODg0YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de","sha":"0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de"}],"sha":"faba2b25da6177fc73700880c4038897369884ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/faba2b25da6177fc73700880c4038897369884ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:45:59Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:45:59Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Point npm() at the existing npmjs 1Password item\n\nThe token lives in the \"Npmjs\" login item, not a new \"npm token\" item.\nReferenced by item ID because two items share that title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e3be2b1bc4bb6bfe39c4ab6e0cfb8229dea956d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/0e3be2b1bc4bb6bfe39c4ab6e0cfb8229dea956d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e3be2b1bc4bb6bfe39c4ab6e0cfb8229dea956d\nparent 75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791049559 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791049559 -0400\n\nPoint npm() at the existing npmjs 1Password item\n\nThe token lives in the \"Npmjs\" login item, not a new \"npm token\" item.\nReferenced by item ID because two items share that title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLfBQVv/saqITNoWFfcGnvHWf9fqt+Dl9ncTELRAhVCjh+JW6M9lhgXcWGOUYjDx8k\nrOzwKgNv4qntwHvNaBAAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:48:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDBmY2E0YjhhZThmZDg2YTUwNDc4NzM0MTM4ZDc5YTI0MTUwZDA3ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2","sha":"75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2"}],"sha":"0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/0fca4b8ae8fd86a50478734138d79a24150d07de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:44:29Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:44:29Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Promote repeated corrections into global Claude rules\n\nI kept retyping the same instructions across projects: \"fix all\" after\nClaude listed fixes it could have made, asking what a compressed line\nmeant, requesting a blind review, re-asking for clipboard copies and\ncompose links, and pulling main by hand after merges. Several repo\nCLAUDE.md files also independently grew the same rules (one source of\ntruth, run checks before committing, don''t upgrade unverified claims).\nMoving them into the global file means every project gets them.\n\nAlso note that tags are signed (so `git tag` needs -m), add a \"gb\"\nshorthand matching the shell alias, and add calendar links alongside\nGmail compose links.\n\nlib/aliases: drop oh-my-zsh''s interactive rm/cp/mv aliases under Claude\nCode. Its shell inherits them with no TTY to answer the prompt, so\ncommands hung until it fell back to `command rm`. My own shell keeps\nthe safety net.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e9e8df88ac7006066e65d99263171a69f049466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/3e9e8df88ac7006066e65d99263171a69f049466"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e9e8df88ac7006066e65d99263171a69f049466\nparent a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791049469 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791049469 -0400\n\nPromote repeated corrections into global Claude rules\n\nI kept retyping the same instructions across projects: \"fix all\" after\nClaude listed fixes it could have made, asking what a compressed line\nmeant, requesting a blind review, re-asking for clipboard copies and\ncompose links, and pulling main by hand after merges. Several repo\nCLAUDE.md files also independently grew the same rules (one source of\ntruth, run checks before committing, don''t upgrade unverified claims).\nMoving them into the global file means every project gets them.\n\nAlso note that tags are signed (so `git tag` needs -m), add a \"gb\"\nshorthand matching the shell alias, and add calendar links alongside\nGmail compose links.\n\nlib/aliases: drop oh-my-zsh''s interactive rm/cp/mv aliases under Claude\nCode. Its shell inherits them with no TTY to answer the prompt, so\ncommands hung until it fell back to `command rm`. My own shell keeps\nthe safety net.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIU+Mot0ACH19lrzlj9Dzz+UuT1+A+nKSrsfoffwXSK8Vf5LI+lj9sLX/+/Grk6nnI\nj2oA9bzdrTYeNBKVt3sQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:48:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDc1ZjNkZThkZTJlYWNiYWNjOWVjMTMxYTJjZjU2OGVkOTlkYWNjYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4","sha":"a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4"}],"sha":"75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/75f3de8de2eacbacc9ec131a2cf568ed99daccc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:43:10Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:43:10Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Read the npm token from 1Password, not the repo\n\n~/.npmrc links into this public repo, so `npm login` wrote a live\nregistry token into a tracked file, one `git add` away from being\npublished. .npmrc now expands ${NPM_TOKEN?} (the `?` sends no auth when\nit''s unset, where a bare ${NPM_TOKEN} sends the literal string and\ngets a 401). An npm() wrapper fills it from 1Password only for commands\nthat need auth, so installs don''t prompt for Touch ID. A config test\nfails on any literal credential in .npmrc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe746914288805952a5fe8db0675ae3c17ec5bb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/fe746914288805952a5fe8db0675ae3c17ec5bb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4","verification":{"payload":"tree fe746914288805952a5fe8db0675ae3c17ec5bb2\nparent 4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791049390 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791049390 -0400\n\nRead the npm token from 1Password, not the repo\n\n~/.npmrc links into this public repo, so `npm login` wrote a live\nregistry token into a tracked file, one `git add` away from being\npublished. .npmrc now expands ${NPM_TOKEN?} (the `?` sends no auth when\nit''s unset, where a bare ${NPM_TOKEN} sends the literal string and\ngets a 401). An npm() wrapper fills it from 1Password only for commands\nthat need auth, so installs don''t prompt for Touch ID. A config test\nfails on any literal credential in .npmrc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNzmmVfzkfolrCDnMn+OLj5dVYI3Q6SnF0+Lb9ixR1iYkDADbCXmu0V4AhLaDPb3ck\nqJ+mig6w1A/rL0vj2T+AE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:48:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGE2Nzg1ODhiYzNmYmM0ZTk1NTRiYjQ2Mzg2YTcyNjljZjRjOTZmYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b","sha":"4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b"}],"sha":"a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a678588bc3fbc4e9554bb46386a7269cf4c96fc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:30:02Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:30:02Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Keep desktop icons sorted by name\n\nThe desktop''s Finder \"Sort By\" setting wasn''t managed, so a new machine\nstarted with loose, unsorted icons. It sits in a nested dict\n(DesktopViewSettings:IconViewSettings:arrangeBy) that osx_defaults can\nonly replace whole, which would also reset icon size and spacing. So the\ntask round-trips the domain through `defaults export`/`import` and sets\nthe one key with PlistBuddy. Editing the plist on disk would be\noverwritten by cfprefsd''s cached copy.\n\nCloses #23\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b021800786d2f8e27b86320b2089d78e4904101","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/5b021800786d2f8e27b86320b2089d78e4904101"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b021800786d2f8e27b86320b2089d78e4904101\nparent b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791048602 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791048602 -0400\n\nKeep desktop icons sorted by name\n\nThe desktop''s Finder \"Sort By\" setting wasn''t managed, so a new machine\nstarted with loose, unsorted icons. It sits in a nested dict\n(DesktopViewSettings:IconViewSettings:arrangeBy) that osx_defaults can\nonly replace whole, which would also reset icon size and spacing. So the\ntask round-trips the domain through `defaults export`/`import` and sets\nthe one key with PlistBuddy. Editing the plist on disk would be\noverwritten by cfprefsd''s cached copy.\n\nCloses #23\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJIEAAtYC1cDTs8hMXRmKBGJfiQiN6D4s4SRECqeZeOgwiQLGsfZ/gYNnHJCkI1ag+\ng+PJZS590jtXE+sfnVawo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:48:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDQ1NzdmZDVhZWVmMGJmY2Y5NDUwNGEyMmNkZmJmYzUwMmQ5Yjc1NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4","sha":"b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4"}],"sha":"4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/4577fd5aeef0bfcf94504a22cdfbfc502d9b755b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:29:16Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:29:16Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Run `up` at the end of script/setup\n\nThe playbook installs packages but not the rest of what `up` does (mas\nupgrade, npm ci, bundle, pip, oh-my-zsh, tldr), so a new machine waited\nfor the first nightly run to get them.\n\nCloses #73\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a875c06deba0c88f3f6e4d759b4efe3059eeba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/9a875c06deba0c88f3f6e4d759b4efe3059eeba4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a875c06deba0c88f3f6e4d759b4efe3059eeba4\nparent a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791048556 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791048556 -0400\n\nRun `up` at the end of script/setup\n\nThe playbook installs packages but not the rest of what `up` does (mas\nupgrade, npm ci, bundle, pip, oh-my-zsh, tldr), so a new machine waited\nfor the first nightly run to get them.\n\nCloses #73\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLgdLGf4lHbTMlevCYzqrV2xnXBkjhpfP8LXkhiypjmKWncivpfyAFm873eKKdUDkB\n9Kg+s6E2b8FwZgNjyhbAI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:48:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGI1YWFkMTkyY2M0MzcwN2FhZjNkZWExOGFkMzNjZTJhZDZmMzkxYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732","sha":"a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732"}],"sha":"b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/b5aad192cc43707aaf3dea18ad33ce2ad6f391c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:59:15Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:59:15Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Close test gaps in audit-casks and update\n\naudit-casks'' \"running now\" check matched the bundle path anywhere in a\nprocess path, so ~/Applications/Foo.app running would count as\n/Applications/Foo.app in use. Anchor it at the start, and test that and\nthe sibling-name case (\"Foo Pro.app\").\n\nAlso cover what earlier tests missed: report-mode labels, steam being kept\nby default, and AUDIT_KEEP leaking in from the caller''s shell. update''s\ntests only ever ran headless, because `run` captures stdout, so the\n`brew upgrade` a manual `up` actually runs (and the no-ask fix for it)\nwas untested. Run it under a pty to cover the terminal-only steps.\n\nThe second test that extends STUBS tripped shellcheck''s SC2030/SC2031,\nwhich script/lint treats as failures; disable them file-wide with why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7aca79d9f9f506c4364cc899f4e5491cd176fad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/7aca79d9f9f506c4364cc899f4e5491cd176fad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732","verification":{"payload":"tree 7aca79d9f9f506c4364cc899f4e5491cd176fad2\nparent 46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046755 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046755 -0400\n\nClose test gaps in audit-casks and update\n\naudit-casks'' \"running now\" check matched the bundle path anywhere in a\nprocess path, so ~/Applications/Foo.app running would count as\n/Applications/Foo.app in use. Anchor it at the start, and test that and\nthe sibling-name case (\"Foo Pro.app\").\n\nAlso cover what earlier tests missed: report-mode labels, steam being kept\nby default, and AUDIT_KEEP leaking in from the caller''s shell. update''s\ntests only ever ran headless, because `run` captures stdout, so the\n`brew upgrade` a manual `up` actually runs (and the no-ask fix for it)\nwas untested. Run it under a pty to cover the terminal-only steps.\n\nThe second test that extends STUBS tripped shellcheck''s SC2030/SC2031,\nwhich script/lint treats as failures; disable them file-wide with why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDu7LmdnZ2iJRysTqCiT4+9rqUzpIoEosO3dObIpC6lQ+Zg1dEoZyl9weexW2OUYNf\n6qrzoC4QL1UFk/DTWSKwI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T16:59:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGE5MzE0ZTk5NWIyNGY5MDdhMWNkOGRiMDA5NDhkNGRjY2E5MDc3MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e","sha":"46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e"}],"sha":"a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a9314e995b24f907a1cd8db00948d4dcca907732"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:57:17Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:57:17Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Stop `up` from pausing at Homebrew''s confirmation prompt\n\nHomebrew made ask mode the default for upgrades and installs, so every\ninteractive `up` stalled at a y/N prompt before `brew upgrade`. The\nscript''s whole job is to apply updates, so set HOMEBREW_NO_ASK for its\nbrew steps. It''s scoped to the script, so manual brew commands still ask.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92b177d2211fe3573f51b3295e395206faedd3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/92b177d2211fe3573f51b3295e395206faedd3b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 92b177d2211fe3573f51b3295e395206faedd3b5\nparent 5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046637 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046637 -0400\n\nStop `up` from pausing at Homebrew''s confirmation prompt\n\nHomebrew made ask mode the default for upgrades and installs, so every\ninteractive `up` stalled at a y/N prompt before `brew upgrade`. The\nscript''s whole job is to apply updates, so set HOMEBREW_NO_ASK for its\nbrew steps. It''s scoped to the script, so manual brew commands still ask.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOVMgeKwGsNSeZ9jt9ueNUoQ+UB9Cy/75yLoBMxLS2ASHkmNwFg+k0ob+t2YewuC7n\nvj9sAmQlBQvVEG3eD5Uwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T16:57:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDQ2MDQ3NDM3YjhjMGNlNjI3MmM5NWY0NzA0MTllZDY2ZTBlMTlhOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217","sha":"5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217"}],"sha":"46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/46047437b8c0ce6272c95f470419ed66e0e19a9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:56:03Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:56:03Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Add \"cpm\" shorthand to global CLAUDE.md\n\nI ask for commit-and-push-to-main often enough that a short alias saves\ntyping, and defining it here means every session understands it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d87a5025f88b7046fd2d1cce6bd1734280e1e9bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/d87a5025f88b7046fd2d1cce6bd1734280e1e9bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217","verification":{"payload":"tree d87a5025f88b7046fd2d1cce6bd1734280e1e9bc\nparent 0f1a02d8ca234b34ed5548bed6f33879439f3035\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046563 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046563 -0400\n\nAdd \"cpm\" shorthand to global CLAUDE.md\n\nI ask for commit-and-push-to-main often enough that a short alias saves\ntyping, and defining it here means every session understands it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPMYkraMs2r3hMJxOz/YFcO6hbw45legC8RhlYMVUZXYWpuNK6qTs2QlOfNn8p+/Zq\nlMMJSAvnU1MUGAiAl1vAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T16:56:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDVmZTVmOGMxNDM1NWJkOGIwZDc3NmM3ZjJkMWRjNmUyZTI5MGYyMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/0f1a02d8ca234b34ed5548bed6f33879439f3035","sha":"0f1a02d8ca234b34ed5548bed6f33879439f3035","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/0f1a02d8ca234b34ed5548bed6f33879439f3035"}],"sha":"5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5fe5f8c14355bd8b0d776c7f2d1dc6e2e290f217"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/0f1a02d8ca234b34ed5548bed6f33879439f3035/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:55:30Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:55:30Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"audit-casks: don''t propose apps that are running or misdated\n\nSpotlight only bumps kMDItemLastUsedDate when an app is launched from\nFinder, the Dock or `open`. OpenLogi runs all day through its login-item\nagent, and Steam''s /Applications bundle is only a bootstrapper for a\nclient in ~/Library/Application Support, so `up` proposed removing both\nwhile they were in regular use.\n\nTreat any app with a process executing from inside its bundle as in use,\nand add an AUDIT_KEEP list (default: steam) for apps whose real binary\nlives elsewhere. The list lives in the script because `brew bundle dump`\nerases inline Brewfile comments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5bccd089c4d30640fae2eef073c28925cad1927f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/5bccd089c4d30640fae2eef073c28925cad1927f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/0f1a02d8ca234b34ed5548bed6f33879439f3035","verification":{"payload":"tree 5bccd089c4d30640fae2eef073c28925cad1927f\nparent a86fdd223bbe90a1d8af7c884d20972dc5a9134d\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046530 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1791046530 -0400\n\naudit-casks: don''t propose apps that are running or misdated\n\nSpotlight only bumps kMDItemLastUsedDate when an app is launched from\nFinder, the Dock or `open`. OpenLogi runs all day through its login-item\nagent, and Steam''s /Applications bundle is only a bootstrapper for a\nclient in ~/Library/Application Support, so `up` proposed removing both\nwhile they were in regular use.\n\nTreat any app with a process executing from inside its bundle as in use,\nand add an AUDIT_KEEP list (default: steam) for apps whose real binary\nlives elsewhere. The list lives in the script because `brew bundle dump`\nerases inline Brewfile comments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgl