dccb971","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGYyNDcyMmQ4NjQzM2ViNDU2YzIzOGM1YjNlNmNhY2IwYmRjY2I5NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20","sha":"5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20"}],"sha":"f24722d86433eb456c238c5b3e6cacb0bdccb971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/f24722d86433eb456c238c5b3e6cacb0bdccb971"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T22:13:42Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T22:14:26Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Skip the Homebrew role under Workbrew instead of fighting its chown\n\nEvery `script/ansible` run left brew unusable:\n\n  Error: /opt/homebrew/Cellar is not writable. You should change the\n  ownership and permissions of /opt/homebrew/Cellar back to your\n  user account: sudo chown -R workbrew /opt/homebrew/Cellar\n\ngeerlingguy.mac.homebrew''s \"Ensure proper ownership on\nhomebrew_install_path subdirs\" chowns homebrew_install_path -- which on\narm64 evaluates to /opt/homebrew itself -- to ansible_facts.user_id:\nuser_gid, recursively, with become, on every run. Workbrew executes brew\nas the `workbrew` user, so handing the prefix to benbalter:staff means\nbrew aborts before doing anything; `brew doctor` listed 26 unwritable\ndirectories. The Workbrew agent repairs only /opt/homebrew and\nbin/brew, never the subdirectories, which is why the prefix was\nworkbrew-owned while everything inside it was not.\n\nIts sibling task \"Ensure proper permissions and ownership on\nhomebrew_brew_bin_path dirs\" chowns that path 0775 to the login user,\nand we point homebrew_brew_bin_path at /opt/workbrew/bin -- the\ndirectory holding the setuid-root brew wrapper. It had been left\nbenbalter:staff drwxrwxr-x; it belongs to root:wheel 0755.\n\nUnder Workbrew the role has nothing else to contribute: brew is already\ninstalled, homebrew_taps / homebrew_installed_packages /\nhomebrew_cask_apps are unset here and default to [],\nhomebrew_upgrade_all_packages is false and homebrew_use_brewfile is\nfalse, so the Brewfile task below does the actual installing. Gate the\nwhole role on the absence of the Workbrew wrapper; CI, which has no\nWorkbrew, is unaffected.\n\nTwo follow-ons:\n\n  * Drop the \"locks dir group-writable\" pre-task. It patched a symptom\n    of the same root cause, and once the prefix is workbrew-owned a\n    chmod as the login user is EPERM.\n  * The LanguageTool copy writes into /opt/homebrew/etc, which is no\n    longer owned by the login user, so it needs become and an explicit\n    owner.\n\nRepairing the machine itself takes `sudo chown -R workbrew\n/opt/homebrew` plus `sudo chown root:wheel /opt/workbrew/bin`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ded022ebf3abf3f3526db5681c7e752c29f86e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/5ded022ebf3abf3f3526db5681c7e752c29f86e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ded022ebf3abf3f3526db5681c7e752c29f86e5\nparent e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789769622 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789769666 -0400\n\nSkip the Homebrew role under Workbrew instead of fighting its chown\n\nEvery `script/ansible` run left brew unusable:\n\n  Error: /opt/homebrew/Cellar is not writable. You should change the\n  ownership and permissions of /opt/homebrew/Cellar back to your\n  user account: sudo chown -R workbrew /opt/homebrew/Cellar\n\ngeerlingguy.mac.homebrew''s \"Ensure proper ownership on\nhomebrew_install_path subdirs\" chowns homebrew_install_path -- which on\narm64 evaluates to /opt/homebrew itself -- to ansible_facts.user_id:\nuser_gid, recursively, with become, on every run. Workbrew executes brew\nas the `workbrew` user, so handing the prefix to benbalter:staff means\nbrew aborts before doing anything; `brew doctor` listed 26 unwritable\ndirectories. The Workbrew agent repairs only /opt/homebrew and\nbin/brew, never the subdirectories, which is why the prefix was\nworkbrew-owned while everything inside it was not.\n\nIts sibling task \"Ensure proper permissions and ownership on\nhomebrew_brew_bin_path dirs\" chowns that path 0775 to the login user,\nand we point homebrew_brew_bin_path at /opt/workbrew/bin -- the\ndirectory holding the setuid-root brew wrapper. It had been left\nbenbalter:staff drwxrwxr-x; it belongs to root:wheel 0755.\n\nUnder Workbrew the role has nothing else to contribute: brew is already\ninstalled, homebrew_taps / homebrew_installed_packages /\nhomebrew_cask_apps are unset here and default to [],\nhomebrew_upgrade_all_packages is false and homebrew_use_brewfile is\nfalse, so the Brewfile task below does the actual installing. Gate the\nwhole role on the absence of the Workbrew wrapper; CI, which has no\nWorkbrew, is unaffected.\n\nTwo follow-ons:\n\n  * Drop the \"locks dir group-writable\" pre-task. It patched a symptom\n    of the same root cause, and once the prefix is workbrew-owned a\n    chmod as the login user is EPERM.\n  * The LanguageTool copy writes into /opt/homebrew/etc, which is no\n    longer owned by the login user, so it needs become and an explicit\n    owner.\n\nRepairing the machine itself takes `sudo chown -R workbrew\n/opt/homebrew` plus `sudo chown root:wheel /opt/workbrew/bin`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBi/il4S8qtZkiZkJ+uSekPjLZB9kYKgIezuNAzia5alw8+ZQnaO5qX/i5dK91XKT2\n8P4mv6znE2FUD8k4aSRw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T22:14:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDU1NDNmYzE5MmZmYjQ0ZWM4MDgxNGJhMzQxYWNhZTYwNDkwZDBjMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234","sha":"e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234"}],"sha":"5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5543fc192ffb44ec80814ba341acae60490d0c20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:48:58Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:48:58Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Rename mise npm shell_out to package_manager\n\nmise 2026.7 renamed the [settings.npm] schema: shell_out is gone and the\ntable now only accepts package_manager (or bun). The stale field made mise\nrefuse to load any config, so every command errored with:\n\n    unknown field `shell_out`, expected `bun` or `package_manager`\n\npackage_manager = \"npm\" is the direct equivalent — install npm tools via\nreal npm instead of mise''s built-in resolver, keeping lifecycle scripts\n(claude-code''s native-binary postinstall) working. No behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5696ce2b0fb0aaceb62e81d07a23204a16e07a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/5696ce2b0fb0aaceb62e81d07a23204a16e07a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234","verification":{"payload":"tree 5696ce2b0fb0aaceb62e81d07a23204a16e07a9e\nparent dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789699738 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789699738 -0400\n\nRename mise npm shell_out to package_manager\n\nmise 2026.7 renamed the [settings.npm] schema: shell_out is gone and the\ntable now only accepts package_manager (or bun). The stale field made mise\nrefuse to load any config, so every command errored with:\n\n    unknown field `shell_out`, expected `bun` or `package_manager`\n\npackage_manager = \"npm\" is the direct equivalent — install npm tools via\nreal npm instead of mise''s built-in resolver, keeping lifecycle scripts\n(claude-code''s native-binary postinstall) working. No behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAIJBJ57EEMM5Njz7UtlC2sUHb5oUgGT+BAt3bTFeymR7GrQuw6e8OJ8gM/YsfPwzc\nS2H/1R9N1sgK5OM1ETWgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T02:49:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGU5MjIzOTllNTMwYmMyMjE1NDBiNjM5YzQyYWMyZmI0Mjk1YjAyMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8","sha":"dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8"}],"sha":"e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/e922399e530bc221540b639c42ac2fb4295b0234"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:40:44Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:40:44Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Use ansible_facts instead of top-level injected facts\n\nINJECT_FACTS_AS_VARS defaulting to True is deprecated and top-level facts stop\nbeing auto-injected in ansible-core 2.24, which would break every ansible_env\nreference. The playbook already read CI via ansible_facts, so this just makes\nthe remaining four call sites consistent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"005bb76ad5ac95a9aa2828c54667a650b1691522","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/005bb76ad5ac95a9aa2828c54667a650b1691522"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8","verification":{"payload":"tree 005bb76ad5ac95a9aa2828c54667a650b1691522\nparent 1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789591244 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789591244 -0400\n\nUse ansible_facts instead of top-level injected facts\n\nINJECT_FACTS_AS_VARS defaulting to True is deprecated and top-level facts stop\nbeing auto-injected in ansible-core 2.24, which would break every ansible_env\nreference. The playbook already read CI via ansible_facts, so this just makes\nthe remaining four call sites consistent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKpfoXNEz5j59apxDUeSdinhlHH6/ORv755kqwkZ0k8lYTj0OFkBAs4kG3pXYRA9XA\nG+goFmBktarN1uhNRq+Qc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T21:05:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGRiZWQ1MTVlMDlhNmI1ZGRmZDllNmNlNjUzYjNiOGRhODI1NGFjYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9","sha":"1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9"}],"sha":"dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/dbed515e09a6b5ddfd9e6ce653b3b8da8254acc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:39:03Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:39:03Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Harden firewall policy, verify effective values, fix TouchID guard\n\nVerification now reads the EFFECTIVE value macOS resolves by merging the user,\nsystem and managed domains via NSUserDefaults, rather than reading back the file\nwe just wrote. A file read only proves the write landed somewhere, which is the\nsame blind spot that hid the com.apple.alf firewall bug: the plist said 1 while\nthe OS ignored the plist entirely. Verified against all 12 system keys with no\nfalse failures.\n\nFirewall: macOS auto-allows any downloaded signed (notarized) app to accept\ninbound connections, which undoes much of the benefit of enabling the firewall\nat all -- Dropbox, Spotify and similar are admitted without ever asking. Manage\nboth signed-software policies explicitly, keeping built-in Apple software\nallowed and turning off the blanket allowance for downloaded apps. Both are\nconfig.yml variables, since the stricter setting costs a burst of one-time\nallow/deny prompts.\n\nTouchID: the guard stat''d /usr/lib/pam/pam_tid.so, which macOS does not ship --\nonly ABI-versioned modules exist (pam_tid.so.2). The guard was therefore always\nfalse and \"Enable TouchID for sudo\" had never run on any machine. The working\nconfig on this host was applied by hand, not by the playbook. Glob for the\nmodule instead so it survives the next ABI bump.\n\nAlso remove the stale askForPassword/askForPasswordDelay keys from\ncom.apple.dock, where they were written for years before being moved to\ncom.apple.screensaver, and disable wake-for-network-access, which keeps a\nsleeping laptop reachable for no benefit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8e7bd47dccdd4bdff9281b48f6bd33fcfcdeceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/c8e7bd47dccdd4bdff9281b48f6bd33fcfcdeceb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9","verification":{"payload":"tree c8e7bd47dccdd4bdff9281b48f6bd33fcfcdeceb\nparent 5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789591143 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789591143 -0400\n\nHarden firewall policy, verify effective values, fix TouchID guard\n\nVerification now reads the EFFECTIVE value macOS resolves by merging the user,\nsystem and managed domains via NSUserDefaults, rather than reading back the file\nwe just wrote. A file read only proves the write landed somewhere, which is the\nsame blind spot that hid the com.apple.alf firewall bug: the plist said 1 while\nthe OS ignored the plist entirely. Verified against all 12 system keys with no\nfalse failures.\n\nFirewall: macOS auto-allows any downloaded signed (notarized) app to accept\ninbound connections, which undoes much of the benefit of enabling the firewall\nat all -- Dropbox, Spotify and similar are admitted without ever asking. Manage\nboth signed-software policies explicitly, keeping built-in Apple software\nallowed and turning off the blanket allowance for downloaded apps. Both are\nconfig.yml variables, since the stricter setting costs a burst of one-time\nallow/deny prompts.\n\nTouchID: the guard stat''d /usr/lib/pam/pam_tid.so, which macOS does not ship --\nonly ABI-versioned modules exist (pam_tid.so.2). The guard was therefore always\nfalse and \"Enable TouchID for sudo\" had never run on any machine. The working\nconfig on this host was applied by hand, not by the playbook. Glob for the\nmodule instead so it survives the next ABI bump.\n\nAlso remove the stale askForPassword/askForPasswordDelay keys from\ncom.apple.dock, where they were written for years before being moved to\ncom.apple.screensaver, and disable wake-for-network-access, which keeps a\nsleeping laptop reachable for no benefit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOJriZXKSaTZN2rlSHTrLdNmNLuljSEtJTVzEDE+U9ZRw2wj5kbCZjl6pKsWES++8a\n4eaYP00ZXejBFl1WXtlwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T21:05:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDExODAzNDViNzEwYTg4M2VlNWM2NTQ2ODgwMjU3MWEyMTE2ODE0Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92","sha":"5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92"}],"sha":"1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/1180345b710a883ee5c65468802571a2116814f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:30:24Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:30:24Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Fix macOS settings tasks that reported success without applying anything\n\nTwo separate bugs, both of which let Ansible report green while the setting\nnever took effect.\n\nFirewall: the Application Firewall is an NEContentFilter on modern macOS, so\n`defaults write com.apple.alf` lands in a vestigial plist nothing reads. The\nfirewall had been off since at least May while config.yml declared it on.\nReplace the three alf defaults with socketfilterfw commands in the security\nblock, each followed by an unconditional read-back that fails the play if the\nsetting did not take. Firewall logging is dropped -- current macOS exposes no\n--setloggingmode flag. Skipped in CI, where a hard failure would go red on a\nrunner nobody intends to harden.\n\nSystem defaults: every macos_defaults.system entry is applied with become: true,\nso a bare domain makes `defaults write` run as root with HOME=/var/root and\nwrite root''s personal preferences instead of the system domain. Only the two\nentries using absolute paths ever worked; the keys that looked applied were\nmacOS''s own native defaults. Switch all system entries to absolute\n/Library/Preferences paths, fix the same bug in the autoLoginUser task, and add\na verification task that reads every key back from its real domain.\n\nAlso correct three keys that were wrong regardless of path:\n- askForPassword/askForPasswordDelay moved from com.apple.dock to\n  com.apple.screensaver, where they are actually read\n- forceLimitAdTracking replaced by allowApplePersonalizedAdvertising and moved\n  to the user list, since it is a per-user preference\n- MCX DisableGuestAccount removed as inert; GuestEnabled is the real control\n\nCI was asserting the wrong askForPassword domain, locking in the bug; updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93335afa097c3ab266a6596ae6969b15031c272c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/93335afa097c3ab266a6596ae6969b15031c272c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92","verification":{"payload":"tree 93335afa097c3ab266a6596ae6969b15031c272c\nparent 26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789590624 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789590624 -0400\n\nFix macOS settings tasks that reported success without applying anything\n\nTwo separate bugs, both of which let Ansible report green while the setting\nnever took effect.\n\nFirewall: the Application Firewall is an NEContentFilter on modern macOS, so\n`defaults write com.apple.alf` lands in a vestigial plist nothing reads. The\nfirewall had been off since at least May while config.yml declared it on.\nReplace the three alf defaults with socketfilterfw commands in the security\nblock, each followed by an unconditional read-back that fails the play if the\nsetting did not take. Firewall logging is dropped -- current macOS exposes no\n--setloggingmode flag. Skipped in CI, where a hard failure would go red on a\nrunner nobody intends to harden.\n\nSystem defaults: every macos_defaults.system entry is applied with become: true,\nso a bare domain makes `defaults write` run as root with HOME=/var/root and\nwrite root''s personal preferences instead of the system domain. Only the two\nentries using absolute paths ever worked; the keys that looked applied were\nmacOS''s own native defaults. Switch all system entries to absolute\n/Library/Preferences paths, fix the same bug in the autoLoginUser task, and add\na verification task that reads every key back from its real domain.\n\nAlso correct three keys that were wrong regardless of path:\n- askForPassword/askForPasswordDelay moved from com.apple.dock to\n  com.apple.screensaver, where they are actually read\n- forceLimitAdTracking replaced by allowApplePersonalizedAdvertising and moved\n  to the user list, since it is a per-user preference\n- MCX DisableGuestAccount removed as inert; GuestEnabled is the real control\n\nCI was asserting the wrong askForPassword domain, locking in the bug; updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJBjihBa6NOThrt0I2xAX8SjoGs3olS1cj3fIPKPLWwZJOr9JItLpsA1bwklfzaI3G\nijUBBWRZhjmR/pEpbn5gw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T20:30:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDVkYzY5NDcwYTIzZjZkMTBlYzA4ODY4MjRlMDE2NDBmNjQ3YjZkOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43","sha":"26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43"}],"sha":"5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/5dc69470a23f6d10ec0886824e01640f647b6d92"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:23:07Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:23:07Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Pin Ansible collections instead of re-downloading them every update\n\nscript/update ran `ansible-galaxy install -r requirements.yml --force`, which\nre-downloaded both roles and collections on every invocation. The flag was not\ngratuitous: collections were pinned to version ranges, and a plain `install`\ntreats an already-satisfied range as done, so --force was the only thing ever\npicking up a new in-range release.\n\nPin the collections to exact versions and let Renovate open the bump PRs. A\nplain `collection install` then converges on its own -- it installs whenever\nthe pin is unsatisfied, in either direction, and no-ops when it already\nmatches -- so the collection half needs no flag at all.\n\nRoles keep --force: `role install` has no --upgrade and otherwise refuses to\ntouch an already-installed role (\"use --force to change version to 2.4.0\"), so\na pin bump would silently never apply.\n\nBump community.general 12.6.5 -> 13.4.0 as part of the switch. The only 13.0.0\nbreaking change makes module_utils collection-private, which has no effect on\nconsumers; osx_defaults and homebrew are both untouched, and geerlingguy.mac\ndeclares community.general >=3.0.0. This also realigns the pin with the 13.4.0\nthat ansible 14.4 already bundles, which the 12.x pin had been shadowing.\n\nDoing the bump by hand also avoids renovatebot/renovate#41294, where the\npep440 `replace` strategy miscalculates upper-bound precision: the dependency\ndashboard had queued `>=13.4.0,<13.5.0`, narrowing the major band to a minor\none. Exact pins sidestep that entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cc1f394927299ee44e8073c3d8667e86c3e8558","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/0cc1f394927299ee44e8073c3d8667e86c3e8558"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43","verification":{"payload":"tree 0cc1f394927299ee44e8073c3d8667e86c3e8558\nparent a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789586587 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789586587 -0400\n\nPin Ansible collections instead of re-downloading them every update\n\nscript/update ran `ansible-galaxy install -r requirements.yml --force`, which\nre-downloaded both roles and collections on every invocation. The flag was not\ngratuitous: collections were pinned to version ranges, and a plain `install`\ntreats an already-satisfied range as done, so --force was the only thing ever\npicking up a new in-range release.\n\nPin the collections to exact versions and let Renovate open the bump PRs. A\nplain `collection install` then converges on its own -- it installs whenever\nthe pin is unsatisfied, in either direction, and no-ops when it already\nmatches -- so the collection half needs no flag at all.\n\nRoles keep --force: `role install` has no --upgrade and otherwise refuses to\ntouch an already-installed role (\"use --force to change version to 2.4.0\"), so\na pin bump would silently never apply.\n\nBump community.general 12.6.5 -> 13.4.0 as part of the switch. The only 13.0.0\nbreaking change makes module_utils collection-private, which has no effect on\nconsumers; osx_defaults and homebrew are both untouched, and geerlingguy.mac\ndeclares community.general >=3.0.0. This also realigns the pin with the 13.4.0\nthat ansible 14.4 already bundles, which the 12.x pin had been shadowing.\n\nDoing the bump by hand also avoids renovatebot/renovate#41294, where the\npep440 `replace` strategy miscalculates upper-bound precision: the dependency\ndashboard had queued `>=13.4.0,<13.5.0`, narrowing the major band to a minor\none. Exact pins sidestep that entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEn0VZIRetTTsTeRtFYKQiGt6uEk225/npbiRh3obMU0oDAvZ6HevjBeDNrm3MWs+Y\neydCUfKIaKuvmmaCcsmgo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T19:23:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKDI2ZDkwMzBmNDhjMjU4ZDAzYzhiOGY4MmRmYjNiNjlmMmIyYjRmNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610","sha":"a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610"}],"sha":"26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/26d9030f48c258d03c8b8f82dfb3b69f2b2b4f43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:23:05Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:23:05Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Bump @types/node to 22.20.3 and brace-expansion to 2.1.7\n\nTransitive lockfile drift picked up by script/update''s `npm update` step.\nNo package.json changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45836b54d6fb5f46dd39a6785699a21e0fedf9b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/45836b54d6fb5f46dd39a6785699a21e0fedf9b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610","verification":{"payload":"tree 45836b54d6fb5f46dd39a6785699a21e0fedf9b0\nparent 4f97c093bf6bd1eae4eeff7d45a7f11703db290f\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789586585 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789586585 -0400\n\nBump @types/node to 22.20.3 and brace-expansion to 2.1.7\n\nTransitive lockfile drift picked up by script/update''s `npm update` step.\nNo package.json changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIHfbdr1qoQZBRdGW1ZNgeFGsPkUJl7WaWRBB7MeTOTdg8h1KYM+SO2dFYJL+eD559\nlivqe18ExKasrg5Yi34As=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T19:23:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610","node_id":"C_kwDOALmu69oAKGEyZWIwMzk0YWQ0ODg3NTY0Nzc2YzA0YjdmMWYwM2VmMGYxMDQ2MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter/dotfiles/commit/4f97c093bf6bd1eae4eeff7d45a7f11703db290f","sha":"4f97c093bf6bd1eae4eeff7d45a7f11703db290f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/4f97c093bf6bd1eae4eeff7d45a7f11703db290f"}],"sha":"a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/a2eb0394ad4887564776c04b7f1f03ef0f104610"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benbalter","id":282759,"login":"benbalter","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mjc1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benbalter","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/commits/4f97c093bf6bd1eae4eeff7d45a7f11703db290f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:12:54Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T19:12:54Z","email":"ben@balter.com","name":"Ben Balter"},"message":"Run claude-code''s postinstall under mise\n\nmise stopped running npm lifecycle scripts when it switched to its built-in\npnpm-style resolver. claude-code ships bin/claude.exe as a 500-byte stub that\nits postinstall replaces with the ~200MB native binary, so every `mise upgrade`\nleft a CLI that errored out on launch:\n\n    Error: claude native binary not installed.\n\nThe platform package was downloaded fine — only the stub swap never happened.\n\nshell_out makes mise call real npm instead of its own resolver; npm_args opts\nthis one package back into its install script. Both are needed: npm_args only\napplies on the shell-out path, and mise passes --ignore-scripts=true by default.\n\nshell_out is global, so it covers the other npm: tools too. That''s the behavior\nthis repo already had before mise changed its backend, not a new exposure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2123cb92f7357803f104c32a9b1e06f147814ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/trees/a2123cb92f7357803f104c32a9b1e06f147814ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/benbalter/dotfiles/git/commits/4f97c093bf6bd1eae4eeff7d45a7f11703db290f","verification":{"payload":"tree a2123cb92f7357803f104c32a9b1e06f147814ae\nparent 9afd5a3a6144fb816336efebdce22207a97daee4\nauthor Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789585974 -0400\ncommitter Ben Balter <ben@balter.com> 1789585974 -0400\n\nRun claude-code''s postinstall under mise\n\nmise stopped running npm lifecycle scripts when it switched to its built-in\npnpm-style resolver. claude-code ships bin/claude.exe as a 500-byte stub that\nits postinstall replaces with the ~200MB native binary, so every `mise upgrade`\nleft a CLI that errored out on launch:\n\n    Error: claude native binary not installed.\n\nThe platform package was downloaded fine — only the stub swap never happened.\n\nshell_out makes mise call real npm instead of its own resolver; npm_args opts\nthis one package back into its install script. Both are needed: npm_args only\napplies on the shell-out path, and mise passes --ignore-scripts=true by default.\n\nshell_out is global, so it covers the other npm: tools too. That''s the behavior\nthis repo already had before mise changed its backend, not a new exposure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAglXOcMjmJIigvM4sxbnhlTp+cJ7\n0kd3+1606Kav0bdzkAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQM5ZWJ8mfxDPFjtzOK2ClRPQM0gL5piTM66IfKsnX/zHMB3q7M03jzrpg0PZ3wQZhu\naeuu+R5fkex4sx95UnRgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","