comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhipster/generator-jhipster/commits/5f439ad5aa5e2afb1c5be27476bd9d7c370ebed4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:56:51Z","email":"markus.bernhardt@me.com","name":"Markus Bernhardt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:56:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(spring-boot): deduplicate custom filters of criteria regardless of field order (#35327)\n\n* fix(spring-boot): deduplicate custom filters of criteria regardless of field order\n\nsortedUniqBy only drops adjacent duplicates, but the custom filters are\ncollected in field order. Fields of the same enum or LocalTime type that\nwere separated by a field with another custom filter declared the same\nnested filter class twice in the entity Criteria, which fails to compile.\nUse uniqBy, which keeps the first occurrence and leaves the output\nunchanged when there were no such duplicates.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(spring-boot): assert one custom filter per type on the prepared entity\n\nCheck the property the fix restores, one entry per type in\nentityJavaCustomFilters, instead of pinning every class declaration of\nthe generated criteria, so the test does not break on unrelated template\nchanges.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11e864490d569929045ffce539b945596b8bf915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhipster/generator-jhipster/git/trees/11e864490d569929045ffce539b945596b8bf915"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhipster/generator-jhipster/git/commits/5f439ad5aa5e2afb1c5be27476bd9d7c370ebed4","verification":{"payload":"tree 11e864490d569929045ffce539b945596b8bf915\nparent 184b76f81ddd1f89b75f2401bb653e8b59d7ca0e\nauthor Markus Bernhardt <markus.bernhardt@me.com> 1791244611 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791244611 -0300\n\nfix(spring-boot): deduplicate custom filters of criteria regardless of field order (#35327)\n\n* fix(spring-boot): deduplicate custom filters of criteria regardless of field order\n\nsortedUniqBy only drops adjacent duplicates, but the custom filters are\ncollected in field order. Fields of the same enum or LocalTime type that\nwere separated by a field with another custom filter declared the same\nnested filter class twice in the entity Criteria, which fails to compile.\nUse uniqBy, which keeps the first occurrence and leaves the output\nunchanged when there were no such duplicates.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(spring-boot): assert one custom filter per type on the prepared entity\n\nCheck the property the fix restores, one entry per type in\nentityJavaCustomFilters, instead of pinning every class declaration of\nthe generated criteria, so the test does not break on unrelated template\nchanges.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxDlDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKxQQAE34U4R2ySfdYutDK+4Uhwos\ntph9tkxrZexq8WzpcN27HcClgHrQmv8zJas5J49GQaZLVkt/kcABDZ6YxTsR4gVI\nhhOoQVXiMY0hdYVaOCh7rTvpod3t/ygyEGHCJIq0914W07YPzRbGJ6ceqhth1bC6\nBuWzmKh9QLYaxEx3gsKzPgzdC6CJM23GAN4QCvshxpSzDkUiF/Egs8hwQxl4s+jv\nekNdR+ngaZ0PsUgZ7ydOAHBfY/lLLGkVM0f/s/wZvWkdMO7j0Yi5pdOvDEKVHDy+\npqhqi0uDUQAegnQF9N78NvO9GQXX3fF8glLGYts/5D2i/6jznt6HOErLKGGTqjQ+\ntwQc7KSd/IU6Lm5LMq2GTgamKhG9d++x7/oV9405KwJWLqEmgw9VknzzMEO/sPAX\nx1xITkRoMO8cELG7E6InIKBzVOuT80frqA/3/o2tzVDRi5aIKG+8JVHLxaT9kV3w\nmucZpOUwqbobH56qFf87D0djFk64LGOqQfLMoVFSAapfQ/uoig3XFwCrT44/40zz\n/5CeFyrOAKST9+tz+QNfq91IWHzZWkc5JhoCapHP5INZgJUAe0CYjZDZqbU3DEDE\n/tavnrkRGd5ObkBIYo3qzRcwXusIkzb+w6mrNwuQDTHOA+38MqS64X6dXF9E8qGj\nMcbTdGbqp/Vdc1bUBk3g\n=iHSI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T23:56:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https: